window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v2-index"]=[{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 1  sakura airi s soliloquy  the volume opens in her pov whole first person monologue chapter   the only non ayanokoji pov chapter opening in year 1  vol  2  foreshadows her role as  an unexpected witness   ch 4   i don t know how to interact with other people  i m bad at talking while making eye contact  i m horrible with crowds  i don t remember how or when i became so hopeless   however  one thing i do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation  no matter how much i may love my solitude  i can t remain totally by myself  so  i came up with a solution  i would adopt a false face and hide my true self  then  i wouldn t be completely honest  but i could be a version of myself  i could continue to live in this dark  lonely world  self aware about her condition  frames the false face as a deliberate  solution  not an accident   same masking logic she later applies to photography   is everyone else putting on a facade  just like me  or do most people show their true selves to the outside world  since i can t connect with people  i suppose there s no way for me to find out the answer  therefore  i remain alone   i m all right by myself  i m all right with being alone   i  i want to connect with someone from the bottom of my heart  her interior voice  short declarative confessions  self questioning  closing cadence  and so i will continue to live quietly  with my eyes downcast  alone  paradox locked in at volume start  wants a heart to heart connection while believing connection is impossible for her   the engine of her year 1  vol  2 arc","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1\">Ch.1 &quot;Sakura Airi&#x27;s Soliloquy&quot;: the volume opens in her POV<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.10<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I don&#x27;t know how to interact with other people. I&#x27;m bad at talking while making eye contact. I&#x27;m horrible with crowds. I don&#x27;t remember how or when I became so hopeless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;However, one thing I do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation. No matter how much I may love my solitude, I can&#x27;t remain totally by myself. So, I came up with a solution. I would adopt a false face…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Is everyone else putting on a façade, just like me? Or do most people show their true selves to the outside world? Since I can&#x27;t connect with people, I suppose there&#x27;s no way for me to find out the answer. Therefore, I remain…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Whole first-person monologue chapter — the only non-Ayanokōji POV chapter opening in Year 1, Vol. 2; foreshadows her role as &quot;An Unexpected Witness&quot; (Ch.4).<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, one thing I do know for certain is that a person cannot live entirely in isolation. No matter how much I may love my solitude, I can&#x27;t remain totally by myself. So, I came up with a solution. I would adopt a false face and hide my true self. Then, I wouldn&#x27;t be completely honest, but I could be a version of myself. I could continue to live in this dark, lonely world.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Self-aware about her condition; frames the false face as a deliberate &quot;solution,&quot; not an accident — same masking logic she later applies to photography.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Is everyone else putting on a façade, just like me? Or do most people show their true selves to the outside world? Since I can&#x27;t connect with people, I suppose there&#x27;s no way for me to find out the answer. Therefore, I remain alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I&#x27;m all right by myself. I&#x27;m all right with being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I… I want to connect with someone from the bottom of my heart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Her interior voice: short declarative confessions, self-questioning, closing cadence &quot;And so I will continue to live quietly, with my eyes downcast. Alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Paradox locked in at volume start: wants a heart-to-heart connection while believing connection is impossible for her — the engine of her Year 1, Vol. 2 arc.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\">→ After: Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner","w":"sudou-ken sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 2 opening  she stumbles on sudou s three on one brawl  the witness birthed  evening of june 30  inside a school building with a staircase  the  special building  named sudou s account p 30 31  while hunting for a good selfie spot  sakura finds three male students writhing on the floor and a red haired boy standing over them   the timing couldn t have been worse  while searching for a place to take a good selfie  i stumbled into something  even a certain famous  diminutive detective would have held his breath when witnessing such a tense situation   his right fist was covered in blood from the students he d pummeled  this was the first brawl i d ever witnessed  terror overrides etiquette but not habit   though i was terrified  i began capturing the scene with my camera  the shutter didn t make a sound  panic freeze   after taking the pictures  i asked myself what i was doing  i couldn t think clearly in my panicked state  my legs didn t obey my command to move  like i was paralyzed   i d heard that that when someone was involved in a crisis  his or her body would lock up  exactly like what was happening now   sic   doubled  that  in corpus   i d hate it if someone were to spot me and involve me in this mess  if that happened  it would cast a dark cloud over my otherwise peaceful school life  sudou  sensing movement  calls  is someone there  toward her hiding spot  she escapes by seconds   i d successfully escaped by a hair s breadth  if i d lagged a mere two seconds  he probably would ve seen me  document first  confront never instinct  she photographs the fight but flees rather than intervene or report  self protection through invisibility  unseen witness to his brawl  nearly discovered by him   she does not know his name to face link yet beyond  sudou kun  heard in his taunts  sec  2 2 lunch  observed by ayanokoji  still eating alone  hunched over a homemade bento  the glasses and plain girl reputation  at one time ike had made a ruckus about how large her breasts were  but because she was considered plain  everyone quickly lost interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\">Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.12–13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening of June 30, inside a school building with a staircase (the &quot;special building,&quot; named Sudou&#x27;s account p.30–31). While hunting for a good selfie spot, Sakura finds three male students writhing on the floor and a red-haired boy standing over them. Sudou, sensing movement, calls &quot;Is someone there?&quot; toward her hiding spot; she escapes by seconds: &quot;I’d successfully escaped by a hair’s breadth. If I’d lagged a mere two seconds, he probably would’ve seen me.&quot; sec. 2.2 lunch, observed by Ayanokōji: still eating alone, hunched over a homemade bento; the glasses-and-plain-girl reputation (&quot;At one time Ike had made a ruckus about how large her breasts were, but because she was considered plain, everyone quickly lost interest.&quot;).<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;The timing couldn’t have been worse. While searching for a place to take a good selfie, I stumbled into something. Even a certain famous, diminutive detective would have held his breath when witnessing such a tense situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;His right fist was covered in blood from the students he’d pummeled. This was the first brawl I’d ever witnessed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Panic freeze: &quot;After taking the pictures, I asked myself what I was doing. I couldn’t think clearly in my panicked state... My legs didn’t obey my command to move, like I was paralyzed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Terror overrides etiquette but not habit: &quot;Though I was terrified, I began capturing the scene with my camera. The shutter didn’t make a sound.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’d heard that that when someone was involved in a crisis, his or her body would lock up, exactly like what was happening now.&quot; (sic — doubled &quot;that&quot; in corpus)<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’d hate it if someone were to spot me and involve me in this mess. If that happened, it would cast a dark cloud over my otherwise peaceful school life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Document-first, confront-never instinct: she photographs the fight but flees rather than intervene or report; self-protection through invisibility.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Unseen witness to his brawl; nearly discovered by him — she does not know his name-to-face link yet beyond &quot;Sudou-kun&quot; heard in his taunts.<span class=\"pg\">p.12–13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1 &quot;Sakura Airi&#x27;s Soliloquy&quot;: the volume opens in her POV<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p12-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 2 opening  one punches three class c boys  finishes the fight post fight tableau seen through sakura s eyes  three boys on the floor  sudou standing over them  right fist bloody   it was an entirely one sided ordeal   he he  so  do you really think that this is the end of it  sudou   one of the beaten class c boys taunts from the floor   speaker unnamed   do you wanna make me laugh  you re in the sorriest state possible  you want to go for another round  huh  next time i won t hold back  grabs the taunter s collar and hauls him face to face   sudou looked as though he was going to kill and then devour his opponent  which was so overwhelming that the defeated boy looked away   are you scared  did you really think you d beat me if you had more people   what a waste of time  tiring me out after practice  give me a break   nothing s more pathetic than a sore loser  no matter how many times you come at me  you won t win  leaves like the winners  corner doesn t matter   dropped the student  picked up his bag  and then turned and walked away as if the defeated three completely disinterested him   is someone there   senses sakura s movement  misses her by two seconds   he never learns there was a witness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p12-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p12-1\">Ch.2 opening: one-punches three Class C boys, finishes the fight<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.12–13<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Post-fight tableau seen through Sakura&#x27;s eyes: three boys on the floor, Sudou standing over them, right fist bloody; &quot;It was an entirely one-sided ordeal.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;He he, so. Do you really think that this is the end of it, Sudou?&quot; (one of the beaten Class C boys taunts from the floor — speaker unnamed)<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Do you wanna make me laugh? You’re in the sorriest state possible. You want to go for another round, huh? Next time I won’t hold back.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Are you scared? Did you really think you’d beat me if you had more people?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Grabs the taunter&#x27;s collar and hauls him face-to-face; &quot;Sudou looked as though he was going to kill and then devour his opponent, which was so overwhelming that the defeated boy looked away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.12<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What a waste of time. Tiring me out after practice. Give me a break,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing’s more pathetic than a sore loser. No matter how many times you come at me, you won’t win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Leaves like the winners&#x27; corner doesn&#x27;t matter: &quot;dropped the student, picked up his bag, and then turned and walked away as if the defeated three completely disinterested him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is someone there?&quot; (senses Sakura&#x27;s movement; misses her by two seconds — he never learns there was a witness)<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: hauled to the faculty room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 1  july 1  first class points  delayed deposit july 1  class d homeroom  abnormally raucous  the first monthly point deposit since enrollment is expected  system recap for the reader   we used these private points to purchase daily necessities  meals  even electrical appliances  at this school  points are currency  they are very important   if you didn t have any private points  you were forced to live day today without spending money  you couldn t use real currency anywhere on campus  class d sat at zero class points since june  every class started with 1000 class points  deposit   class points   100 paid into each private account on day 1   however  my perspective changed when i bought a point for the midterm test    private points can change your situation  you  could likely purchase more than just test points   are you disappointed because the gap between the classes has widened  horikita   the sharp witted hirata hadn t missed a beat  splendid   hirata decoding horikita s  get something  reads chabashira s hedged closing  if there are still points left  that is  as deliberate   there was deeper meaning behind chabashira sensei s words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): first class points, delayed deposit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.15–18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">July 1, Class D homeroom, abnormally raucous: the first monthly point deposit since enrollment is expected.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> System recap for the reader: &quot;We used these private points to purchase daily necessities, meals, even electrical appliances. At this school, points are currency. They are very important.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If you didn’t have any private points, you were forced to live day-today without spending money. You couldn’t use real currency anywhere on campus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Are you disappointed because the gap between the classes has widened, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D sat at zero class points since June; every class started with 1000 class points; deposit = class points × 100 paid into each private account on day 1.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, my perspective changed when I bought a point for the midterm test.&quot; — private points can change your situation; you &quot;could likely purchase more than just test points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The sharp-witted Hirata hadn’t missed a beat. Splendid.&quot; (Hirata decoding Horikita&#x27;s &quot;get something&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads Chabashira&#x27;s hedged closing (&quot;If there are still points left, that is.&quot;) as deliberate: &quot;There was deeper meaning behind Chabashira-sensei’s words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16–19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p15-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points july 1  the app mechanics  first payout  delayed deposit school app functions enumerated  balance inquiry  personal balance  collective class points  and point transfer to another student  point types suffixed  cl   class  and  pr   private   on the first day of every month  they multiplied the cl points  or class points  by 100  then deposited that amount into our private point accounts  zero class points   zero spending money  real currency is refused anywhere on campus  free cafeteria meals are the floor for broke students  every class admitted with 1000 class points  class d bled to 0 by may and stayed 0 through june  july 1 board  class a 1004  slightly above admission baseline  classes b c each  100 over june  class d 87   first nonzero total  interpretive precedent  horikita  a uniform  100 jump for all first year classes reads as the midterm completion reward  not merit  relative rank  not raw points  drives promotion  deposits can be delayed institution wide   the first year students  point distribution has been delayed  chabashira s rider   once the trouble has been resolved  you ll receive your points  if there are still points left  that is  school supermarket offers free ingredients  same subsidy logic as the free cafeteria set    horikita s bento runs on them  disciplinary economics  first instance  an unresolved inter class fight threatens both an individual summer suspension for sudou and a class wide point deduction  the school granted a proof window until  next tuesday  before ruling fault  sample drain rate  ayanokoji s post midterm point purchase balance 8 320 private points  87 class points would have paid  8700 yen per student","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p15-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p15-1\">July 1: the app mechanics, first payout, delayed deposit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.15–20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> School app functions enumerated: Balance Inquiry, personal balance, collective class points, and point transfer to another student; point types suffixed &quot;cl&quot; (class) and &quot;pr&quot; (private).<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> &quot;On the first day of every month, they multiplied the cl points, or class points, by 100, then deposited that amount into our private point accounts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Zero class points = zero spending money; real currency is refused anywhere on campus; free cafeteria meals are the floor for broke students.<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Every class admitted with 1000 class points; Class D bled to 0 by May and stayed 0 through June.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> July 1 board: Class A 1004 (slightly above admission baseline); Classes B/C each ~+100 over June; Class D 87 — first nonzero total.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Interpretive precedent (Horikita): a uniform ~+100 jump for all first-year classes reads as the midterm-completion reward, not merit; relative rank, not raw points, drives promotion.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Deposits can be delayed institution-wide: &quot;The first-year students’ point distribution has been delayed.&quot; Chabashira&#x27;s rider: &quot;Once the trouble has been resolved, you’ll receive your points. If there are still points left, that is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> School supermarket offers free ingredients (same subsidy logic as the free cafeteria set) — Horikita&#x27;s bento runs on them.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Disciplinary economics, first instance: an unresolved inter-class fight threatens both an individual summer suspension for Sudou and a class-wide point deduction; the school granted a proof window until &quot;next Tuesday&quot; before ruling fault.<span class=\"pg\">p.31–32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Sample drain rate: Ayanokōji&#x27;s post-midterm-point-purchase balance 8,320 private points; 87 class points would have paid ~8700 yen per student.<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: what a disciplinary case does to a class&#x27;s balance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 1  july 1  the point board  and a deposit with a rider she  strode into the classroom as the homeroom bell rang  to a class d more raucous than usual  the first payout day since enrollment   good morning  everyone  you all seem more restless than usual today   oh  so that s why you re all so restless   don t jump to conclusions  listen to what i have to say first  you re correct  ike  you have all worked harder than ever before  i recognize that  naturally  the school understands full well how you all feel  puts a paper listing the month s point totals on the board  class a at the top  rather than letting the class read the app s numbers unexplained   well then  without further ado  here are this month s point totals   well  this time there was a little trouble  the first year students  point distribution has been delayed  i m sorry  but you ll have to wait a bit longer   don t blame me  this was the school s decision  there s nothing i can do about it  once the trouble has been resolved  you ll receive your points  if there are still points left  that is  the same method as entrance day  now in maintenance mode  buy the room s acknowledgment first  you re correct  ike  then deliver the bad news  then assign it to the school and refuse responsibility   closing on a conditional no student asks her to unpack  ayanokoji is the only one who hears the rider as a warning   there was deeper meaning behind chabashira sensei s words  ak s memory of her entrance day line is what taught the class to spend  he  understood that our homeroom teacher  chabashira sensei  hadn t been kidding when she told us   at this school  you can buy anything with your points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): the point board, and a deposit with a rider<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.16–18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She &quot;strode into the classroom as the homeroom bell rang&quot; to a Class D more raucous than usual, the first payout day since enrollment. Puts a paper listing the month&#x27;s point totals on the board, Class A at the top, rather than letting the class read the app&#x27;s numbers unexplained.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Good morning, everyone. You all seem more restless than usual today.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Oh, so that’s why you’re all so restless?”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Don’t jump to conclusions. Listen to what I have to say first. You’re correct, Ike. You have all worked harder than ever before. I recognize that. Naturally, the school understands full well how you all feel.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then. Without further ado, here are this month’s point totals.”<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, this time there was a little trouble. The first-year students’ point distribution has been delayed. I’m sorry, but you’ll have to wait a bit longer,”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t blame me. This was the school’s decision, there’s nothing I can do about it. Once the trouble has been resolved, you’ll receive your points. If there are still points left, that is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The same method as entrance day, now in maintenance mode: buy the room&#x27;s acknowledgment first (&quot;You’re correct, Ike&quot;), then deliver the bad news, then assign it to the school and refuse responsibility — closing on a conditional no student asks her to unpack.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Ayanokōji is the only one who hears the rider as a warning: &quot;There was deeper meaning behind Chabashira-sensei’s words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s memory of her entrance-day line is what taught the class to spend: he &quot;understood that our homeroom teacher, Chabashira-sensei, hadn’t been kidding when she told us, &#x27;At this school, you can buy anything with your points.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 2 sec  2 1  decoding horikita in public  the class leader  hirata yousuke  answered for her    after horikita bait and silences the class on  get something   i believe that horikita san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout april and may  in other words  we didn t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late  reads peers  half thoughts accurately and translates them for the room without seeking credit  ak   the sharp witted hirata hadn t missed a beat  splendid  named by ak as an expert advice pillar  if it were horikita or hirata here  they d probably be able to give expert advice    but unusable on sudou s case because  sudou hates hirata  still the object of sudou s hatred from the fake expulsion episode  hirata is not in the crisis s inner circle at all  ak holds him up as the standard he himself declines to be","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;The class leader, Hirata Yousuke, answered for her.&quot; — after Horikita bait-and-silences the class on &quot;get something.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;I believe that Horikita-san is referring to the deductions we incurred throughout April and May. In other words, we didn’t see a reduction in points for talking in class or being late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads peers&#x27; half-thoughts accurately and translates them for the room without seeking credit; AK: &quot;The sharp-witted Hirata hadn’t missed a beat. Splendid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Named by AK as an expert-advice pillar (&quot;If it were Horikita or Hirata here, they’d probably be able to give expert advice.&quot;) — but unusable on Sudou&#x27;s case because &quot;Sudou hates Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36–37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Still the object of Sudou&#x27;s hatred from the fake-expulsion episode; Hirata is not in the crisis&#x27;s inner circle at all.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK holds him up as the standard he himself declines to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2 sec  2 1  july 1  reading the point board correctly  this isn t good  could they have figured out a way to increase their point total   it s too early to celebrate  all the other classes saw a similar increase in their points  we didn t close the distance at all  this might just be a reward first year students receive for getting through the midterm  every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points   so that s what happened  i thought it odd that we d been awarded points so quickly   no  that s not it  we managed to get something this time  after all   to ak s jab about the widening gap  then falls silent  refusing to explain  only student tracking other classes  totals  celebration proof   measures relative gap  not absolute gain","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.17–18<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;This isn’t good. Could they have figured out a way to increase their point total?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class…<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;So that’s what happened. I thought it odd that we’d been awarded points so quickly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s too early to celebrate. All the other classes saw a similar increase in their points. We didn’t close the distance at all. This might just be a reward first-year students receive for getting through the midterm. Every class seems to have gotten at least 100 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, that’s not it. We managed to get something this time, after all.&quot; (to AK&#x27;s jab about the widening gap; then falls silent, refusing to explain)<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Only student tracking other classes&#x27; totals; celebration-proof — measures relative gap, not absolute gain.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 2  lunch  having friends and still eating alone  meanwhile  i don t really belong anywhere   however  now i was experiencing a strange phenomenon  i had friends  yet i was still on my own   i m over here  guys  it s okay for you to invite me  my glances were filled with selfishness and anticipation  i was flooded by feelings of self loathing  fear of the low tier friend question   did they all consider me a low tier friend  or was our friendship all in my head   you seem completely used to solitude   to horikita  meant as sarcasm  taken by her as sincere   doesn t it cost quite a bit and take a lot of effort to make your own lunch   don t tell me  not only are you a bright scholar  you re an accomplished cook as well  that doesn t seem to fit your personality   but why did you decide to go through the trouble of making your own lunch   do i already miss riding the big cafeteria bound wave of students  koenji assessment   he didn t love solitude  but rather  loved himself and cared little for others  i respected that he didn t seem bothered at all by being alone  notes the quiet bespectacled classmate  sakura  making her own bento   she was always alone  and i d never seen her talk to anyone  sticks to horikita despite constant insults   i wished i had a comeback for that  but i couldn t argue  i just wanted her to cut me a break","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19–21<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;You seem completely used to solitude,&quot; (to Horikita; meant as sarcasm, taken by her as sincere)<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Doesn’t it cost quite a bit and take a lot of effort to make your own lunch?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Don’t tell me. Not only are you a bright scholar, you’re an accomplished cook as well? That doesn’t seem to fit your personality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Meanwhile, I don’t really belong anywhere.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;However, now I was experiencing a strange phenomenon: I had friends, yet I was still on my own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’m over here, guys. It’s okay for you to invite me. My glances were filled with selfishness and anticipation. I was flooded by feelings of self-loathing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Fear of the low-tier-friend question: &quot;Did they all consider me a low-tier friend? Or was our friendship all in my head?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But why did you decide to go through the trouble of making your own lunch?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do I already miss riding the big cafeteria-bound wave of students?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Kōenji assessment: &quot;He didn’t love solitude, but rather, loved himself and cared little for others. I respected that he didn’t seem bothered at all by being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Notes the quiet bespectacled classmate (Sakura) making her own bento: &quot;She was always alone, and I’d never seen her talk to anyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sticks to Horikita despite constant insults: &quot;I wished I had a comeback for that, but I couldn’t argue. I just wanted her to cut me a break.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p15-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): first class points, delayed deposit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2 sec  2 2  lunch  the bento era  you re still not used to it  you re as pathetic as ever  ayanokouji kun   noticing him scanning for lunch invitations   i m quite fine  thank you   his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally   i m not sure about that  the school supermarket provides free ingredients  you know   anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the internet  our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools  as well   the cafeteria is noisy  it s much more relaxing to eat here  wouldn t you say   you re always staring out at the ocean  but you don t have a surfboard  you lack even the determination to ride the wave  don t you  and you talk about missing it  you re awfully full of yourself  new budget coping routine  home made bento from free supermarket ingredients  refuses the free cafeteria subsidy optics  roasts ak with ocean surfboard metaphor unprompted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19–21<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You’re still not used to it. You’re as pathetic as ever, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; (noticing him scanning for lunch invitations)<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’m quite fine, thank you.&quot; (his sarcasm about her solitude taken literally)<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’m not sure about that. The school supermarket provides free ingredients, you know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyone can cook by looking up a recipe in a book or on the Internet. Our dorms come equipped with all of the necessary tools, as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The cafeteria is noisy. It’s much more relaxing to eat here, wouldn’t you say?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re always staring out at the ocean, but you don’t have a surfboard. You lack even the determination to ride the wave, don’t you? And you talk about missing it? You’re awfully full of yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.21<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> New budget coping routine: home-made bento from free supermarket ingredients; refuses the free-cafeteria-subsidy optics; roasts AK with ocean/surfboard metaphor unprompted.<span class=\"pg\">p.19–21<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): reading the point board correctly<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2 sec  2 2  the social ceiling  narrated ak s snapshot of her position   she s extremely popular and has many friends  both girls and boys  she gets in person invitations  along with constant invites over the phone and through email  when she eats with friends she appears to have a real life","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s snapshot of her position: &quot;She’s extremely popular and has many friends, both girls and boys. She gets in-person invitations, along with constant invites over the phone and through email... when she eats with friends she appears to have a real life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 2 sec  2 2   sec  2 4  crew member  key club member lunch ensemble   you ve got people like ike and yamauchi  who aren t very popular with girls  they eat with their group of guy friends  including sudou and hondou  almost every day  one of  the rest of us  who made duplicate keycards to ayanokoji s room and treat it as the group s meeting spot  sudou refuses to surrender his clone  still grouped with ike as the class s non popular boy clique two months in","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2 &amp; sec. 2.4: crew member, key-club member<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.19, p.27–28<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch ensemble: &quot;you’ve got people like Ike and Yamauchi, who aren’t very popular with girls. They eat with their group of guy friends, including Sudou and Hondou, almost every day.&quot;<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> One of &quot;the rest of us&quot; who made duplicate keycards to Ayanokōji&#x27;s room and treat it as the group&#x27;s meeting spot; Sudou refuses to surrender his clone.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Still grouped with Ike as the class&#x27;s non-popular boy clique two months in.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\">→ After: Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 2 sec  2 2  lunch  the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria lunch in the class d room  horikita  ayanokoji and koenji are the students still at their desks while the rest have gone to eat    a few students were still all alone  ak s account of how his social calendar changed   on first starting here  he d enjoyed the company of girls from other classes and grade levels  however  once he ran low on points  he began to spend most of his time in the classroom   he was currently completely lost in examining his face in a hand mirror  his daily routine  ak s correction of the usual reading of him   he didn t love solitude  but rather  loved himself and cared little for others  i respected that he didn t seem bothered at all by being alone   he was the sole heir to the kouenji conglomerate group  one of the largest corporations in japan    ak repeats the fact here as background for why koenji is unbothered  his own dismissal of class rank belongs to volume 1 and is recorded there  what he eats  and whether he buys anything at all in july  is never stated  the text here says only that he has stopped leaving the classroom to be entertained","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.20<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch in the Class D room: Horikita, Ayanokōji and Kōenji are the students still at their desks while the rest have gone to eat — &quot;a few students were still all alone&quot;. &quot;He was currently completely lost in examining his face in a hand mirror, his daily routine.&quot;<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s account of how his social calendar changed: &quot;On first starting here, he’d enjoyed the company of girls from other classes and grade levels. However, once he ran low on points, he began to spend most of his time in the classroom.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s correction of the usual reading of him: &quot;He didn’t love solitude, but rather, loved himself and cared little for others. I respected that he didn’t seem bothered at all by being alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> &quot;He was the sole heir to the Kouenji conglomerate group, one of the largest corporations in Japan.&quot; — AK repeats the fact here as background for why Kōenji is unbothered; his own dismissal of class rank belongs to Volume 1 and is recorded there.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> What he eats, and whether he buys anything at all in July, is never stated; the text here says only that he has stopped leaving the classroom to be entertained.<span class=\"pg\">p.20<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 3  after school  horikita  kushida  and the  hate  chat  there was some value in being able to vanish like a ninja into a crowd  if i hung toward the back of some group of friends  i could pretend i was one of them   i don t really think so  what about you  horikita  you were the only person who gave sudou a helping hand  on walking home with horikita   since we didn t have lunch together or just casually hang out  i found it odd  then again  we had the same path back to the dormitory   that reminds me  you should join in the chat now and again  you re the only one who hasn t caught up in a long time   telling horikita to catch up on the class group chat  she keeps notifications off and is  not interested   i wonder  well  if i had to think of a reason  i guess i got used to attending school  and then i made some friends  also  kushida was probably a big influence   i admit i found it shocking when she said that she hated you  horikita  but i think it s only natural that everyone has people they like and people they hate  there s no point being concerned about it  i mean  you still pretend to get along well with kushida san even though she said she hates you  right   hey    followed by   what the heck  it really hurt when she said it straight out like that   were you testing me   no need  i m fine with the kushida we have now     even though i d spoken the words  i did feel disgusted with myself  routine walking and talking pair now  she notices he is  quite talkative lately  he admits he only relaxes around a few specific people  if she were another girl  i probably wouldn t have been able to converse normally","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t really think so. What about you, Horikita? You were the only person who gave Sudou a helping hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That reminds me. You should join in the chat now and again. You’re the only one who hasn’t caught up in a long time.&quot; (telling Horikita to catch up on the class group chat; she keeps notifications off and is &quot;not interested&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I wonder. Well, if I had to think of a reason, I guess I got used to attending school, and then I made some friends. Also, Kushida was probably a big influence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;There was some value in being able to vanish like a ninja into a crowd. If I hung toward the back of some group of friends, I could pretend I was one of them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On walking home with Horikita: &quot;Since we didn’t have lunch together or just casually hang out, I found it odd. Then again, we had the same path back to the dormitory.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I admit I found it shocking when she said that she hated you, Horikita. But I think it’s only natural that everyone has people they like and people they hate. There’s no point being concerned about it. I mean, you still pretend to get along well with Kushida-san even though she said she hates you, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey…&quot; — followed by: &quot;What the heck? It really hurt when she said it straight out like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Were you testing me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No need. I’m fine with the Kushida we have now,&quot; — &quot;Even though I’d spoken the words, I did feel disgusted with myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Routine walking-and-talking pair now; she notices he is &quot;quite talkative lately&quot;; he admits he only relaxes around a few specific people (&quot;If she were another girl, I probably wouldn’t have been able to converse normally.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–26<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): having friends and still eating alone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 2 sec  2 3  collecting sudou for the faculty room  sudou  i have to talk to you about something  come to the faculty room   i ve already spoken with the advisor  you don t have to come with me if you don t want to  but you will face the consequences later   that all depends on you  the longer you stand there  the more time you waste  she removes the excuse before she makes the request   the club advisor has already been told  so his  i ve got basketball practice now  buys nothing  refuses to estimate how long it will take  that all depends on you  first direct contact since she cancelled his expulsion at the midterm  private summons  no audience in front of the class  and he  clicked his tongue  and followed  her out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Sudou. I have to talk to you about something. Come to the faculty room,”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I’ve already spoken with the advisor. You don’t have to come with me if you don’t want to, but you will face the consequences later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “That all depends on you. The longer you stand there, the more time you waste.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She removes the excuse before she makes the request — the club advisor has already been told, so his &quot;I’ve got basketball practice now&quot; buys nothing. Refuses to estimate how long it will take (&quot;That all depends on you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> First direct contact since she cancelled his expulsion at the midterm: private summons, no audience in front of the class, and he &quot;clicked his tongue, and followed&quot; her out.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1 (July 1): the point board, and a deposit with a rider<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 2 sec  2 3  after school  points paranoia  chat refusal  oil and water  do you think so  too  that it would have been better if sudou kun were expelled   opening  while packing every textbook   hmm  well  we still don t know whether our points would go up as a class  really   on her own midterm rescue of sudou   feigned disinterest   i m a little worried about what chabashira sensei said this morning   yes  she said that there was trouble  but did she mean that it was a problem for the school  or a problem for us  the students  if it s the latter  then   i hope that s the case  trouble directly affects our points   i m not interested in the slightest  also  i keep my notifications turned off   class group chat  joined but zero participation  keeps the app so leaving won t notify kushida   you ve been quite talkative lately  ayanokouji kun   it s a slight difference  but you ve changed   did something make you change   you seem to be getting along quite well with kushida san  aren t you bothered  especially knowing about her other side   hmm  well  you may have a point there  it s true that i hate you  too  ayanokouji kun  yet i talk to you normally  i don t really mind  then   that s what i m getting at  if someone says that they hate another person  it s fine  but if someone says that they hate you  don t you feel a little bad   i don t have any intention of getting in her way  but kushida san and i are like oil and water  i think it s better not to associate with her   who knows  she probably doesn t know that much about me   if you re that curious  why don t you ask her yourself  directly   what you just said was really disgusting  you know that   reaction to  i m fine with the kushida we have now  runs the worst case simulation on every institutional signal  her hate lines are delivered analytically  then re used as a lesson about honesty  deliberate testing of ak  his   were you testing me  daily walk back ritual  she monitors his behavioral drift and says so  conversation register now includes open hostility as rapport  it s true that i hate you  too  ayanokouji kun  yet i talk to you normally  declares them  like oil and water  refuses any shared group engagement with her  genuinely does not know kushida s rooftop face  won t call for his expulsion yet discounts defending him publicly  frames everything through class point consequences","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–26<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Do you think so, too? That it would have been better if Sudou-kun were expelled?&quot; (opening, while packing every textbook)<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Hmm. Well, we still don’t know whether our points would go up as a class, really,&quot; (on her own midterm rescue of Sudou — feigned disinterest)<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’m a little worried about what Chabashira-sensei said this morning,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes. She said that there was trouble, but did she mean that it was a problem for the school, or a problem for us, the students? If it’s the latter, then…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I hope that’s the case. Trouble directly affects our points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not interested in the slightest. Also, I keep my notifications turned off.&quot; (class group chat: joined but zero participation; keeps the app so leaving won&#x27;t notify Kushida)<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’ve been quite talkative lately, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s a slight difference, but you’ve changed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did something make you change?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You seem to be getting along quite well with Kushida-san. Aren’t you bothered, especially knowing about her other side?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm. Well, you may have a point there. It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally. I don’t really mind, then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s what I’m getting at. If someone says that they hate another person, it’s fine. But if someone says that they hate you, don’t you feel a little bad?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t have any intention of getting in her way, but Kushida-san and I are like oil and water. I think it’s better not to associate with her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who knows? She probably doesn’t know that much about me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you’re that curious, why don’t you ask her yourself? Directly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What you just said was really disgusting, you know that?&quot; (reaction to &quot;I&#x27;m fine with the Kushida we have now&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Runs the worst-case simulation on every institutional signal; her hate lines are delivered analytically, then re-used as a lesson about honesty; deliberate testing of AK (his: &quot;Were you testing me?&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.22–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Daily walk-back ritual; she monitors his behavioral drift and says so; conversation register now includes open hostility-as-rapport (&quot;It’s true that I hate you, too, Ayanokouji-kun, yet I talk to you normally&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.19–26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Declares them &quot;like oil and water&quot;; refuses any shared-group engagement with her; genuinely does not know Kushida&#x27;s rooftop face.<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Won&#x27;t call for his expulsion yet discounts defending him publicly; frames everything through class-point consequences.<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): the bento era<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p22-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 2 sec  2 3  hauled to the faculty room tries to bolt to basketball practice when chabashira calls him  lazily flashes his sports uniform  only follows her after her consequence threat  clicking his tongue   huh  what do you want with me  i ve got basketball practice now   what  will this be over quickly  a classmate s mutter sums his reputation   i thought that he might have changed  but i guess sudou s the same as ever  wouldn t it have been better if he just got kicked out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p22-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: hauled to the faculty room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.22–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Tries to bolt to basketball practice when Chabashira calls him; lazily flashes his sports uniform; only follows her after her consequence threat, clicking his tongue.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Huh? What do you want with me? I’ve got basketball practice now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;What? Will this be over quickly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> A classmate&#x27;s mutter sums his reputation: &quot;I thought that he might have changed, but I guess Sudou’s the same as ever. Wouldn’t it have been better if he just got kicked out?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 opening: one-punches three Class C boys, finishes the fight<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: confesses the fight to AK + Kushida, begs for secrecy<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2 sec  2 3  group chat wistfulness kushida was the one who doubted horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite  kushida had doubted whether horikita would actually participate  since she hated talking with others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.24<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida was the one who doubted Horikita would ever join the class group chat after the midterm invite (&quot;Kushida had doubted whether Horikita would actually participate, since she hated talking with others.&quot;).<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2: the social ceiling, narrated<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">→ After: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 2 sec  2 4  night  sudou s brawl  duplicate keys  kushida s pressure private balance after the midterm point purchase   i saw that i had 8 320 private points     i had nearly bankrupted myself just to buy the point sudou needed to pass   converted  the points came to roughly 8700 yen  although that wasn t a giant improvement  it was still big bucks   87 class points expected payout   why re you here  actually  forget that   how did you even get in   i learned this extremely important fact just now   learning the group cloned his room key   no  i can t forget about it  hand over the key   what an illogical argument  even if you re ignorant of committing a crime  it s still a crime  friendship doesn t mean automatically allowing people to do whatever they want   if you need advice or you re worried about something  why not ask ike or yamauchi   did you insult chabashira sensei  by any chance   then what  did you grab her by the collar and threaten to kill her or something   you beat them up  so  uh  why did you do that   well  i wonder about that  i don t think it s quite that simple   well  the school doesn t trust you  right  it wouldn t be that odd for someone in your class  like kushida  for instance  to support you even if you re lying  after all  they don t want their points to go down   even if the other party is at fault  it s still highly likely that sudou will take some of the blame  legal literacy play   sudou hit them  but they didn t hit sudou  i think that s a big part of it  in such a case  claiming it as legitimate self defense is difficult  had they come at you with a knife or a metal bat  i think things would have been quite different  self defense means that you have the right to defend yourself against sudden  dangerous attacks made against your person  so  i don t think we can really claim that this was self defense   i think the school might have offered an extension because they found it difficult to make a judgment at this time   whoever reported it first has the advantage  the victim s testimony can work as evidence  his read on class c s plan  flagged as imagination   that was what i imagined their plan to be  anyway   they let themselves be beaten to destroy sudou s regular spot   if trying to explain the situation won t work  then we ll need to find ironclad proof   so there might be an eyewitness   no  at this stage it s probably only being discussed by the school and the people involved   if those guys in class c had intended to spread rumors  we probably would ve heard about it already   yeah  it wouldn t be good if the accused tried anything   there s just not much i can do  i mean  i can only really respond to sudou s story  if it were horikita or hirata here  they d probably be able to give expert advice  toward kushida   as kushida looked up at me with uneasy eyes  i had the sudden urge to embrace her  i stretched my back out and tried to shake those thoughts  on the duplicate keys   wasn t it fine for kushida to have a key  anyway  i suppose that in the delusional part of my brain  giving her a key made it feel like she was my girlfriend  men certainly are devious creatures   i don t know if i should be happy about that or not   i m trying  more or less  i just haven t been able to  like right now  i didn t have the guts to promise that i d help   kushida  you re going to help  aren t you   remember when i said it d be better to talk with horikita or hirata  well  sudou hates hirata  so that makes horikita the obvious choice   don t know  we ll have to ask and find out  i don t think she ll just quietly stand by and watch as class d collapses  probably   is it okay if i m useless   it s risky  aside from the question of who started the fight  those three reported it to the school  that means they have the upper hand  also  i just don t think it would work  since they started it  chapter close   no matter how much i thought about it  i couldn t come up with any solutions  sudou came to him first for help   kushida   he came to you before horikita san  hirata kun  or even ike kun  keeps her double nature in view while cooperating   i remembered that kushida once directly told me that she hated me  but i might get burned if i forgot about it entirely  under pressure he interrogates facts  then produces a dispassionate procedural analysis  evidence  reporting order  self defense definition  rather than emotional reassurance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Why’re you here? Actually, forget that – how did you even get in?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I learned this extremely important fact just now,&quot; (learning the group cloned his room key)<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;No, I can’t forget about it. Hand over the key.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Private balance after the midterm point purchase: &quot;I saw that I had 8,320 private points.&quot; — &quot;I had nearly bankrupted myself just to buy the point Sudou needed to pass.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Converted, the points came to roughly 8700 yen. Although that wasn’t a giant improvement, it was still big bucks.&quot; (87 class points expected payout)<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;What an illogical argument. Even if you’re ignorant of committing a crime, it’s still a crime. Friendship doesn’t mean automatically allowing people to do whatever they want.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you need advice or you’re worried about something, why not ask Ike or Yamauchi?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you insult Chabashira-sensei, by any chance?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then what? Did you grab her by the collar and threaten to kill her or something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You beat them up? So, uh, why did you do that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I wonder about that. I don’t think it’s quite that simple.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, the school doesn’t trust you, right? It wouldn’t be that odd for someone in your class, like Kushida, for instance, to support you even if you’re lying. After all, they don’t want their points to go down.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even if the other party is at fault, it’s still highly likely that Sudou will take some of the blame.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Legal-literacy play: &quot;Sudou hit them, but they didn’t hit Sudou. I think that’s a big part of it. In such a case, claiming it as legitimate self-defense is difficult. Had they come at you with a knife or a metal bat, I think things would have been quite different. Self-defense means that you have the right to defend yourself against sudden, dangerous attacks made against your person. So, I don’t think we can really claim that this was self-defense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think the school might have offered an extension because they found it difficult to make a judgment at this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Whoever reported it first has the advantage. The victim’s testimony can work as evidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His read on Class C&#x27;s plan, flagged as imagination: &quot;That was what I imagined their plan to be, anyway.&quot; (they let themselves be beaten to destroy Sudou&#x27;s regular spot)<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If trying to explain the situation won’t work, then we’ll need to find ironclad proof,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So there might be an eyewitness?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, at this stage it’s probably only being discussed by the school and the people involved.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If those guys in Class C had intended to spread rumors, we probably would’ve heard about it already.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. It wouldn’t be good if the accused tried anything,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s just not much I can do. I mean, I can only really respond to Sudou’s story. If it were Horikita or Hirata here, they’d probably be able to give expert advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Toward Kushida: &quot;As Kushida looked up at me with uneasy eyes, I had the sudden urge to embrace her. I stretched my back out and tried to shake those thoughts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the duplicate keys: &quot;Wasn’t it fine for Kushida to have a key, anyway? I suppose that in the delusional part of my brain, giving her a key made it feel like she was my girlfriend. Men certainly are devious creatures.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t know if I should be happy about that or not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m trying, more or less. I just haven’t been able to. Like right now, I didn’t have the guts to promise that I’d help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Kushida, you’re going to help, aren’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Remember when I said it’d be better to talk with Horikita or Hirata? Well, Sudou hates Hirata, so that makes Horikita the obvious choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t know. We’ll have to ask and find out. I don’t think she’ll just quietly stand by and watch as Class D collapses. Probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is it okay if I’m useless?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s risky. Aside from the question of who started the fight, those three reported it to the school. That means they have the upper hand. Also, I just don’t think it would work, since they started it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Chapter close: &quot;No matter how much I thought about it, I couldn’t come up with any solutions.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Sudou came to him first for help — Kushida: &quot;He came to you before Horikita-san, Hirata-kun, or even Ike-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Keeps her double-nature in view while cooperating: &quot;I remembered that Kushida once directly told me that she hated me... But I might get burned if I forgot about it entirely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Under pressure he interrogates facts, then produces a dispassionate procedural analysis (evidence, reporting order, self-defense definition) rather than emotional reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): Horikita, Kushida, and the &quot;hate&quot; chat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 2 sec  2 4  sudou s crisis conference   angel mode with an icy seam knocks during ak s kettle moment   kushida  the madonna of class d  poked her head through the entrance  she looked as cute as ever   oh  sudou kun s already here   yeah  i do  that s so we can meet up here  wait  did you not know about that  ayanokouji kun   she also holds a duplicate key to his room   assumed he d consented   umm  well should i return it to you   apologetically offers the key back   s suspended   oh  i got it  ayanokouji kun  he viciously beat chabashira sensei and then he spit on her   ha ha  i m only joking  sudou kun wouldn t go that far   the joke lands wrong   sudou s shock proves the secret is real   just wait a minute  sudou kun  can you please start over  and go a bit more slowly   a regular player  that s amazing  sudou kun  congratulations   still  that s amazing  we ve only just started school   so then they painted you as the bad guy  sudou kun   if class c started this  then sudou kun isn t at fault   we should tell chabashira sensei tomorrow  we should tell her it wasn t sudou kun s fault   sudou kun  you didn t lie to the teacher  did you  i mean  it seems strange  they didn t believe you even though you said you didn t do anything wrong  right   i guess that their plan is to severely punish sudou for punching them  huh   let s just come out and ask those three class c students to be honest  if they feel like what they did was wrong  then surely they d feel guilty about it  right   there are two ways we can prove your innocence  sudou kun  the first way is to simply get those boys in class c to admit that they lied  since you weren t at fault  it s probably best to get them to acknowledge that   the other idea is to find the eyewitness you talked about  sudou kun  if someone happened to see the fight  then we should be able to get to the heart of the matter   asking people one by one  or we could simply address each class as a whole   h huh  you don t want us to tell anyone   but won t the students in class c talk about how sudou kun was violent  i mean  that would work in their favor  i d think   sudou kun  i think it would be better if you kept your distance   sudou must stay away while accused   i don t think it s being dumped on us  we want you to rely on us  sudou kun  i don t know how much we can do  but we ll try our best  okay   i have a few things i wanted to talk to you about  ayanokouji kun  you didn t seem very enthusiastic about helping sudou kun   maybe  but sudou kun came to you  ayanokouji kun  he came to you before horikita san  hirata kun  or even ike kun  the mask slips mid conversation   for an instant  kushida s glare turned icy  which perplexed me    then she recomposes into advice   i think it might be better if you made more effort to blend in  ayanokouji kun   of course  we re friends  so what will you do  ayanokouji kun   do you think horikita san will help us   i know that you re trying to dodge the question  but you ll help  too  won t you  ayanokouji kun   you won t be useless  i m sure you ll be useful  somehow   so what should we do  sudou kun said that it wouldn t help  but i think it d be good to talk with the three students he fought  to tell you the truth  i m friends with komiya kun and the others  therefore  it might be possible to persuade them  hmm  it may be dangerous  though   well then  i guess looking for the eyewitness is our best bet  structured empathy  jokes to defuse  then imposes an agenda  two proof routes  volunteers her cross class network  komiya et al  in c  as a tool  and pins ak to a commitment he keeps dodging  her pressure only works socially   ak admits  like right now  i didn t have the guts to promise that i d help  her icy glare is the only lever that lands  officially takes his side  secures his cooperation with warmth  keeps the secrecy bargain  escalates one on one after sudou leaves  demands he publicly invest in the case  he internally recalls her  i hate you  warning while complying outwardly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Knocks during AK&#x27;s kettle moment; &quot;Kushida, the Madonna of Class D, poked her head through the entrance. She looked as cute as ever.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Oh, Sudou-kun’s already here,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Yeah, I do. That’s so we can meet up here… Wait, did you not know about that, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; (she also holds a duplicate key to his room — assumed he&#x27;d consented)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Umm, well…should I return it to you?&quot; (apologetically offers the key back)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>33 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;S-suspended?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, I got it, Ayanokouji-kun. He viciously beat Chabashira-sensei and then he spit on her!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha, I’m only joking! Sudou-kun wouldn’t go that far.&quot; (the joke lands wrong — Sudou&#x27;s shock proves the secret is real)<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just wait a minute, Sudou-kun. Can you please start over, and go a bit more slowly?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A regular player? That’s amazing, Sudou-kun! Congratulations!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Still, that’s amazing. We’ve only just started school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then they painted you as the bad guy, Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Class C started this, then Sudou-kun isn’t at fault.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should tell Chabashira-sensei tomorrow. We should tell her it wasn’t Sudou-kun’s fault,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, you didn’t lie to the teacher, did you? I mean, it seems strange. They didn’t believe you even though you said you didn’t do anything wrong. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess that their plan is to severely punish Sudou for punching them, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s just come out and ask those three Class C students to be honest. If they feel like what they did was wrong, then surely they’d feel guilty about it. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are two ways we can prove your innocence, Sudou-kun. The first way is to simply get those boys in Class C to admit that they lied. Since you weren’t at fault, it’s probably best to get them to acknowledge that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The other idea is to find the eyewitness you talked about, Sudou-kun. If someone happened to see the fight, then we should be able to get to the heart of the matter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Asking people one by one? Or we could simply address each class as a whole,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;H-huh? You don’t want us to tell anyone?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But won’t the students in Class C talk about how Sudou-kun was violent? I mean, that would work in their favor, I’d think.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun, I think it would be better if you kept your distance,&quot; (Sudou must stay away while accused)<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think it’s being dumped on us. We want you to rely on us, Sudou-kun. I don’t know how much we can do, but we’ll try our best. Okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a few things I wanted to talk to you about, Ayanokouji-kun. You didn’t seem very enthusiastic about helping Sudou-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Maybe, but Sudou-kun came to you, Ayanokouji-kun. He came to you before Horikita-san, Hirata-kun, or even Ike-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The mask slips mid-conversation: &quot;For an instant, Kushida’s glare turned icy, which perplexed me.&quot; — then she recomposes into advice.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think it might be better if you made more effort to blend in, Ayanokouji-kun,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. We’re friends. So what will you do, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think Horikita-san will help us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I know that you’re trying to dodge the question, but you’ll help, too. Won’t you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You won’t be useless. I’m sure you’ll be useful, somehow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So what should we do? Sudou-kun said that it wouldn’t help, but I think it’d be good to talk with the three students he fought. To tell you the truth, I’m friends with Komiya-kun and the others. Therefore, it might be possible to persuade them. Hmm, it may be dangerous, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, I guess looking for the eyewitness is our best bet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Structured empathy: jokes to defuse, then imposes an agenda (two proof routes), volunteers her cross-class network (Komiya et al. in C) as a tool, and pins AK to a commitment he keeps dodging.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her pressure only works socially — AK admits &quot;Like right now, I didn’t have the guts to promise that I’d help.&quot;; her icy glare is the only lever that lands.<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Officially takes his side, secures his cooperation with warmth, keeps the secrecy bargain.<span class=\"pg\">p.35–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Escalates one-on-one after Sudou leaves; demands he publicly invest in the case; he internally recalls her &quot;I hate you&quot; warning while complying outwardly.<span class=\"pg\">p.36–38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: group-chat wistfulness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p27-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 2 sec  2 4  confesses the fight to ak   kushida  begs for secrecy bursts into ayanokoji s locked room  duplicate keycard made by ike s group  with a beet red face  he may be suspended   save me  ayanokouji   this the room where our group meets  isn t it  ike and the rest of us made duplicate keys  didn t you know that  everyone else in the group has a key  too   huh  why  i bought this with my own points  it s mine   refusing to surrender the cloned key   i can t ask them  they re stupid   why not ike yamauchi   buy some carpet  will ya  my butt hurts   thuds onto ak s bare floor   you know how our homeroom teacher called me today  well  it s  uh  the truth is i may be suspended  for a long time  actually   it s probably worse than you re thinking   to tell you the truth  i beat up some kids from class c yesterday  then  i got suspended  the suspension is probably my punishment   just so you know  it wasn t my fault  okay  the jerks in class c started it and tried to pick a fight with me  i just responded to the situation and turned the tables on them  then they said that i started the fight  they re a bunch of liars   sorry  i guess i just kind of skipped to the end and left a lot out   i was talking with the club advisor about being a regular for the summer tournament   well  nothing s set in stone yet  it s just a possibility for now   yeah  i suppose  actually  i was the only first year student nominated to be a regular player  still  it s not like it s definite  anyway  when i was on my way back to the dorm  komiya and kondou  who re in the basketball club with me  called me over to the special building  they said they wanted to talk to me about something  i could ve just ignored them  but i mean  i occasionally talk to those two guys during basketball  i thought it d be better to just hear them out  so of course  i went to meet with them  right  then  there was this ishizaki guy there  waiting for me  he s komiya and kondou s friend  they said that they couldn t stand that someone like me from class d had been chosen as a regular  they threatened me  and said to quit basketball or there d be a lot of pain in my future  i refused to quit  i beat them up  and now i m here   right  i seriously don t get this  i can t believe that teacher  either   they said they would give me until next tuesday to come up with proof  if i can t do that  they ll say i m at fault and i ll be suspended until summer  on top of that  the whole class will lose points  too   what do you mean  you wonder  you re not doubting me  are you   huh  why  it was legitimate self defense  wasn t it  huh   smacks the table at ak s verdict   i m sorry  i just got a little mad   instantly apologizes when kushida flinches   i i don t understand  though  i was up against three people  three  that seems plenty dangerous   i still don t get it  i m the victim here  being suspended isn t some kind of joke  if i m punished for this  forget being a regular player  i won t even be able to play in the tournament   those guys aren t idiots  they won t be honest  goddamn it  i won t ever forgive them  those damn nobodies   snaps ak s ballpoint pen in two   there might be something  though  this might just be a misunderstanding on my part  but when i was fighting those guys i felt something odd  like someone was nearby  watching me   yeah  i think so  i don t have proof anyone was there  though   what should i do   head in hands   this might sound kind of shameless  but can you guys not tell anyone about this   if word gets out  it ll definitely get around to the basketball team  i don t want that to happen  you understand  right   please understand  ayanokouji  if i can t play basketball  i have nothing   grips ak s shoulders   but  if i dump this on you guys   all right  i know this is a bother for you guys  but i ll leave it to you   well  we ll head back to our rooms  i m sorry for barging in here  basketball is his entire identity  keeps the secret circle tiny  ak   kushida  not even horikita hirata  still won t give up the cloned key  apology reflex toward girls  kushida s stiffened shoulders  comes to ak before anyone else   trust earned via the midterm point purchase  ak grudgingly keeps hosting him  comfortable venting in front of her  softens instantly when she s startled  still hates hirata  per ak   sudou hates hirata  so that makes horikita the obvious choice  rates ike yamauchi as useless for advice  they re stupid  yet keeps using their cloned key club","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p27-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p27-1\">Ch.2 sec. 2.4: confesses the fight to AK + Kushida, begs for secrecy<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.27–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Bursts into Ayanokōji&#x27;s locked room (duplicate keycard made by Ike&#x27;s group) with a beet-red face: he may be suspended.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Save me, Ayanokouji!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;This the room where our group meets, isn’t it? Ike and the rest of us made duplicate keys. Didn’t you know that? Everyone else in the group has a key, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Huh? Why? I bought this with my own points. It’s mine.&quot; (refusing to surrender the cloned key)<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t ask them. They’re stupid.&quot; (why not Ike/Yamauchi)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Buy some carpet, will ya? My butt hurts,&quot; (thuds onto AK&#x27;s bare floor)<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know how our homeroom teacher called me today? Well, it’s… Uh… The truth is…I may be suspended. For a long time, actually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s probably worse than you’re thinking…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.29<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To tell you the truth, I beat up some kids from Class C yesterday. Then, I got suspended. The suspension is probably my punishment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just so you know, it wasn’t my fault, okay? The jerks in Class C started it and tried to pick a fight with me. I just responded to the situation and turned the tables on them. Then they said that I started the fight. They’re a bunch of liars.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, I guess I just kind of skipped to the end and left a lot out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was talking with the club advisor about being a regular for the summer tournament.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, nothing’s set in stone yet. It’s just a possibility for now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I suppose. Actually, I was the only first-year student nominated to be a regular player. Still, it’s not like it’s definite. Anyway, when I was on my way back to the dorm, Komiya and Kondou, who’re in the basketball club with me, called me over to the special building. They said they wanted to talk to me about something. I could’ve just ignored them, but I mean, I occasionally talk to those two guys during basketball. I thought it’d be better to just hear them out. So of course, I went to meet with them, right? Then, there was this Ishizaki guy there, waiting for me. He’s Komiya and Kondou’s friend. They said that they couldn’t stand that someone like me from Class D had been chosen as a regular. They threatened me, and said to quit basketball or there’d be a lot of pain in my future. I refused to quit, I beat them up, and now I’m here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Right? I seriously don’t get this. I can’t believe that teacher, either!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;They said they would give me until next Tuesday to come up with proof. If I can’t do that, they’ll say I’m at fault and I’ll be suspended until summer. On top of that, the whole class will lose points, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What do you mean, you wonder? You’re not doubting me, are you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? Why? It was legitimate self-defense, wasn’t it? Huh?!&quot; (smacks the table at AK&#x27;s verdict)<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry, I just got a little mad.&quot; (instantly apologizes when Kushida flinches)<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-I don’t understand, though. I was up against three people. Three! That seems plenty dangerous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I still don’t get it. I’m the victim here! Being suspended isn’t some kind of joke! If I’m punished for this, forget being a regular player. I won’t even be able to play in the tournament!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Those guys aren’t idiots. They won’t be honest. Goddamn it, I won’t ever forgive them! Those damn nobodies!&quot; (snaps AK&#x27;s ballpoint pen in two)<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There might be something, though. This might just be a misunderstanding on my part, but when I was fighting those guys I felt something…odd. Like someone was nearby, watching me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I think so. I don’t have proof anyone was there, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What should I do?&quot; (head in hands)<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This might sound kind of shameless, but…can you guys not tell anyone about this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If word gets out, it’ll definitely get around to the basketball team. I don’t want that to happen. You understand, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please understand, Ayanokouji. If I can’t play basketball, I have nothing,&quot; (grips AK&#x27;s shoulders)<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But, if I dump this on you guys—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;All right. I know this is a bother for you guys, but I’ll leave it to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, we’ll head back to our rooms. I’m sorry for barging in here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Basketball is his entire identity; keeps the secret circle tiny (AK + Kushida, not even Horikita/Hirata); still won&#x27;t give up the cloned key; apology reflex toward girls (Kushida&#x27;s stiffened shoulders).<span class=\"pg\">p.27–38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Comes to AK before anyone else — trust earned via the midterm point purchase; AK grudgingly keeps hosting him.<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Comfortable venting in front of her; softens instantly when she&#x27;s startled.<span class=\"pg\">p.29–36<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Still hates Hirata (per AK: &quot;Sudou hates Hirata, so that makes Horikita the obvious choice.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.37<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Rates Ike/Yamauchi as useless for advice (&quot;They’re stupid.&quot;) yet keeps using their cloned-key club.<span class=\"pg\">p.28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: hauled to the faculty room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p40-1\">→ After: Ch.3 open: his defence collapses in front of the class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 open  july 2 homeroom  the fight goes public chabashira briefs class d on the sudou class c incident  the classroom erupts  ak watches her  serene beauty  of total neutrality   i planned to fade out  but   his protest to himself at being swept into lunch with the group   this was typical of japanese people  they would follow suit when someone took the lead  though they probably mocked him in their hearts  they would help sudou a little bit   well  i guessed i didn t have to take a turn  i wouldn t be any good at this  anyway  better to just leave it to them and fade out quietly","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira briefs Class D on the Sudou–Class C incident; the classroom erupts; AK watches her &quot;serene beauty&quot; of total neutrality.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I planned to fade out… But…&quot; (his protest to himself at being swept into lunch with the group)<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;This was typical of Japanese people. They would follow suit when someone took the lead. Though they probably mocked him in their hearts, they would help Sudou a little bit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Well, I guessed I didn’t have to take a turn. I wouldn’t be any good at this, anyway. Better to just leave it to them and fade out quietly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4 (night): Sudou&#x27;s brawl, duplicate keys, Kushida&#x27;s pressure<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 3 open  july 2 homeroom  she makes sudou s fight public about to leave homeroom  she  assaulted us with one of her infamously brief and off hand announcements  naming sudou and class c in front of the whole class   i have an announcement for you all  there was a bit of trouble the other day  an incident between the student sitting there  sudou  and some students from class c  in short  there was a fight  ak s read of the delivery   her face was so devoid of emotion or interest when she spoke that there was a certain serene beauty to it  she inserted no personal bias whatsoever when she addressed the class  and explained the situation from a position of neutrality   the complaint came from class c  they claim that the fight was one sided  however  when we spoke to the accused  sudou said that their claims were false  he insists that the students class c called him over and started the fight   so in other words  we don t yet know the truth  therefore  we have put our decision on hold for now  our response  and the punishment  will come when we find out who was at fault   so speaks the accused  but i wouldn t say that you have a high level of credibility right now  if there is an eyewitness  as sudou seems to believe  then the situation may change  if anyone here witnessed the fight  please raise your hand   chabashira sensei continued talking in a robotic  flat voice  no students raised their hands in response to her question   too bad  sudou  it appears there are no witnesses in this class   in order to check for witnesses  every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident   anyway  that is all  we ll make our final judgment next tuesday  taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence  with that  let s end homeroom for the day  she destroys sudou s containment plan as a side effect of doing her job neutrally  no editorialising  no protection  and the school wide notification she volunteers is the step that turns a class matter into a cohort matter  ak   the school probably had no say in the matter  the disciplinary process stated on the page  accusation and defence both recorded  decision held pending eyewitness or evidence  judgment date fixed  next tuesday  and every class informed so witnesses can be found outside class d  she leaves and  sudou followed right after her    ak s read  he stayed out of the room rather than lose his temper at his classmates","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–41<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">About to leave homeroom, she &quot;assaulted us with one of her infamously brief and off-hand announcements&quot;, naming Sudou and Class C in front of the whole class. &quot;Chabashira-sensei continued talking in a robotic, flat voice. No students raised their hands in response to her question.&quot; She leaves and &quot;Sudou followed right after her&quot; — AK&#x27;s read: he stayed out of the room rather than lose his temper at his classmates.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “I have an announcement for you all. There was a bit of trouble the other day, an incident between the student sitting there, Sudou, and some students from Class C. In short, there was a fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “The complaint came from Class C. They claim that the fight was one-sided. However, when we spoke to the accused, Sudou said that their claims were false. He insists that the students Class C called him over and started the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “So in other words, we don’t yet know the truth. Therefore, we have put our decision on hold for now. Our response, and the punishment, will come when we find out who was at fault.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s read of the delivery: &quot;Her face was so devoid of emotion or interest when she spoke that there was a certain serene beauty to it. She inserted no personal bias whatsoever when she addressed the class, and explained the situation from a position of neutrality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The complaint came from Class C. They claim that the fight was one-sided. However, when we spoke to the accused, Sudou said that their claims were false. He insists that the students Class C called him over and started the fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So speaks the accused, but I wouldn’t say that you have a high level of credibility right now. If there is an eyewitness, as Sudou seems to believe, then the situation may change. If anyone here witnessed the fight, please raise your hand.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Too bad, Sudou. It appears there are no witnesses in this class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In order to check for witnesses, every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Anyway, that is all. We’ll make our final judgment next Tuesday, taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence. With that, let’s end homeroom for the day.”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She destroys Sudou&#x27;s containment plan as a side effect of doing her job neutrally: no editorialising, no protection, and the school-wide notification she volunteers is the step that turns a class matter into a cohort matter. AK: &quot;The school probably had no say in the matter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.40–41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The disciplinary process stated on the page: accusation and defence both recorded, decision held pending eyewitness or evidence, judgment date fixed (next Tuesday), and every class informed so witnesses can be found outside Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3: collecting Sudou for the faculty room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 3  the one standing voice for sudou  umm  so why hasn t this issue been resolved already    ak calls it  a rather reasonable question  the first thing anyone asks chabashira after the announcement   i want to believe him   if a student in another class were casting doubt on him  i could understand it   but i think it s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away  shouldn t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need  stands in support of kushida s appeal for sudou   hirata  the class hero  uttered those words as he stood in support of kushida  his appearance was dashing  and he clearly wasn t drunk on the same anti sudou kool aid as everyone else  his stance converts the room by example  not argument   ak   starting with those three  we launched our investigation to prove sudou s innocence  and  hirata  kushida  and karuizawa had attracted the rest of our class s admiration  the conversion is fragile and ak says so plainly   though they probably mocked him in their hearts  they would help sudou a little bit    the class follows the lead  it does not change its opinion  after school he organizes the canvassing as a team  ak names  the hero   gal team  that he leads with karuizawa  searching campus themselves  publicly defends the classmate who refuses him privately  the year 1  vol  2 ch2 note stands   sudou will not ask him  so the defence costs hirata nothing with sudou and gains sudou nothing with him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Stands in support of Kushida&#x27;s appeal for Sudou: &quot;Hirata, the class hero, uttered those words as he stood in support of Kushida. His appearance was dashing, and he clearly wasn’t drunk on the same anti-Sudou Kool-Aid as everyone else.&quot; After school he organizes the canvassing as a team: AK names &quot;the Hero &amp; Gal Team&quot; that he leads with Karuizawa, searching campus themselves.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “Umm. So why hasn’t this issue been resolved already?” — AK calls it &quot;a rather reasonable question&quot;, the first thing anyone asks Chabashira after the announcement.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I want to believe him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “If a student in another class were casting doubt on him, I could understand it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But I think it’s wrong to doubt a fellow classmate right away. Shouldn’t friends do everything within their power to help someone in need?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His stance converts the room by example, not argument — AK: &quot;Starting with those three, we launched our investigation to prove Sudou’s innocence&quot;, and &quot;Hirata, Kushida, and Karuizawa had attracted the rest of our class’s admiration.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The conversion is fragile and AK says so plainly: &quot;Though they probably mocked him in their hearts, they would help Sudou a little bit&quot; — the class follows the lead, it does not change its opinion.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Publicly defends the classmate who refuses him privately; the Year 1, Vol. 2 ch2 note stands — Sudou will not ask him, so the defence costs Hirata nothing with Sudou and gains Sudou nothing with him.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p17-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.1: decoding Horikita in public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 3  the witness sits in the room and says nothing chabashira puts the ask to the classroom   if anyone here witnessed the fight  please raise your hand     no students raised their hands in response to her question  this is inference  stated as inference  sakura was in that homeroom  pp 40 43 is class d s classroom  and she is a class d student  but chapter 3 never singles her out  never names her  and never says whether she looked up  all this page can assert is that no hand went up  kushida re asks the same question in a form a witness could answer privately    if anyone knows someone who saw what happened  whether it s someone in class  a friend  or an upperclassman  please tell me  you can contact me at any time    the one line in the chapter that would have been safe for her to answer  and she does not  she holds the only neutral visual record of pp 12 13   silent camera photographs she has not shown anyone   and chapter 3 closes with it still hidden  the window that her silence consumes is fixed and public   we ll make our final judgment next tuesday  taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence  and  in order to check for witnesses  every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident  the school is now actively canvassing every class in the year for her  ak  in a classroom with  about one third of our class remained in the room   suddenly  i felt a sensation  like someone was watching me  i turned around  the text never says who watched him and never resolves it inside the chapter  do not read it as sakura   it is an unanswered beat  not a link  her chapter 1 creed  and so i will continue to live quietly  with my eyes downcast  alone  is what the whole chapter quietly costs sudou  invisibility works  and it works on the class s behalf too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–65<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Chabashira puts the ask to the classroom: &quot;If anyone here witnessed the fight, please raise your hand.&quot; — &quot;No students raised their hands in response to her question.&quot; Kushida re-asks the same question in a form a witness could answer privately — &quot;If anyone knows someone who saw what happened, whether it’s someone in class, a friend, or an upperclassman, please tell me. You can contact me at any time.&quot; — the one line in the chapter that would have been safe for her to answer, and she does not.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This is inference, stated as inference: Sakura was in that homeroom (pp.40–43 is Class D&#x27;s classroom, and she is a Class D student), but Chapter 3 never singles her out, never names her, and never says whether she looked up. All this page can assert is that no hand went up.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She holds the only neutral visual record of pp.12–13 — silent-camera photographs she has not shown anyone — and Chapter 3 closes with it still hidden.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–65<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The window that her silence consumes is fixed and public: &quot;We’ll make our final judgment next Tuesday, taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence,&quot; and &quot;In order to check for witnesses, every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident.&quot; The school is now actively canvassing every class in the year for her.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> AK, in a classroom with &quot;about one third of our class remained in the room&quot;: &quot;Suddenly, I felt a sensation, like someone was watching me. I turned around.&quot; The text never says who watched him and never resolves it inside the chapter. Do not read it as Sakura — it is an unanswered beat, not a link.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her Chapter 1 creed (&quot;And so I will continue to live quietly, with my eyes downcast. Alone.&quot;) is what the whole chapter quietly costs Sudou: invisibility works, and it works on the class&#x27;s behalf too.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–65<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p12-1\">← Before: Ch.2 opening: she stumbles on Sudou&#x27;s three-on-one brawl (the witness birthed)<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 3 open  his defence collapses in front of the class  it wasn t my fault  it was self defense  self defense  i tell you  he shouts it  as he shouldered his classmates  icy glares    the class is already against him before chabashira finishes   what evidence  i don t have any   all i know is that i m innocent  if anything  i ought to receive a settlement for my trouble   looks that way   his own answer to  there are no witnesses in this class   when chabashira sensei cast a doubtful look at sudou  he glanced downward   huh  you re telling everyone   damn it  ak s verdict on the strategy   sudou s plan had already fallen apart  the secrecy he begged for two nights earlier dies the moment the school canvasses every class for a witness  he leaves with chabashira immediately   chabashira sensei left  and sudou followed right after her  he probably realized that if he stayed in the classroom  he d lose his temper with someone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3 open: his defence collapses in front of the class<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–41<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He shouts it &quot;as he shouldered his classmates’ icy glares&quot; — the class is already against him before Chabashira finishes. &quot;When Chabashira-sensei cast a doubtful look at Sudou, he glanced downward.&quot; He leaves with Chabashira immediately: &quot;Chabashira-sensei left, and Sudou followed right after her. He probably realized that if he stayed in the classroom, he’d lose his temper with someone.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “It wasn’t my fault! It was self-defense! Self-defense, I tell you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “What evidence? I don’t have any.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “All I know is that I’m innocent. If anything, I ought to receive a settlement for my trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Looks that way,” (his own answer to &quot;there are no witnesses in this class&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?! You’re telling everyone?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Damn it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s verdict on the strategy: &quot;Sudou’s plan had already fallen apart.&quot; The secrecy he begged for two nights earlier dies the moment the school canvasses every class for a witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: confesses the fight to AK + Kushida, begs for secrecy<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p42-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the class&#x27;s own memory of him is the case against him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p40-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 3 sec  3 1  what a disciplinary case does to a class s balance the two headed cost of a fight  stated by the school   depending on the degree of responsibility that class c saddled him with  sudou could face suspension  and we might see a reduction in our class points  individual punishment and class punishment are separate dials turned by the same incident  punishment is deferred against evidence  not against pleas   we ll make our final judgment next tuesday  taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence  a witness is worth a stay of execution  the search is institutionally widened  which is itself a cost   in order to check for witnesses  every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident    the incident s reputation is now school wide property  class d s own arithmetic on the risk  from ike   if we lose points because of sudou  will we be at zero again this month    with 87 class points deposited  p 17  any deduction returns the class to zero private income  horikita states the recovery model out loud   for class d to rise through the ranks  it s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible  however  we probably won t get any points now  thanks to you    a deduction is priced not as the points lost but as the month s income forfeited  the argument she refuses to accept is moral  not economic   you keep focusing on who started the fight  but that s a trivial detail    under this system the school s liability finding  not the truth of who swung first  sets the deduction  a witness is only worth what their class position allows   even if there had been a witness  it d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from class c  it would be natural for a class c student to hide the truth in order to protect his or her fellow classmates  this school was a hierarchy  after all  class interest predicts who will help  ak opens with class b because it is  the class that would most want a witness     between d and c  which class most threatens class b    and skips class a on the grounds that  i don t think they d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points  nowhere in chapter 3 is a point figure transferred  held in escrow  or offered as inducement  every lever in this chapter is the threat of a future deduction  and no student pays or receives points for the witness search","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p40-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p40-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: what a disciplinary case does to a class&#x27;s balance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.40–47<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The two-headed cost of a fight, stated by the school: &quot;Depending on the degree of responsibility that Class C saddled him with, Sudou could face suspension, and we might see a reduction in our class points.&quot; Individual punishment and class punishment are separate dials turned by the same incident.<span class=\"pg\">p.40<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Punishment is deferred against evidence, not against pleas: &quot;We’ll make our final judgment next Tuesday, taking into account any eyewitnesses and evidence.&quot; A witness is worth a stay of execution.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The search is institutionally widened, which is itself a cost: &quot;In order to check for witnesses, every teacher will inform their classes of the details of this incident.&quot; — the incident&#x27;s reputation is now school-wide property.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D&#x27;s own arithmetic on the risk, from Ike: &quot;If we lose points because of Sudou, will we be at zero again this month?&quot; — with 87 class points deposited (p.17), any deduction returns the class to zero private income.<span class=\"pg\">p.41<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Horikita states the recovery model out loud: &quot;For Class D to rise through the ranks, it’s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible. However, we probably won’t get any points now, thanks to you.&quot; — a deduction is priced not as the points lost but as the month&#x27;s income forfeited.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The argument she refuses to accept is moral, not economic: &quot;You keep focusing on who started the fight, but that’s a trivial detail.&quot; — under this system the school&#x27;s liability finding, not the truth of who swung first, sets the deduction.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> A witness is only worth what their class position allows: &quot;even if there had been a witness, it’d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from Class C. It would be natural for a Class C student to hide the truth in order to protect his or her fellow classmates. This school was a hierarchy, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Class interest predicts who will help: AK opens with Class B because it is &quot;the class that would most want a witness&quot; — &quot;Between D and C, which class most threatens Class B?&quot; — and skips Class A on the grounds that &quot;I don’t think they’d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nowhere in Chapter 3 is a point figure transferred, held in escrow, or offered as inducement; every lever in this chapter is the threat of a future deduction, and no student pays or receives points for the witness search.<span class=\"pg\">p.40–61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p15-1\">← Before: July 1: the app mechanics, first payout, delayed deposit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p68-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the price of a class change, and the points nobody told Class D about<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3 open  she takes the class s anger apart in front of everyone with the uproar starting to get out of hand  ak s note on her motive   naturally  kushida didn t want this to happen    she is defending the class s cohesion  not sudou   everyone  can you please listen to what i have to say   what our teacher said seems to be true  sudou kun may have been in a fight  however  sudou kun was dragged into it  she tells the room sudou s whole account   the regular player nomination  the envious clubmates  the threat  the self defence   kushida conveyed yesterday s story to the whole class   i d like to ask you all again  if anyone knows someone who saw what happened  whether it s someone in class  a friend  or an upperclassman  please tell me  you can contact me at any time  i would sincerely appreciate it  ak measures the difference between her and the teacher saying the same thing   even though she d basically said the same thing as chabashira sensei  the class had a very different response  she had an innate ability to connect with people  her presence glowed so bright that i could almost feel it  charisma alone does not carry it  after yamauchi s accusation   kushida s appeal for sudou s innocence didn t seem to have reached anyone  it takes hirata standing up   and then karuizawa   to turn the room  he backs her appeal publicly  ak credits the pair of them plus karuizawa with converting the class  which is the closest the volume comes to the two leaders acting together  ak s paired mechanism  stated in the same breath   if kushida lived by the softness of her heart  then karuizawa lived by the strength of her will","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.41–43<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">With the uproar starting to get out of hand, AK&#x27;s note on her motive: &quot;Naturally, Kushida didn’t want this to happen.&quot; — she is defending the class&#x27;s cohesion, not Sudou. She tells the room Sudou&#x27;s whole account — the regular-player nomination, the envious clubmates, the threat, the self-defence: &quot;Kushida conveyed yesterday’s story to the whole class.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Everyone, can you please listen to what I have to say?”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “What our teacher said seems to be true. Sudou-kun may have been in a fight. However, Sudou-kun was dragged into it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I’d like to ask you all again. If anyone knows someone who saw what happened, whether it’s someone in class, a friend, or an upperclassman, please tell me. You can contact me at any time. I would sincerely appreciate it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK measures the difference between her and the teacher saying the same thing: &quot;Even though she’d basically said the same thing as Chabashira-sensei, the class had a very different response. She had an innate ability to connect with people. Her presence glowed so bright that I could almost feel it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Charisma alone does not carry it: after Yamauchi&#x27;s accusation, &quot;Kushida’s appeal for Sudou’s innocence didn’t seem to have reached anyone.&quot; It takes Hirata standing up — and then Karuizawa — to turn the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> He backs her appeal publicly; AK credits the pair of them plus Karuizawa with converting the class, which is the closest the volume comes to the two leaders acting together.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> AK&#x27;s paired mechanism, stated in the same breath: &quot;If Kushida lived by the softness of her heart, then Karuizawa lived by the strength of her will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p27-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.4: Sudou&#x27;s crisis conference — angel mode with an icy seam<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p42-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 3 sec  3 1  the class s own memory of him is the case against him classmates answer kushida s appeal with their own sightings  speakers unnamed   i saw him grab some kid by the collar just because they bumped into each other in the hallway     i saw him cut in line in the cafeteria and lash out when someone tried to tell him that wasn t okay  yamauchi s public counter testimony  which turns the room  that sudou  lied so he could justify what he did  that  he talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high  he even told us how much fun it was to beat people up  in the cafeteria he pleads to horikita in flat  external terms   sudou spoke to horikita with indifference  almost as if he were describing someone else s problems   i m sorry  horikita  i ve caused trouble for you again  but it really wasn t my fault this time  all i did was blow up those class c jerks  plans   wait  you might be right about that  but i m not the one at fault here  those guys picked a fight with me  what part of that is my fault   what s trivial about it  it makes all the difference  i didn t do anything wrong   so you re not gonna help  i thought we were friends   what the hell is her deal  goddamn it  his temper performs the argument against him in real time   unable to direct his rage anywhere else  sudou slammed his fists on the cafeteria table  spilling a nearby student s miso soup  the student glared  but when he saw how scary sudou looked  he remained silent  he assumes the friendship she refused to name  her answer   that she has  never once considered you a friend    is the first time the class hears her draw that line out loud","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p42-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the class&#x27;s own memory of him is the case against him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.42–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Classmates answer Kushida&#x27;s appeal with their own sightings, speakers unnamed: &quot;I saw him grab some kid by the collar just because they bumped into each other in the hallway.&quot; / &quot;I saw him cut in line in the cafeteria and lash out when someone tried to tell him that wasn’t okay.&quot; In the cafeteria he pleads to Horikita in flat, external terms: &quot;Sudou spoke to Horikita with indifference, almost as if he were describing someone else’s problems.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “I’m sorry, Horikita. I’ve caused trouble for you again. But it really wasn’t my fault this time. All I did was blow up those Class C jerks’ plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Wait. You might be right about that, but I’m not the one at fault here! Those guys picked a fight with me! What part of that is my fault?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “What’s trivial about it? It makes all the difference! I didn’t do anything wrong!”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Yamauchi&#x27;s public counter-testimony, which turns the room: that Sudou &quot;lied so he could justify what he did&quot;, that &quot;He talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high. He even told us how much fun it was to beat people up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So you’re not gonna help? I thought we were friends!”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What the hell is her deal?! Goddamn it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His temper performs the argument against him in real time: &quot;Unable to direct his rage anywhere else, Sudou slammed his fists on the cafeteria table, spilling a nearby student’s miso soup. The student glared, but when he saw how scary Sudou looked, he remained silent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He assumes the friendship she refused to name; her answer — that she has &quot;never once considered you a friend&quot; — is the first time the class hears her draw that line out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open: his defence collapses in front of the class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p46-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: he cannot accept that her refusal has a reason<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken ike-kanji yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3  one sentence from him undoes kushida s whole appeal  hey  kushida chan  i just can t believe what sudou said  i think he lied so he could justify what he did  he talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high  he even told us how much fun it was to beat people up  he is the pivot of the homeroom  ak marks the turn as his    instantly  silence enveloped the classroom  the first to speak wasn t the eyewitness  but yamauchi  and  after yamauchi voiced his concerns  the rest of the class murmured their dissatisfaction with sudou in turn  at the cafeteria table he volunteers first for the case   i guess it s just up to us    sudou reads it as loyalty   i knew for sure you d understand  yamauchi  i m really counting on you too  ayanokouji  the same boy who supplies the class s proof that sudou is a habitual bully is then trusted as  one of us  when sudou needs helpers  ak notes the ranking his own name gets behind yamauchi s  his accusation is spoken to kushida by name and lands because the class already half believes it   he says out loud what sudou has bragged about to him and ike privately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\">Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.42–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the cafeteria table he volunteers first for the case: “I guess it’s just up to us.” — Sudou reads it as loyalty: &quot;I knew for sure you’d understand, Yamauchi. I’m really counting on you too, Ayanokouji.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Hey, Kushida-chan. I just can’t believe what Sudou said. I think he lied so he could justify what he did. He talked about beating up kids all the time in junior high. He even told us how much fun it was to beat people up.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is the pivot of the homeroom: AK marks the turn as his — &quot;Instantly, silence enveloped the classroom. The first to speak wasn’t the eyewitness, but Yamauchi.&quot; and &quot;After Yamauchi voiced his concerns, the rest of the class murmured their dissatisfaction with Sudou in turn.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42–43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The same boy who supplies the class&#x27;s proof that Sudou is a habitual bully is then trusted as &quot;one of us&quot; when Sudou needs helpers; AK notes the ranking his own name gets behind Yamauchi&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.42, p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> His accusation is spoken to Kushida by name and lands because the class already half-believes it — he says out loud what Sudou has bragged about to him and Ike privately.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p19-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 &amp; sec. 2.4: crew member, key-club member<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p43-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 3  hirata s vote  cast out loud  i agree   if it were a false charge  that d be a problem  wouldn t it  in any case  you d feel bad for him if he were innocent  right  introduced by ak in the middle of the uproar as  heroic hirata s girlfriend   brushing her bangs aside with her hand as she spoke  ak s paired contrast of the two girls who moved the class   if kushida lived by the softness of her heart  then karuizawa lived by the strength of her will  perhaps it was because of kushida and karuizawa s influence that many of the girls started to express their support  after school she works the canvassing with him   hirata and karuizawa led the hero   gal team  seconding his stance is enough to open the flood of support  she moves the girls as a block  which is where her influence in class d actually lives","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p43-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p43-1\">Ch.3: Hirata&#x27;s vote, cast out loud<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.43, p.54<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After school she works the canvassing with him: &quot;Hirata and Karuizawa led the Hero &amp; Gal Team&quot;.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I agree!”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “If it were a false charge, that’d be a problem, wouldn’t it? In any case, you’d feel bad for him if he were innocent, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Introduced by AK in the middle of the uproar as &quot;heroic Hirata&#x27;s girlfriend&quot;, &quot;brushing her bangs aside with her hand as she spoke&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s paired contrast of the two girls who moved the class: &quot;If Kushida lived by the softness of her heart, then Karuizawa lived by the strength of her will. Perhaps it was because of Kushida and Karuizawa’s influence that many of the girls started to express their support.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Seconding his stance is enough to open the flood of support; she moves the girls as a block, which is where her influence in Class D actually lives.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0 &amp; sec. 4.2: she wants Class A out loud, and is judged too blunt for Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 1  cafeteria  horikita s refusal dissected  the boys  romance council on being ranked   apparently i was second to yamauchi  judging by the  too   sudou s  i m really counting on you too  ayanokouji   even if you ask me to help  you do know that there s not much i can do  right   just as expected  ike couldn t come up with how i d be useful  i looked over at kushida smugly  it was like i was showing off a talentless person s power   i had no idea how to answer  did they think i was her user manual  i took a huge mouthful of rice to avoid the question  his private read of horikita  she saw  the ending  when the teachers announced the incident    the possibility of a happy ending was almost nonexistent  she d probably been cold towards sudou on purpose  however  if i told them that now  they d probably become discouraged   ah  well  this might not be relevant  but i d like to say something  i think that horikita usually speaks in a rather brusque manner  but i think  that you guys misunderstand her   i think that she wouldn t help without any reason to do so   well  yeah  i m just guessing like you said  sudou   horikita is smart  right  so i think she probably had some idea   well  it d be great if a witness stepped forward  the teachers are going around and talking to each class about the incident  when they do find someone  things should get settled quickly   it wasn t unreasonable for horikita to throw in the towel  besides  even if there had been a witness  it d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from class c  this school was a hierarchy  after all   why would you say that  you know such a statement will alienate about half of the students here  right    his answer to ike s  i think people who participate in clubs are stupid  which is ike s line  on ike s page   nope   nothing between him and horikita   anyone     nope  no one    internally   if i had to choose someone  i probably would have picked  kushida  she was the person i talked to the most  so that was only natural  but knowing that she didn t like me  i couldn t really imagine things progressing   unlike you guys  i don t really know any girls apart from horikita and kushida   isn t it kind of pathetic that you re trying to introduce me to girls when you don t have a girlfriend yourself   i wondered if participating in such a shameless competition would actually make me their friend  it sounded difficult   although it was fine for them to get all excited  sudou s problem still hadn t been resolved  his verdict on ike s location tracking of kushida   he crossed his arms and wore a confident smile  what he was doing sounded just like stalking  another step forward and it would be appropriate to involve the police    he names the behaviour and does nothing about it  on the boys  fantasies aloud at the lunch table   in some ways  i felt a little sorry for kushida  she was most likely the subject of their nightly fantasies  in group defense he self deprecates on purpose  deflects horikita analysis into  just guessing  to protect morale  keeps score of his own low usefulness claims while privately holding the sharpest read in the room  ike s grudging  at least him being there is better than not  i guess  probably    ak s utility officially unexplained even to his defenders  publicly defends her reasoning to the boys  ike reads it as romance leaning  she s important to him  right","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Even if you ask me to help, you do know that there’s not much I can do, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Ah. Well, this might not be relevant, but I’d like to say something. I think that Horikita usually speaks in a rather brusque manner. But I think… that you guys misunderstand her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I think that she wouldn’t help without any reason to do so.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On being ranked: &quot;Apparently I was second to Yamauchi, judging by the &#x27;too.&#x27;&quot; (Sudou&#x27;s &quot;I&#x27;m really counting on you too, Ayanokouji.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Just as expected, Ike couldn’t come up with how I’d be useful. I looked over at Kushida smugly. It was like I was showing off a talentless person’s power.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I had no idea how to answer. Did they think I was her user manual? I took a huge mouthful of rice to avoid the question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private read of Horikita: she saw &quot;the ending&quot; when the teachers announced the incident — &quot;the possibility of a happy ending was almost nonexistent... she’d probably been cold towards Sudou on purpose. However, if I told them that now, they’d probably become discouraged.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well… Yeah, I’m just guessing like you said, Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita is smart, right? So I think she probably had some idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, it’d be great if a witness stepped forward. The teachers are going around and talking to each class about the incident. When they do find someone, things should get settled quickly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It wasn’t unreasonable for Horikita to throw in the towel. Besides, even if there had been a witness, it’d be checkmate for us if that witness happened to come from Class C... This school was a hierarchy, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why would you say that? You know such a statement will alienate about half of the students here, right?&quot; — his answer to Ike&#x27;s &quot;I think people who participate in clubs are stupid&quot;, which is Ike&#x27;s line, on Ike&#x27;s page.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nope.&quot; (nothing between him and Horikita)<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyone…&quot; → &quot;Nope, no one,&quot; — internally: &quot;If I had to choose someone, I probably would have picked… Kushida? She was the person I talked to the most, so that was only natural. But knowing that she didn’t like me, I couldn’t really imagine things progressing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Unlike you guys, I don’t really know any girls apart from Horikita and Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn’t it kind of pathetic that you’re trying to introduce me to girls when you don’t have a girlfriend yourself?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered if participating in such a shameless competition would actually make me their friend. It sounded difficult.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Although it was fine for them to get all excited, Sudou’s problem still hadn’t been resolved.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His verdict on Ike&#x27;s location-tracking of Kushida: &quot;He crossed his arms and wore a confident smile. What he was doing sounded just like stalking. Another step forward and it would be appropriate to involve the police.&quot; — he names the behaviour and does nothing about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the boys&#x27; fantasies aloud at the lunch table: &quot;In some ways, I felt a little sorry for Kushida. She was most likely the subject of their nightly fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> In group defense he self-deprecates on purpose; deflects Horikita-analysis into &quot;just guessing&quot; to protect morale; keeps score of his own low usefulness claims while privately holding the sharpest read in the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–53<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Ike&#x27;s grudging &quot;At least him being there is better than not, I guess? Probably?&quot; — AK&#x27;s utility officially unexplained even to his defenders.<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Publicly defends her reasoning to the boys; Ike reads it as romance-leaning (&quot;She’s important to him, right?&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): the fight goes public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3 sec  3 1  cafeteria  refusing sudou in front of the group  you seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again  sudou kun   sorry  but i don t feel like helping you this time   for class d to rise through the ranks  it s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible  however  we probably won t get any points now  thanks to you  you hindered those plans   you keep focusing on who started the fight  but that s a trivial detail  did you never consider that   is that so  well  best of luck to you   don t make me laugh  i ve never once considered you a friend  nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn t recognize his own stupidity  goodbye  the refusal is delivered as arithmetic  not malice   horikita appeared more exasperated than angry  she let out a deep sigh  and left  she takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria  ak watches her  looking slightly irritated  while the group tries to work out her reasons without her   what idea  to toss me out like the trash   sudou throwing her refusal back at ak","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44–47<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes her tray and sits elsewhere in the cafeteria; AK watches her &quot;looking slightly irritated&quot; while the group tries to work out her reasons without her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You seem to get yourself into trouble time and time again, Sudou-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Sorry, but I don’t feel like helping you this time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “For Class D to rise through the ranks, it’s important to recover the class points we lost as quickly as possible. However, we probably won’t get any points now, thanks to you. You hindered those plans.”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You keep focusing on who started the fight, but that’s a trivial detail. Did you never consider that?”<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Is that so? Well, best of luck to you.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t make me laugh. I’ve never once considered you a friend. Nothing makes me more uncomfortable than being around someone who doesn’t recognize his own stupidity. Goodbye.”<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The refusal is delivered as arithmetic, not malice: &quot;Horikita appeared more exasperated than angry. She let out a deep sigh, and left.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What idea? To toss me out like the trash?” (Sudou throwing her refusal back at AK)<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.3 (after school): points paranoia, chat refusal, oil and water<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3 sec  3 1  keeping ayanokoji inside the group she assembles the lunch table   ak  horikita  ike  yamauchi  sudou   by asking him directly   when lunchtime came  kushida had invited me with a smile  she d said   want to get lunch  i d said okay  of course  i mean  i didn t have any choice in the matter  she leaves the table early to work her own network   ah  sorry  i have to go for a bit  i m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.44, p.47<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She assembles the lunch table — AK, Horikita, Ike, Yamauchi, Sudou — by asking him directly: &quot;When lunchtime came, Kushida had invited me with a smile. She’d said, &#x27;Want to get lunch?&#x27; I’d said okay, of course. I mean, I didn’t have any choice in the matter.&quot; She leaves the table early to work her own network: “Ah, sorry. I have to go for a bit. I’m going to try asking my upperclassmen friends if they saw anything.”<\/p><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p41-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open: she takes the class&#x27;s anger apart in front of everyone<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p45-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"midterm and final written exams ch 3 sec  3 1  the midterm s social residue gets spent two weeks after the results  the shared prep is invoked as an obligation on sudou s behalf   this is a little disheartening  i thought that preparing for that test together brought us all a bit closer    ak s tag   said a disappointed ike  the exam s after effect runs one way only  it buys group feeling  and horikita is the one student who refuses to spend it on sudou  i ve never once considered you a friend  no pass rule  threshold or buyback from the midterm is restated  revised or appealed anywhere in chapter 3  the reward the class was promised is still the horizon the boys talk over   hey  sae chan sensei said that we d have a vacation this summer  right    the vacation  not the scores  is what the midterm is remembered as in july","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p45-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/midterm-final-written.html#sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p45-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the midterm&#x27;s social residue gets spent<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.45, p.52–53<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/midterm-final-written.html\">Midterm and Final Written Exams<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Two weeks after the results, the shared prep is invoked as an obligation on Sudou&#x27;s behalf: “This is a little disheartening. I thought that preparing for that test together brought us all a bit closer,” — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;said a disappointed Ike.&quot;<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The exam&#x27;s after-effect runs one way only: it buys group feeling, and Horikita is the one student who refuses to spend it on Sudou (&quot;I’ve never once considered you a friend.&quot;). No pass rule, threshold or buyback from the midterm is restated, revised or appealed anywhere in Chapter 3.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The reward the class was promised is still the horizon the boys talk over: “Hey, Sae-chan-sensei said that we’d have a vacation this summer, right?&quot; — the vacation, not the scores, is what the midterm is remembered as in July.<span class=\"pg\">p.52–53<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: the exam as the only lever, priced by a Class B student<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p46-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 3 sec  3 1  he cannot accept that her refusal has a reason  i don t really want to think about it  but i guess it might be true   is it because she hates sudou  i mean  she just said she didn t consider him a friend    read as kushida s line to the group  on sudou s behalf  the text attributes neither to a named speaker   what s trivial about it      see p 44  he returns to the same refusal to examine his own part   what idea  to toss me out like the trash   so what  you don t have a reason  ak s diagnosis  which horikita states herself one page later  he will not accept a reason for the refusal  only a verdict   since horikita was definitely on his mind  he probably wasn t too pleased about her rejection  he accepts her defence of him and never credits it  his own attitude flip in this chapter comes from ike being recruited by her  not from him changing anything","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p46-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p46-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: he cannot accept that her refusal has a reason<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.46–47<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “I don’t really want to think about it, but I guess it might be true.”<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Is it because she hates Sudou? I mean, she just said she didn’t consider him a friend.” — read as Kushida&#x27;s line to the group, on Sudou&#x27;s behalf; the text attributes neither to a named speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “What’s trivial about it? ...” — see p.44; he returns to the same refusal to examine his own part.<span class=\"pg\">p.46<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What idea? To toss me out like the trash?”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So what? You don’t have a reason?”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> AK&#x27;s diagnosis, which Horikita states herself one page later: he will not accept a reason for the refusal, only a verdict. &quot;Since Horikita was definitely on his mind, he probably wasn’t too pleased about her rejection.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.46–47<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> He accepts her defence of him and never credits it; his own attitude flip in this chapter comes from Ike being recruited by her, not from him changing anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p42-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the class&#x27;s own memory of him is the case against him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p51-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the Horikita fantasy, stated in front of the class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3 sec  3 1  the other half of the crush council  no way  you seriously think she ll stoop to your level  ike   h hey  what are you fantasizing about  spill it    ak   apparently yamauchi couldn t stand the fact that ike could do as he pleased in his fantasies   damn it  i won t be outdone  i ve also thought of a few things   it would be best if kushida chan were my girlfriend  it would be the best if she were my girlfriend    ak counts the repetition   yamauchi said it twice  it must ve been important to him   but wait  since kushida chan is so cute  don t you think she ll get a boyfriend any day now    ike has to reply  don t say that  yamauchi   i see  i feel like i can imagine that  so cute    on sudou s fantasy horikita   yamauchi glanced at horikita and got lost in his delusional fantasies  competitive rather than romantic  his desire for kushida is measured against ike s and voiced as one upmanship  i won t be outdone  and he can transfer the same script onto horikita minutes after hearing sudou describe her  she is his stated girlfriend target  named twice in one breath  ak s pity for her is aimed at exactly this pair  he is lost in a horikita fantasy while she is  at that same table  refusing sudou outright   the gap between his version of her and the real one is the joke ak records","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.48–52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “No way. You seriously think she’ll stoop to your level, Ike?”<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “H-hey, what are you fantasizing about?! Spill it!” — AK: &quot;Apparently Yamauchi couldn’t stand the fact that Ike could do as he pleased in his fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Damn it! I won’t be outdone! I’ve also thought of a few things!”<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It would be best if Kushida-chan were my girlfriend… It would be the best if she were my girlfriend…” — AK counts the repetition: &quot;Yamauchi said it twice. It must’ve been important to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But wait. Since Kushida-chan is so cute, don’t you think she’ll get a boyfriend any day now?” — Ike has to reply &quot;Don’t say that, Yamauchi!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see… I feel like I can imagine that. So cute.” — on Sudou&#x27;s fantasy Horikita: &quot;Yamauchi glanced at Horikita and got lost in his delusional fantasies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Competitive rather than romantic: his desire for Kushida is measured against Ike&#x27;s and voiced as one-upmanship (&quot;I won’t be outdone&quot;), and he can transfer the same script onto Horikita minutes after hearing Sudou describe her.<span class=\"pg\">p.48–52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She is his stated girlfriend target, named twice in one breath; AK&#x27;s pity for her is aimed at exactly this pair.<span class=\"pg\">p.50<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He is lost in a Horikita fantasy while she is, at that same table, refusing Sudou outright — the gap between his version of her and the real one is the joke AK records.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p42-1\">← Before: Ch.3: one sentence from him undoes Kushida&#x27;s whole appeal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\">→ After: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p51-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 3 sec  3 1  the horikita fantasy  stated in front of the class  just to be sure  there s really nothing between you and horikita   okay  fine then  i guess i misunderstood  i thought you were clinging to her too much  that d be a bother for horikita   you guys don t know anything  horikita is hands down better than kushida  anyway   i mean  if it was any other guy  she d probably turn them down  but if you were her boyfriend  then it d be okay  right  then she d show you a secret side that no one else gets to see  ak s frame on the speech  he  crossed his arms and nodded  boasting about his personal preferences    he reads horikita s coldness as a stage of courtship rather than a refusal  which is exactly the non recognition she named on p 45  the three of them run a rivalry about who gets a girlfriend while his own suspension clock runs down  yamauchi s  but the horikita of your dreams seems to have tossed you aside  sudou  lands  and he answers  well  i guess so  damn it  now i feel all depressed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p51-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p51-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the Horikita fantasy, stated in front of the class<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Just to be sure, there’s really nothing between you and Horikita?”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Okay, fine then. I guess I misunderstood. I thought you were clinging to her too much. That’d be a bother for Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “You guys don’t know anything. Horikita is hands down better than Kushida, anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I mean, if it was any other guy, she’d probably turn them down. But if you were her boyfriend, then it’d be okay, right? Then she’d show you a secret side that no one else gets to see.”<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s frame on the speech: he &quot;crossed his arms and nodded, boasting about his personal preferences&quot; — he reads Horikita&#x27;s coldness as a stage of courtship rather than a refusal, which is exactly the non-recognition she named on p.45.<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The three of them run a rivalry about who gets a girlfriend while his own suspension clock runs down; Yamauchi&#x27;s &quot;But the Horikita of your dreams seems to have tossed you aside, Sudou&quot; lands, and he answers &quot;Well, I guess so. Damn it! Now I feel all depressed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p46-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: he cannot accept that her refusal has a reason<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p74-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he never claimed a witness, and nobody had understood that<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3 sec  3 2 3 3  roped in by kushida  the class b strategy session team map  hirata   karuizawa lead the  hero   gal team  kushida the  beautiful girl   entourage team  ak tries to slip out   what  do you need something   i m sorry  kushida  i m going to steel my heart and refuse your invitation     thinks   p 55   i couldn t refuse  slightly upturned eyes   pleading   lethal  with the willpower breakdown analogy  everyone has their breaking point  it s a human mechanism   well  i can t argue with you there   kushida s chase horikita plan   busy  but everyone else is busy with sudou s case right now   blurted  earns horikita s glare   please stop saying that i understand you   after horikita tells kushida to ask him  the perpetrator lecture to kushida   i understand a little of what horikita meant  at the very least  sudou does share some fault in this case  he s the type who gets angry easily  right  whenever he s faced with someone he doesn t like  he lashes out  and speaks and acts in an aggressive  domineering way  when i heard he was being considered for a regular spot on the basketball team  i was both surprised and impressed  no one disagrees that he s an incredible player  but if he acts so arrogant and prideful  some people will come to hate him  those who work incredibly hard for their spot would probably see sudou as a rather disagreeable person  then there are the rumors  right  people say that sudou s been fighting people since junior high  i haven t met anyone who knew sudou at his previous school  but considering how many people are talking about it  there might be something to the rumor   this was bound to happen eventually  that s why horikita said sudou was a perpetrator   yeah  as long as he continues to antagonize those around him  trouble will inevitably follow  also  if there s no proof  then people will use his image against him  in other words  they ll judge him based on their impressions  for example  let s say there was a murder case  there are two suspects  one of them has committed murder in the past  while the other is a good  upstanding citizen  based on that information  who would you believe   the truth might be different  however  the less information you have upon which to base your judgment  the more you have to rely on whatever meager information you have at hand  that s what s happening here  horikita cannot overlook the fact that sudou doesn t recognize his flaws   i didn t think this was exactly a  you reap what you sow  situation  though   i guess so  yeah  by punishing him  she wants him to understand himself better   you should act according to your own principles  kushida  i don t think it s wrong to want to help sudou   however  i think it would be better if we carefully considered whether or not to directly point out sudou s problems  if he doesn t actually take the time to reflect  there s no point  there are certain realizations you can only come to on your own   kushida arched her back and stretched  i d changed her thinking    influence over the class s social engine  exercised quietly and without credit   if no one has any objections  how about we start by asking around class b   because that s the class that would most want a witness   between d and c  which class most threatens class b  or to put it another way  which class is more likely to threaten b s place in the ranking   we know too little about class a  i don t think they d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points  it s also possible that class a students don t care  as they feel no connection to what goes on between c and d  caution about b   if they had a particularly cunning person  he or she might have devised a plan to defeat not only c  but class d as well   stop   reflexively grabbing kushida s collar to halt her charge   it is certainly true that your excellent communication skills are indispensable  however  this isn t the same as casually strolling into another class and trying to make friends   do you know anyone in class b     well then  let s talk to those people first then   i see  you might be right about that  we should do what you think is best  kushida   concedes the one by one vs group ask debate   suddenly  i felt a sensation  like someone was watching me  i turned around    watched sense in a one third empty classroom  unresolved in chapter   so cuuute  reaction   she was probably being adorable on purpose  despite thinking that  my heart pounded like crazy   i wanna go home   grumbling at the window during the class b visit   you re probably right   to ike s anti club rant   agreeing while internally cataloguing club benefits   you gained the skills necessary to build relationships with other people  and you also got to experience victory and defeat   i waited for a few minutes until i received kushida s report  i certainly didn t expect what she told me    chapter ending hook into ch 4  she commands his schedule by asking nicely  he concedes plans to her judgment while supplying the strategy  collar grab intimacy registers as both protectiveness and fluster","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–64<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Team map: Hirata &amp; Karuizawa lead the &quot;Hero &amp; Gal Team,&quot; Kushida the &quot;Beautiful Girl &amp; Entourage Team&quot;; AK tries to slip out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;What? Do you need something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Well, I can’t argue with you there.&quot; (Kushida&#x27;s chase-Horikita plan)<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Busy? But everyone else is busy with Sudou’s case right now,&quot; (blurted; earns Horikita&#x27;s glare)<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>26 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry, Kushida. I’m going to steel my heart and refuse your invitation.&quot; → [thinks] (p.55) &quot;I couldn’t refuse. Slightly upturned eyes + pleading = lethal.&quot; with the willpower-breakdown analogy (&quot;everyone has their breaking point. It’s a human mechanism.&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Please stop saying that I understand you.&quot; (after Horikita tells Kushida to ask him)<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The perpetrator lecture to Kushida: &quot;I understand a little of what Horikita meant. At the very least, Sudou does share some fault in this case. He’s the type who gets angry easily, right? Whenever he’s faced with someone he doesn’t like, he lashes out, and speaks and acts in an aggressive, domineering way. When I heard he was being considered for a regular spot on the basketball team, I was both surprised and impressed. No one disagrees that he’s an incredible player, but if he acts so arrogant and prideful, some people will come to hate him. Those who work incredibly hard for their spot would probably see Sudou as a rather disagreeable person. Then there are the rumors, right? People say that Sudou’s been fighting people since junior high. I haven’t met anyone who knew Sudou at his previous school, but considering how many people are talking about it, there might be something to the rumor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This was bound to happen eventually. That’s why Horikita said Sudou was a perpetrator.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. As long as he continues to antagonize those around him, trouble will inevitably follow. Also, if there’s no proof, then people will use his image against him. In other words, they’ll judge him based on their impressions. For example, let’s say there was a murder case. There are two suspects. One of them has committed murder in the past, while the other is a good, upstanding citizen. Based on that information, who would you believe?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The truth might be different. However, the less information you have upon which to base your judgment, the more you have to rely on whatever meager information you have at hand. That’s what’s happening here. Horikita cannot overlook the fact that Sudou doesn’t recognize his flaws.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I didn’t think this was exactly a &#x27;you reap what you sow&#x27; situation, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess so, yeah. By punishing him, she wants him to understand himself better.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should act according to your own principles, Kushida. I don’t think it’s wrong to want to help Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, I think it would be better if we carefully considered whether or not to directly point out Sudou’s problems. If he doesn’t actually take the time to reflect, there’s no point. There are certain realizations you can only come to on your own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Kushida arched her back and stretched; I’d changed her thinking.&quot; — influence over the class&#x27;s social engine, exercised quietly and without credit.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If no one has any objections, how about we start by asking around Class B?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Because that’s the class that would most want a witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Between D and C, which class most threatens Class B? Or to put it another way, which class is more likely to threaten B’s place in the ranking?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We know too little about Class A. I don’t think they’d want to get involved in a troublesome affair that might negatively impact their points. It&#x27;s also possible that Class A students don’t care, as they feel no connection to what goes on between C and D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Caution about B: &quot;If they had a particularly cunning person, he or she might have devised a plan to defeat not only C, but Class D as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stop.&quot; (reflexively grabbing Kushida&#x27;s collar to halt her charge)<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It is certainly true that your excellent communication skills are indispensable. However, this isn’t the same as casually strolling into another class and trying to make friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you know anyone in Class B?&quot; → &quot;Well then, let’s talk to those people first then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. You might be right about that. We should do what you think is best, Kushida.&quot; (concedes the one-by-one vs group-ask debate)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Suddenly, I felt a sensation, like someone was watching me. I turned around.&quot; — watched-sense in a one-third-empty classroom; unresolved in-chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;So cuuute!&quot; reaction: &quot;She was probably being adorable on purpose… Despite thinking that, my heart pounded like crazy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wanna go home.&quot; (grumbling at the window during the Class B visit)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re probably right,&quot; (to Ike&#x27;s anti-club rant — agreeing while internally cataloguing club benefits: &quot;You gained the skills necessary to build relationships with other people, and you also got to experience victory and defeat.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I waited for a few minutes until I received Kushida’s report. I certainly didn’t expect what she told me.&quot; — chapter-ending hook into Ch.4.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She commands his schedule by asking nicely; he concedes plans to her judgment while supplying the strategy; collar-grab intimacy registers as both protectiveness and fluster.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): Horikita&#x27;s refusal dissected, the boys&#x27; romance council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 3 sec  3 2  walked out on  chased down  and still not moved announces  all right  i m going to the dorms  nods  without hesitation  and leaves  she  didn t quail under everyone s gazes  which all expressed variations on  you re leaving  ak s portrait of the manner   she would probably grow up to be a fierce woman  the type that leaves social outings without reading the room and concludes meetings exactly on time   what is it   i thought i already declined  a few minutes ago  no less   you re free to run about for sudou kun s sake  i ve no right to stop you  however  if you need help  try someone else  i m busy   i have an important daily routine  so i need my alone time  it s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me   even if i step in and save him now  he ll land himself in trouble again  it s a vicious cycle  isn t it  you seem to think that sudou kun is the victim here  but i think differently   maybe the class c students really did start this fight  but sudou kun was also one of the perpetrators   why was he dragged into the fight  this problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question  got it  i do not wish to help until that question is answered  since you weren t able to convince me  why don t you ask the guy standing next to you  even though he pretends not to understand what i m thinking  he probably does  kushida s  necessary to reach class a  argument bounces off her because she is not arguing about points  she sets a precondition  explain why the fight happened  that no one in the class is willing to meet  then walks  in front of kushida she claims ak reads her mind   the first time the private shorthand between them is asserted to a third party  ak s reaction is refusal   please stop saying that i understand you  ak s gloss on her motive  said only in his own head   horikita wasn t the type to teach through kindness  she didn t feel an obligation to others","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–57<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Announces &quot;All right, I’m going to the dorms,&quot; nods &quot;without hesitation&quot; and leaves; she &quot;didn’t quail under everyone’s gazes, which all expressed variations on &#x27;You’re leaving?&#x27;&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What is it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I thought I already declined? A few minutes ago, no less.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “You’re free to run about for Sudou-kun’s sake. I’ve no right to stop you. However, if you need help, try someone else. I’m busy,”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s portrait of the manner: &quot;She would probably grow up to be a fierce woman, the type that leaves social outings without reading the room and concludes meetings exactly on time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have an important daily routine, so I need my alone time. It’s unpleasant to have that time stolen from me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Even if I step in and save him now, he’ll land himself in trouble again. It’s a vicious cycle, isn’t it? You seem to think that Sudou-kun is the victim here, but I think differently.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Maybe the Class C students really did start this fight, but Sudou-kun was also one of the perpetrators.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why was he dragged into the fight? This problem will persist until we understand that fundamental question. Got it? I do not wish to help until that question is answered. Since you weren’t able to convince me, why don’t you ask the guy standing next to you? Even though he pretends not to understand what I’m thinking, he probably does.”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s &quot;necessary to reach Class A&quot; argument bounces off her because she is not arguing about points: she sets a precondition (explain why the fight happened) that no one in the class is willing to meet, then walks.<span class=\"pg\">p.56–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> In front of Kushida she claims AK reads her mind — the first time the private shorthand between them is asserted to a third party. AK&#x27;s reaction is refusal: &quot;Please stop saying that I understand you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> AK&#x27;s gloss on her motive, said only in his own head: &quot;Horikita wasn’t the type to teach through kindness. She didn’t feel an obligation to others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1 (cafeteria): refusing Sudou in front of the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 3 sec  3 2 3 3  horikita  the lesson  and class b  are you really heading back  horikita san   you will help us out  won t you   stopping ak from slipping out  ak   i couldn t refuse  slightly upturned eyes   pleading   lethal   i want to get horikita san to help us out this time  can you try asking her again   yeah  i want to chase after her  if horikita san helps  i think she ll make a big difference  she takes ak s arm in front of ike and yamauchi and walks him out with her  ike and yamauchi are left behind because  as ak notes   you certainly couldn t claim those two were friendly with horikita   i really want you to help us with sudou s case  is that possible   i know you did  but but  i think this is necessary to reach class a   w wait  what do you mean  wasn t sudou kun dragged into the fight   sudou kun is a perpetrator  is that true   i don t agree with abandoning sudou kun just to punish him  if she s dissatisfied with him  i think she should at least talk to him directly  that s what friends would do   okay  i understand  i ll follow your advice  ayanokouji kun  ak s definition of her  offered as a limit on himself   she would extend her hand to a friend in need as many times as it took  it sounds simple  but it was actually difficult  only someone like kushida could do such a thing  she is moved mid conversation and lets it show   kushida arched her back and stretched  i d changed her thinking    then converts the new position into action  okay  let s go hunt for the witness   no  i m sorry  i failed   well then  let s go to class b right away   i also think you re being too negative  i do think it s a good idea to ask class b  but i also think we should ask several people at once  if not  we may not find the witness in time   i m sorry  ayanokouji kun   overruling his one at a time plan with ike and yamauchi behind her  and apologising for it  ak withdraws   kushida s plan had convinced me  so i withdrew my own  in the class b room she is the only one of the four who moves   kushida was the only one who remained unfazed  in fact  she found her class b friends and  with a smile on her face  waved to them and headed over  ak s note on the transferability of her manner   she chatted with people regardless of gender  exactly how she acted in class d  no one was more jealous of this than ike and yamauchi  she pitches sudou s case to the roughly ten class b students still in the room   the first cross class advocacy of the volume  her network has a ceiling she cannot see  ak s whole plan for class b rests on the class s self interest  and she is running on friendship  which is why the report she brings back surprises him   what the report is  the text withholds until the next chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54–63<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes AK&#x27;s arm in front of Ike and Yamauchi and walks him out with her; Ike and Yamauchi are left behind because, as AK notes, &quot;You certainly couldn’t claim those two were friendly with Horikita.&quot; In the Class B room she is the only one of the four who moves: &quot;Kushida was the only one who remained unfazed. In fact, she found her Class B friends and, with a smile on her face, waved to them and headed over.&quot; She pitches Sudou&#x27;s case to the roughly ten Class B students still in the room — the first cross-class advocacy of the volume.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “Are you really heading back? Horikita-san?”<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “You will…help us out, won’t you?” (stopping AK from slipping out; AK: &quot;I couldn’t refuse. Slightly upturned eyes + pleading = lethal.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> “I want to get Horikita-san to help us out this time. Can you try asking her again?”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I want to chase after her. If Horikita-san helps, I think she’ll make a big difference.”<span class=\"pg\">p.55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I really want you to help us with Sudou’s case. Is that possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know you did, but…but, I think this is necessary to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait. What do you mean? Wasn’t Sudou-kun dragged into the fight?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sudou-kun is a perpetrator? Is that…true?”<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don’t agree with abandoning Sudou-kun just to punish him. If she’s dissatisfied with him, I think she should at least talk to him directly. That’s what friends would do.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Okay. I understand. I’ll follow your advice, Ayanokouji-kun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s definition of her, offered as a limit on himself: &quot;She would extend her hand to a friend in need as many times as it took. It sounds simple, but it was actually difficult. Only someone like Kushida could do such a thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is moved mid-conversation and lets it show: &quot;Kushida arched her back and stretched; I’d changed her thinking.&quot; — then converts the new position into action (&quot;Okay, let’s go hunt for the witness.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No, I’m sorry. I failed,”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, let’s go to Class B right away!”<span class=\"pg\">p.61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I also think you’re being too negative. I do think it’s a good idea to ask Class B, but I also think we should ask several people at once. If not, we may not find the witness in time.”<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m sorry, Ayanokouji-kun.” (overruling his one-at-a-time plan with Ike and Yamauchi behind her, and apologising for it; AK withdraws: &quot;Kushida’s plan had convinced me, so I withdrew my own.&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s note on the transferability of her manner: &quot;She chatted with people regardless of gender, exactly how she acted in Class D. No one was more jealous of this than Ike and Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her network has a ceiling she cannot see: AK&#x27;s whole plan for Class B rests on the class&#x27;s self-interest, and she is running on friendship, which is why the report she brings back surprises him. (What the report is, the text withholds until the next chapter.)<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p44-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: keeping Ayanokōji inside the group<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 3 sec  3 2 3 3  held in the classroom  then frozen in class b conscripted as the waiting crew while kushida chases horikita   okay  the boys chorused  in the doorway of class b   even ike and yamauchi appeared to be shaking in their boots  they simply stood frozen in the classroom doorway  unable to move     the pair  comrades in vexation  grasped each other s arms   don t panic  ike  it s okay  we re in kushida chan s class  so we re one step ahead of them  ak s measure of the pair in class b  the gap between them and the people kushida chats up is what they notice  not the witness list   no one was more jealous of this than ike and yamauchi  kushida was happily chatting with people who were clearly more attractive than they  he is asked to canvass and does stand in a doorway  no witness lead in chapter 3 is ever traced to him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\">Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.54, p.61–63<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Conscripted as the waiting crew while Kushida chases Horikita: &quot;“Okay!” the boys chorused.&quot; In the doorway of Class B: &quot;Even Ike and Yamauchi appeared to be shaking in their boots. They simply stood frozen in the classroom doorway, unable to move.&quot; — &quot;The pair, comrades in vexation, grasped each other’s arms.&quot; AK&#x27;s measure of the pair in Class B: the gap between them and the people Kushida chats up is what they notice, not the witness list. &quot;No one was more jealous of this than Ike and Yamauchi. Kushida was happily chatting with people who were clearly more attractive than they.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Don’t panic, Ike. It’s okay. We’re in Kushida-chan’s class, so we’re one step ahead of them!”<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He is asked to canvass and does stand in a doorway; no witness lead in Chapter 3 is ever traced to him.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–63<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p48-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the other half of the crush council<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 0 4 1  the class change rule  and the mean teacher read on the search s division of labour   meanwhile  i was alone  like always  i could talk to kushida  but felt disadvantaged when it came to a big group  i couldn t really talk  so i asked kushida to fill in me later  the only witness to horikita s contempt for the grievance session   as her neighbor  i was the only one who noticed    and on her book   at a glance  i saw she was reading dostoevsky s demons  a good choice  he is one of two who can authenticate the class change claim  and he reads the teacher s glance   chabashira sensei shot a quick glance over at horikita and me  we had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school  his prior on the teacher  stated as a rule of the school   chabashira sensei sometimes withheld information  but she didn t lie  his verdict on the club points reveal   at any rate  i deduced that our homeroom teacher was being extremely and deliberately mean    followed by an even handed note on ike s side   if someone were to join a club simply for the sake of earning points  he or she probably wouldn t see great results  on the other hand  someone who joined the club for the sake of points might discover that they possessed a talent for it   horikita  doesn t this mean there s some value in saving sudou    the argument he chooses to make when he decides to move her  points  not feeling   it s better to have a lot of private points  right  he can supplement his own grade if he fails  and he can save others   whether class points or private points  it was better to have a lot of them  there were absolutely no negatives to that  also  we knew very little about how else to earn points at this stage  if our chances improved with sudou in the class  then that was reason enough to make an effort  he stops the moment she concedes   i considered it unnecessary to say more  so i stopped talking  horikita pondered the issue in silence  his self assessment on the canvassing   i hung behind kushida  ike  and the others  trailing them like a ghost  i was impressed  surprised  and in awe of their natural conversation skills  how could they talk with people they d never met before and behave like old friends  monsters  on horikita s refusal of kushida s invitations  which he watches daily   my neighbor who continued to reject kushida s invitations  no matter what sat with a nonchalant expression as she prepared for class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops the moment she concedes: &quot;I considered it unnecessary to say more, so I stopped talking. Horikita pondered the issue in silence.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On the search&#x27;s division of labour: &quot;Meanwhile, I was alone, like always. I could talk to Kushida, but felt disadvantaged when it came to a big group. I couldn’t really talk, so I asked Kushida to fill in me later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Horikita. Doesn’t this mean there’s some value in saving Sudou?&quot; — the argument he chooses to make when he decides to move her: points, not feeling.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It’s better to have a lot of private points, right? He can supplement his own grade if he fails, and he can save others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only witness to Horikita&#x27;s contempt for the grievance session: &quot;As her neighbor, I was the only one who noticed.&quot; — and on her book: &quot;At a glance, I saw she was reading Dostoevsky’s Demons. A good choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> He is one of two who can authenticate the class-change claim, and he reads the teacher&#x27;s glance: &quot;Chabashira-sensei shot a quick glance over at Horikita and me. We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His prior on the teacher, stated as a rule of the school: &quot;Chabashira-sensei sometimes withheld information, but she didn’t lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His verdict on the club-points reveal: &quot;At any rate, I deduced that our homeroom teacher was being extremely and deliberately mean.&quot; — followed by an even-handed note on Ike&#x27;s side: &quot;If someone were to join a club simply for the sake of earning points, he or she probably wouldn’t see great results... On the other hand, someone who joined the club for the sake of points might discover that they possessed a talent for it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Whether class points or private points, it was better to have a lot of them. There were absolutely no negatives to that. Also, we knew very little about how else to earn points at this stage. If our chances improved with Sudou in the class, then that was reason enough to make an effort.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His self-assessment on the canvassing: &quot;I hung behind Kushida, Ike, and the others, trailing them like a ghost. I was impressed, surprised, and in awe of their natural conversation skills... How could they talk with people they’d never met before and behave like old friends? Monsters.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Horikita&#x27;s refusal of Kushida&#x27;s invitations, which he watches daily: &quot;my neighbor—who continued to reject Kushida’s invitations, no matter what—sat with a nonchalant expression as she prepared for class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: roped in by Kushida; the Class B strategy session<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4 sec  4 0  the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has his team s canvass produced records  not results   i heard that hirata and his group hadn t obtained any valuable information  they d recorded the names of the people to whom they d spoken  and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones   then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again    and the reason he gives   it s only been three months since we started here    ak   our classroom hero didn t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech  the girls immediately blushed in response   i understand how you feel  however  it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality  the most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible  the cost of that line on himself  watched by the class s worst judge   ike  who considered hirata a goody two shoes  eyed him suspiciously   even if sudou was at fault    however  hirata nodded without a moment s hesitation  it was as though he believed self sacrifice was unimportant  ike immediately looked downward  as if pressed under the weight of hirata s noble intentions   you know  if you think back on it now  it was obvious from the start    the one student who had already connected the school s signals   remember what our p e  instructor higashiyama sensei said when we went to the pool  he said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points  that was a stepping stone to prepare us for other opportunities  it seems plausible  right  his memory of a teacher s throwaway promise is the evidence that the club points track exists  and ike cannot supply any of it   ike scratched his head and slumped   i don t remember  he said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–72<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His team&#x27;s canvass produced records, not results: &quot;I heard that Hirata and his group hadn’t obtained any valuable information. They’d recorded the names of the people to whom they’d spoken, and occasionally taken notes on their cell phones.&quot; The cost of that line on himself, watched by the class&#x27;s worst judge: &quot;Ike, who considered Hirata a goody two shoes, eyed him suspiciously. &#x27;Even if Sudou was at fault?&#x27; ... However, Hirata nodded without a moment’s hesitation. It was as though he believed self-sacrifice was unimportant. Ike immediately looked downward, as if pressed under the weight of Hirata’s noble intentions.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech.…<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;I understand how you feel. However, it can be dangerous to cling to our points and lose sight of reality. The most important thing is to treasure our friends as much as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He…<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then it would be a good idea for everyone to start saving up again,&quot; — and the reason he gives: &quot;It’s only been three months since we started here.&quot; — AK: &quot;Our classroom hero didn’t waver as he delivered his magnificent speech. The girls immediately blushed in response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You know, if you think back on it now, it was obvious from the start.&quot; — the one student who had already connected the school&#x27;s signals: &quot;Remember what our P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei said when we went to the pool? He said the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points. That was a stepping stone to prepare us for other opportunities. It seems plausible, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His memory of a teacher&#x27;s throwaway promise is the evidence that the club-points track exists, and Ike cannot supply any of it: &quot;Ike scratched his head and slumped. &#x27;I don’t remember,&#x27; he said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the one standing voice for Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 4 sec  4 0   sec  4 2  she wants class a out loud  and is judged too blunt for sakura  i think what you re saying is reasonable  hirata kun  but i still want my points  the students in class a get nearly 100 000 points every month  i m super envious of them  there are girls in their class who buy lots of stylish clothes and accessories  aren t we just the bottom of the barrel compared to them  her posture while the class pleads   karuizawa s legs dangled over her desk  people looked bitter when she pointed out the stark difference between our classes   why couldn t i have been in class a from the start  if i were in class a  i d probably be loving every second of my student life  she says the class s unsayable arithmetic in front of everyone and then makes it about her own life   the strength of will half of the pair ak set against kushida s softness now has a policy position  her status in the sudou case is relational before it is moral   karuizawa wore a particularly proud expression  perhaps because she was the one he d chosen to be his girlfriend  hirata rules her out of the witness interview in advance  and ak agrees with the reasoning   also  if i asked karuizawa san to talk with her  that might cause a few problems     a conversation between the super assertive karuizawa and sakura san was difficult to imagine  she answers his speeches with her own terms rather than opposing them  and her bluntness is treated by him as a liability to be routed around instead of an asset to be used","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p66-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0 &amp; sec. 4.2: she wants Class A out loud, and is judged too blunt for Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–67, p.83<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her posture while the class pleads: &quot;Karuizawa’s legs dangled over her desk. People looked bitter when she pointed out the stark difference between our classes.&quot; Her status in the Sudou case is relational before it is moral: &quot;Karuizawa wore a particularly proud expression, perhaps because she was the one he’d chosen to be his girlfriend.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “I think what you’re saying is reasonable, Hirata-kun, but I still want my points. The students in Class A get nearly 100,000 points every month. I’m super envious of them. There are girls in their class who buy lots of stylish…”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “Why couldn’t I have been in Class A from the start? If I were in Class A, I’d probably be loving every second of my student life.”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think what you’re saying is reasonable, Hirata-kun, but I still want my points. The students in Class A get nearly 100,000 points every month. I’m super envious of them. There are girls in their class who buy lots of stylish clothes and accessories. Aren’t we just the bottom of the barrel compared to them?”<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She says the class&#x27;s unsayable arithmetic in front of everyone and then makes it about her own life — the strength-of-will half of the pair AK set against Kushida&#x27;s softness now has a policy position.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Hirata rules her out of the witness interview in advance, and AK agrees with the reasoning: &quot;Also, if I asked Karuizawa-san to talk with her, that might cause a few problems.&quot; — &quot;A conversation between the super assertive Karuizawa and Sakura-san was difficult to imagine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> She answers his speeches with her own terms rather than opposing them, and her bluntness is treated by him as a liability to be routed around instead of an asset to be used.<span class=\"pg\">p.67, p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p43-1\">← Before: Ch.3: Hirata&#x27;s vote, cast out loud<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: she survives in the volume as a standard, not a participant<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4 sec  4 0 4 1  she runs the search  and is the only one who can name sakura s seat  as long as we can find a witness  it s not impossible  let s keep trying our best  ike kun    the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless  her method of remembering is exact   it s certainly true that sudou kun didn t say he saw anyone  he said that he had a feeling that someone was there    she corrects the class s summary of a claim three days old  she re engineers the search from the witness to the witness s surroundings   we might want to change our methods a little  for example  let s look for someone who might have found a witness    ak s judgement   that wasn t a bad idea  horikita arrives at the room and kushida is the reason she stays   kushida peered over at the entrance  probably concerned that horikita wouldn t return   ah  horikita san  kushida said  kushida smiled and waved to horikita   if you didn t come here to help  then why did you come    and then  instead of pressing   well  i m happy if you just want to listen to us talk  i hoped you could give some advice  she is the class s map of itself   no  you re both wrong  she sits diagonally ahead of sudou kun to the right    ak   kushida corrected them  a slightly pouty look on her face  she defends a classmate she has never spoken to  in public  against ike   it s not good to remember people based on something like that  ikekun  that s pathetic  the phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing   no luck  the call didn t go through  i can try again later  but this may be a delicate matter  and  she gave me her contact information  but she doesn t know me very well  she might be confused if i tried to call her  she reads the room s failure before it happens and shrinks the plan to one person   well  i ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow  i think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her  she holds sakura s number and sakura s seating position and none of sakura s trust  and is the one student whose name she will not let ike reduce to a body","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.66–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Horikita arrives at the room and Kushida is the reason she stays: &quot;Kushida peered over at the entrance, probably concerned that Horikita wouldn’t return. &#x27;Ah, Horikita-san!&#x27; Kushida said. Kushida smiled and waved to Horikita.&quot; She is the class&#x27;s map of itself: &quot;No, you’re both wrong. She sits diagonally ahead of Sudou-kun to the right.&quot; — AK: &quot;Kushida corrected them, a slightly pouty look on her face.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;As long as we can find a witness, it’s not impossible. Let’s keep trying our best, Ike-kun.&quot; — the pep line she gives the boy who has just declared the case hopeless.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad…<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;If you didn’t come here to help, then why did you come?&quot; — and then, instead of pressing: &quot;Well, I’m happy if you just want to listen to us talk. I hoped you could give some advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her method of remembering is exact: &quot;It’s certainly true that Sudou-kun didn’t say he saw anyone. He said that he had a feeling that someone was there.&quot; — she corrects the class&#x27;s summary of a claim three days old.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She re-engineers the search from the witness to the witness&#x27;s surroundings: &quot;We might want to change our methods a little. For example, let’s look for someone who might have found a witness.&quot; — AK&#x27;s judgement: &quot;That wasn’t a bad idea.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She defends a classmate she has never spoken to, in public, against Ike: &quot;It’s not good to remember people based on something like that, Ikekun! That’s pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The phone attempt fails and she names why it is a delicate thing: &quot;No luck. The call didn’t go through. I can try again later, but this may be a delicate matter.&quot; and &quot;She gave me her contact information, but she doesn’t know me very well. She might be confused if I tried to call her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She reads the room&#x27;s failure before it happens and shrinks the plan to one person: &quot;Well, I’ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow. I think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> She holds Sakura&#x27;s number and Sakura&#x27;s seating position and none of Sakura&#x27;s trust, and is the one student whose name she will not let Ike reduce to a body.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: Horikita, the lesson, and Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 0  the class change question  and a point based reason to save sudou she is the only student in the room who reacts to the class s griping with contempt  and ak is the only one who sees it   horikita spontaneously broke into derisive laughter in response to ike and karuizawa s delusions  as her neighbor  i was the only one who noticed  her reading material while the class argues about points   horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading  almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise  at a glance  i saw she was reading dostoevsky s demons  chabashira s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first   horikita looked up from her book  probably trying to gauge whether chabashira sensei was lying   may i ask one question  please    ak   the watchful horikita raised her hand  she looked quite determined  considering this was a potential road to class a   what is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school  i m just asking for the sake of reference   so  you re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods  12 million points is about the limit    ak s tag   horikita muttered  she drops the subject the moment the answer arrives   horikita returned to reading  likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all   we should save him because he s in a club    her first question back to ak s argument that sudou has point value   i have a hard time imagining that he d use his points altruistically  though   i won t say that i ll help  but i suppose i ought to acknowledge sudou s existence  at least a little    the movement ak gets out of her in this chapter  stated as little as possible   horikita s language was harsh  but she acknowledged the connection to her own interests  she asks the school for data  not for sympathy  the only two questions she volunteers in the chapter are about the maximum points ever saved and whether the rule is a lie   and she stops arguing the moment the arithmetic says no  chabashira s claim that a class can be bought is verified by exactly two people in the room  and the teacher s glance names them   chabashira sensei shot a quick glance over at horikita and me  we had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.67–73<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her reading material while the class argues about points: &quot;Horikita immediately took out a library book and began reading, almost as if she was trying not to be distracted by the noise. At a glance, I saw she was reading Dostoevsky’s Demons.&quot; Chabashira&#x27;s announcement of a paid class change lands on her first: &quot;Horikita looked up from her book, probably trying to gauge whether Chabashira-sensei was lying.&quot; She drops the subject the moment the answer arrives: &quot;Horikita returned to reading, likely feeling idiotic for bothering to raise her hand at all.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;May I ask one question, please?&quot; — AK: &quot;The watchful Horikita raised her hand. She looked quite determined, considering this was a potential road to Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What is the highest number of points that a student has saved since the opening of this school? I’m just asking for the sake of reference.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;So, you’re saying that even if we were to use criminal methods, 12 million points is about the limit?&quot; — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Horikita muttered.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She is the only student in the room who reacts to the class&#x27;s griping with contempt, and AK is the only one who sees it: &quot;Horikita spontaneously broke into derisive laughter in response to Ike and Karuizawa’s delusions. As her neighbor, I was the only one who noticed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should save him because he’s in a club?&quot; — her first question back to AK&#x27;s argument that Sudou has point value.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a hard time imagining that he’d use his points altruistically, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won’t say that I’ll help, but I suppose I ought to acknowledge Sudou’s existence, at least a little.&quot; — the movement AK gets out of her in this chapter, stated as little as possible: &quot;Horikita’s language was harsh, but she acknowledged the connection to her own interests.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the school for data, not for sympathy: the only two questions she volunteers in the chapter are about the maximum points ever saved and whether the rule is a lie — and she stops arguing the moment the arithmetic says no.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Chabashira&#x27;s claim that a class can be bought is verified by exactly two people in the room, and the teacher&#x27;s glance names them: &quot;Chabashira-sensei shot a quick glance over at Horikita and me. We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2: walked out on, chased down, and still not moved<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p68-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 0  the price of a class change  and the points nobody told class d about class change is a purchase  announced by the school itself   i said that there s a way to reach class a without class points  and  i told you on the day you arrived  i said there s nothing you cannot buy with your points at this school  in other words  you can change classes by using your personal points  the price is fixed and stated as a rule  not a rumour   twenty million  do your best to conserve points  do that  and you can enter whichever class you like  why the number is that high   if i were reduce the number by one digit  there would probably be over 100 people in class a come graduation  then there d be no point to our system   sic    if i were reduce  the honest ceiling  from the school   even if you perfectly maintain your class points upon starting school here  after three years you d only have 3 6 million  class a could raise points enough to reach four million  normally  you simply wouldn t be able to do it  nobody has ever paid it   unfortunately  no  no one has done it before  the record  and how it ended   about three years ago  one student from class b saved nearly 12 million points before graduating     he was expelled before graduation  however  so he was unable to save those 20 million points in the end  he was engaged in a large scale fraudulent operation to save up points  what the fraud was  and the school s verdict on the motive   he took advantage of the newly admitted first year students who didn t yet understand the system  he went to them one by one and scammed points out of them  so he could reach the 20 million points necessary to move to class a     i don t think that his goal was particularly bad  but people who break the rules must be punished  a second  unadvertised income track exists   there are cases where individuals may win points based on their efforts in club activities  or their degree of participation  for example  if someone in a calligraphy club were to win a contest  they could receive corresponding points for that award  the information was unevenly distributed by design or by carelessness    the other classes should have already been well informed of this    and class d had not been told at all  three months in  the school s position on points driven club joining   do you really think you would ve been able to see any results after joining a club  results like winning prizes or being in games  with such shallow feelings  a remembered instance of the club track  told secondhand by hirata rather than shown  their p e  instructor higashiyama sensei had promised  the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points  the scale gap is the real content of the announcement   for students in class d  who dreamed of a mere 100 or 200 private points  reaching 20 million was a faraway dream  ak and horikita are the only two who can verify the claim from experience    we had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school    the volume 1 english point purchase is the private proof behind a school wide rule","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p68-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p68-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the price of a class change, and the points nobody told Class D about<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.68–72<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Class change is a purchase, announced by the school itself: &quot;I said that there’s a way to reach Class A without class points.&quot; and &quot;I told you on the day you arrived. I said there’s nothing you cannot buy with your points at this school. In other words, you can change classes by using your personal points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The price is fixed and stated as a rule, not a rumour: &quot;Twenty million. Do your best to conserve points. Do that, and you can enter whichever class you like.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Why the number is that high: &quot;If I were reduce the number by one digit, there would probably be over 100 people in Class A come graduation. Then there’d be no point to our system.&quot; (sic — &quot;If I were reduce&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The honest ceiling, from the school: &quot;Even if you perfectly maintain your class points upon starting school here, after three years you’d only have 3.6 million. Class A could raise points enough to reach four million. Normally, you simply wouldn’t be able to do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Nobody has ever paid it: &quot;Unfortunately, no. No one has done it before.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The record, and how it ended: &quot;About three years ago, one student from Class B saved nearly 12 million points before graduating.&quot; — &quot;He was expelled before graduation, however, so he was unable to save those 20 million points in the end. He was engaged in a large-scale fraudulent operation to save up points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> What the fraud was, and the school&#x27;s verdict on the motive: &quot;He took advantage of the newly admitted first-year students who didn’t yet understand the system. He went to them one by one and scammed points out of them, so he could reach the 20 million points necessary to move to Class A.&quot; — &quot;I don’t think that his goal was particularly bad, but people who break the rules must be punished.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> A second, unadvertised income track exists: &quot;There are cases where individuals may win points based on their efforts in club activities, or their degree of participation. For example, if someone in a calligraphy club were to win a contest, they could receive corresponding points for that award.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71–72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The information was unevenly distributed by design or by carelessness — &quot;The other classes should have already been well informed of this.&quot; — and Class D had not been told at all, three months in.<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The school&#x27;s position on points-driven club joining: &quot;Do you really think you would’ve been able to see any results after joining a club, results like winning prizes or being in games, with such shallow feelings?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A remembered instance of the club track, told secondhand by Hirata rather than shown: their P.E. instructor Higashiyama-sensei had promised &quot;the student who got the best time during our first class would get 5000 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The scale gap is the real content of the announcement: &quot;For students in Class D, who dreamed of a mere 100 or 200 private points, reaching 20 million was a faraway dream.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> AK and Horikita are the only two who can verify the claim from experience — &quot;We had tested out that very method ourselves by buying a test point from the school.&quot; — the Volume 1 English-point purchase is the private proof behind a school-wide rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.68<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: what a disciplinary case does to a class&#x27;s balance<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.3–4.4: the cameras that grade you, and the tracks Class D was never told about<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p74-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 4 sec  4 1  he never claimed a witness  and nobody had understood that  what happened today  did you make any progress    he comes to the conference at ak s room the morning after being told tuesday is the deadline  the sentence that quietly invalidates three days of searching   huh  i never said there was someone there  i said that it felt like someone was there  while the group works he plays a phone basketball game and celebrates   after he won the match  he struck a victory pose    ak s title for it   i think the game was called generation of miracles or something  his temper keeps ike from saying what ike thinks   even though sudou couldn t really help  ike and yamauchi still appeared disgruntled at the sight of him  however  they concealed their dissatisfaction  probably because they were scared of sudou s counterattack   did you decide to help out  i m super glad you re here    to horikita  five minutes after she refused him in the cafeteria  ak notes he  was happiest to see her  his one piece of sharp thinking in the chapter  wasted on a name   so you re saying that there s a high probability that this sakura  or kokura  or whoever is the witness    ak   a sharp observation  something a fool would be unlikely to say   did you really do this for me  after all  and  after she denies it   umm  but still  the point is that you saved us  right   yeah  i m happy there s a witness  but who s sakura  do you know her  and  diagonally ahead to the right  i can t remember at all  i m sure there s someone there  though   what a tsundere     sudou wore a happy smile  chuckling and scratching his nose with his finger  after horikita leaves again  ak s correction   she wasn t tsun and she wasn t dere  she was a non tsun  non dere  he has the sense to see the witness is hostile to him and says so before anyone else   why is a gloomy girl like her my witness  this sucks  she doesn t want to help me at all   i know  if she were planning to say something  she would have  she restrained herself  because she s an adult   don t make jokes  i m innocent  innocent  i hit them  but it was out of self defense   what the hell  you guys  didn t you say that you d help me    as ike gives up aloud and the class lets him   why do i have to suffer like this  you bunch of useless jerks  koenji s line about his  ugly  life ends the argument with a kicked desk   suddenly  there was a huge crashing sound  a desk flew through the air and splintered on the ground after being kicked  everyone froze  sudou  silent and intense  walked over to kouenji   bring it on  i ll smash your face in and take you down a peg  he is stopped by hirata rather than by reason and leaves by force   sudou glared at kouenji and left the classroom  slamming the door on his way out  his whole defence is a feeling he cannot evidence and a story he told so loosely that the class built three days of work on a misreading of it  his violence stays available on demand and is the only thing in the chapter that reliably changes the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p74-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p74-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he never claimed a witness, and nobody had understood that<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.74–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">While the group works he plays a phone basketball game and celebrates: &quot;After he won the match, he struck a victory pose.&quot; — AK&#x27;s title for it: &quot;I think the game was called Generation of Miracles or something.&quot; His temper keeps Ike from saying what Ike thinks: &quot;Even though Sudou couldn’t really help, Ike and Yamauchi still appeared disgruntled at the sight of him. However, they concealed their dissatisfaction, probably because they were scared of Sudou’s counterattack.&quot; He has the sense to see the witness is hostile to him and says so before anyone else: “Why is a gloomy girl like her my witness? This sucks. She doesn’t want to help me at all.” Kōenji&#x27;s line about his &quot;ugly&quot; life ends the argument with a kicked desk: &quot;Suddenly, there was a huge crashing sound. A desk flew through the air and splintered on the ground after being kicked. Everyone froze. Sudou, silent and intense, walked over to Kouenji.&quot; He is stopped by Hirata rather than by reason and leaves by force: &quot;Sudou glared at Kouenji and left the classroom, slamming the door on his way out.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “What happened today? Did you make any progress?” — he comes to the conference at AK&#x27;s room the morning after being told Tuesday is the deadline.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> The sentence that quietly invalidates three days of searching: “Huh? I never said there was someone there. I said that it felt like someone was there.”<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “Did you decide to help out? I’m super glad you’re here.” — to Horikita, five minutes after she refused him in the cafeteria; AK notes he &quot;was happiest to see her&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His one piece of sharp thinking in the chapter, wasted on a name: “So you’re saying that there’s a high probability that this Sakura, or Kokura, or whoever is the witness?” — AK: &quot;A sharp observation, something a fool would be unlikely to say.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you really do this for me, after all?!” and, after she denies it, “Umm. But still, the point is that you saved us, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. I’m happy there’s a witness, but who’s Sakura? Do you know her?” and “Diagonally ahead to the right? I can’t remember at all. I’m sure there’s someone there, though.”<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What a tsundere.” — &quot;Sudou wore a happy smile, chuckling and scratching his nose with his finger,&quot; after Horikita leaves again; AK&#x27;s correction: &quot;She wasn’t tsun and she wasn’t dere... She was a non-tsun, non-dere.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I know. If she were planning to say something, she would have. She restrained herself, because she’s an adult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t make jokes. I’m innocent. Innocent! I hit them, but it was out of self-defense.”<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What the hell, you guys? Didn’t you say that you’d help me?” — as Ike gives up aloud and the class lets him.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Why do I have to suffer like this? You bunch of useless jerks!”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Bring it on. I’ll smash your face in and take you down a peg,”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His whole defence is a feeling he cannot evidence and a story he told so loosely that the class built three days of work on a misreading of it; his violence stays available on demand and is the only thing in the chapter that reliably changes the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.74–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p51-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the Horikita fantasy, stated in front of the class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p146-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the witness is secured for him, in a mall, without him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 1  horikita names the witness  and he cannot place her either he notices the game sudou is playing while the meeting works   the person of interest  sudou  was completely engrossed in some kind of digital basketball game on his phone  i think the game was called generation of miracles or something  but i still didn t quite understand   she spoke as if she had already found the hypothetical witness    and the room s verdict on it   no one  myself included  really believed her until we heard her next words  horikita s observation beats his own  and he says so plainly   i hadn t noticed that at all  i was genuinely impressed by horikita s observational prowess  horikita s jab at him lands by name   since you were one of the people who also stares at kushida san  it s not surprising you didn t notice  his own contribution to identifying sakura is a memory of a name only   i probably know her  i feel like i ve heard her name somewhere before     i felt like i almost had something  but not quite  on being lumped in with the boys  appraisal of sakura s body without having said anything   even though i hadn t said anything  i felt like i was being lumped into the same category as ike and yamauchi  kushida s bitter smile seemed to say  you re also fixated on boobs  aren t you  you disgusting pervert  granted  that was my persecution complex speaking   i could barely match sakura s name to a face  i recalled seeing her back when we were making bets  the bet had been about boobs  though  i guess we were birds of a feather after all  his taxonomy of the class s four kinds of solitude  with himself as a category   kushida and hirata were proactive and able to open up to just about anyone  horikita didn t feel the agony of solitude  so what about sakura  did she like being alone  like horikita  or was she suffering because she didn t know how to connect with people  like me","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.75–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He notices the game Sudou is playing while the meeting works: &quot;the person of interest, Sudou, was completely engrossed in some kind of digital basketball game on his phone... I think the game was called Generation of Miracles or something, but I still didn’t quite understand.&quot; His taxonomy of the class&#x27;s four kinds of solitude, with himself as a category: &quot;Kushida and Hirata were proactive and able to open up to just about anyone. Horikita didn’t feel the agony of solitude. So what about Sakura? Did she like being alone, like Horikita? Or was she suffering because she didn’t know how to connect with people, like me?&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;She spoke as if she had already found the hypothetical witness.&quot; — and the room&#x27;s verdict on it: &quot;No one, myself included, really believed her…until we heard her next words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Horikita&#x27;s jab at him lands by name: &quot;Since you were one of the people who also stares at Kushida-san, it’s not surprising you didn’t notice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His own contribution to identifying Sakura is a memory of a name only: &quot;I probably know her. I feel like I’ve heard her name somewhere before,&quot; — &quot;I felt like I almost had something, but not quite.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s observation beats his own, and he says so plainly: &quot;I hadn’t noticed that at all. I was genuinely impressed by Horikita’s observational prowess.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On being lumped in with the boys&#x27; appraisal of Sakura&#x27;s body without having said anything: &quot;Even though I hadn’t said anything, I felt like I was being lumped into the same category as Ike and Yamauchi. Kushida’s bitter smile seemed to say, You’re also fixated on boobs, aren’t you? You disgusting pervert. Granted, that was my persecution complex speaking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I could barely match Sakura’s name to a face. I recalled seeing her back when we were making bets. The bet had been about boobs, though. I guess we were birds of a feather after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: the class-change rule, and the mean-teacher read<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 1  she names the witness  and refuses the credit she appears at ak s door unannounced  the first time in the volume she seeks him out   just then  my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared  while i considered who this new visitor might be  she peered through the door   have you made any progress finding the witness    ak   asked horikita  looking as if she already knew the response   i m only telling you this because it s you  but i may have found out something    she stops mid sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave  kushida s wave forces her in   i didn t particularly plan on helping  you don t appear to have found the witness yet  right  her verdict on kushida s plan  given without being asked to join it   i wouldn t say it s a bad plan  provided you have sufficient time  your labors may actually bear fruit   i ll give you just one piece of advice  to help your pathetic odds    then the advice itself   it s hard to see what s right in front of you  if someone actually witnessed sudou s incident  then that person is close by   sakura san    then  on being pressed   she s the witness  she saw the incident  the whole method  in one answer   when kushida san said that she was looking for a witness in class  sakura looked down  a lot of students were staring at kushida san  sakura was the only one who didn t appear interested  she wouldn t have acted that way without some connection to the incident  ak s measure of what she did   i hadn t noticed that at all  i was genuinely impressed by horikita s observational prowess  she d noticed a classmate s very minor gesture    and his summary of the chapter s turn   while we d been paralyzed by uncertainty  horikita had stepped up and taken control   no  sakura san is undoubtedly the witness  her actions confirmed it  although she may not admit to it  she is definitely the one  she rejects the rescue narrative outright   don t misunderstand  i just didn t want to waste more time looking for the witness  and letting other classes see us in such a shameful light  that s all  and  you are free to interpret things however you wish  but i m telling you that you re wrong  she will move on reasons but never on appeal   the difference between ak s point argument  which lands  and ike s or sudou s gratitude  which she calls wrong  ike s playful shove on the shoulder ends with her tossing him to the ground and putting him in a headlock   don t touch me  this is your one warning  the next time you try it  i ll despise you all the way to graduation  ak s note on the technique   those weren t the defensive moves of a normal girl  since i knew that her older brother practiced karate and aikido  she might have learned something  too  she leaves the second the room turns to teasing her    goodbye    before anyone can convert her help into belonging  kushida is the one who physically keeps her in the room and then the one who asks for her advice  she answers kushida s plan with a judgement  not participation  she refuses to let him believe she did it for him  twice  in the same breath in which she hands him the witness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.75–81<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She appears at AK&#x27;s door unannounced, the first time in the volume she seeks him out: &quot;Just then, my doorbell rang and a visitor appeared... While I considered who this new visitor might be, she peered through the door.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Have you made any progress finding the witness?&quot; — AK: &quot;asked Horikita, looking as if she already knew the response.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.75<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’m only telling you this because it’s you, but I may have found out something—&quot; — she stops mid-sentence on seeing shoes at the door and turns to leave; Kushida&#x27;s wave forces her in.<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I didn’t particularly plan on helping. You don’t appear to have found the witness yet, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on Kushida&#x27;s plan, given without being asked to join it: &quot;I wouldn’t say it’s a bad plan. Provided you have sufficient time, your labors may actually bear fruit.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll give you just one piece of advice, to help your pathetic odds,&quot; — then the advice itself: &quot;It’s hard to see what’s right in front of you. If someone actually witnessed Sudou’s incident, then that person is close by.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san.&quot; — then, on being pressed: &quot;She’s the witness. She saw the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The whole method, in one answer: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who didn’t appear interested. She wouldn’t have acted that way without some connection to the incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> AK&#x27;s measure of what she did: &quot;I hadn’t noticed that at all. I was genuinely impressed by Horikita’s observational prowess. She’d noticed a classmate’s very minor gesture.&quot; — and his summary of the chapter&#x27;s turn: &quot;While we’d been paralyzed by uncertainty, Horikita had stepped up and taken control.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, Sakura-san is undoubtedly the witness. Her actions confirmed it. Although she may not admit to it, she is definitely the one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She rejects the rescue narrative outright: &quot;Don’t misunderstand. I just didn’t want to waste more time looking for the witness, and letting other classes see us in such a shameful light. That’s all.&quot; and &quot;You are free to interpret things however you wish, but I’m telling you that you’re wrong.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She will move on reasons but never on appeal — the difference between AK&#x27;s point argument, which lands, and Ike&#x27;s or Sudou&#x27;s gratitude, which she calls wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.73, p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Ike&#x27;s playful shove on the shoulder ends with her tossing him to the ground and putting him in a headlock: &quot;Don’t touch me. This is your one warning. The next time you try it, I’ll despise you all the way to graduation.&quot; AK&#x27;s note on the technique: &quot;those weren’t the defensive moves of a normal girl. Since I knew that her older brother practiced karate and aikido, she might have learned something, too?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She leaves the second the room turns to teasing her — &quot;Goodbye.&quot; — before anyone can convert her help into belonging.<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida is the one who physically keeps her in the room and then the one who asks for her advice; she answers Kushida&#x27;s plan with a judgement, not participation.<span class=\"pg\">p.76–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> She refuses to let him believe she did it for him, twice, in the same breath in which she hands him the witness.<span class=\"pg\">p.78<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p67-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the class-change question, and a point-based reason to save Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4 sec  4 1  she is named  and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her  sakura san    the first time anyone in class d says her name out loud in the volume  spoken by horikita in ayanokoji s room  horikita s proof  which is entirely about sakura s own behaviour   when kushida san said that she was looking for a witness in class  sakura looked down  a lot of students were staring at kushida san  sakura was the only one who didn t appear interested  she is now identified as the witness by the one student who was watching the wrong student  and horikita s confidence is absolute   no  sakura san is undoubtedly the witness  her actions confirmed it  although she may not admit to it  she is definitely the one  nobody in the room can place her body in the room  sudou and yamauchi  exchanged looks  they didn t seem to know who sakura even was  the seating is argued wrong twice before kushida fixes it    she sits diagonally ahead of sudou kun to the right  sudou s admission of the class s real opinion of her   diagonally ahead to the right  i can t remember at all  i m sure there s someone there  though  ak s verdict on why that matters for the case   sakura certainly didn t stand out very much  the fact we didn t really know her was a problem  ike  asked to describe her  offers one fact   would it help if i said she has the biggest boobs in class  her boobs are insanely huge    and yamauchi converts it into a stereotype on the spot   oh  she s that plain girl with glasses  right  kushida defends her  in the only defence she gets in the chapter   it s not good to remember people based on something like that  ikekun  that s pathetic  her phone goes unanswered when kushida calls   she listened to her phone ring for about 20 seconds  but then she shook her head and hung up    ak s reading   sakura might just be pretending to be out  too  kushida s account of what sakura actually gave her   she gave me her contact information  but she doesn t know me very well  she might be confused if i tried to call her  her invisibility is total enough to make the room s memory unreliable  sudou misnames her on the spot    this sakura  or kokura  or whoever    and yamauchi disowns having ever confessed to her  it wasn t sakura  it was a girl from the next class over  not a gloomy and ugly girl like sakura  then drops the subject mid sentence by claiming a message  even the class s most charitable description is an apology for her   it s certainly true that sakura was plain  but she wasn t ugly  i d never gotten a good look at her face before  but she seemed to have very nice features  even so  i couldn t say that with complete confidence  probably because sakura had so little presence  the plan the chapter ends on is to let one girl approach her alone   well  i ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow  i think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her  kushida said   and ak s gloss   if kushida couldn t manage it  then i doubted anyone else would be able to get through to sakura  the only class d student who ever looked at her closely is the one who does not like being looked at  horikita s read of sakura s downcast eyes is the chapter s hinge and sakura never learns it happened  kushida holds her contact number  her seating position and the class s only defence of her  and still cannot reach her by phone  all of this is class d talking about her in a room she is not in  chapter 4 gives her no line of her own until her own section later in the chapter  nothing here is her choice","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.77–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Nobody in the room can place her body in the room: Sudou and Yamauchi &quot;exchanged looks. They didn’t seem to know who Sakura even was&quot;; the seating is argued wrong twice before Kushida fixes it — &quot;She sits diagonally ahead of Sudou-kun to the right.&quot; Kushida defends her, in the only defence she gets in the chapter: &quot;It’s not good to remember people based on something like that, Ikekun! That’s pathetic.&quot; The plan the chapter ends on is to let one girl approach her alone: &quot;Well, I’ll try to talk to her myself tomorrow. I think she might be on her guard if a lot of people approach her,&quot; Kushida said — and AK&#x27;s gloss: &quot;If Kushida couldn’t manage it, then I doubted anyone else would be able to get through to Sakura.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Sakura-san.&quot; — the first time anyone in Class D says her name out loud in the volume, spoken by Horikita in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Horikita&#x27;s proof, which is entirely about Sakura&#x27;s own behaviour: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who…<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Sudou&#x27;s admission of the class&#x27;s real opinion of her: &quot;Diagonally ahead to the right? I can’t remember at all. I’m sure there’s someone there, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s proof, which is entirely about Sakura&#x27;s own behaviour: &quot;When Kushida-san said that she was looking for a witness in class, Sakura looked down. A lot of students were staring at Kushida-san. Sakura was the only one who didn’t appear interested.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She is now identified as the witness by the one student who was watching the wrong student, and Horikita&#x27;s confidence is absolute: &quot;No, Sakura-san is undoubtedly the witness. Her actions confirmed it. Although she may not admit to it, she is definitely the one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77–78<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s verdict on why that matters for the case: &quot;Sakura certainly didn’t stand out very much. The fact we didn’t really know her was a problem.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Ike, asked to describe her, offers one fact: &quot;Would it help if I said she has the biggest boobs in class? Her boobs are insanely huge.&quot; — and Yamauchi converts it into a stereotype on the spot: &quot;Oh, she’s that plain girl with glasses, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.79–80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her phone goes unanswered when Kushida calls: &quot;She listened to her phone ring for about 20 seconds, but then she shook her head and hung up.&quot; — AK&#x27;s reading: &quot;Sakura might just be pretending to be out, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s account of what Sakura actually gave her: &quot;She gave me her contact information, but she doesn’t know me very well. She might be confused if I tried to call her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her invisibility is total enough to make the room&#x27;s memory unreliable: Sudou misnames her on the spot — &quot;this Sakura, or Kokura, or whoever&quot; — and Yamauchi disowns having ever confessed to her (&quot;It wasn’t Sakura; it was a girl from the next class over. Not a gloomy and ugly girl like Sakura.&quot;), then drops the subject mid-sentence by claiming a message.<span class=\"pg\">p.78, p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Even the class&#x27;s most charitable description is an apology for her: &quot;It’s certainly true that Sakura was plain, but she wasn’t ugly. I’d never gotten a good look at her face before, but she seemed to have very nice features. Even so, I couldn’t say that with complete confidence, probably because Sakura had so little presence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The only Class D student who ever looked at her closely is the one who does not like being looked at; Horikita&#x27;s read of Sakura&#x27;s downcast eyes is the chapter&#x27;s hinge and Sakura never learns it happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida holds her contact number, her seating position and the class&#x27;s only defence of her, and still cannot reach her by phone.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of this is Class D talking about her in a room she is not in. Chapter 4 gives her no line of her own until her own section later in the chapter; nothing here is her choice.<span class=\"pg\">p.77–82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the witness sits in the room and says nothing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4 sec  4 1  he has the only confident opinion of sakura  and it is invented he is the one surprised by sudou s blankness about the girl who sits near him   yamauchi appeared quite surprised   can t we just go to sakura s room right now  we don t have much time    ak   i thought that yamauchi s proposal seemed innocuous  but it all came down to sakura s personality and behavior   she s plain  that s it  talk about a waste  man  like pearls before swine    ak s staging of the line   while yamauchi spoke  he gestured with his hands near his chest  to represent sakura s breasts   uh  ahh well  i may or may not have said something like that    cornered by ike s memory of a confession to sakura   n no  i wasn t  i wasn t lying  it was just a misunderstanding  it wasn t sakura  it was a girl from the next class over  not a gloomy and ugly girl like sakura  err  hold on  sorry  i got a message    ak   yamauchi dodged the question by whipping out his phone  he will say anything about a girl he has never spoken to and retract it in the same breath to stay socially safe  his cruelty is reflexive and his cowardice immediate  the volume s only claim that anyone ever confessed to her is a claim he withdraws under pressure   and the withdrawal describes her as  gloomy and ugly  while doing it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.79–82<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He is the one surprised by Sudou&#x27;s blankness about the girl who sits near him: &quot;Yamauchi appeared quite surprised.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Can’t we just go to Sakura’s room right now? We don’t have much time.” — AK: &quot;I thought that Yamauchi’s proposal seemed innocuous, but it all came down to Sakura’s personality and behavior.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “She’s plain, that’s it. Talk about a waste, man. Like pearls before swine.” — AK&#x27;s staging of the line: &quot;While Yamauchi spoke, he gestured with his hands near his chest, to represent Sakura’s breasts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> “Uh, ahh…well, I may or may not have said something like that.” — cornered by Ike&#x27;s memory of a confession to Sakura.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “N-no, I wasn’t. I wasn’t lying. It was just a misunderstanding. It wasn’t Sakura; it was a girl from the next class over. Not a gloomy and ugly girl like Sakura. Err, hold on. Sorry, I got a message.” — AK: &quot;Yamauchi dodged the question by whipping out his phone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He will say anything about a girl he has never spoken to and retract it in the same breath to stay socially safe; his cruelty is reflexive and his cowardice immediate.<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The volume&#x27;s only claim that anyone ever confessed to her is a claim he withdraws under pressure — and the withdrawal describes her as &quot;gloomy and ugly&quot; while doing it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p54-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.2–3.3: held in the classroom, then frozen in Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.8, sec. 4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4 sec  4 2 4 3  he will greet sakura but not ask her  and he physically stops sudou  good morning  ayanokouji kun     hirata called to me  his expression as fresh and friendly as usual  the sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him  why he does not go to the witness himself   me  no  i m going to greet her  that s all  i ve wanted to talk to her since she s always by herself  but as a guy i don t want to come off as forceful or anything  also  if i asked karuizawa san to talk with her  that might cause a few problems   i think that for the time being  we ll just wait for more information from kushida san    the hero s plan is to let someone else do the asking  his reason for briefing ak at all   not for any particular reason  i guess it s because you have a connection to horikita san  she doesn t talk to anyone except for you  so i thought you d pass it along    ak   there was no real reason for him to tell me any of this  i wasn t really part of the team  he invites ak into his own social life  girlfriend included   oh  that reminds me  if you re up for it  we should hang out sometime soon  what do you think  and  are you fine with my girlfriend coming  too    and reads ak s refusal when ak himself cannot   i m sorry  do you not really want to  when sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on koenji  he is the only one who moves   he was the only boy able to move in this awful situation  my heart pounded in my chest   all right  that s enough  calm down  you two    and he puts the blame on both sides in front of the class   sudou kun  you certainly are part of the problem here  but kouenji kun  you re in the wrong  too   stop it already  i don t want to see my friends fight  is kushida s  his is the follow up that picks a side for the record   it s just like kushida says  i don t know about kouenji kun  but i m your ally  sudou kun    ak   hirata was way too cool  it would ve been fitting if he changed his name to  hero  his last line to sudou is the school s argument  not his own feeling   i m going to stop this  sudou kun  you should act more mature  if you cause another huge disturbance  the school s evaluation of you will only worsen  right  then  alone with koenji after sudou slams out   kouenji kun  i don t intend to compel you to help  but you were wrong to blame him    and ak s conclusion from watching the pair   watching their bizarre interaction unfold  i realized that our class lacked unity  he never asks the witness anything  never challenges horikita s write off of sudou  and stops a fight by citing the school s evaluation   leadership that avoids being the one who pressures anyone","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.83–84, p.92–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He invites AK into his own social life, girlfriend included: &quot;Oh, that reminds me. If you’re up for it, we should hang out sometime soon. What do you think?&quot; and &quot;Are you fine with my girlfriend coming, too?&quot; — and reads AK&#x27;s refusal when AK himself cannot: &quot;I’m sorry. Do you not really want to?&quot; When Sudou kicks a desk apart and walks on Kōenji, he is the only one who moves: &quot;He was the only boy able to move in this awful situation. My heart pounded in my chest.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — &quot;Hirata called to me, his expression as fresh and friendly as usual. The sweet yet subtle fragrance of flowers always emanated from him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked…<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> &quot;I think that for the time being, we’ll just wait for more information from Kushida-san.&quot; — the hero&#x27;s plan is to let someone else do the asking.<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Why he does not go to the witness himself: &quot;Me? No. I’m going to greet her, that’s all. I’ve wanted to talk to her since she’s always by herself, but as a guy I don’t want to come off as forceful or anything. Also, if I asked Karuizawa-san to talk with her, that might cause a few problems.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His reason for briefing AK at all: &quot;Not for any particular reason. I guess it’s because you have a connection to Horikita-san. She doesn’t talk to anyone except for you, so I thought you’d pass it along.&quot; — AK: &quot;There was no real reason for him to tell me any of this. I wasn’t really part of the team.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;All right, that’s enough. Calm down, you two,&quot; — and he puts the blame on both sides in front of the class: &quot;Sudou-kun. You certainly are part of the problem here. But Kouenji-kun, you’re in the wrong, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Stop it already. I don’t want to see my friends fight…&quot; is Kushida&#x27;s; his is the follow-up that picks a side for the record: &quot;It’s just like Kushida says. I don’t know about Kouenji-kun, but I’m your ally, Sudou-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Hirata was way too cool. It would’ve been fitting if he changed his name to &#x27;Hero.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> His last line to Sudou is the school&#x27;s argument, not his own feeling: &quot;I’m going to stop this. Sudou-kun, you should act more mature. If you cause another huge disturbance, the school’s evaluation of you will only worsen. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then, alone with Kōenji after Sudou slams out: &quot;Kouenji-kun. I don’t intend to compel you to help. But you were wrong to blame him.&quot; — and AK&#x27;s conclusion from watching the pair: &quot;Watching their bizarre interaction unfold, I realized that our class lacked unity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> He never asks the witness anything, never challenges Horikita&#x27;s write-off of Sudou, and stops a fight by citing the school&#x27;s evaluation — leadership that avoids being the one who pressures anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the speech that wins the room and the recall nobody else has<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.7, sec. 4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 2 4 3  the theory of personal space  and the cameras he had already found he diagnoses kushida s failure analytically  in the middle of an awkward conversation  by citing a discipline   cultural anthropologist edward hall further divided the idea of personal space into four parts  one such zone is the so called  intimate space    and applies it   however  sakura had clearly rejected kushida  no rather  it looked like she was running away  what he notices about sakura s body that nobody else in the room reports   sakura concealed her dominant hand while also avoiding eye contact  even if she weren t comfortable meeting someone s eyes  people generally looked in the direction of those to whom they were speaking  his own reading of kushida s one to one manner  held alongside the class s   though it was mostly out of formal obligation  sakura had exchanged numbers with kushida  kushida s behavior in a one on one conversation was different  though  i don t think horikita was wrong to feel some discomfort when speaking with kushida  i d found something a bit off putting about it myself   i don t think self defense is all that helpful in this case    ak   ah  i d accidentally said that aloud  the slip is the same conclusion he gave sudou privately in ch 2  p 33  said now without choosing to  kushida invades his space to ask for his loyalty and he catalogues his own reaction instead   man  kushida looked super cute up close  rather than feeling uncomfortable about this invasion of my personal space  i wanted her to come even closer   well  yeah  i am  why are you asking me that again  though   that he is sudou s ally  asserted without qualification   if even sakura  the key witness  denied sudou her help  then we d made no progress   there s a popular expression in this world  great talents mature late  sudou could probably become a professional player in the nba  right  i think there s a possibility that he ll make a great contribution to society  the power of youth is infinite    his own verdict on the performance   i uttered a catchphrase that sounded about as original as a television commercial  his discovery of the classroom cameras and the reason no one else saw them   well  ordinary people don t typically concern themselves with hidden cameras  or they might have accidentally spotted them  horikita asks him to walk back and he touches her forehead first   after hearing that invitation  i reflexively placed my hand against her forehead  it felt nice and cool  but i noticed the softness of her skin     it was rare for horikita to invite me anywhere  with the world going so topsy turvy  i wondered if it would rain tomorrow  hirata briefs him on the witness for horikita relay reasons  and invites him to hang out with the couple  ak s interior reaction is the volume s most explicit record of wanting to be included   hirata smiled  agreeably  if i were a girl  i would have gone from zero to 100 right there  and  ahh  i said the exact opposite of what i d been thinking  damn  curse my terrible mouth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.86–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida invades his space to ask for his loyalty and he catalogues his own reaction instead: &quot;Man, Kushida looked super cute up close. Rather than feeling uncomfortable about this invasion of my personal space, I wanted her to come even closer.&quot; Horikita asks him to walk back and he touches her forehead first: &quot;After hearing that invitation, I reflexively placed my hand against her forehead. It felt nice and cool, but I noticed the softness of her skin.&quot; — &quot;It was rare for Horikita to invite me anywhere. With the world going so topsy-turvy, I wondered if it would rain tomorrow.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t think self-defense is all that helpful in this case.&quot; — AK: &quot;Ah, I’d accidentally said that aloud.&quot; The slip is the same conclusion he gave Sudou privately in Ch.2 (p.33), said now without choosing to.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Well… Yeah, I am. Why are you asking me that again, though?&quot; (that he is Sudou&#x27;s ally, asserted without qualification)<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;There’s a popular expression in this world: Great talents mature late. Sudou could probably become a professional player in the NBA, right? I think there’s a possibility that he’ll make a great contribution to society. The power…<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He diagnoses Kushida&#x27;s failure analytically, in the middle of an awkward conversation, by citing a discipline: &quot;Cultural anthropologist Edward Hall further divided the idea of personal space into four parts. One such zone is the so-called “intimate space.”&quot; — and applies it: &quot;However, Sakura had clearly rejected Kushida. No…rather, it looked like she was running away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he notices about Sakura&#x27;s body that nobody else in the room reports: &quot;Sakura concealed her dominant hand while also avoiding eye contact. Even if she weren’t comfortable meeting someone’s eyes, people generally looked in the direction of those to whom they were speaking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His own reading of Kushida&#x27;s one-to-one manner, held alongside the class&#x27;s: &quot;Though it was mostly out of formal obligation, Sakura had exchanged numbers with Kushida. Kushida’s behavior in a one on one conversation was different, though. I don’t think Horikita was wrong to feel some discomfort when speaking with Kushida. I’d found something a bit off-putting about it myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If even Sakura, the key witness, denied Sudou her help, then we’d made no progress.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s a popular expression in this world: Great talents mature late. Sudou could probably become a professional player in the NBA, right? I think there’s a possibility that he’ll make a great contribution to society. The power of youth is infinite.&quot; — his own verdict on the performance: &quot;I uttered a catchphrase that sounded about as original as a television commercial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His discovery of the classroom cameras and the reason no one else saw them: &quot;Well, ordinary people don’t typically concern themselves with hidden cameras... Or they might have accidentally spotted them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Hirata briefs him on the witness for Horikita-relay reasons, and invites him to hang out with the couple; AK&#x27;s interior reaction is the volume&#x27;s most explicit record of wanting to be included: &quot;Hirata smiled, agreeably. If I were a girl, I would have gone from zero to 100 right there&quot; and &quot;Ahh, I said the exact opposite of what I’d been thinking. Damn, curse my terrible mouth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: Horikita names the witness, and he cannot place her either<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4 sec  4 2 4 3  the approach fails in front of the whole class  class was over  kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards sakura  who was quietly preparing to leave  kushida seemed oddly nervous   sakura san  then  i wanted to ask you something  sakura san  do you have a moment  it s about sudou s case   can you please make some time  this is important  so i d like to talk to you  when sudou kun was involved in the incident  were you perhaps somewhere nearby   can t you please spare just a few minutes now    the third ask  the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching  ak s post mortem of her judgement  in her own terms   kushida probably had expected this conversation to go more smoothly  and had gone into this situation thinking she wasn t going to be rejected  that explained why this was currently falling apart  she takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers   i i m sorry  it s because i came up and talked to you so suddenly  that    and is answered flatly   no  that s not it  i was just careless  that s all  anyway  goodbye  even after failing she keeps the case alive by asking the quietest boy in the room   ayanokouji kun  you re sudou kun s ally  aren t you     well  it s just that things seem to a bit tense  everyone s desire to save sudou is fading  she uses his proximity as a resource twice in one day  the ally question  and the earlier instruction that he keep horikita reachable  hirata briefs ak about her because  she doesn t talk to anyone except for you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.86–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Class was over. Kushida stood up right as homeroom ended and walked over towards Sakura, who was quietly preparing to leave. Kushida seemed oddly nervous.&quot; She takes the blame for a broken camera that was not hers: &quot;I-I’m sorry. It’s because I came up and talked to you so suddenly, that…&quot; — and is answered flatly: &quot;No, that’s not it. I was just careless, that’s all… Anyway, goodbye.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Sakura-san?&quot; then &quot;I wanted to ask you something, Sakura-san. Do you have a moment? It’s about Sudou’s case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Can you please make some time? This is important, so I’d like to talk to you. When Sudou-kun was involved in the incident, were you perhaps somewhere nearby?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Can’t you please spare just a few minutes now?&quot; — the third ask, the one that turns the conversation into a scene the room is watching.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> AK&#x27;s post-mortem of her judgement, in her own terms: &quot;Kushida probably had expected this conversation to go more smoothly, and had gone into this situation thinking she wasn’t going to be rejected. That explained why this was currently falling apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Even after failing she keeps the case alive by asking the quietest boy in the room: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you’re Sudou-kun’s ally, aren’t you?&quot; — &quot;Well, it’s just that things seem to a bit tense. Everyone’s desire to save Sudou is fading.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She uses his proximity as a resource twice in one day: the ally question, and the earlier instruction that he keep Horikita reachable (Hirata briefs AK about her because &quot;she doesn’t talk to anyone except for you&quot;).<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0–4.1: she runs the search, and is the only one who can name Sakura&#x27;s seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 2 4 3  she writes sudou off out loud  and prices the witness  my  how unfortunate  kushida failed to persuade her    spoken as kushida s approach to sakura collapses in front of the class  ak agrees   horikita was correct  if kushida couldn t do it  then i didn t think that anyone else in our class would be able to  the thesis she alone will say  that a bad witness is a better outcome   she won t testify on your behalf  they ll determine you caused the incident  in the end  class d will be affected by your actions  but we ll be okay  we have testimony that they lied about the violence  it s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident  that way we ll only lose 87 points  and you won t face expulsion  however  we ll shoulder more of the blame than class c will  ak s tag on that speech   horikita relentlessly spoke her thoughts out loud  as if she d been hiding them deep inside her all this time   i don t think self defense is all that helpful in this case    to sudou  after he invokes it again   even your friends don t wish to help you  how unfortunate    and when sudou calls the class useless jerks   what an interesting thing to say  sudou kun  haven t you noticed that everyone is turning on you   i don t show mercy to people who don t attempt to better themselves  he s caused us nothing but harm  and has no redeeming features    ak s silent counter   well  you don t exactly show any mercy even to people who do attempt such things   i don t intend to deny that it could happen in 10 years  time  but i m looking for things to help me reach class a right now  if he can t help us right now  then he s worthless to me  ike is the one she interrogates about sudou s actual character   you get along with sudou  don t you  you eat together with him  her evidentiary standard  delivered as a dismissal of the whole search   considering the circumstances  even if we get sakura san s testimony  i believe it ll have minimal impact  the school will probably have doubts about a witness just suddenly appearing from class d  and  they ll consider the witness s testimony along with her possible intentions  they won t take her word as absolute proof  the only case that would actually work   the best and most miraculous situation would be if there was a trusted witness from another class or grade who saw the entire incident from start to finish  there isn t anyone who fits that description  though    ak   said horikita with confidence  and  i thought the same  she takes no part in stopping sudou from hitting koenji  the physical intervention is hirata s  and her contribution is the sentence that made him angry enough to need it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.88–94<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ike is the one she interrogates about Sudou&#x27;s actual character: &quot;You get along with Sudou, don’t you? You eat together with him.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in…<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have…<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I don’t think self-defense is all that helpful in this case.&quot; — to Sudou, after he invokes it again.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My, how unfortunate. Kushida failed to persuade her.&quot; — spoken as Kushida&#x27;s approach to Sakura collapses in front of the class; AK agrees: &quot;Horikita was correct. If Kushida couldn’t do it, then I didn’t think that anyone else in our class would be able to.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The thesis she alone will say, that a bad witness is a better outcome: &quot;She won’t testify on your behalf. They’ll determine you caused the incident. In the end, Class D will be affected by your actions, but we’ll be okay. We have testimony that they lied about the violence. It’s hard to imagine that the school would penalize us by more than 100 or 200 points for being involved in this incident. That way we’ll only lose 87 points, and you won’t face expulsion. However, we’ll shoulder more of the blame than Class C will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90–91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s tag on that speech: &quot;Horikita relentlessly spoke her thoughts out loud, as if she’d been hiding them deep inside her all this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Even your friends don’t wish to help you. How unfortunate,&quot; — and when Sudou calls the class useless jerks: &quot;What an interesting thing to say, Sudou-kun. Haven’t you noticed that everyone is turning on you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t show mercy to people who don’t attempt to better themselves. He’s caused us nothing but harm, and has no redeeming features.&quot; — AK&#x27;s silent counter: &quot;Well, you don’t exactly show any mercy even to people who do attempt such things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to deny that it could happen in 10 years’ time, but I’m looking for things to help me reach Class A right now. If he can’t help us right now, then he’s worthless to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her evidentiary standard, delivered as a dismissal of the whole search: &quot;Considering the circumstances, even if we get Sakura-san’s testimony, I believe it’ll have minimal impact. The school will probably have doubts about a witness just suddenly appearing from Class D.&quot; and &quot;They’ll consider the witness’s testimony along with her possible intentions. They won’t take her word as absolute proof.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The only case that would actually work: &quot;the best and most miraculous situation would be if there was a trusted witness from another class or grade who saw the entire incident from start to finish. There isn’t anyone who fits that description, though,&quot; — AK: &quot;said Horikita with confidence.&quot; and &quot;I thought the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She takes no part in stopping Sudou from hitting Kōenji; the physical intervention is Hirata&#x27;s, and her contribution is the sentence that made him angry enough to need it.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p75-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she names the witness, and refuses the credit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4 sec  4 3  he speaks to sudou s face without looking at him his intervention is announced by the mirror  not the man   the voice came from a boy checking his reflection in a hand mirror to fix his hair  it was kouenji rokusuke  an especially odd guy even amongst the remarkably strange people of our class   don t you think it would ve been better if you d been expelled  your existence is far from beautiful  no  in fact  i could say your life is an ugly one  red hair kun    he nicknames sudou by his hair  the same detail the class s witness used for him  ak on the delivery   kouenji didn t even look at sudou as he spoke  it was as if this were a soliloquy   it would be inefficient for me to tell you  no matter how many times i did  if i know that you re dim witted  then it doesn t matter how many times i try to lecture you  does it   puh  i don t think i ve experienced being wrong since i was born  you must be mistaken    to hirata  the one classmate who tells him he is in the wrong   unfortunately  i ve never experienced being wrong  not once in my entire life  oh  looks like it s about time for my date  well  if you ll excuse me    he leaves mid argument on a scheduled date  no date is ever shown  what his two sentences cost  a desk is kicked apart  sudou walks on him  and the class s last organised effort to save anyone collapses into hirata physically holding sudou back  he is the only student in the volume who treats expulsion as a preference rather than a threat  and he says it to the one student whose expulsion risk he cannot lose anything from","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.92–93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">His intervention is announced by the mirror, not the man: &quot;The voice came from a boy checking his reflection in a hand mirror to fix his hair. It was Kouenji Rokusuke, an especially odd guy even amongst the remarkably strange people of our class.&quot; AK on the delivery: &quot;Kouenji didn’t even look at Sudou as he spoke. It was as if this were a soliloquy.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Don’t you think it would’ve been better if you’d been expelled? Your existence is far from beautiful. No, in fact, I could say your life is an ugly one, Red Hair-kun.” — he nicknames Sudou by his hair, the same detail the…”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “It would be inefficient for me to tell you, no matter how many times I did. If I know that you’re dim-witted, then it doesn’t matter how many times I try to lecture you, does it?”<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> “Puh. I don’t think I’ve experienced being wrong since I was born. You must be mistaken.” — to Hirata, the one classmate who tells him he is in the wrong.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Don’t you think it would’ve been better if you’d been expelled? Your existence is far from beautiful. No, in fact, I could say your life is an ugly one, Red Hair-kun.” — he nicknames Sudou by his hair, the same detail the class&#x27;s witness used for him.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Unfortunately, I’ve never experienced being wrong. Not once in my entire life. Oh, looks like it’s about time for my date. Well, if you’ll excuse me.” — he leaves mid-argument on a scheduled date; no date is ever shown.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> What his two sentences cost: a desk is kicked apart, Sudou walks on him, and the class&#x27;s last organised effort to save anyone collapses into Hirata physically holding Sudou back.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He is the only student in the volume who treats expulsion as a preference rather than a threat, and he says it to the one student whose expulsion risk he cannot lose anything from.<span class=\"pg\">p.92–93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p20-1\">← Before: Ch.2 sec. 2.2 (lunch): the balance that bought him out of the cafeteria<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6, sec. 4.8: he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people&#x27;s summary<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 4  she invites ayanokoji out  and decides on class b she initiates  for the first time in the volume   ayanokouji kun  do you want to head back together    and asks for a ten minute stop on the way   it should only take about 10 minutes  she absorbs an unasked for physical check without punishment  after ak s hand goes to her forehead she says only  do you mind  your hand    where minutes earlier she had put ike in a headlock for touching her shoulder  a contrast ak s own line records  her first question at the special building is about him  not the case   you ve really changed  haven t you  it s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case  the witness has already been found  and we ve confirmed that there s nothing left to be done  what are you even trying to do   well  your way of thinking isn t relevant to me  ayanokouji kun  so you re free to think whatever you like  also  i appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with    and on being asked whether she just hates hirata and kushida   having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation  she audits the building for evidence rather than waiting for it    looks like there aren t any here  too bad  and  when asked what she means   cameras  like the ones in the classrooms  if there were cameras here  we d have solid evidence  i can t find any    and sets the rule s boundary   if i had to think of places where they wouldn t be installed  i d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms  right  her actual objective  once she stops pretending she has none   sudou has many qualities i can t stomach  however  i want to lessen the blame they re placing upon him  the best possible outcome is we ll still have some points  even if class d s image worsens    ak s note   she sounded honest  normally  she wasn t quite so candid   like i said  unless a perfect witness appears  proving sudou kun s innocence will be impossible  if those class c students admitted that they lied  i suppose things might turn out fine  do you think that s likely  she steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears   i have something i d like to ask you  sakura san    and ak has to physically restrain her from pursuing   i tried to gently restrain horikita  gesturing for her for stop chasing sakura   i can t help but think there s an ulterior motive    to ichinose  uninvited  before any question is answered   i don t want to talk with someone who is  just curious  do what you want    ak   horikita tried to put some distance between them   are you finished  you heard what you wanted     horikita spoke sharply and with a sigh  trying to drive ichinose away  the reversal  in one sentence  after weighing nothing out loud   let s accept her help  ayanokouji kun    ak   horikita had made a decision  probably determining that the benefits outweighed the risks  she gives her name first  which ak reads as the act of opening an alliance   horikita gave her name candidly  as if doing so approved our cooperative relationship   this is the first i m hearing about it affecting our class points  i ll have to complain to chabashira sensei later    ak   mumbled horikita  a little disgruntled  she accepts being cast as the threat in his speech to sakura without argument   are you talking about me    muttered  then dropped  hostility on sight  then a partnership in the same afternoon  she is the one who says no twice  the one who says yes  and the one whose name seals it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.95–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She initiates, for the first time in the volume: &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, do you want to head back together?&quot; — and asks for a ten-minute stop on the way, &quot;It should only take about 10 minutes.&quot; She steps at a stranger the instant an opening appears: &quot;I have something I’d like to ask you, Sakura-san,&quot; — and AK has to physically restrain her from pursuing: &quot;I tried to gently restrain Horikita, gesturing for her for stop chasing Sakura.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and…<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points…<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She absorbs an unasked-for physical check without punishment: after AK&#x27;s hand goes to her forehead she says only &quot;Do you mind? Your hand.&quot; — where minutes earlier she had put Ike in a headlock for touching her shoulder, a contrast AK&#x27;s own line records.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her first question at the special building is about him, not the case: &quot;You’ve really changed, haven’t you? It’s odd that you stuck your neck out in this case. The witness has already been found, and we’ve confirmed that there’s nothing left to be done. What are you even trying to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, your way of thinking isn’t relevant to me, Ayanokouji-kun, so you’re free to think whatever you like. Also, I appreciate that you say those two are hard to deal with.&quot; — and on being asked whether she just hates Hirata and Kushida: &quot;Having a common enemy tends to lead to cooperation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She audits the building for evidence rather than waiting for it — &quot;Looks like there aren’t any here. Too bad,&quot; and, when asked what she means: &quot;Cameras, like the ones in the classrooms. If there were cameras here, we’d have solid evidence. I can’t find any.&quot; — and sets the rule&#x27;s boundary: &quot;If I had to think of places where they wouldn’t be installed, I’d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her actual objective, once she stops pretending she has none: &quot;Sudou has many qualities I can’t stomach. However, I want to lessen the blame they’re placing upon him. The best possible outcome is we’ll still have some points, even if Class D’s image worsens.&quot; — AK&#x27;s note: &quot;She sounded honest. Normally, she wasn’t quite so candid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Like I said, unless a perfect witness appears, proving Sudou-kun’s innocence will be impossible. If those Class C students admitted that they lied, I suppose things might turn out fine. Do you think that’s likely?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99–100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but think there’s an ulterior motive,&quot; — to Ichinose, uninvited, before any question is answered.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to talk with someone who is ‘just curious.’ Do what you want.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita tried to put some distance between them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you finished? You heard what you wanted.&quot; — &quot;Horikita spoke sharply and with a sigh, trying to drive Ichinose away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The reversal, in one sentence, after weighing nothing out loud: &quot;Let’s accept her help, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — AK: &quot;Horikita had made a decision, probably determining that the benefits outweighed the risks.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She gives her name first, which AK reads as the act of opening an alliance: &quot;Horikita gave her name candidly, as if doing so approved our cooperative relationship.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the first I’m hearing about it affecting our class points. I’ll have to complain to Chabashira-sensei later,&quot; — AK: &quot;mumbled Horikita, a little disgruntled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She accepts being cast as the threat in his speech to Sakura without argument: &quot;Are you talking about me?&quot; — muttered, then dropped.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Hostility on sight, then a partnership in the same afternoon: she is the one who says no twice, the one who says yes, and the one whose name seals it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p88-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: she writes Sudou off out loud, and prices the witness<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p95-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 3 4 4  the cameras that grade you  and the tracks class d was never told about classrooms are recorded  and the recording is the grading instrument   the school checks those cameras to see if we talk or fall asleep during class  otherwise  they wouldn t be able to accurately assess our monthly performance    ak locates them physically   i pointed at the two or so cameras affixed to the ceiling near the corners of the classroom  they were small enough that they wouldn t be a distraction  and they blended in well with their surroundings  but they were undeniably security cameras  the cameras  evidentiary value  established the same day   well  there are cameras that record what goes on in the classrooms  right  therefore  if anything did happen  there d be evidence of it  those recordings would blow the class c guys  lies away  the coverage boundary  checked on site  the special building s hallways have no cameras    there were electrical outlets by the ceiling  but no signs they were being used    and ak generalises   it probably wasn t just the special building  the hallways in the main school buildings probably didn t have cameras  either  horikita s own limit case   if i had to think of places where they wouldn t be installed  i d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms  right  club performance is not a private income side track only  it feeds the class total   the school evaluates club and philanthropic activities  right  so if he enters a tournament and does well  sudou kun could earn points  those ll be tied to your class points  too  wait  did you guys not know that    spoken by a class b student  and class d had heard only the private points half of it  the staff side of the same machine  offered as explanation for a teacher s apathy   did you know that the school evaluates homeroom teachers when their class graduates    ichinose s claim  the school itself never states it in this volume  nobody in class d knew about the cameras either   seriously  i never knew that  and  they re not easily spotted  i also didn t notice until they talked about points for the first time  three system facts in one day  classroom cameras  club points reaching the class total  teacher evaluation  all arrived from a teacher s slip  a student s memory or another class   none of them from an official notice  the information gap  not the point maths  is what class d keeps paying for","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p95-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p95-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.3–4.4: the cameras that grade you, and the tracks Class D was never told about<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.95, p.107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Classrooms are recorded, and the recording is the grading instrument: &quot;The school checks those cameras to see if we talk or fall asleep during class. Otherwise, they wouldn’t be able to accurately assess our monthly performance.&quot; — AK locates them physically: &quot;I pointed at the two or so cameras affixed to the ceiling near the corners of the classroom. They were small enough that they wouldn’t be a distraction, and they blended in well with their surroundings, but they were undeniably security cameras.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The cameras&#x27; evidentiary value, established the same day: &quot;Well, there are cameras that record what goes on in the classrooms, right? Therefore, if anything did happen, there’d be evidence of it. Those recordings would blow the Class C guys’ lies away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The coverage boundary, checked on site: the special building&#x27;s hallways have no cameras — &quot;There were electrical outlets by the ceiling, but no signs they were being used.&quot; — and AK generalises: &quot;It probably wasn’t just the special building. The hallways in the main school buildings probably didn’t have cameras, either.&quot; Horikita&#x27;s own limit case: &quot;If I had to think of places where they wouldn’t be installed, I’d probably say the bathrooms and the locker rooms. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98–99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Club performance is not a private-income side track only; it feeds the class total: &quot;the school evaluates club and philanthropic activities, right? So if he enters a tournament and does well, Sudou-kun could earn points. Those’ll be tied to your class points, too. Wait… Did you guys not know that?&quot; — spoken by a Class B student, and Class D had heard only the private-points half of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The staff side of the same machine, offered as explanation for a teacher&#x27;s apathy: &quot;Did you know that the school evaluates homeroom teachers when their class graduates?&quot; — Ichinose&#x27;s claim; the school itself never states it in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Nobody in Class D knew about the cameras either: &quot;Seriously?! I never knew that!&quot; and &quot;They’re not easily spotted. I also didn’t notice until they talked about points for the first time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Three system facts in one day (classroom cameras, club points reaching the class total, teacher evaluation) all arrived from a teacher&#x27;s slip, a student&#x27;s memory or another class — none of them from an official notice. The information gap, not the point maths, is what Class D keeps paying for.<span class=\"pg\">p.95–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p68-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0: the price of a class change, and the points nobody told Class D about<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the teacher&#x27;s own incentive, and the roles Class D never made<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 4  the special building  and the friend line he chooses to say  sudou was the first friend that i made here  i want to help him    said to horikita at the scene of the fight  nothing in his narration supports it  and she answers it as a contradiction   you re as contradictory as ever  since you re helping out a friend   i decided to take some initiative by myself  since i m not very good at interacting with hirata  kushida  or large groups of people  being social s definitely not my forte  i thought everyone would make me run around the school or the classroom today  so i decided to bolt instead  i like to avoid trouble  remember    the cover persona  offered as his own explanation for being at the building   of course i haven t  it s your job to come up with plans  horikita  i won t ask you to save sudou  but it d be nice for you to point class d in the right direction  his read of horikita s candor  and of everyone else s   most people aren t suited for loneliness  therefore  they sometimes behave hypocritically  like saving someone out of feigned altruism in order to make other people adore them  that didn t seem to be horikita s style  though  the case in one line  as he states it to himself at the scene   one party  either sudou or the class c students  had summoned the other to the special building  after that  as if by destiny  the two enemies started brawling  that was the whole case     our only proof was sudou s word  we were completely in the dark   you shouldn t feel obligated to appear as the witness  sakura  it d be pointless to force you to testify  but if someone scary is trying to intimidate you or something  please talk to us  i have no idea how much i can help  but i ll try    and his note on the recipient   sakura stopped  but didn t turn around   are you talking about me  horikita muttered    ignoring the existence of such a scary monster  i decided to let sakura go   then that s fine  however  if someone else tries to hound you about it  please tell me  how much horikita s certainty is worth   so far  we d been operating based purely on horikita s dogmatism and prejudices  it was quite possible that sakura wasn t the witness  like she said  he volunteers the whole case to a class b stranger   i told her that three people from class c had called sudou over  and there was a fistfight    his stated reason   since there wasn t much information to be gained anyway  it may not have been worth keeping quiet  his running account of ichinose s offer   obviously  i couldn t trust ichinose yet  she was a student from class b  and she gained nothing by involving herself  if helping others out of sheer goodwill was reflected in class or private points  then i could understand her motivation  on who decides   i glanced over to see what horikita thought  i didn t really have the power to decide in the first place  that was horikita s job  the information gap is now his explicit grievance against the school   this was yet another oversight  another instance where chabashira sensei had failed to disclose something important  a usual  our teacher didn t even pretend to give us equal treatment  i felt discriminated against","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.97–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Sudou was the first friend that I made here. I want to help him.&quot; — said to Horikita at the scene of the fight; nothing in his narration supports it, and she answers it as a contradiction: &quot;you’re as contradictory as ever, since…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I decided to take some initiative by myself, since I’m not very good at interacting with Hirata, Kushida, or large groups of people. Being social’s definitely not my forte. I thought everyone would make me run around the school…<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Of course I haven’t. It’s your job to come up with plans, Horikita. I won’t ask you to save Sudou, but it’d be nice for you to point Class D in the right direction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou was the first friend that I made here. I want to help him.&quot; — said to Horikita at the scene of the fight; nothing in his narration supports it, and she answers it as a contradiction: &quot;you’re as contradictory as ever, since you’re helping out a friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I decided to take some initiative by myself, since I’m not very good at interacting with Hirata, Kushida, or large groups of people. Being social’s definitely not my forte. I thought everyone would make me run around the school or the classroom today, so I decided to bolt instead. I like to avoid trouble, remember?&quot; — the cover persona, offered as his own explanation for being at the building.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His read of Horikita&#x27;s candor, and of everyone else&#x27;s: &quot;most people aren’t suited for loneliness. Therefore, they sometimes behave hypocritically, like saving someone out of feigned altruism in order to make other people adore them. That didn’t seem to be Horikita’s style, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.99<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The case in one line, as he states it to himself at the scene: &quot;One party, either Sudou or the Class C students, had summoned the other to the special building. After that, as if by destiny, the two enemies started brawling... That was the whole case.&quot; — &quot;Our only proof was Sudou’s word. We were completely in the dark.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You shouldn’t feel obligated to appear as the witness, Sakura. It’d be pointless to force you to testify. But if someone scary is trying to intimidate you or something, please talk to us. I have no idea how much I can help, but I’ll try.&quot; — and his note on the recipient: &quot;Sakura stopped, but didn’t turn around.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Are you talking about me?&quot; Horikita muttered — &quot;Ignoring the existence of such a scary monster, I decided to let Sakura go.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then that’s fine. However, if someone else tries to hound you about it, please tell me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> How much Horikita&#x27;s certainty is worth: &quot;So far, we’d been operating based purely on Horikita’s dogmatism and prejudices. It was quite possible that Sakura wasn’t the witness, like she said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> He volunteers the whole case to a Class B stranger: &quot;I told her that three people from Class C had called Sudou over, and there was a fistfight...&quot; — his stated reason: &quot;since there wasn’t much information to be gained anyway, it may not have been worth keeping quiet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His running account of Ichinose&#x27;s offer: &quot;Obviously, I couldn’t trust Ichinose yet. She was a student from Class B, and she gained nothing by involving herself. If helping others out of sheer goodwill was reflected in class or private points, then I could understand her motivation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On who decides: &quot;I glanced over to see what Horikita thought... I didn’t really have the power to decide in the first place; that was Horikita’s job.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The information gap is now his explicit grievance against the school: &quot;This was yet another oversight, another instance where Chabashira-sensei had failed to disclose something important... A usual, our teacher didn’t even pretend to give us equal treatment. I felt discriminated against.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the theory of personal space, and the cameras he had already found<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p102-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 4 sec  4 4  she walks into the special building alone and offers class b s help her entrance is unannounced and physically striking to the narrator   we turned in response to the unexpected voice  a beautiful girl with strawberry blonde hair stood behind us  i recognized her  though i hadn t ever spoken to her before  she was a student from class b  ichinose  rumor had it she was a superb student   hey  you two  what are you doing   sorry to interrupt you like that  do you have a moment  oh  if you happen to be in the middle of a so so date  though  i d like you to break it up right away   ha ha  i see  this place is a little too hot to be a date spot  she has been watching class d without speaking to it   i ve met you twice before  we didn t talk directly  though  i remember seeing you in the library once  too   i have a very good memory  you know    ak s receipt of it as a backhanded comment on his own unremarkableness  her reason for being there is the case itself   i thought that surely there d be something here related to the brawl  i wasn t here yesterday when class b heard about the witness  later  i heard that class d was looking for evidence of sudou s innocence  and  hmm  a connection  well  i m not connected  when i heard about what happened  i had some doubts  so i thought i d come here myself to take a look  would you mind filling me in  she takes refusal as data  not as an insult   guess not  huh  well  if the other classes were interested  to horikita s accusation of an ulterior motive   ulterior motive  you think we re working in the shadows to undermine both c and class d     ichinose wore a baffled expression   do you need to be that on guard  i m really just curious  that s all  her first principle  aimed at class d s own logic   so that s what happened  this story hasn t made its way to class b yet  hey  isn t this a pretty big problem  though  it doesn t really matter who lied since it s an issue about violence  right  shouldn t you be hurrying to uncover the truth  the question she asks instead of taking a side   so you believe sudou kun because he s your classmate  and your friend  of course  that much is obvious  so class d is in an uproar because sudou is being falsely charged  right  the answer she gets back  from one of the two class d students   the text does not say which   i d report on it honestly  after all  covering for a lie would only come back to haunt us later    and her reaction is agreement  not argument  ak s own line follows   yeah  okay  i think so  too  she does not take the dismissal personally   are you finished  you heard what you wanted  is horikita s  her answer is  hmm  yeah  how about i help you out  to look for the witness  or whatever  you re bound to get further with more people  right  her argument for intervening in another class s discipline case  stated as system logic   are classes d and b completely unrelated to each other  we don t know when these cases will spring up  or whom they ll involve  since the classes are in constant competition  there s always the chance that this will happen  this was the merely the first case  if the party that lied wins  that d set a bad precedent  also  i personally can t turn away now that i know what happened   sic    the merely  she prices her own value honestly  including the downside   if class b works with you  wouldn t that dramatically improve your credibility  though i suppose the opposite could be true  too  class d may suffer greater consequences if the truth s uncovered  and  what do you think  i don t believe it s a bad suggestion  she is taken on  horikita says yes  gives her own name first  and ak records the result    we had unexpectedly made ichinose of class b s acquaintance and accepted her as an ally  there was still the risk that this could lead to bad things  no matter what  things were going to change  she knows ayanokoji s name the moment horikita gives her own   it s nice to meet you  horikita san  and you too  ayanokouji kun    against ak s assumption a minute earlier that  she probably didn t even know my name  i was only one of many students to her  her reading of class d s witness problem   well  that means there isn t another witness  i mean  i guess someone from another class might have witnessed it  but it isn t likely  she is the source of the class points half of the club rule  which class d s own teacher had never given them   the school evaluates club and philanthropic activities  right  so if he enters a tournament and does well  sudou kun could earn points  those ll be tied to your class points  too  wait  did you guys not know that  did your teacher not tell you  her diagnosis of the school s teaching staff   your homeroom teacher is kind of weird     she doesn t seem motivated to tell us anything  she s completely apathetic  some teachers are like that     did you know that the school evaluates homeroom teachers when their class graduates  she arrives with nothing to gain  says so twice  is called a liar s ally to her face  and still ends the afternoon as class d s first outside partner   the volume s first class b agent and the counter example to horikita s theory that nobody helps for free  horikita suspects her on sight and hires her within the same conversation  the two are the pair who decide  over sakura s silence  to bring another class in  this is her first direct contact with ayanokoji in the volume  every fact about her here comes from what she says in one afternoon  and no class b student corroborates any of it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p102-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p102-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4: she walks into the special building alone and offers Class B&#x27;s help<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.102–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her entrance is unannounced and physically striking to the narrator: &quot;We turned in response to the unexpected voice. A beautiful girl with strawberry-blonde hair stood behind us. I recognized her, though I hadn’t ever spoken to her before. She was a student from Class B, Ichinose. Rumor had it she was a superb student.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Hey, you two. What are you doing?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Sorry to interrupt you like that. Do you have a moment? Oh, if you happen to be in the middle of a so-so date, though, I’d like you to break it up right away.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ha ha, I see. This place is a little too hot to be a date spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>19 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She has been watching Class D without speaking to it: “I’ve met you twice before. We didn’t talk directly, though. I remember seeing you in the library once, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I have a very good memory, you know.” — AK&#x27;s receipt of it as a backhanded comment on his own unremarkableness.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her reason for being there is the case itself: “I thought that surely there’d be something here related to the brawl. I wasn’t here yesterday when Class B heard about the witness. Later, I heard that Class D was looking for evidence of Sudou’s innocence.” and “Hmm, a connection? Well, I’m not connected. When I heard about what happened, I had some doubts. So I thought I’d come here myself to take a look. Would you mind filling me in?”<span class=\"pg\">p.103–104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She takes refusal as data, not as an insult: “Guess not, huh? Well, if the other classes were interested…”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> To Horikita&#x27;s accusation of an ulterior motive: “Ulterior motive? You think we’re working in the shadows to undermine both C and Class D?” — &quot;Ichinose wore a baffled expression. &#x27;Do you need to be that on guard? I’m really just curious, that’s all.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her first principle, aimed at Class D&#x27;s own logic: “So that’s what happened. This story hasn’t made its way to Class B yet. Hey, isn’t this a pretty big problem, though? It doesn’t really matter who lied since it’s an issue about violence, right? Shouldn’t you be hurrying to uncover the truth?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The question she asks instead of taking a side: “So you believe Sudou-kun because he’s your classmate. And your friend, of course, that much is obvious. So Class D is in an uproar because Sudou is being falsely charged, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The answer she gets back, from one of the two Class D students — the text does not say which: “I’d report on it honestly. After all, covering for a lie would only come back to haunt us later.” — and her reaction is agreement, not argument; AK&#x27;s own line follows, &quot;Yeah, okay. I think so, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She does not take the dismissal personally: “Are you finished? You heard what you wanted.” is Horikita&#x27;s; her answer is “Hmm. Yeah, how about I help you out? To look for the witness, or whatever. You’re bound to get further with more people, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her argument for intervening in another class&#x27;s discipline case, stated as system logic: “Are Classes D and B completely unrelated to each other? We don’t know when these cases will spring up, or whom they’ll involve. Since the classes are in constant competition, there’s always the chance that this will happen. This was the merely the first case. If the party that lied wins, that’d set a bad precedent. Also, I personally can’t turn away now that I know what happened.” (sic — &quot;the merely&quot;)<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She prices her own value honestly, including the downside: “If Class B works with you, wouldn’t that dramatically improve your credibility? Though I suppose the opposite could be true, too. Class D may suffer greater consequences if the truth’s uncovered…” and “What do you think? I don’t believe it’s a bad suggestion.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> She is taken on: Horikita says yes, gives her own name first, and AK records the result — &quot;We had unexpectedly made Ichinose of Class B’s acquaintance and accepted her as an ally. There was still the risk that this could lead to bad things. No matter what, things were going to change.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She knows Ayanokōji&#x27;s name the moment Horikita gives her own: “It’s nice to meet you, Horikita-san. And you too, Ayanokouji-kun.” — against AK&#x27;s assumption a minute earlier that &quot;she probably didn’t even know my name. I was only one of many students to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her reading of Class D&#x27;s witness problem: “Well, that means there isn’t another witness. I mean, I guess someone from another class might have witnessed it, but it isn’t likely.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> She is the source of the class-points half of the club rule, which Class D&#x27;s own teacher had never given them: “the school evaluates club and philanthropic activities, right? So if he enters a tournament and does well, Sudou-kun could earn points. Those’ll be tied to your class points, too. Wait… Did you guys not know that? Did your teacher not tell you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her diagnosis of the school&#x27;s teaching staff: “Your homeroom teacher is kind of weird.” / “She doesn’t seem motivated to tell us anything. She’s completely apathetic. Some teachers are like that.” / “Did you know that the school evaluates homeroom teachers when their class graduates?”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She arrives with nothing to gain, says so twice, is called a liar&#x27;s ally to her face, and still ends the afternoon as Class D&#x27;s first outside partner — the volume&#x27;s first Class B agent and the counter-example to Horikita&#x27;s theory that nobody helps for free.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Horikita suspects her on sight and hires her within the same conversation; the two are the pair who decide, over Sakura&#x27;s silence, to bring another class in.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> This is her first direct contact with Ayanokōji in the volume; every fact about her here comes from what she says in one afternoon, and no Class B student corroborates any of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: what Class B&#x27;s representative actually does<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 4 4 5  she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is her only environmental protest in the volume  delivered to a stranger   a school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst    ichinose laughs anyway   ha ha ha  that s probably true  you re pretty interesting  she outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look   horikita shot me a look that seemed to say  i don t want to do it  give her yours  she declines a spare key to his room before being offered one  and calls the visit itself a failing   for your room  ike kun asked earlier if i wanted one  i refused     after all  it s rare for me to visit your room  ayanokouji kun  besides  coming here is a shameful act in itself  a disgrace  understand    ak   i wasn t hurt at all  i definitely wasn t thinking anything like  wow  that was unexpectedly harsh  the one moment of her own body language he gets to see  and she names it herself   why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger     to hide my pounding heart  or something  her agenda for the visit  stated as two problems   ayanokouji kun  i want to hear your thoughts on sudou kun s case once again  also  i find kushida san s actions a bit concerning   impossible  the very person in question didn t recognize what was happening  i m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class  frankly  i still think it would have been better to abandon him  the pedagogical claim she makes for not saving him   that was different  even if we managed to miraculously prove his innocence  do you think he ll mature  saving him might have the opposite effect    ak s tag   her defiant glare seemed to say  do you understand my point  she turns his own reasoning back on him in real time   knowing sudou s flawed personality  you realized from the very beginning how difficult it would be to prove his innocence  didn t you  that way  it s easier to think he d be better off accepting his punishment  especially better for those who hate him    ak s record of being caught   i felt like i d been backed against a wall  unable to run  if i tried to forcefully deny  she would just dig deeper  her verdict on the rest of class d  delivered as mercilessly as ak notes   kushida san and ike kun and the others haven t noticed at all  it seems  they simply believe in sudou kun  and want to save him from the lie for his sake and our class s sake  they don t understand the urgency of the situation   a little bit  so she realized it by herself  then  and  you told her  didn t you    ak   she cornered me with her words  it was like being interrogated  a little scary  the accusation that he engineered the midterm operations   you came up with the idea of getting the old test questions  and purchasing exam points  i can t say i m surprised  you do seem quite cunning at times  but i m dissatisfied  her full description of him  the volume s closest attempt at a characterisation of ayanokoji by another student   honestly  there s so much about you that i don t understand  you re a mystery  you re the most difficult person to predict in our class  you re versatile  yet you often idle your time away  you never seem to stay still  it s as though you cannot be categorized  then the sentence he cannot deflect   i guess what i should say is that you re just blending in and hiding your true talents  you re hiding in plain sight  you disgust me more than anyone else  she does not actually know what he did  and stops at a feeling   i see  i wondered if being called out like that was normal  it seemed i d taken the bait and gotten caught in horikita s trap  a small failure on my part    ak s own accounting of the conversation s cost  her koenji assessment  offered as the counter example to his mysteriousness   he s surprisingly easy to understand  he studies well  is athletic  and gets excellent grades  his personality is the problem  in the end  i can easily categorize and summarize his behavioral problems in only a few words  he s self centered  she is candid only in private and only with one person  the entire volume s worth of her actual analysis of class d   sudou  kushida  ayanokoji  koenji   is delivered in his room in one sitting  and none of it survives as anything but privately held when she re enters a classroom  ak s own note on the setting  which should not be over read   i wondered why i felt a little nervous being alone with horikita behind closed doors  ak s projection of her  the chapter s last word on her   at this rate  when she reached adulthood  she d probably become a teacher like chabashira sensei","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.108–113<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She outsources the social half of the alliance to him with a look: &quot;Horikita shot me a look that seemed to say, I don’t want to do it. Give her yours.&quot; The one moment of her own body language he gets to see, and she names it herself: “Why are you tracing letters on the wall with your finger?” / “To hide my pounding heart. Or something.”<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s…<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room…<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her agenda for the visit, stated as two problems: “Ayanokouji-kun, I want to hear your thoughts on Sudou-kun’s case once again. Also, I find Kushida-san’s actions a bit concerning.”<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her only environmental protest in the volume, delivered to a stranger: “A school that constantly runs air conditioning in empty buildings and is unkind to the environment is the worst,” — Ichinose laughs anyway: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s probably true. You’re pretty interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She declines a spare key to his room before being offered one, and calls the visit itself a failing: “For your room? Ike-kun asked earlier if I wanted one. I refused.” … “After all, it’s rare for me to visit your room, Ayanokouji-kun. Besides, coming here is a shameful act in itself. A disgrace. Understand?” — AK: &quot;I wasn’t hurt at all. I definitely wasn’t thinking anything like, Wow, that was unexpectedly harsh.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Impossible. The very person in question didn’t recognize what was happening. I’m only now reluctantly offering to help for the sake of our class. Frankly, I still think it would have been better to abandon him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110–111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The pedagogical claim she makes for not saving him: “That was different. Even if we managed to miraculously prove his innocence, do you think he’ll mature? Saving him might have the opposite effect.” — AK&#x27;s tag: &quot;Her defiant glare seemed to say, Do you understand my point?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She turns his own reasoning back on him in real time: “Knowing Sudou’s flawed personality, you realized from the very beginning how difficult it would be to prove his innocence, didn’t you? That way, it’s easier to think he’d be better off accepting his punishment. Especially better for those who hate him.” — AK&#x27;s record of being caught: &quot;I felt like I’d been backed against a wall, unable to run. If I tried to forcefully deny, she would just dig deeper.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her verdict on the rest of Class D, delivered as mercilessly as AK notes: “Kushida-san and Ike-kun and the others haven’t noticed at all, it seems. They simply believe in Sudou-kun, and want to save him from the lie for his sake and our class’s sake. They don’t understand the urgency of the situation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A little bit? So she realized it by herself, then?” and “You told her, didn’t you?” — AK: &quot;She cornered me with her words. It was like being interrogated. A little scary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The accusation that he engineered the midterm operations: “You came up with the idea of getting the old test questions, and purchasing exam points. I can’t say I’m surprised. You do seem quite cunning at times, but…I’m dissatisfied.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her full description of him, the volume&#x27;s closest attempt at a characterisation of Ayanokōji by another student: “Honestly, there’s so much about you that I don’t understand. You’re a mystery. You’re the most difficult person to predict in our class. You’re versatile, yet you often idle your time away. You never seem to stay still. It’s as though you cannot be categorized.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Then the sentence he cannot deflect: “I guess what I should say is that you’re just blending in and hiding your true talents. You’re hiding in plain sight. You disgust me more than anyone else.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She does not actually know what he did, and stops at a feeling: &quot;I see. I wondered if being called out like that was normal. It seemed I’d taken the bait and gotten caught in Horikita’s trap. A small failure on my part.&quot; — AK&#x27;s own accounting of the conversation&#x27;s cost.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her Kōenji assessment, offered as the counter-example to his mysteriousness: “He’s surprisingly easy to understand. He studies well, is athletic, and gets excellent grades. His personality is the problem. In the end, I can easily categorize and summarize his behavioral problems in only a few words: he’s self-centered.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is candid only in private and only with one person; the entire volume&#x27;s worth of her actual analysis of Class D — Sudou, Kushida, Ayanokōji, Kōenji — is delivered in his room in one sitting, and none of it survives as anything but privately held when she re-enters a classroom.<span class=\"pg\">p.110–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> AK&#x27;s own note on the setting, which should not be over-read: &quot;I wondered why I felt a little nervous being alone with Horikita behind closed doors.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> AK&#x27;s projection of her, the chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;At this rate, when she reached adulthood, she’d probably become a teacher like Chabashira-sensei.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: she invites Ayanokōji out, and decides on Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p108-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 4 sec  4 4 4 6  what class b s representative actually does the reason her own teacher is different  given as a third party s motto   our homeroom teacher  hoshinomiya sensei  says it like it s her motto  she says she wants to do her best because the homeroom teacher for class a gets a special bonus  looks like it s pretty different for you guys   i think it would probably be good for us to meet up and discuss things    horikita s answer  which she takes without offence   i never thought i d receive aid from the enemy   this seems like a problem we need to address before we can fight  we re not really on equal footing  are we    the clearest statement in the volume of what the class rank system does between classes  she says the quiet part about class d s teacher out loud   i m envious of your relationship with your homeroom teacher  and your class environment  horikita  who has just insulted her  is charmed   ha ha ha  that s probably true  you re pretty interesting  her contact details are exchanged on her initiative   how about we exchange contact information  so things can progress smoothly    and ak learns her given name in the process   also  i learned that ichinose s first name was honami an unnecessary bit of information  her reliability is measurable   every time she wanted permission to try something she d contact us  even though she d already said to leave things to her  i didn t think she needed to limit herself so severely  a month after the entrance exam she is already her class s channel to the school s staff   thank you very much  it s been a pleasure    she has been at the dormitory manager s desk handling other students  complaints   some people from my class wanted to make requests about their dorms  i gathered everyone s thoughts on the matter and told the dorm manager  stuff like water usage  noise  and so on  class b s self organisation is the fact this scene exists to reveal   class rep  why class rep     i m my class s representative  it seems like that  anyway  and  no  that s just something class b set up on its own  i think it s good to have some assigned roles  right  the full informal officer set  in her own words   whether or not they serve a function is a different question  but we do have other roles for formality s sake  stuff like vice class representative  and secretary  they could be more useful when we have a cultural fair  or sports festival  or something  we could try deciding things on the spot  but that might lead to trouble  ak s read of why she holds the role   most people wouldn t want to be class representative  they d be forced to do annoying stuff  however  with ichinose taking the initiative for class b  she probably didn t foist things on others  i d bet she handled her duties smoothly  she refuses the grandeur of it   do you think it s weird  it s all purely informal  besides  there are quite a few troublemakers  we have to deal with a lot of stuff    ak s note   as she said   we have to deal with a lot of stuff  ichinose laughed  her physical entrance in this section is written by ak as attraction  it is his narration  not her characterisation   she had beautiful long  wavy hair and big eyes  the second button of her blazer strained over her large chest  her upright posture matched her dignified personality  i found myself more attracted to her cool temperament than how cute she was  she is the first person outside class d horikita will negotiate with  and the negotiation is conducted entirely by horikita s hostility plus horikita s yes  two weeks in  she greets him first  knows his name  and walks to school with him   while he is still cataloguing her as an asset with unclear motive","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p108-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: what Class B&#x27;s representative actually does<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.108–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her contact details are exchanged on her initiative: “How about we exchange contact information, so things can progress smoothly?” — and AK learns her given name in the process: &quot;Also, I learned that Ichinose’s first name was Honami—an unnecessary bit of information.&quot; A month after the entrance exam she is already her class&#x27;s channel to the school&#x27;s staff: &quot;Thank you very much. It’s been a pleasure.&quot; — she has been at the dormitory manager&#x27;s desk handling other students&#x27; complaints: “Some people from my class wanted to make requests about their dorms. I gathered everyone’s thoughts on the matter and told the dorm manager. Stuff like water usage, noise, and so on.” Her physical entrance in this section is written by AK as attraction; it is his narration, not her characterisation: &quot;She had beautiful long, wavy hair and big eyes. The second button of her blazer strained over her large chest. Her upright posture matched her dignified personality. I found myself more attracted to her cool temperament than how cute she was.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The reason her own teacher is different, given as a third party&#x27;s motto: “Our homeroom teacher, Hoshinomiya-sensei, says it like it’s her motto. She says she wants to do her best because the homeroom teacher for Class A gets a…<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “I think it would probably be good for us to meet up and discuss things.” — Horikita&#x27;s answer, which she takes without offence: “I never thought I’d receive aid from the enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “This seems like a problem we need to address before we can fight. We’re not really on equal footing, are we?” — the clearest statement in the volume of what the class-rank system does between classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The reason her own teacher is different, given as a third party&#x27;s motto: “Our homeroom teacher, Hoshinomiya-sensei, says it like it’s her motto. She says she wants to do her best because the homeroom teacher for Class A gets a special bonus. Looks like it’s pretty different for you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She says the quiet part about Class D&#x27;s teacher out loud: “I’m envious of your relationship with your homeroom teacher. And your class environment.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Horikita, who has just insulted her, is charmed: &quot;Ha ha ha, that’s probably true. You’re pretty interesting.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her reliability is measurable: &quot;Every time she wanted permission to try something she’d contact us, even though she’d already said to leave things to her. I didn’t think she needed to limit herself so severely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class B&#x27;s self-organisation is the fact this scene exists to reveal: “Class Rep? Why Class Rep?” — “I’m my class’s representative. It seems like that, anyway.” and “No, that’s just something Class B set up on its own. I think it’s good to have some assigned roles, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The full informal officer set, in her own words: “Whether or not they serve a function is a different question, but we do have other roles for formality’s sake. Stuff like vice class representative, and secretary. They could be more useful when we have a cultural fair, or sports festival, or something. We could try deciding things on the spot, but that might lead to trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> AK&#x27;s read of why she holds the role: “Most people wouldn’t want to be class representative. They’d be forced to do annoying stuff... However, with Ichinose taking the initiative for Class B, she probably didn’t foist things on others. I’d bet she handled her duties smoothly.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> She refuses the grandeur of it: “Do you think it’s weird? It’s all purely informal. Besides, there are quite a few troublemakers. We have to deal with a lot of stuff.” — AK&#x27;s note: &quot;As she said, &#x27;We have to deal with a lot of stuff,&#x27; Ichinose laughed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She is the first person outside Class D Horikita will negotiate with, and the negotiation is conducted entirely by Horikita&#x27;s hostility plus Horikita&#x27;s yes.<span class=\"pg\">p.108–110<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Two weeks in, she greets him first, knows his name, and walks to school with him — while he is still cataloguing her as an asset with unclear motive.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p102-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: she walks into the special building alone and offers Class B&#x27;s help<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school, and what she thinks the class system is hiding<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p108-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 4 4 6  the teacher s own incentive  and the roles class d never made the staff side of the class system  from a class b student   the homeroom teacher for class a gets a special bonus    reported as hoshinomiya sensei s stated motivation  and the first explanation the volume offers for why teaching quality is uneven between classes  class d s own reading of the gap  ak on chabashira    our teacher appeared to lack ambition  or even an interest in money  it felt like even if we collapsed into failure  she d just say it was great  and  other classes pitied us  if anything  this showed how little interest chabashira sensei felt for her own students  classes may invent their own governance with no school mandate  class b elected a class representative  a vice representative and a secretary  purely informal   something class b set up on its own    and the roles are justified as machinery for the cultural fair and sports festival  class d has none   i understood her point  but we certainly weren t going to assign our own class representative    the volume s explanation of why class d organises through four individuals  hirata  kushida  horikita  ayanokoji  instead of through offices  neither fact is confirmed by the school  both arrive as secondhand report from class b  the bonus claim is the volume s only stated material incentive attached to a teacher  and it is never repeated by a teacher","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p108-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the teacher&#x27;s own incentive, and the roles Class D never made<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.108, p.114–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The staff side of the class system, from a Class B student: &quot;the homeroom teacher for Class A gets a special bonus&quot; — reported as Hoshinomiya-sensei&#x27;s stated motivation, and the first explanation the volume offers for why teaching quality is uneven between classes.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D&#x27;s own reading of the gap: AK on Chabashira — &quot;Our teacher appeared to lack ambition, or even an interest in money. It felt like even if we collapsed into failure, she’d just say it was great.&quot; and &quot;Other classes pitied us. If anything, this showed how little interest Chabashira-sensei felt for her own students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Classes may invent their own governance with no school mandate: Class B elected a class representative, a vice representative and a secretary &quot;purely informal&quot;, &quot;something Class B set up on its own&quot; — and the roles are justified as machinery for the cultural fair and sports festival.<span class=\"pg\">p.114–115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D has none: &quot;I understood her point, but we certainly weren’t going to assign our own class representative.&quot; — the volume&#x27;s explanation of why Class D organises through four individuals (Hirata, Kushida, Horikita, Ayanokōji) instead of through offices.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Neither fact is confirmed by the school; both arrive as secondhand report from Class B. The bonus claim is the volume&#x27;s only stated material incentive attached to a teacher, and it is never repeated by a teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.108, p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p95-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.3–4.4: the cameras that grade you, and the tracks Class D was never told about<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: the first figures any student says out loud<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p116-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"","q":"midterm and final written exams ch 4 sec  4 6  the exam as the only lever  priced by a class b student  i ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island    the reward class d was promised at the end of the previous volume reaches the rest of the year as rumour  the link back to their own teacher   that sparked a memory  i d forgotten about it  but chabashira sensei had mentioned a vacation   so far  the midterm is all that s given us a chance to raise our class points  so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us  i mean  even class a has lost points    two weeks after the results  class b s representative states the midterm as the only point raiser the school has run so far  her expectation of what comes next   i think there might be a hidden task  one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams  nothing in this stretch is a school announcement  the vacation is rumour  the point totals are a student s report  and the july final is named only as one of the two events the summer task would outweigh","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/exam/midterm-final-written.html#sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p116-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6: the exam as the only lever, priced by a Class B student<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.116–117<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/exam/midterm-final-written.html\">Midterm and Final Written Exams<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island.&quot; — the reward Class D was promised at the end of the previous volume reaches the rest of the year as rumour.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">The link back to their own teacher: &quot;That sparked a memory. I’d forgotten about it, but Chabashira-sensei had mentioned a vacation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\">Her expectation of what comes next: &quot;I think there might be a hidden task, one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;So far, the midterm is all that’s given us a chance to raise our class points, so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us. I mean, even Class A has lost points.&quot; — two weeks after the results, Class B&#x27;s representative states the midterm as the only point-raiser the school has run so far.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Nothing in this stretch is a school announcement: the vacation is rumour, the point totals are a student&#x27;s report, and the July final is named only as one of the two events the summer task would outweigh.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-midterm-final-written-y1v2-p45-1\">← Before: Ch.3 sec. 3.1: the midterm&#x27;s social residue gets spent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 6  walking to school with class b s representative  it seemed i could have normal  relationship building conversations after all   i don t have to leave so early  i usually hang around my room for about 20 minutes    his answer to her question   aren t you usually a little late   was this the so called popularity phase i was told would occur three times in my life  i hadn t experienced it yet  it was about time that i entered my first phase  his default reading of any gift the school gives   it was all incredibly suspicious  i really didn t think our school was going to be so good to be true  they had to be keeping something from us  his own price for the coming summer event   it would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points  however  it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1 000 points   only people who have meaningful friendships can enjoy a vacation to its fullest  there s nothing quite as uncomfortable as traveling without close friends  especially when you re traveling with a group  just imagining it made me feel like throwing up   i don t hate it  i don t think i do  anyway    to  do you hate traveling   just recalled something a little bit traumatic    his own staging of the line   my dry laugher echoed through the hot hallway   translation typo kept as printed  the only trip he owns   i d never traveled with a friend before  i had gone to new york with my parents a long  long time ago  not a single millisecond of it had been fun  his private sorting of class d s misplacement  and the first naming of yukimura   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone   isn t that how societal competition works  though  i don t think there s anything particularly strange about that   wouldn t it be wiser not to talk to someone from another class about this     i asked ichinose  feeling slightly worried  what he is actually checking for   after all  it was possible she could ve given me a valuable hint  and i d do something with it   i m not smart enough to engage in an exchange of ideas  all i can say is   i m sorry   that wasn t in the any of the hundred million books i d read    his reaction to her question about confessions  the grammar is the translation s  kept as printed  his unspoken defence  written as a line of dialogue inside his own head   was she going to call me disgusting  or a virgin  or a shitty moron   did someone confess to you   i don t think there s much point in looking for evidence or another witness  doing that would be a waste of time and a headache    his own dismissal of the case he is still working  speaker fixed by her answer   but you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate  right   even though i knew absolutely nothing was going to happen  i was pretty excited  that was what being a man was all about","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.116–122<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t have to leave so early. I usually hang around my room for about 20 minutes.&quot; — his answer to her question, &quot;Aren’t you usually a little late?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t hate it. I don’t think I do, anyway…&quot; — to &quot;Do you hate traveling?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Just recalled something a little bit traumatic.&quot; — his own staging of the line: &quot;My dry laugher echoed through the hot hallway.&quot; (translation typo kept as printed).<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It seemed I could have normal, relationship-building conversations after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Was this the so-called popularity phase I was told would occur three times in my life? I hadn’t experienced it yet; it was about time that I entered my first phase.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His default reading of any gift the school gives: &quot;It was all incredibly suspicious. I really didn’t think our school was going to be so good to be true. They had to be keeping something from us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His own price for the coming summer event: &quot;It would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points. However, it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1,000 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Only people who have meaningful friendships can enjoy a vacation to its fullest. There’s nothing quite as uncomfortable as traveling without close friends, especially when you’re traveling with a group. Just imagining it made me feel like throwing up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only trip he owns: &quot;I’d never traveled with a friend before. I had gone to New York with my parents a long, long time ago. Not a single millisecond of it had been fun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private sorting of Class D&#x27;s misplacement, and the first naming of Yukimura: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Isn’t that how societal competition works, though? I don’t think there’s anything particularly strange about that,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wouldn’t it be wiser not to talk to someone from another class about this?&quot; — &quot;I asked Ichinose, feeling slightly worried.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he is actually checking for: &quot;After all, it was possible she could’ve given me a valuable hint, and I’d do something with it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m not smart enough to engage in an exchange of ideas. All I can say is, ‘I’m sorry.’&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;That…wasn’t in the any of the hundred million books I’d read.&quot; — his reaction to her question about confessions; the grammar is the translation&#x27;s, kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His unspoken defence, written as a line of dialogue inside his own head: &quot;Was she going to call me disgusting, or a virgin, or a shitty moron?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did someone confess to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think there’s much point in looking for evidence or another witness. Doing that would be a waste of time and a headache.&quot; — his own dismissal of the case he is still working; speaker fixed by her answer, &quot;But you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even though I knew absolutely nothing was going to happen, I was pretty excited. That was what being a man was all about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p97-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4: the special building, and the friend line he chooses to say<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p116-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 4 sec  4 6  walking to school  and what she thinks the class system is hiding  aren t you usually a little late  this reminds me that i ve never seen you around this time    his narration of the ask   ichinose s question sounded harmless  as if she were following some kind of template   i just stand out because i m the class rep  that s all    and his read of whether that is modesty   it didn t seem like she was trying to act modest  apparently that s what she truly thought  the corridor s reaction  in one line each   ichinose  who was walking next to me  monopolized all of the girls  attention   ah  that reminds me  did you hear about summer break  ayanokoujikun    printed without the hyphen in his name  kept as the translation has it   i ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island   i can t believe it  though  could we really go on a vacation   it s suspicious  after all  i think it s going to be a turning point     but i saw from her bitter smile that she also had doubts   yeah  yeah  i think there might be a hidden task  one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams  otherwise  the difference between class a and us wouldn t close much  we could diminish the gap little by little  the only class point figures a student volunteers all volume   we have about 600 points  so our classes are around 350 points apart   so far  the midterm is all that s given us a chance to raise our class points  so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us  i mean  even class a has lost points   i m concerned  but i think that there s a chance for us to make a comeback  i intend to focus all of my emotional energy on making those preparations   we re in a tight spot ourselves  if the gap widens any further  we won t be able to catch up   but if we actually did vacation on a tropical island  that would be awesome   hey  i still have some things on my mind  may i ask you some questions   we ve been separated into four classes from the start  right  do you really think they separated us by ability   i ve been thinking about it since we started here  someone might be good at studying  but bad at physical activity  another might be good at physical activities  but bad at studying  but if students are ranked by overall ability  doesn t that mean that the lower classes are at an overwhelming disadvantage   if we were competing as individuals  sure  but this is a competition between classes  right  if you simply put all of the superior students into class a  then doesn t that mean the rest of us have virtually no chance of succeeding   there s definitely a big difference between classes a through d right now  however  i think they re trying to hide something  but going about it in a weird way  don t you agree   ha  no reason  really  it s just something that popped into my head  if it weren t true  then it d be fair to say the whole situation is cruel  i think that good students and good athletes were placed into class d for a reason  as a countermeasure   i don t think so  there s a lot to be gained from an exchange of ideas  also  since we re cooperating now  there shouldn t be any problems    his gloss   she wasn t complacent about being in class b  that was just ichinose s natural personality   i don t mind if i m the one who does the talking and thinking  if you think it s helpful information  then it s okay for you to use it   has a girl ever confessed her feelings to you    the question she stops herself from explaining  she works out the class sorting problem in front of a stranger from the worst class in the school  offers her conclusion to him  and refuses to treat it as leverage  the only structural analysis of the four class system a student gives all volume arrives unprompted and unguarded  she asks the question she cannot follow up on   oh no  i m sorry  it s nothing    and his note on it   it didn t look like it was nothing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p116-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school, and what she thinks the class system is hiding<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.116–121<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Aren’t you usually a little late? This reminds me that I’ve never seen you around this time.&quot; — his narration of the ask: &quot;Ichinose’s question sounded harmless, as if she were following some kind of template.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I just stand out because I’m the class rep. That’s all.&quot; — and his read of whether that is modesty: &quot;It didn’t seem like she was trying to act modest. Apparently that’s what she truly thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Ah, that reminds me. Did you hear about summer break, Ayanokoujikun?&quot; — printed without the hyphen in his name; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>21 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The corridor&#x27;s reaction, in one line each: &quot;Ichinose, who was walking next to me, monopolized all of the girls’ attention.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t believe it, though. Could we really go on a vacation?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s suspicious, after all. I think it’s going to be a turning point.&quot; — &quot;But I saw from her bitter smile that she also had doubts.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, yeah. I think there might be a hidden task, one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams. Otherwise, the difference between Class A and us wouldn’t close much. We could diminish the gap little by little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The only class-point figures a student volunteers all volume: &quot;We have about 600 points, so our classes are around 350 points apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So far, the midterm is all that’s given us a chance to raise our class points, so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us. I mean, even Class A has lost points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m concerned, but I think that there’s a chance for us to make a comeback. I intend to focus all of my emotional energy on making those preparations.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’re in a tight spot ourselves. If the gap widens any further, we won’t be able to catch up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But if we actually did vacation on a tropical island, that would be awesome!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, I still have some things on my mind. May I ask you some questions?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’ve been separated into four classes from the start, right? Do you really think they separated us by ability?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ve been thinking about it since we started here. Someone might be good at studying, but bad at physical activity. Another might be good at physical activities, but bad at studying. But if students are ranked by overall ability, doesn’t that mean that the lower classes are at an overwhelming disadvantage?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If we were competing as individuals, sure. But this is a competition between classes, right? If you simply put all of the superior students into Class A, then doesn’t that mean the rest of us have virtually no chance of succeeding?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s definitely a big difference between classes A through D right now. However, I think they’re trying to hide something, but going about it in a weird way. Don’t you agree?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha, no reason, really. It’s just something that popped into my head. If it weren’t true, then it’d be fair to say the whole situation is cruel. I think that good students and good athletes were placed into Class D for a reason, as a countermeasure.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t think so. There’s a lot to be gained from an exchange of ideas. Also, since we’re cooperating now, there shouldn’t be any problems.&quot; — his gloss: &quot;She wasn’t complacent about being in Class B. That was just Ichinose’s natural personality.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t mind if I’m the one who does the talking and thinking. If you think it’s helpful information, then it’s okay for you to use it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Has a girl ever confessed her feelings to you?&quot; — the question she stops herself from explaining.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She works out the class-sorting problem in front of a stranger from the worst class in the school, offers her conclusion to him, and refuses to treat it as leverage: the only structural analysis of the four-class system a student gives all volume arrives unprompted and unguarded.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She asks the question she cannot follow up on: &quot;Oh no, I’m sorry. It’s nothing.&quot; — and his note on it: &quot;It didn’t look like it was nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: what Class B&#x27;s representative actually does<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p121-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: she tries to dodge a confession and is made to give it<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p116-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 6  the first figures any student says out loud  i ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island    the summer reward exists in july only as a rumour a class b student repeats  the school has announced nothing  the connection back to class d s own teacher   that sparked a memory  i d forgotten about it  but chabashira sensei had mentioned a vacation  what class b expects the break to be worth   i think there might be a hidden task  one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams  otherwise  the difference between class a and us wouldn t close much  we could diminish the gap little by little  class b s standing  given freely   we have about 600 points  so our classes are around 350 points apart   so far  the midterm is all that s given us a chance to raise our class points  so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us  i mean  even class a has lost points    the first statement in the volume that a drop in class points is normal rather than punishment  class d s actual month   class d had only managed to get 87 points this month  we weren t anywhere close to being able to compete with the others  the narrator s own sizing of the coming event   it would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points  however  it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1 000 points  every figure in this stretch is a student s report  not a school announcement  and the only two classes whose numbers are compared are b and a  class c is absent from the account entirely","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p116-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6: the first figures any student says out loud<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.116–118<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\">&quot;I’ve heard rumors that we might be taking a vacation to a tropical island.&quot; — the summer reward exists in July only as a rumour a Class B student repeats; the school has announced nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\">The connection back to Class D&#x27;s own teacher: &quot;That sparked a memory. I’d forgotten about it, but Chabashira-sensei had mentioned a vacation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> What Class B expects the break to be worth: &quot;I think there might be a hidden task, one that has a bigger impact on us than the midterms or final exams. Otherwise, the difference between Class A and us wouldn’t close much. We could diminish the gap little by little.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class B&#x27;s standing, given freely: &quot;We have about 600 points, so our classes are around 350 points apart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;So far, the midterm is all that’s given us a chance to raise our class points, so losing at least a few points was unavoidable for us. I mean, even Class A has lost points.&quot; — the first statement in the volume that a drop in class points is normal rather than punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Class D&#x27;s actual month: &quot;Class D had only managed to get 87 points this month. We weren’t anywhere close to being able to compete with the others.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s own sizing of the coming event: &quot;It would probably be worth more than 10 or 20 points. However, it was difficult to imagine that it would change things by 500 or even 1,000 points.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Every figure in this stretch is a student&#x27;s report, not a school announcement, and the only two classes whose numbers are compared are B and A; Class C is absent from the account entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.6: the teacher&#x27;s own incentive, and the roles Class D never made<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p138-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the shops licensed to the school, and what a warranty is worth<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 4 sec  4 6 4 8  named by everyone  present nowhere the narrator s roster of who is actually carrying class d  in his own words   actually  the ones who had to work especially hard were horikita  hirata  and kushida  the first name in his private list of students wrongly sorted into class d   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone  kushida  relaying her conclusion to the one person horikita will not speak to directly   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  kushida s summary of her  offered as the standing question of the class   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in class d  kushida s probe about her   but doesn t she behave normally with you  ayanokouji kun  how ayanokoji describes her to a third party  which is the only version of her kushida receives   when i think of my relationship with horikita  it s like there s a wall between us  or perhaps i should say that s the extent of our relationship  if you understand what i m getting at  his withheld verdict on her exceptionalism  kept off the phone   horikita wasn t special  she belonged to a unique class of people  i kept quiet  though  afraid that if i badmouthed her she d find out about it  the plan that would place her beside the witness is cancelled before it is proposed  by the person organising the errand   while taking horikita along would probably be the best option  it was delusional to think that horikita and kushida would spend their day off together  all of this is secondhand  the second half of chapter 4 contains no horikita scene  her last appearance is alone with ayanokoji in his room  and the class s entire summer facing strategy is discussed without her in the room where it is decided","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.118–130<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kushida, relaying her conclusion to the one person Horikita will not speak to directly: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me…<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Kushida&#x27;s probe about her: &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s roster of who is actually carrying Class D, in his own words: &quot;Actually, the ones who had to work especially hard were Horikita, Hirata, and Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The first name in his private list of students wrongly sorted into Class D: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Kushida&#x27;s summary of her, offered as the standing question of the class: &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> How Ayanokōji describes her to a third party, which is the only version of her Kushida receives: &quot;When I think of my relationship with Horikita, it’s like there’s a wall between us. Or perhaps I should say that’s the extent of our relationship, if you understand what I’m getting at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His withheld verdict on her exceptionalism, kept off the phone: &quot;Horikita wasn’t special. She belonged to a unique class of people. I kept quiet, though, afraid that if I badmouthed her she’d find out about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan that would place her beside the witness is cancelled before it is proposed, by the person organising the errand: &quot;While taking Horikita along would probably be the best option, it was delusional to think that Horikita and Kushida would spend their day off together.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> All of this is secondhand. The second half of Chapter 4 contains no Horikita scene; her last appearance is alone with Ayanokōji in his room, and the class&#x27;s entire summer-facing strategy is discussed without her in the room where it is decided.<span class=\"pg\">p.118–130<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.4–4.5: she follows him to his room and names what she thinks he is<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kouenji-rokusuke","q":"koenji rokusuke ch 4 sec  4 6  sec  4 8  he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people s summary in the narrator s private list of students who were wrongly sorted into class d   horikita  kouenji  and yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone  kushida  reopening the corridor incident on the phone   that reminds me  it was really scary when kouenji kun and sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting    printed as one word  kept as the translation has it  in ayanokoji s estimate of what that fight would have become   kouenji always seemed laid back  but if sudou started taking swings at him  he would fight  if that happened  it d be a disaster  he has no scene of his own after p 93  the second half of chapter 4 keeps him as a recollection and a hypothesis","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p119-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.6, sec. 4.8: he exists in the rest of the chapter as other people&#x27;s summary<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.119, p.129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Kushida, reopening the corridor incident on the phone: &quot;That reminds me. It was really scary when Kouenji-kun and Sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting.&quot; — printed as one word; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the narrator&#x27;s private list of students who were wrongly sorted into Class D: &quot;Horikita, Kouenji, and Yukimura were undoubtedly three people who deserved to be at the top based on their academics alone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.119<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> In Ayanokōji&#x27;s estimate of what that fight would have become: &quot;Kouenji always seemed laid-back, but if Sudou started taking swings at him, he would fight. If that happened, it’d be a disaster.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> He has no scene of his own after p.93; the second half of Chapter 4 keeps him as a recollection and a hypothesis.<span class=\"pg\">p.119–129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v2-p92-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.3: he speaks to Sudou&#x27;s face without looking at him<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 4 sec  4 7  sec  4 11  he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly kushida  on the phone about the corridor fight   i couldn t even move  hirata kun was so amazing  though    ayanokoji s jealous gloss on the praise   hearing her praise hirata like that made me a little jealous  the couple the class copies   it seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like hirata and karuizawa  he is invoked as a teacher of social technique by the one person who watches him most closely   what should i do  please  hirata  teach me  she credits him and herself  in the same breath  for class d s cohesion   class d was able to come together  thanks to you and hirata  in the second half of chapter 4 he appears only as other students  measure of themselves  his own scenes ended at p 93","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.7, sec. 4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.120, p.149<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Kushida, on the phone about the corridor fight: &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot; — Ayanokōji&#x27;s jealous gloss on the praise: &quot;Hearing her praise Hirata like that made me a little jealous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The couple the class copies: &quot;It seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like Hirata and Karuizawa.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is invoked as a teacher of social technique by the one person who watches him most closely: &quot;What should I do? Please, Hirata. Teach me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She credits him and herself, in the same breath, for Class D&#x27;s cohesion: &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> In the second half of Chapter 4 he appears only as other students&#x27; measure of themselves; his own scenes ended at p.93.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p83-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: he will greet Sakura but not ask her, and he physically stops Sudou<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p120-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"karuizawa-kei","q":"karuizawa kei ch 4 sec  4 7  she survives in the volume as a standard  not a participant  it seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like hirata and karuizawa    the only mention of her in the second half of chapter 4  and it is a comparator other students are measured against  after her p 83 exclusion from the witness interview she has no scene  no line and no decision in chapter 4","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p120-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p120-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.7: she survives in the volume as a standard, not a participant<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;It seemed like many students were striving every day to couple up like Hirata and Karuizawa.&quot; — the only mention of her in the second half of Chapter 4, and it is a comparator other students are measured against.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After her p.83 exclusion from the witness interview she has no scene, no line and no decision in Chapter 4.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v2-p66-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.0 &amp; sec. 4.2: she wants Class A out loud, and is judged too blunt for Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p121-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 4 sec  4 7  she tries to dodge a confession and is made to give it  huh  oh  yeah  kind of    that someone has confessed to her   well  if you re okay with it  can you spare a little time after class  i have some questions about confessions  i know all too well how busy you are with the incident right now  but   but you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate  right    class b is tracking class d s movements on the sudo case   i ll be waiting at the school entrance after class   i was a little worried about finding ichinose  but my anxieties quickly disappeared  she stood out even in this sea of students  his attempt at a definition of her popularity   i could only describe it as an intoxicating  gentle power  a power that was amplified by how many of the first year students recognized her  it was similar to kushida  but even more so  and  ichinose was popular with boys and girls alike  they greeted her one after another   ah  ayanokouji kun  over here  over here   i plan to finish this as soon as possible  follow me  she has already chosen the place and already knows what will happen there   i think someone will confess their feelings to me here  she said   love is kind of alien to me  i don t how to respond without hurting her feelings  i also don t know if we can stay good friends afterwards  i want you to help me    the missing word is the translation s  kept as printed   the person confessing her feelings to me is from class b   i d like for you to keep this secret  if not  things will probably get unpleasant  knowing you  ayanokouji kun  i doubt you ll go around telling people   huh  n no way  not at all  i ve never experienced this before     if she hadn t told me herself  i absolutely would not have believed it   so will you please pretend to be my boyfriend   i did a bit of research  and discovered that the rejected person hurts less if the object of their affection is already in a relationship   i could say that you and i broke up  or that you left me or something  the plan fails the moment it has to be spoken   ichinose probably meant to say that yes  yes i was  but guilt over lying seemed to stopper her answer  the words got stuck in her throat  his discovery of the weak point behind the office   i d expected ichinose to be a stalwart  reliable person  but apparently she had an unexpected weak point  and  ichinose  seeing chihiro s tears  grew flustered  uncertain of what to do  she started panicking   this is ayanokouji kun  from class d  i m sorry for bringing someone that you don t know  chihiro chan   so  ayanokouji kun  he s  well  he s my    the sentence he cuts off   i was wrong  i didn t respect chihiro chan s feelings  i just wanted to avoid hurting her  and to run away  that was my mistake  love is really tough  huh     ichinose muttered as she leaned against the handrail next to me   i asked her if we could carry on like usual  but  i don t know if we can go back to how things were   yeah  thanks for today  for coming along with me for such an odd request   i guess our positions got reversed  huh  i planned on helping you  but then you ended up helping me   there s no need for you to apologize  ayanokouji kun  none at all   now it s my turn to help you  if there s anything i can do  i will  she goes back and tells the truth anyway  the only account of the aftermath is his   i wondered how class b s ichinose honami planned to resolve this difficult situation  one morning walk  one aborted lie  one promise to help him in return   the volume s only relationship that starts by asking him for something that is not information  chihiro is named only in this scene  a class b girl who writes a love letter with a heart sticker and arranges to be confessed to in person behind the gymnasium  no surname  no other appearance in this volume","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p121-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p121-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.7: she tries to dodge a confession and is made to give it<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.121–127<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She has already chosen the place and already knows what will happen there: &quot;I think someone will confess their feelings to me here,&quot; she said.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Huh? Oh, yeah. Kind of.&quot; — that someone has confessed to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Well, if you’re okay with it, can you spare a little time after class? I have some questions about confessions. I know all too well how busy you are with the incident right now, but…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;But you went to the scene of the crime the other day to investigate, right?&quot; — Class B is tracking Class D&#x27;s movements on the Sudō case.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll be waiting at the school entrance after class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;I was a little worried about finding Ichinose, but my anxieties quickly disappeared. She stood out even in this sea of students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> His attempt at a definition of her popularity: &quot;I could only describe it as an intoxicating, gentle power. A power that was amplified by how many of the first-year students recognized her. It was similar to Kushida, but even more so.&quot; and &quot;Ichinose was popular with boys and girls alike. They greeted her one after another.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah. Ayanokouji-kun. Over here, over here!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I plan to finish this as soon as possible. Follow me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Love is kind of alien to me. I don’t how to respond without hurting her feelings. I also don’t know if we can stay good friends afterwards. I want you to help me.&quot; — the missing word is the translation&#x27;s, kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The person confessing her feelings to me…is from Class B.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’d like for you to keep this secret. If not, things will probably get unpleasant. Knowing you, Ayanokouji-kun, I doubt you’ll go around telling people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh?! N-no way. Not at all! I’ve never experienced this before.&quot; — &quot;If she hadn’t told me herself, I absolutely would not have believed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So…will you please pretend to be my boyfriend?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I did a bit of research, and discovered that the rejected person hurts less if the object of their affection is already in a relationship…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I could say that you and I broke up, or that you left me or something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan fails the moment it has to be spoken: &quot;Ichinose probably meant to say that yes, yes I was. But guilt over lying seemed to stopper her answer. The words got stuck in her throat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> His discovery of the weak point behind the office: &quot;I’d expected Ichinose to be a stalwart, reliable person, but apparently she had an unexpected weak point.&quot; and &quot;Ichinose, seeing Chihiro’s tears, grew flustered. Uncertain of what to do, she started panicking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is Ayanokouji-kun, from Class D. I’m sorry for bringing someone that you don’t know, Chihiro-chan.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, Ayanokouji-kun, he’s… Well, he’s my—&quot; — the sentence he cuts off.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was wrong. I didn’t respect Chihiro-chan’s feelings. I just wanted to avoid hurting her, and to run away. That was my mistake. Love is really tough, huh?&quot; — &quot;Ichinose muttered as she leaned against the handrail next to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I asked her if we could carry on like usual, but… I don’t know if we can go back to how things were.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah… Thanks for today. For coming along with me for such an odd request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess our positions got reversed, huh? I planned on helping you, but then you ended up helping me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s no need for you to apologize, Ayanokouji-kun. None at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Now it’s my turn to help you. If there’s anything I can do, I will.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She goes back and tells the truth anyway; the only account of the aftermath is his: &quot;I wondered how Class B’s Ichinose Honami planned to resolve this difficult situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> One morning walk, one aborted lie, one promise to help him in return — the volume&#x27;s only relationship that starts by asking him for something that is not information.<span class=\"pg\">p.116–127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chihiro is named only in this scene: a Class B girl who writes a love letter with a heart sticker and arranges to be confessed to in person behind the gymnasium. No surname, no other appearance in this volume.<span class=\"pg\">p.125–127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school, and what she thinks the class system is hiding<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: a message board, a leaked past, and a screen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 7  he refuses to be the lie in someone else s confession  so  what should i do next   no way  did ichinose plan to confess to me    the misread the section is built on  corrected in the next line by her  i think someone will confess their feelings to me here   wouldn t it be better if i weren t here   i don t really think i m the person to ask for this  i don t have any experience with romantic confessions  there are probably other people in class b who could help   but ichinose  aren t you used to people confessing their feelings to you   i understand that you don t want to hurt anyone  but won t it be worse if they find out you lied   honestly  i think it would be much better for you to talk with this person one on one  truthfully   i m just a friend     i cut ichinose off before she could finish   ichinose  i didn t think this was something i should say  considering no one s ever confessed to me before  but i think it was a mistake for you to call me here     i spoke honestly  for both their sakes  the lecture on confession   it s true that confessing your feelings isn t easy to do  you spend every day in complete anguish  as you create the experience in your head over and over  and yet  you still can t confess your feelings  even when you think the time has come to actually do it  you can t say the words  i like you  they get stuck in your throat  that s what i think  don t you think you should answer someone when they desperately long to express their feelings  if you make the situation unclear  both of you may regret it later   trying to prevent someone s pain was useless  if you turned someone down  their feelings would inevitably be hurt  and then  even more hurt if the excuse were built on a lie   i left without waiting for ichinose s reply   that depends on you both   i m sorry for acting so full of myself back there     i said   i wondered how class b s ichinose honami planned to resolve this difficult situation  i had to admit  i was looking forward to seeing it  the one extended piece of sincere moral advice he gives all volume is about someone else s confession  delivered to a girl who did not ask for it  and followed by walking away before the answer arrives","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.123–127<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;So, what should I do next?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Wouldn’t it be better if I weren’t here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t really think I’m the person to ask for this. I don’t have any experience with romantic confessions. There are probably other people in Class B who could help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;No way… Did Ichinose plan to confess to me?!&quot; — the misread the section is built on, corrected in the next line by her &quot;I think someone will confess their feelings to me here&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But Ichinose, aren’t you used to people confessing their feelings to you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand that you don’t want to hurt anyone, but won’t it be worse if they find out you lied?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Honestly, I think it would be much better for you to talk with this person one-on-one. Truthfully.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m just a friend.&quot; — &quot;I cut Ichinose off before she could finish.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ichinose. I didn’t think this was something I should say, considering no one’s ever confessed to me before. But I think it was a mistake for you to call me here.&quot; — &quot;I spoke honestly, for both their sakes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The lecture on confession: &quot;It’s true that confessing your feelings isn’t easy to do. You spend every day in complete anguish, as you create the experience in your head over and over. And yet, you still can’t confess your feelings. Even when you think the time has come to actually do it, you can’t say the words ‘I like you’. They get stuck in your throat. That’s what I think. Don’t you think you should answer someone when they desperately long to express their feelings? If you make the situation unclear, both of you may regret it later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Trying to prevent someone’s pain was useless. If you turned someone down, their feelings would inevitably be hurt.&quot; and then &quot;Even more hurt if the excuse were built on a lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I left without waiting for Ichinose’s reply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That depends on you both.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry for acting so full of myself back there,&quot; — &quot;I said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered how Class B’s Ichinose Honami planned to resolve this difficult situation. I had to admit, I was looking forward to seeing it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The one extended piece of sincere moral advice he gives all volume is about someone else&#x27;s confession, delivered to a girl who did not ask for it, and followed by walking away before the answer arrives.<span class=\"pg\">p.126–127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: walking to school with Class B&#x27;s representative<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 8  the first call she makes to him  and the silence she cannot finish  caller id displayed the name  kushida kikyou  i did a double take to make sure of what i saw  knowing i wouldn t have the guts to call her back  i rolled my chair across the room  snatched my phone off the stand  and dove onto the bed   i don t think you should feel responsible  kushida  not in the least  besides  she s going to get it fixed  right  since it s so important to her  wouldn t she get it repaired no matter what  he corrects his own answer mid call   however  as i spoke i realized it probably wasn t that simple  and  it was probably similar to how someone might feel about dining alone in a restaurant   do you want me to ask if she knows anything about sudou s incident   kushida had probably chosen me through the process of elimination  as i was the least harmful candidate  if she d invited ike or yamauchi along  they would have had eyes only for kushida   okay  i understand  let s go     my voice cracked with a little too much excitement   it was proof that she could invade my personal space without causing discomfort  in my mind  i d firmly recognized her as my friend  his real opinion of horikita s singularity  withheld   horikita wasn t special  she belonged to a unique class of people  i kept quiet  though  afraid that if i badmouthed her she d find out about it   when i think of my relationship with horikita  it s like there s a wall between us  or perhaps i should say that s the extent of our relationship  if you understand what i m getting at   ah  that reminds me  i wanted to ask you something  your room is on the ninth floor  right  kushida   oh  no reason  just curious   ah  if only i were a pretty boy with excellent communication skills  i couldn t help but wish for that   it s getting late  should i hang up now     i asked  unable to bear the silence  his self assessment on the edge of her almost sentence   sorry  kushida  if i were on the battlefield  i d be the sniper  the chicken who would stay far away from the fighting  forgive me  one modest reply in this call carries no speaker tag in the translation and is not assigned here  after kushida credits  you and hirata  for class d coming together  an unattributed voice disowns any specialness and is answered   i think hirata would definitely say the same thing  she calls him first  late  to ask a favour  he reports her near confession and does not ask her to finish it   i lacked the courage to say  and  to her  so i let it go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.128–131<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Caller ID displayed the name: Kushida Kikyou. I did a double take to make sure of what I saw. Knowing I wouldn’t have the guts to call her back, I rolled my chair across the room, snatched my phone off the stand, and dove onto the bed.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I don’t think you should feel responsible, Kushida. Not in the least. Besides, she’s going to get it fixed, right? Since it’s so important to her, wouldn’t she get it repaired no matter what?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Do you want me to ask if she knows anything about Sudou’s incident?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Okay, I understand. Let’s go.&quot; — &quot;My voice cracked with a little too much excitement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He corrects his own answer mid-call: &quot;However, as I spoke I realized it probably wasn’t that simple.&quot; and &quot;It was probably similar to how someone might feel about dining alone in a restaurant.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Kushida had probably chosen me through the process of elimination, as I was the least harmful candidate. If she’d invited Ike or Yamauchi along, they would have had eyes only for Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;It was proof that she could invade my personal space without causing discomfort. In my mind, I’d firmly recognized her as my friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His real opinion of Horikita&#x27;s singularity, withheld: &quot;Horikita wasn’t special. She belonged to a unique class of people. I kept quiet, though, afraid that if I badmouthed her she’d find out about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When I think of my relationship with Horikita, it’s like there’s a wall between us. Or perhaps I should say that’s the extent of our relationship, if you understand what I’m getting at.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, that reminds me. I wanted to ask you something. Your room is on the ninth floor, right, Kushida?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no reason. Just curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Ah, if only I were a pretty boy with excellent communication skills. I couldn’t help but wish for that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s getting late. Should I hang up now?&quot; — &quot;I asked, unable to bear the silence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His self-assessment on the edge of her almost-sentence: &quot;Sorry, Kushida. If I were on the battlefield, I’d be the sniper, the chicken who would stay far away from the fighting. Forgive me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> One modest reply in this call carries no speaker tag in the translation and is not assigned here: after Kushida credits &quot;you and Hirata&quot; for Class D coming together, an unattributed voice disowns any specialness and is answered, &quot;I think Hirata would definitely say the same thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129–130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She calls him first, late, to ask a favour; he reports her near-confession and does not ask her to finish it: &quot;I lacked the courage to say&quot; and &quot;to her, so I let it go.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128–131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p123-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: he refuses to be the lie in someone else&#x27;s confession<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4 sec  4 8  she phones him at night  and cannot finish what she starts the first time she reaches him unbidden  after ten   i m sorry for calling you so late  you re still up  she asked   sakura san s digital camera was broken  right  i feel like i m partially to blame since i made her so flustered  so i wanted to take responsibility for that   yeah  she seemed hesitant at first  but then said that she d be fine with the day after tomorrow  i think that sakura s digital camera is probably really important to her   if we were just going to get it repaired  i suppose  but  there s another thing  i d like your help with it  ayanokouji kun  what horikita has concluded  carried by the one person horikita will not speak to   horikita san seems convinced that sakura saw everything  after getting a bit closer to sakura san  i also think she knows something  but there has to be some reason why she s keeping quiet  since she keeps denying that she witnessed it   that reminds me  it was really scary when kouenji kun and sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting    printed as one word  kept as the translation has it   i couldn t even move  hirata kun was so amazing  though   class d was able to come together  thanks to you and hirata  the fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part  too   speaking of special  don t you think that horikita san is way more special than someone like me  she s great at studying and excels at sports  it makes me wonder why she s in class d   but doesn t she behave normally with you  ayanokouji kun   huh  ah  yeah  it is  why  what about it    he has asked whether her room is on the ninth floor  her gift with the class s outliers  described from the outside   kushida had done a wonderful job taking the proper first steps to earn sakura s trust  the only silence the volume records her in   suddenly  kushida fell silent  it was unexpected silence  without warning  our conversation  which had been smooth up until now  came to a screeching halt  she starts a confession three times and stops   hey  then  i if  well  i  i  then  no  it s nothing    and the recorder s verdict   that sure didn t seem like nothing   well  i ll see you the day after tomorrow  ayanokouji kun    the call s last line  with the unfinished one still in the air  she is the only classmate who tests his account of horikita instead of accepting it   and his reaction to being read is discomfort rather than deflection   i didn t like being misunderstood by kushida  she hesitates immediately after being asked for her floor number  and the volume never says whether the two are connected  what is recorded is only the sequence  the question  the halt  the swallowed sentence  the goodbye","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.128–131<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The first time she reaches him unbidden, after ten: &quot;I’m sorry for calling you so late. You’re still up?&quot; she asked.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Sakura-san’s digital camera was broken, right? I feel like I’m partially to blame since I made her so flustered. So I wanted to take responsibility for that…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Yeah. She seemed hesitant at first, but then said that she’d be fine with the day after tomorrow. I think that Sakura’s digital camera is probably really important to her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;If we were just going to get it repaired, I suppose. But, there’s another thing. I’d like your help with it, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> What Horikita has concluded, carried by the one person Horikita will not speak to: &quot;Horikita-san seems convinced that Sakura saw everything. After getting a bit closer to Sakura-san, I also think she knows something. But there has to be some reason why she’s keeping quiet, since she keeps denying that she witnessed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That reminds me. It was really scary when Kouenji-kun and Sudoukun looked like they were about to start fighting.&quot; — printed as one word; kept as the translation has it.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I couldn’t even move. Hirata-kun was so amazing, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Class D was able to come together, thanks to you and Hirata. The fact that the boys and girls are separated plays a big part, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Speaking of special, don’t you think that Horikita-san is way more special than someone like me? She’s great at studying and excels at sports. It makes me wonder why she’s in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But doesn’t she behave normally with you, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? Ah, yeah, it is. Why? What about it?&quot; — he has asked whether her room is on the ninth floor.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her gift with the class&#x27;s outliers, described from the outside: &quot;Kushida had done a wonderful job taking the proper first steps to earn Sakura’s trust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The only silence the volume records her in: &quot;Suddenly, Kushida fell silent. It was unexpected silence, without warning. Our conversation, which had been smooth up until now, came to a screeching halt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She starts a confession three times and stops: &quot;Hey—&quot; then &quot;I-If… Well… I… I—&quot; then &quot;No, it’s nothing.&quot; — and the recorder&#x27;s verdict: &quot;That sure didn’t seem like nothing…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’ll see you the day after tomorrow, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — the call&#x27;s last line, with the unfinished one still in the air.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only classmate who tests his account of Horikita instead of accepting it — and his reaction to being read is discomfort rather than deflection: &quot;I didn’t like being misunderstood by Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.130–131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She hesitates immediately after being asked for her floor number, and the volume never says whether the two are connected. What is recorded is only the sequence: the question, the halt, the swallowed sentence, the goodbye.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p86-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.2–4.3: the approach fails in front of the whole class<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 4 sec  4 8  sec  4 11  he is a category in someone else s phone etiquette he is ruled out of kushida s errand before it is offered   if she d invited ike or yamauchi along  they would have had eyes only for kushida  in the narrator s ranking of callers he is in the call back later tier   if it were ike or yamauchi  i d call them back later  but if it were horikita i d have to think about it  he has no scene of his own in the second half of chapter 4  both mentions are the class s assumptions about him rather than anything he does","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.8, sec. 4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.129, p.148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is ruled out of Kushida&#x27;s errand before it is offered: &quot;If she’d invited Ike or Yamauchi along, they would have had eyes only for Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> In the narrator&#x27;s ranking of callers he is in the call-back-later tier: &quot;If it were Ike or Yamauchi, I’d call them back later. But if it were Horikita…I’d have to think about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He has no scene of his own in the second half of Chapter 4; both mentions are the class&#x27;s assumptions about him rather than anything he does.<span class=\"pg\">p.129–148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p79-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he has the only confident opinion of Sakura, and it is invented<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the magazine fight<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 9 4 10  the mall  and the form he fills in himself  our back and forth felt like the template for a date   seeing kushida in casual attire for the first time was so overwhelming  i couldn t look away  the gathering he was not told about   last week  really glad i came despite that  what the heck was she talking about  and  this was the first i d heard about it  i didn t recall any previous  hidden event   i looked up to the heavens and lamented my worthlessness  it s not like ike and the others were bad for not inviting me  i was the bad guy  the one who hadn t been invited   don t worry about it  really  i don t care  was it fun   i think we ve had really nice weather lately     worried that we were heading into cliched territory  i steered the conversation in another direction   ah  sorry  i think i might look a little out of place next to you   so  you re saying someone simple like me is a good match for you  i should accept an insult like that   i felt the quick thrust of a knife  maybe i d dug my own grave by setting myself up like that  but it was still a shock   perhaps it was love at first sight   no  i don t think you blend in too much  i definitely felt your presence   had sakura really been sitting there the entire time  amazing that we hadn t noticed her at all  not a sign of her presence or aura   because kushida didn t show any signs of disliking the conversation  he probably thought he could successfully ask her out  however  i believed she would try her hardest to sidestep the invitation  what he sees and neither girl does   both sakura and kushida were looking down at the form  so they didn t notice  but the clerk had unsettling eyes  even men would find it a little creepy   can i see that for a second   when the repairs are finished  please contact me   the manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase  also  i doubt there d be any legal problems with me putting my information down  it should be perfectly fine if the user s name is different than the purchaser s   or  is there a reason why she specifically has to enter her information   if that s all it takes to please you  then it actually makes me sorry for you   well  you re making it out to be bigger than it was  honestly  i was only watching out for that rather weird clerk  i guess he gave the impression that he really  really loved girls   although my imagination ran wild  i couldn t let it show on my face  i had to remain neutral  the question about whether sakura photographs people carries no speaker tag and is not assigned  only her refusal and his report of it are recorded   it sounded like she didn t want to go into the details with me   hey professor  do you have a minute   professor  did you buy your laptop computer from the school  with your points   i m looking for something     i explained the gist of what i wanted  although many similar products sat on the displays in front of me  i didn t know which one to choose  why he phones a classmate instead of the clerk   it probably would ve been faster to just ask the store clerk  but i didn t want to for various reasons   sotomura s nickname was professor  which undoubtedly made it sound like he was rather intelligent  in reality  he was just a huge otaku  he gathered information daily  comprehensively spanning a wide variety of topics  from dating sims to anime and manga   today was just a preliminary inspection  i don t have enough points to buy anything   when entering a subject that i didn t understand  it was important to find an expert  the object he is shopping for is not named in chapter 4  it is described only as something with  many similar products  on the display  the visit is booked as a  preliminary inspection  and the purchase is deferred for lack of points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;Our back and forth felt like the template for a date.&quot; The question about whether Sakura photographs people carries no speaker tag and is not assigned; only her refusal and his report of it are recorded: &quot;It sounded like she didn’t want to go into the details with me.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Don’t worry about it. Really, I don’t care. Was it fun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I think we’ve had really nice weather lately.&quot; — &quot;Worried that we were heading into clichéd territory, I steered the conversation in another direction.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Ah. Sorry. I think I might look a little out of place next to you,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>25 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Seeing Kushida in casual attire for the first time was so overwhelming, I couldn’t look away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The gathering he was not told about: &quot;Last week? Really glad I came despite that? What the heck was she talking about?&quot; and &quot;This was the first I’d heard about it. I didn’t recall any previous, hidden event.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I looked up to the heavens and lamented my worthlessness. It’s not like Ike and the others were bad for not inviting me. I was the bad guy, the one who hadn’t been invited.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, you’re saying someone simple like me is a good match for you? I should accept an insult like that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I felt the quick thrust of a knife. Maybe I’d dug my own grave by setting myself up like that, but it was still a shock.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps it was love at first sight?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I don’t think you blend in too much. I definitely felt your presence,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Had Sakura really been sitting there the entire time? Amazing that we hadn’t noticed her at all. Not a sign of her presence or aura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Because Kushida didn’t show any signs of disliking the conversation, he probably thought he could successfully ask her out. However, I believed she would try her hardest to sidestep the invitation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he sees and neither girl does: &quot;Both Sakura and Kushida were looking down at the form, so they didn’t notice. But the clerk had unsettling eyes. Even men would find it a little creepy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can I see that for a second?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When the repairs are finished, please contact me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase. Also, I doubt there’d be any legal problems with me putting my information down. It should be perfectly fine if the user’s name is different than the purchaser’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Or, is there a reason why she specifically has to enter her information?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If that’s all it takes to please you, then it actually makes me sorry for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, you’re making it out to be bigger than it was. Honestly, I was only watching out for that rather weird clerk. I guess he gave the impression that he really, really loved girls.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Although my imagination ran wild, I couldn’t let it show on my face. I had to remain neutral.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey Professor, do you have a minute?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Professor, did you buy your laptop computer from the school, with your points?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m looking for something.&quot; — &quot;I explained the gist of what I wanted. Although many similar products sat on the displays in front of me, I didn’t know which one to choose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Why he phones a classmate instead of the clerk: &quot;It probably would’ve been faster to just ask the store clerk, but I didn’t want to for various reasons.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Sotomura’s nickname was Professor, which undoubtedly made it sound like he was rather intelligent. In reality, he was just a huge otaku. He gathered information daily, comprehensively spanning a wide variety of topics, from dating sims to anime and manga.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Today was just a preliminary inspection. I don’t have enough points to buy anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;When entering a subject that I didn’t understand, it was important to find an expert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The object he is shopping for is not named in Chapter 4: it is described only as something with &quot;many similar products&quot; on the display, the visit is booked as a &quot;preliminary inspection&quot;, and the purchase is deferred for lack of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.143–144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: the first call she makes to him, and the silence she cannot finish<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4 sec  4 9 4 10  how she works on someone who cannot be worked on  good morning  and  sorry  were you waiting long   this is the first time we ve met up on a day off  it s refreshing  the opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class   weren t you really busy during your downtime last week  i m glad that you came despite that  ayanokouji kun    then  precisely   i m talking about ike kun and the others going to that cafe  of course   by any chance   i didn t mean anything  i m sorry  i guess i said something wrong    and when he says he does not care   you do seem to care   no  no  that s not true at all  i think we re great together    to his  i think i might look a little out of place next to you   you re that surprisingly delicate  ayanokouji kun  i don t really care what others say  i don t think it s an insult at all  i really think we suit each other   she asked me to invite you  ayanokouji kun  didn t sakura san contact you    sakura s invitation came through kushida  and kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly   right now  how about we sit and wait   let s see  i m sure they have a repair counter somewhere  let s check it out   there it is  the repairs counter   what s the matter  sakura san    she is the only one of the three who asks about sakura s fear out loud  the transaction as an act of translation   kushida s worldly wisdom was certainly impressive  even though it was her first time meeting the store clerk  she was soon talking to him as if they were longtime friends  she reads the clerk s interest and manages it without refusing him   in order to conclude their business  she urged sakura to hand over the camera   that clerk sure was something else  he talked with such incredible passion  i was just so shocked   n no  i wasn t disgusted by him  do you know something  about that clerk    the question that lets sakura say she was afraid   did you know about this  ayanokouji kun     kushida seemed to have an epiphany  she turned to me with wide eyes   you really looked out for sakura san   oh  no need to thank me  and then  sakura san  you really like your camera  don t you   i think being knowledgeable and liking things are separate matters  it s wonderful to be so passionate about something   sakura san  have we met somewhere before     kushida murmured  the ask that sakura refuses   sorry  it s just that when i look at you  i get this feeling that we ve met before  sakura san  hey  weird question  but could you try removing your glasses   we should hang out together again  sakura san  not just with me  but with my other friends  too  her offer of a normal relationship  phrased as a complaint about speech   you can talk to us normally  you know  if it s okay with you  we re in the same grade  it sounds a little weird when you speak so formally to us   it s not really a bad thing  i mean  i d be happy if you didn t speak so formally to me  though   it s okay  though  you don t need to force yourself  the ask that finally gets the witness   so  does that mean that you saw sudou kun fight with those other students  and then  no  we do  why did you decide to tell us now  though  i mean  i m happy you did  but i don t want you to force yourself  you don t have to do this just because you re grateful  you know   is that really true  you re not forcing yourself  kushida asked    the same question twice in one minute  because the first answer was a shake of the head   thank you  sakura san  i m sure sudou kun will be really happy     kushida took sakura s hand  the case the whole class failed to move in three weeks is closed by a hand hold and two refusals to press   i wondered if a new friendship had been born right here  right now  at any rate  we had sudou s witness  she is the only person in class d who gets things done by being with people rather than by being right about them  the volume records her succeeding at exactly the task horikita wrote off as worthless  from a camera knocked over in a classroom  p 90  to a promise to testify in a shopping mall  the whole distance is crossed by kushida refusing to make anything harder than it already is  she recruits him by asking  tests whether he has been left out of his own friend group  and lets him fill in a form  he is her one witness that she is capable of a plain conversation  her instinct to close on sakura stops short of the truth  she asks about the glasses  gets refused  and  kushida seemed to feel that it would make trouble if she pressed the issue  so she kept quiet  or rather  she didn t ask anything else","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–145<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Good morning!&quot; and &quot;Sorry. Were you waiting long?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;This is the first time we’ve met up on a day off. It’s refreshing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and…<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>32 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The opening test of whether he has been excluded from his own class: &quot;Weren’t you really busy during your downtime last week? I’m glad that you came despite that, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — then, precisely: &quot;I’m talking about Ike-kun and the others going to that café, of course.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;By any chance…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn’t mean anything… I’m sorry, I guess I said something wrong…&quot; — and when he says he does not care: &quot;You do seem to care…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, no, that’s not true at all. I think we’re great together,&quot; — to his &quot;I think I might look a little out of place next to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re that surprisingly delicate, Ayanokouji-kun? I don’t really care what others say. I don’t think it’s an insult at all. I really think we suit each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She asked me to invite you, Ayanokouji-kun. Didn’t Sakura-san contact you?&quot; — Sakura&#x27;s invitation came through Kushida, and Kushida did not know he had not been contacted directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Right now, how about we sit and wait?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Let’s see, I’m sure they have a repair counter somewhere. Let’s check it out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There it is! The repairs counter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s the matter, Sakura-san?&quot; — she is the only one of the three who asks about Sakura&#x27;s fear out loud.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The transaction as an act of translation: &quot;Kushida’s worldly wisdom was certainly impressive. Even though it was her first time meeting the store clerk, she was soon talking to him as if they were longtime friends.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She reads the clerk&#x27;s interest and manages it without refusing him: &quot;In order to conclude their business, she urged Sakura to hand over the camera.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That clerk sure was something else. He talked with such incredible passion, I was just so shocked,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, I wasn’t disgusted by him. Do you know something? About that clerk?&quot; — the question that lets Sakura say she was afraid.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did you know about this, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot; — &quot;Kushida seemed to have an epiphany. She turned to me with wide eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You really looked out for Sakura-san,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no need to thank me.&quot; and then &quot;Sakura-san, you really like your camera. Don’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think being knowledgeable and liking things are separate matters. It’s wonderful to be so passionate about something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, have we met somewhere before?&quot; — &quot;Kushida murmured.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that Sakura refuses: &quot;Sorry. It’s just that when I look at you, I get this feeling that we’ve met before, Sakura-san. Hey, weird question, but could you try removing your glasses?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We should hang out together again, Sakura-san. Not just with me, but with my other friends, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her offer of a normal relationship, phrased as a complaint about speech: &quot;you can talk to us normally, you know? If it’s okay with you. We’re in the same grade. It sounds a little weird when you speak so formally to us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s not really a bad thing! I mean, I’d be happy if you didn’t speak so formally to me, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s okay, though. You don’t need to force yourself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The ask that finally gets the witness: &quot;So, does that mean that you saw Sudou-kun fight with those other students?&quot; and then &quot;No, we do. Why did you decide to tell us now, though? I mean, I’m happy you did, but I don’t want you to force yourself. You don’t have to do this just because you’re grateful, you know?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that really true? You’re not forcing yourself?&quot; Kushida asked. — the same question twice in one minute, because the first answer was a shake of the head.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san. I’m sure Sudou-kun will be really happy.&quot; — &quot;Kushida took Sakura’s hand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The case the whole class failed to move in three weeks is closed by a hand-hold and two refusals to press: &quot;I wondered if a new friendship had been born right here, right now. At any rate, we had Sudou’s witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She is the only person in Class D who gets things done by being with people rather than by being right about them; the volume records her succeeding at exactly the task Horikita wrote off as worthless.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> From a camera knocked over in a classroom (p.90) to a promise to testify in a shopping mall: the whole distance is crossed by Kushida refusing to make anything harder than it already is.<span class=\"pg\">p.138–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She recruits him by asking, tests whether he has been left out of his own friend group, and lets him fill in a form; he is her one witness that she is capable of a plain conversation.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her instinct to close on Sakura stops short of the truth: she asks about the glasses, gets refused, and &quot;Kushida seemed to feel that it would make trouble if she pressed the issue, so she kept quiet. Or rather, she didn’t ask anything else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p128-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.8: she phones him at night, and cannot finish what she starts<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4 sec  4 9 4 10  she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter she has already arrived and is unnoticed at her own meeting   had sakura really been sitting there the entire time  amazing that we hadn t noticed her at all  not a sign of her presence or aura   i m sorry  i don t stand out much  i suppose  good morning    the first line she speaks aloud in the volume  and she apologises for it before it is needed   oh  you don t need to say that for my sake  ayanokouji kun    his compliment that he felt her presence is declined  her chosen disguise  as read by the boy who has never seen her before   sakura was wearing a hat  and even a surgical face mask  which made it difficult to recognize her at a glance  and  she didn t seem to have a cold  rather  she seemed like the type to wear the mask in order to avoid attention  she must have really hated standing out   yeah  i suppose so  i think i do stand out  especially here    and the mask comes off   sheepishly  she removed her mask   so anyway  about my digital camera  is it okay if we go to the electronics store in the mall    the ask that opens the day  and it is hers   i wonder if they ll fix it right away     sakura  looked rather anxious as she took out her digital camera and held it tight   yeah  it s weird  isn t it    on being asked whether she loves the camera  the repair counter stops her cold in front of two classmates   for some reason  sakura suddenly stopped in her tracks  when i glanced over at her  i noticed she was wearing an expression of blatant fear and revulsion   ah  umm  well  and then  it s nothing     she donned an earnest smile  and walked to the repair counter  kushida takes the entire transaction   sakura  the camera s owner  spoke only when she needed to give her consent or to clarify something  what the camera actually is  technically   when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents  he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall  that was why the camera wouldn t turn on properly  fortunately  because sakura still had the warranty card  the item could be repaired free of charge    the contents are never described  the cost of having her address written down by someone else   sakura gently patted her chest and sighed in apparent relief  but when she learned it d take two weeks for the camera to be repaired  she grew discouraged  her shoulders slumped   didn t you feel kind of disgusted    to kushida  about the clerk  the first time she questions someone else s reading of a room   that was kind of what i was trying to get at before  i was scared to go to the repair shop alone because of that  she turns to the quietest of the three for a verdict on a man who frightened her   turning to me  she asked  and then  what do you think  ayanokouji kun   th thank you ayanokouji kun  you really saved me   since you were with me today  kushida san  we completed our task without me having to talk at all  thank you  the camera s history  given unprompted   yeah  i ve liked cameras ever since i was little  my dad bought me one before i entered junior high  and i absolutely fell in love with it  or i suppose you could say that i just love taking pictures  i m not really wellinformed when it comes to this stuff  though    the missing hyphen is the translation s  the one question that makes her physically retreat   sakura stepped backwards  looking quite flustered  then  sakura shut her mouth  and her body stiffened  and  th that s a secret   w well  it s just  it s embarrassing     replied sakura  her cheeks reddening  she looked down as she spoke  whether she photographs people is asked but not answered in this volume  and the asker is not tagged in the translation  only her refusal is hers","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.132–142<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She has already arrived and is unnoticed at her own meeting: &quot;Had Sakura really been sitting there the entire time? Amazing that we hadn’t noticed her at all. Not a sign of her presence or aura.&quot; What the camera actually is, technically: &quot;when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents, he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall. That was why the camera wouldn’t turn on properly. Fortunately, because Sakura still had the warranty card, the item could be repaired free of charge.&quot; — the contents are never described. She turns to the quietest of the three for a verdict on a man who frightened her: &quot;Turning to me, she asked&quot; and then &quot;What do you think, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I’m sorry, I don’t stand out much, I suppose… Good morning,&quot; — the first line she speaks aloud in the volume, and she apologises for it before it is needed.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Oh, you don’t need to say that for my sake, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot; — his compliment that he felt her presence is declined.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Yeah, I suppose so. I think I do stand out, especially here,&quot; — and the mask comes off: &quot;Sheepishly, she removed her mask.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>16 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her chosen disguise, as read by the boy who has never seen her before: &quot;Sakura was wearing a hat, and even a surgical face mask, which made it difficult to recognize her at a glance.&quot; and &quot;She didn’t seem to have a cold. Rather, she seemed like the type to wear the mask in order to avoid attention. She must have really hated standing out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So anyway, about my digital camera. Is it okay if we go to the electronics store in the mall?&quot; — the ask that opens the day, and it is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.136<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I wonder if they’ll fix it right away…&quot; — &quot;Sakura, looked rather anxious as she took out her digital camera and held it tight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. It’s weird, isn’t it?&quot; — on being asked whether she loves the camera.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The repair counter stops her cold in front of two classmates: &quot;For some reason, Sakura suddenly stopped in her tracks. When I glanced over at her, I noticed she was wearing an expression of blatant fear and revulsion.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, umm… Well…&quot; and then &quot;It’s nothing.&quot; — &quot;She donned an earnest smile, and walked to the repair counter.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Kushida takes the entire transaction: &quot;Sakura, the camera’s owner, spoke only when she needed to give her consent or to clarify something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The cost of having her address written down by someone else: &quot;Sakura gently patted her chest and sighed in apparent relief, but when she learned it’d take two weeks for the camera to be repaired, she grew discouraged. Her shoulders slumped.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Didn’t you feel kind of disgusted?&quot; — to Kushida, about the clerk; the first time she questions someone else&#x27;s reading of a room.<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That was kind of what I was trying to get at before… I was scared to go to the repair shop alone because of that…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Th-thank you…Ayanokouji-kun. You really…saved me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since you were with me today, Kushida-san, we completed our task without me having to talk at all. Thank you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.141<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The camera&#x27;s history, given unprompted: &quot;Yeah… I’ve liked cameras ever since I was little. My dad bought me one before I entered junior high, and I absolutely fell in love with it. Or I suppose you could say that I just love taking pictures… I’m not really wellinformed when it comes to this stuff, though.&quot; — the missing hyphen is the translation&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The one question that makes her physically retreat: &quot;Sakura stepped backwards, looking quite flustered.&quot; then &quot;Sakura shut her mouth, and her body stiffened.&quot; and &quot;Th-that’s a secret.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;W-well, it’s just… It’s embarrassing,&quot; — &quot;replied Sakura, her cheeks reddening. She looked down as she spoke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whether she photographs people is asked but not answered in this volume, and the asker is not tagged in the translation; only her refusal is hers.<span class=\"pg\">p.142<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p77-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: she is named, and stays a rumour to the people who sit near her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p138-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 10  the shops licensed to the school  and what a warranty is worth  there were some incredibly famous  nationally known stores that did business with our school  even though their customers were only students and the stores themselves weren t too very big  they sold items for everyday use and electronic appliances  the camera s fault  and its cure   when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents  he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall  that was why the camera wouldn t turn on properly  fortunately  because sakura still had the warranty card  the item could be repaired free of charge  the wait  the repair is quoted at two weeks  and chapter 4 ends long before the camera comes back  a student s own account of consumer law  used to shield a classmate from handing over her address   the manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase  also  i doubt there d be any legal problems with me putting my information down  it should be perfectly fine if the user s name is different than the purchaser s  the store accepts it without argument   n no  not at all  i understand  there s nothing to worry about  the clerk said","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p138-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p138-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the shops licensed to the school, and what a warranty is worth<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.138–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> &quot;There were some incredibly famous, nationally known stores that did business with our school. Even though their customers were only students and the stores themselves weren’t too very big, they sold items for everyday use and electronic appliances.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The camera&#x27;s fault, and its cure: &quot;when the store clerk opened up the camera to confirm the contents, he saw that part of it had been damaged from the fall. That was why the camera wouldn’t turn on properly. Fortunately, because Sakura still had the warranty card, the item could be repaired free of charge.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The wait: the repair is quoted at two weeks, and Chapter 4 ends long before the camera comes back.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> A student&#x27;s own account of consumer law, used to shield a classmate from handing over her address: &quot;The manufacturer warranty explicitly shows where the item was sold and the date of purchase. Also, I doubt there’d be any legal problems with me putting my information down. It should be perfectly fine if the user’s name is different than the purchaser’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The store accepts it without argument: &quot;N-no, not at all. I understand. There’s nothing to worry about,&quot; the clerk said.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.6: the first figures any student says out loud<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p143-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: a price a student actually paid<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p143-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 4 sec  4 10  a price a student actually paid the one hard price named by a student in the volume  in the buyer s own words   yes  i most certainly did  it cost 80 000 points  but what of it  that points can be spent on electronics at all is established only by this purchase and by the shopping trip it prompts  no rule about what may be bought  or from which pool  is stated  the narrator s ceiling  stated to the two girls waiting beside him   today was just a preliminary inspection  i don t have enough points to buy anything  the contact is stored in his phone as  sotomura  professor    students trade points and expertise with each other faster than the school explains either  the thing he is price checking is not named in chapter 4  the trip is a preliminary inspection and the purchase is postponed for lack of points","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p143-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p143-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10: a price a student actually paid<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.143–144<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The one hard price named by a student in the volume, in the buyer&#x27;s own words: &quot;Yes, I most certainly did. It cost 80,000 points. But what of it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> That points can be spent on electronics at all is established only by this purchase and by the shopping trip it prompts; no rule about what may be bought, or from which pool, is stated.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s ceiling, stated to the two girls waiting beside him: &quot;Today was just a preliminary inspection. I don’t have enough points to buy anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Detail<\/span> The contact is stored in his phone as &quot;Sotomura (Professor)&quot; — students trade points and expertise with each other faster than the school explains either.<span class=\"pg\">p.143<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The thing he is price-checking is not named in Chapter 4; the trip is a preliminary inspection and the purchase is postponed for lack of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.143–144<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p138-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the shops licensed to the school, and what a warranty is worth<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: paying informants, and paying them anonymously<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4 sec  4 10  she is offered a friendship and answers with the case kushida asks her to take off her glasses and she refuses in front of a stranger s question   huh  b but that s  my eyesight is so bad  i wouldn t be able to see a thing     sakura put her hand up and waved it  signaling to kushida that she did not want to   umm  thank you for everything today  you really helped me out   i didn t mean to sound that way  i wasn t aware of it  i sound weird    on being told she speaks too formally for a classmate   ah  o okay  i i got it  i ll do my best   i it s okay  i will    and the delivery of even that   sakura kept her eyes down as she spoke  partway through her sentence she began to sputter  and her words faded so much that we couldn t hear them  however  it didn t seem as though she felt uncomfortable  she accepts a change in how she talks rather than lose the two people who came with her   i thought that sakura would have rejected the notion  but she managed to squeak out a few words of agreement   well     sakura spoke in a small voice  but looked straight at us  when our gazes met  however  she immediately averted her eyes   about sudou kun  as my way of saying thanks for today  i  well  that might be a little misleading  but if you like   i i may be able to help you with sudou kun s case    the volume s hinge  offered as a gift in exchange for a day of errands   in her own words  sakura told us that she was the witness   yes  i saw everything  it was a total coincidence  though  i m sure you don t believe me  her stated reason for three weeks of silence   it s okay  i think that if i kept quiet  i d probably come to regret it  i don t want to cause trouble for my classmates  but  if i spoke up as a witness  then i would definitely stand out  i hated the thought of that  i m sorry  she apologises while giving the class exactly what it has been asking for   while sakura apologized to us repeatedly  full of remorse  she also promised kushida that she would testify  everything the case needed was available from her on the first day  what changed is not her courage but her company   she testifies the moment she has two people standing beside her instead of a crowd asking her alone  she tells kushida the camera history  refuses kushida the glasses  and hands kushida the testimony   the friendship is real before the evidence is  he wrote his own name and dorm room on her repair form so she would not have to hand over her address  her first unscheduled call is to him  not to kushida","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.144–146<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Kushida asks her to take off her glasses and she refuses in front of a stranger&#x27;s question: &quot;Huh?! B-but that’s… My eyesight is so bad, I wouldn’t be able to see a thing…&quot; — &quot;Sakura put her hand up and waved it, signaling to Kushida that she did not want to.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Umm… Thank you for everything today. You really helped me out,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I didn’t mean to sound that way. I wasn’t aware of it… I sound weird?&quot; — on being told she speaks too formally for a classmate.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Ah… O-okay… I…I got it. I’ll do my best.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-It’s okay. I…will.&quot; — and the delivery of even that: &quot;Sakura kept her eyes down as she spoke. Partway through her sentence she began to sputter, and her words faded so much that we couldn’t hear them. However, it didn’t seem as though she felt uncomfortable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She accepts a change in how she talks rather than lose the two people who came with her: &quot;I thought that Sakura would have rejected the notion, but she managed to squeak out a few words of agreement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well!&quot; — &quot;Sakura spoke in a small voice, but looked straight at us. When our gazes met, however, she immediately averted her eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;About Sudou-kun… As my way of saying thanks for today, I… Well, that might be a little misleading, but if you like…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-I may be able to help you with Sudou-kun’s case.&quot; — the volume&#x27;s hinge, offered as a gift in exchange for a day of errands: &quot;In her own words, Sakura told us that she was the witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yes. I saw everything. It was a total coincidence, though… I’m sure you don’t believe me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her stated reason for three weeks of silence: &quot;It’s okay… I think that if I kept quiet, I’d probably come to regret it. I…don’t want to cause trouble for my classmates. But, if I spoke up as a witness, then…I would definitely stand out. I hated the thought of that… I’m sorry.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She apologises while giving the class exactly what it has been asking for; &quot;While Sakura apologized to us repeatedly, full of remorse, she also promised Kushida that she would testify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Everything the case needed was available from her on the first day; what changed is not her courage but her company — she testifies the moment she has two people standing beside her instead of a crowd asking her alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.132–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> She tells Kushida the camera history, refuses Kushida the glasses, and hands Kushida the testimony — the friendship is real before the evidence is.<span class=\"pg\">p.142, p.144–146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He wrote his own name and dorm room on her repair form so she would not have to hand over her address; her first unscheduled call is to him, not to Kushida.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: she lets two people take a camera to a repair counter<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\">→ After: Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4 sec  4 10 4 11  the wall around sakura  and the call that goes nowhere  perhaps this was how people became friends  little by little  even sakura  who seemed to have hardly interacted with another person ever  was steadily growing closer to kushida  his stated theory of how to reach an unsociable person  in the same breath as kushida s practice of it   if you tried to strong arm people who weren t good at socializing  it could backfire  rather than be grateful  they d probably find it off putting  rather than draw them nearer  being overbearing would probably end up pushing them further away   the fact that sakura had waited until now to talk proved that she was more concerned about sudou s case than anything else  i wondered if getting a foothold on friendship made her want to cooperate   i wondered if a new friendship had been born right here  right now  at any rate  we had sudou s witness   that reminds me  why did you try to get sakura to take off her glasses     i asked kushida   back when her camera fell and sakura had bent down to pick it up  i d seen her glasses from the side  something about them had struck me as being out of place   i felt like there s something a little off  like she s wearing fake glasses   although real glasses and fake ones appear similar at first glance  there is definitely a difference between them  real glasses show some distortion on the lenses  there wasn t any distortion on sakura s glasses   or maybe it s to cover up some kind of complex  like how someone thinks they ll appear intelligent by putting on glasses   in sakura s case  though  she probably wears them because she doesn t want others to see her true self  she s always slouching and won t look people in the eye  i doubt it s simply because she dislikes other people   i felt like there was some hidden way to get over that wall  something  his caller priority rule  stated in full   if it were ike or yamauchi  i d call them back later  but if it were horikita i d have to think about it   i answered sakura s call before it cut out   even when i formally exchanged contact information with someone  nine times out of ten i wouldn t get a call   what should i do  please  hirata  teach me   something about the emotion behind her words made me uneasy  so i cast a verbal line to see if i could reel in anything else  however  the line tautened and snapped as soon as it touched water   did something happen  he remembers kushida s morning wording  and remembers it wrongly   i was asked to invite you as well  ayanokouji kun  did you talk to sakura san    what she actually said at the mall was  she asked me to invite you  ayanokouji kun  the only thing he contributed that day  by his own inventory   sakura and kushida struck up most of the conversations  but i d broached a topic  namely  the clerk at the store who d helped with the repair order  i hadn t brought up anything else   all of the puzzle pieces i d collected were too small  and too few  i was able to conjure up several scenarios and speculations  but they all lacked credibility  i didn t have enough information to come to a definitive decision  why he will not simply go and ask her   if i just went up and started talking to sakura  who normally didn t talk to anyone  it would make her stand out  she wouldn t like that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.145–151<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">&quot;I answered Sakura’s call before it cut out.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;That reminds me, why did you try to get Sakura to take off her glasses?&quot; — &quot;I asked Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I felt like there’s something a little off, like she’s wearing fake glasses.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Although real glasses and fake ones appear similar at first glance, there is definitely a difference between them. Real glasses show some distortion on the lenses. There wasn’t any distortion on Sakura’s glasses.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Perhaps this was how people became friends, little by little. Even Sakura, who seemed to have hardly interacted with another person ever, was steadily growing closer to Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His stated theory of how to reach an unsociable person, in the same breath as Kushida&#x27;s practice of it: &quot;If you tried to strong-arm people who weren’t good at socializing, it could backfire. Rather than be grateful, they’d probably find it off-putting. Rather than draw them nearer, being overbearing would probably end up pushing them further away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The fact that Sakura had waited until now to talk proved that she was more concerned about Sudou’s case than anything else. I wondered if getting a foothold on friendship made her want to cooperate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I wondered if a new friendship had been born right here, right now. At any rate, we had Sudou’s witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Back when her camera fell and Sakura had bent down to pick it up, I’d seen her glasses from the side. Something about them had struck me as being out of place.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Or maybe it’s to cover up some kind of complex? Like how someone thinks they’ll appear intelligent by putting on glasses?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In Sakura’s case, though, she probably wears them because she doesn’t want others to see her true self. She’s always slouching and won’t look people in the eye. I doubt it’s simply because she dislikes other people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I felt like there was some hidden way to get over that wall. Something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His caller-priority rule, stated in full: &quot;If it were Ike or Yamauchi, I’d call them back later. But if it were Horikita…I’d have to think about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even when I formally exchanged contact information with someone, nine times out of ten I wouldn’t get a call.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;What should I do? Please, Hirata. Teach me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Something about the emotion behind her words made me uneasy, so I cast a verbal line to see if I could reel in anything else. However, the line tautened and snapped as soon as it touched water.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Did something happen?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He remembers Kushida&#x27;s morning wording, and remembers it wrongly: &quot;I was asked to invite you as well, Ayanokouji-kun. Did you talk to Sakura-san?&quot; — what she actually said at the mall was &quot;She asked me to invite you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The only thing he contributed that day, by his own inventory: &quot;Sakura and Kushida struck up most of the conversations, but I’d broached a topic. Namely, the clerk at the store who’d helped with the repair order. I hadn’t brought up anything else.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;All of the puzzle pieces I’d collected were too small, and too few. I was able to conjure up several scenarios and speculations, but they all lacked credibility. I didn’t have enough information to come to a definitive decision.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Why he will not simply go and ask her: &quot;If I just went up and started talking to Sakura, who normally didn’t talk to anyone, it would make her stand out. She wouldn’t like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: the mall, and the form he fills in himself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p146-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 4 sec  4 10  the witness is secured for him  in a mall  without him the obstacle the whole class failed to move for three weeks clears while he is not in the room   in her own words  sakura told us that she was the witness  what she is promised to him for   thank you  sakura san  i m sure sudou kun will be really happy  by the close of chapter 4 he has a witness  obtained by kushida and ayanokoji over a camera repair  he never asks sakura anything  and the volume does not show him learning that she saw it  the pattern the volume settles  other people s social labour is what saves him  and he is only ever told about it afterwards  as good news","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p146-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p146-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the witness is secured for him, in a mall, without him<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.146<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The obstacle the whole class failed to move for three weeks clears while he is not in the room: &quot;In her own words, Sakura told us that she was the witness.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> What she is promised to him for: &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san. I’m sure Sudou-kun will be really happy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> By the close of Chapter 4 he has a witness, obtained by Kushida and Ayanokōji over a camera repair; he never asks Sakura anything, and the volume does not show him learning that she saw it.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The pattern the volume settles: other people&#x27;s social labour is what saves him, and he is only ever told about it afterwards, as good news.<span class=\"pg\">p.90–146<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p74-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.1: he never claimed a witness, and nobody had understood that<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: told he will be there, and certain of the outcome<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 4 sec  4 11  the same evening  on two calls  we got closer to sakura  but  is it really okay for me to say that    her voice on the phone that night  the translation leaves the reply s speaker untagged and it is not assigned  her reason for the glasses  which turns out not to be a reason   well  i mean  i thought saying so might be kind of cruel  but  i just feel like her glasses don t really suit her  for some reason  it s like she doesn t really need them  or something  i don t understand it myself  i also thought that we d met somewhere before  but that was probably just a misunderstanding   huh  sakura san wears fake glasses  but she said that her eyesight was really bad   appearing fashionable with glasses  hmm  that doesn t sound normal   there s that  wearing glasses does make you look smart   i knew it was right to bring you along  ayanokouji kun  i feel like you re very observant of people   oh  sure  sorry for talking so long    the line she says when he cuts her off to answer sakura   though there was a heavy regret in those parting words  she is asked whether sakura called her and did not receive the call   a few minutes later  kushida confirmed that she hadn t heard back from sakura  the volume leaves sakura s unfinished sentence on one side of the exchange and kushida s unfinished sentence on the other","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.147–150<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;We got closer to Sakura, but… Is it really okay for me to say that?&quot; — her voice on the phone that night; the translation leaves the reply&#x27;s speaker untagged and it is not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really…<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Huh? Sakura-san wears fake glasses? But she said that her eyesight was really bad…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> Her reason for the glasses, which turns out not to be a reason: &quot;Well, I mean… I thought saying so might be kind of cruel, but… I just feel like her glasses don’t really suit her, for some reason. It’s like she doesn’t really need them, or something. I don’t understand it myself. I also thought that we’d met somewhere before, but that was probably just a misunderstanding.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Appearing fashionable with glasses? Hmm, that doesn’t sound normal.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s that. Wearing glasses does make you look smart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I knew it was right to bring you along, Ayanokouji-kun. I feel like you’re very observant of people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, sure. Sorry for talking so long.&quot; — the line she says when he cuts her off to answer Sakura; &quot;Though there was a heavy regret in those parting words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is asked whether Sakura called her and did not receive the call: &quot;A few minutes later, Kushida confirmed that she hadn’t heard back from Sakura.&quot; The volume leaves Sakura&#x27;s unfinished sentence on one side of the exchange and Kushida&#x27;s unfinished sentence on the other.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p132-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.9–4.10: how she works on someone who cannot be worked on<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 4 sec  4 11  the call she cannot finish the name on ayanokoji s screen that night   i answered sakura s call before it cut out   um  hello  this is sakura   thank you for coming out with me today  the only question she asks anyone in the volume   what were you thinking about    his own report of its shape   sakura asked me a rather ambiguous question   i m sorry  it s nothing  goodnight     sakura ended the call without even giving me a chance to reply  no  please wait  or  hold on  her attempt to reach him fails in silence rather than in words  two stretches of quiet  then an apology  then a hang up   and the volume s last sight of her before class d s punishment falls is a girl who tried to say something twice and did not  she did not call kushida either   a few minutes later  kushida confirmed that she hadn t heard back from sakura  whatever she wanted is not in the record  his reading of it is a guess about the store clerk","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\">Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.148–150<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The name on Ayanokōji&#x27;s screen that night: &quot;I answered Sakura’s call before it cut out.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Um… Hello. This is Sakura…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Thank you for coming out with me today,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> The only question she asks anyone in the volume: &quot;What were you…thinking about?&quot; — his own report of its shape: &quot;Sakura asked me a rather ambiguous question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry, it’s nothing. Goodnight.&quot; — &quot;Sakura ended the call without even giving me a chance to reply. No &#x27;please wait&#x27; or &#x27;hold on.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.149<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her attempt to reach him fails in silence rather than in words: two stretches of quiet, then an apology, then a hang-up — and the volume&#x27;s last sight of her before Class D&#x27;s punishment falls is a girl who tried to say something twice and did not.<span class=\"pg\">p.149–150<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She did not call Kushida either: &quot;A few minutes later, Kushida confirmed that she hadn’t heard back from Sakura.&quot; Whatever she wanted is not in the record; his reading of it is a guess about the store clerk.<span class=\"pg\">p.150<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p144-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: she is offered a friendship and answers with the case<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 0  the last day  and a screen he should not have seen one day before the meeting  the class is united but  it was obvious that we lacked firm  irrefutable evidence  a flyer on the bulletin board by the stairway offers points to anyone with information on sudou and class c  kanzaki of class b posted it on friday   i saw the paper on the bulletin board  did you post it  ichinose   huh  this wasn t you  introduced to kanzaki   he was tall and slender  a pretty boy  but in a different way from hirata   nice to meet you  kanzaki  the leaked account of ishizaki changes his picture of the fight   yet sudou had turned the tables  and beat them all without once being hit himself  then  i couldn t help but feel there was something unnatural about that  his private odds  said to no one   if we got testimony from class d  though  our chances would probably be 6 to 4  or maybe 7 to 3   no  we can t say anything yet    and he keeps her out of it   i concealed sakura s name since we were still negotiating  the payment mechanism  taught at the counter   from your id number  you can issue a temporary token key  if you open that  and send the key  you should get a request for payment  he walks ichinose through the points screen  being close enough to notice her scent makes his heart rate climb  what he sees on her phone is never described  only its effect   the fragment of screen i d noticed had burned itself into my mind and wouldn t go away  then  ichinose might prove a huge obstacle for horikita in her quest to reach class a  the chapter does not name what was on the screen  it stays open","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.152–158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">One day before the meeting; the class is united but &quot;it was obvious that we lacked firm, irrefutable evidence&quot;. A flyer on the bulletin board by the stairway offers points to anyone with information on Sudou and Class C; Kanzaki of Class B posted it on Friday. Introduced to Kanzaki: &quot;He was tall and slender. A pretty boy, but in a different way from Hirata.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I saw the paper on the bulletin board. Did you post it, Ichinose?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Huh? This wasn’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Nice to meet you, Kanzaki.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The leaked account of Ishizaki changes his picture of the fight: &quot;Yet Sudou had turned the tables, and beat them all without once being hit himself.&quot; then &quot;I couldn’t help but feel there was something unnatural about that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His private odds, said to no one: &quot;If we got testimony from Class D, though, our chances would probably be 6 to 4, or maybe 7 to 3.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, we can’t say anything yet.&quot; — and he keeps her out of it: &quot;I concealed Sakura’s name since we were still negotiating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The payment mechanism, taught at the counter: &quot;From your ID number, you can issue a temporary token key. If you open that, and send the key, you should get a request for payment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks Ichinose through the points screen; being close enough to notice her scent makes his heart rate climb.<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> What he sees on her phone is never described, only its effect: &quot;The fragment of screen I’d noticed had burned itself into my mind and wouldn’t go away.&quot; then &quot;Ichinose might prove a huge obstacle for Horikita in her quest to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter does not name what was on the screen; it stays open.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p145-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10–4.11: the wall around Sakura, and the call that goes nowhere<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p152-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 5 sec  5 0  a message board  a leaked past  and a screen outside the shoe cubbies  she shows her phone  a message on the school homepage s board seeking witnesses  with a view count still in the dozens   have you ever checked out the school homepage  there s a message board  i requested that people come forward with information there  i said that if there anyone witnessed a violent incident at our school  i d like to hear about it   ah  regarding the stuff about points  don t worry  we just decided to do that on our own  besides  it will probably be difficult for us to get new information now  ah   it looks like i just got two messages regarding the post  there might be a little information   it looks like one of the boys from class c  ishizaki kun  was a bad seed in junior high  he was good at fighting  and terrorized the locals  a kid from his hometown probably leaked this   yeah  i think so too  i knew you d figure it out  kanzaki kun  great work  if we can verify this information  then we could be one step closer to proving sudou kun s innocence  but what we have is still pretty weak  isn t it   it ll be okay  besides  both class c and class a originally targeted us  anyway   anyway  we ll have to transfer points over to anyone who provides us with information  ah  but what if someone does so anonymously  in that case  how would we transfer over the points   ichinose and kanzaki made it pretty clear that they wanted to be fair and square when competing against the school and the other students  she leans in to point at her screen while he explains the token key  the page records his reaction  not hers  what he glimpses on her phone is left unnamed in this chapter  anything stronger would be a guess","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p152-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.0: a message board, a leaked past, and a screen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.152–158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Outside the shoe cubbies, she shows her phone: a message on the school homepage&#x27;s board seeking witnesses, with a view count still in the dozens. She leans in to point at her screen while he explains the token key; the page records his reaction, not hers.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Have you ever checked out the school homepage? There’s a message board. I requested that people come forward with information there. I said that if there anyone witnessed a violent incident at our school, I’d like to hear about…<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Ah, regarding the stuff about points, don’t worry. We just decided to do that on our own. Besides, it will probably be difficult for us to get new information now. Ah!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;It looks like I just got two messages regarding the post. There might be a little information.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have you ever checked out the school homepage? There’s a message board. I requested that people come forward with information there. I said that if there anyone witnessed a violent incident at our school, I’d like to hear about it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It looks like one of the boys from Class C, Ishizaki-kun, was a bad seed in junior high. He was good at fighting, and terrorized the locals. A kid from his hometown probably leaked this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah, I think so too. I knew you’d figure it out, Kanzaki-kun. Great work. If we can verify this information, then we could be one step closer to proving Sudou-kun’s innocence. But what we have is still pretty weak, isn’t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.156<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’ll be okay. Besides, both Class C and Class A originally targeted us, anyway.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Anyway, we’ll have to transfer points over to anyone who provides us with information. Ah, but what if someone does so anonymously? In that case, how would we transfer over the points?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Ichinose and Kanzaki made it pretty clear that they wanted to be fair and square when competing against the school and the other students.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> What he glimpses on her phone is left unnamed in this chapter; anything stronger would be a guess.<span class=\"pg\">p.158<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p121-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.7: she tries to dodge a confession and is made to give it<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p214-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: waiting at the entranceway<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p152-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 5 sec  5 0  paying informants  and paying them anonymously a bulletin board flyer promises points for information about sudou and class c  it is the first time in the volume that students offer their own points as a bounty  a school homepage message board is used to canvass witnesses  the view counter is  still only in the dozens  the bounty is class b s own money  not the school s   we just decided to do that on our own  anonymous payouts run on a temporary token key   from your id number  you can issue a temporary token key  if you open that  and send the key  you should get a request for payment  the points screen shows the user s id number in the upper left corner  the mechanism is demonstrated rather than explained  ayanokoji walks ichinose through the remittance screen step by step","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p152-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p152-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.0: paying informants, and paying them anonymously<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.152–158<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> A bulletin-board flyer promises points for information about Sudou and Class C; it is the first time in the volume that students offer their own points as a bounty.<span class=\"pg\">p.152<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> A school-homepage message board is used to canvass witnesses; the view counter is &quot;still only in the dozens&quot;.<span class=\"pg\">p.153<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The bounty is Class B&#x27;s own money, not the school&#x27;s: &quot;We just decided to do that on our own.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.154<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> Anonymous payouts run on a temporary token key: &quot;From your ID number, you can issue a temporary token key. If you open that, and send the key, you should get a request for payment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.157–158<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Fact<\/span> The points screen shows the user&#x27;s ID number in the upper left corner.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The mechanism is demonstrated rather than explained: Ayanokōji walks Ichinose through the remittance screen step by step.<span class=\"pg\">p.157<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p143-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: a price a student actually paid<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p234-1\">→ After: Ch.7: loans, fees, and the cost of a withdrawn case<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 1 5 5  the night visit  and a definition of friendship he refuses the obvious reading of horikita s face and then accepts it as a baffling realization   in that moment  i had come to a rather baffling realization  he explains the seating outcome to himself   it was precisely because they might not make the best team that i d been appointed as a substitute  i supposed  her email asks him to room 1106  the girls  floor is open to boys  but entry is prohibited after 8 00 pm  her remark about eyes turns into self examination   so  was it like insight into a person s true self  when someone looked at me  would they see that i was insubstantial and lack ambition   i think you should do what you want  sakura   sakura  i think you ll be able to make friends with someone in no time   it might be presumptuous for me to say this  but i think that we re like friends  we are   well  why not go out with me for a while  if it s not a bother  of course  he picks up the fallen glasses  confirms there are no lenses  and hands them back without comment  the advice he gives her   for sudou  for kushida  for your classmates  throw all of those thoughts away  then  tell the truth for your own sake  do that  and sudou will be saved  that s enough  his reason for giving it   maybe i did it because i understood how it felt to be wanted","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–177<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her email asks him to room 1106; the girls&#x27; floor is open to boys, but entry is prohibited after 8:00 PM.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I think you should do what you want, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Sakura, I think you’ll be able to make friends with someone in no time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It might be presumptuous for me to say this, but I think that we’re like friends. We are,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.173<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He refuses the obvious reading of Horikita&#x27;s face and then accepts it as a baffling realization: &quot;In that moment, I had come to a rather baffling realization.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He explains the seating outcome to himself: &quot;It was precisely because they might not make the best team that I’d been appointed as a substitute, I supposed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Her remark about eyes turns into self-examination: &quot;So, was it like insight into a person’s true self? When someone looked at me, would they see that I was insubstantial and lack ambition?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, why not go out with me for a while? If it’s not a bother, of course.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He picks up the fallen glasses, confirms there are no lenses, and hands them back without comment.<span class=\"pg\">p.174<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> The advice he gives her: &quot;For Sudou. For Kushida. For your classmates. Throw all of those thoughts away.&quot; then &quot;Tell the truth for your own sake. Do that, and Sudou will be saved. That’s enough.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His reason for giving it: &quot;Maybe I did it because I understood how it felt to be wanted.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: the last day, and a screen he should not have seen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5 sec  5 1  the face she does not intend to make morning  the classroom  she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls  an icy voice   did you spend your day off with kushida san   really  i didn t intend to make any kind of face  i should look the same as i always do  however  i will say that i admire how freely you ve been moving  when i ask you for help  you re often reluctant  but when kushida san asks you  you accept readily  i was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us  the denial is contradicted on the page   i looked over at my neighbor  and saw an expression on horikita s face that i d never glimpsed before  then  she did not remotely look calm and discreet  kushida reads the same face as exclusion  the narrator refuses that reading and then concedes a realization he cannot name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning, the classroom; she asks about his day off in what the narrator calls &quot;an icy voice&quot;.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Did you spend your day off with Kushida-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks…<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Really? I didn’t intend to make any kind of face. I should look the same as I always do. However, I will say that I admire how freely you’ve been moving. When I ask you for help, you’re often reluctant, but when Kushida-san asks you, you accept readily. I was calmly and discretely analyzing the difference between us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The denial is contradicted on the page: &quot;I looked over at my neighbor, and saw an expression on Horikita’s face that I’d never glimpsed before.&quot; then &quot;She did not remotely look calm and discreet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159–160<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida reads the same face as exclusion; the narrator refuses that reading and then concedes a realization he cannot name.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p118-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.6–4.8: named by everyone, present nowhere<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5 sec  5 1  she reads horikita better than horikita reads herself  good morning  ayanokouji kun   thanks for yesterday  you really saved me   let s hang out again sometime  okay  she does not come in  she  briefly peeked into the classroom  and calls him out to the hallway   i have a feeling i just saw something really incredible   that s not it  i think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited   she probably doesn t know how she feels  i m sure she s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them  though  that s a good thing  a good thing   perhaps you re realizing something fundamental  ayanokouji kun  horikita san is upset that you didn t invite her to come along  the reading is hers alone  the narrator calls it  a bizarre thought  and cannot accept it  she names horikita s feeling as loneliness while disliking her  and says it in the hallway where horikita cannot hear","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.159–162<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She does not come in; she &quot;briefly peeked into the classroom&quot; and calls him out to the hallway.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Good morning! Ayanokouji-kun!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Thanks for yesterday. You really saved me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Let’s hang out again sometime, okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.159<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have a feeling I just saw something really incredible!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not it. I think she feels alienated and lonely over not being invited.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;She probably doesn’t know how she feels… I’m sure she’s probably noticed how much fun it is to spend time with friends and talk to them, though. That’s a good thing, a good thing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps you’re realizing something fundamental, Ayanokouji-kun. Horikita-san is upset that you didn’t invite her to come along.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The reading is hers alone; the narrator calls it &quot;a bizarre thought&quot; and cannot accept it.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She names Horikita&#x27;s feeling as loneliness while disliking her, and says it in the hallway where Horikita cannot hear.<span class=\"pg\">p.162<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p147-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the same evening, on two calls<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 5 sec  5 2  the teacher who will not take the witness on trust the faculty room  after homeroom  at the class s request  ayanokoji hangs back   a witness  for sudou s case   i understand what you re said  however  i can t simply accept what you re telling me   sakura  why are you testifying now  when i reported the issue during homeroom  you didn t step forward  it s not as though you were absent that day  right   you re not good at talking with other people  and yet you ve decided to testify now  isn t that strange   i m speaking to sakura right now  her interrogation of a frightened witness reduces the girl physically   sakura hunched and shrank away  much like a frog cornered by a snake  the narrator adds that she  should have understood what kind of girl sakura was  and that speaking up at all  had made great progress    the method is exact and costly   i see  so  then you mustered up the courage to come forward   i see  well if you are a witness as you say  naturally i m obligated to relay that information to the school  however  while the school will listen to the whole story  sudou may not be declared innocent   are you really the witness  sakura  that s what i m getting at  i think that it may be a lie made up by class d because the students are afraid of receiving a negative evaluation   horrible  if you really had witnessed an event  you should have come forward on the first day  it s natural to feel suspicious when someone steps up just in the nick of time  considering that the witness is from class d  it s doubly suspicious  any reasonable person would have doubts  don t you think so  conveniently  a student from the same class happened to be in an infrequently visited building and happened to witness the entire event   however  a witness is a witness  i cannot determine if she s lying  so for the time being  i will accept her testimony  so  sakura  i will ask for you to join us on the day of deliberation  i understand that you do not like to associate with others  but can you do this   if you don t like it  you do have the option to withdraw  also  we ll tell sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation   if sudou himself consents  i will approve it  however  we cannot allow that many people  only a maximum of two may sit in on the deliberation  please think on that carefully  she tests the witness by making her imagine the room   as if she were testing the girl  the narrator s judgment of her method  kept as his   as our teacher  chabashira sensei should have understood what kind of girl sakura was","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–166<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The faculty room, after homeroom, at the class&#x27;s request; Ayanokōji hangs back.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;A witness? For Sudou’s case?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;I understand what you’re said. However, I can’t simply accept what you’re telling me,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Sakura, why are you testifying now? When I reported the issue during homeroom, you didn’t step forward. It’s not as though you were absent that day, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re not good at talking with other people, and yet you’ve decided to testify now? Isn’t that strange?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m speaking to Sakura right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her interrogation of a frightened witness reduces the girl physically: &quot;Sakura hunched and shrank away, much like a frog cornered by a snake.&quot; The narrator adds that she &quot;should have understood what kind of girl Sakura was&quot; and that speaking up at all &quot;had made great progress&quot; — the method is exact and costly.<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So, then you mustered up the courage to come forward?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. Well if you are a witness as you say, naturally I’m obligated to relay that information to the school. However, while the school will listen to the whole story, Sudou may not be declared innocent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you really the witness, Sakura? That’s what I’m getting at. I think that it may be a lie made up by Class D because the students are afraid of receiving a negative evaluation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horrible? If you really had witnessed an event, you should have come forward on the first day. It’s natural to feel suspicious when someone steps up just in the nick of time. Considering that the witness is from Class D, it’s doubly suspicious. Any reasonable person would have doubts. Don’t you think so? Conveniently, a student from the same class happened to be in an infrequently visited building and happened to witness the entire event?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, a witness is a witness. I cannot determine if she’s lying, so for the time being, I will accept her testimony. So, Sakura, I will ask for you to join us on the day of deliberation. I understand that you do not like to associate with others, but can you do this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you don’t like it, you do have the option to withdraw. Also, we’ll tell Sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Sudou himself consents, I will approve it. However, we cannot allow that many people. Only a maximum of two may sit in on the deliberation. Please think on that carefully.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She tests the witness by making her imagine the room: &quot;as if she were testing the girl.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164–165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s judgment of her method, kept as his: &quot;As our teacher, Chabashira-sensei should have understood what kind of girl Sakura was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p40-1\">← Before: Ch.3 open (July 2 homeroom): she makes Sudou&#x27;s fight public<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5 sec  5 2 5 3  she brings the witness  then loses the seat  yes  sakura san saw everything from start to finish   kushida called for sakura  who stood quietly behind her   sensei  sakura san is    cut off   chabashira sensei cut kushida off sharply   chabashira sensei  that s a horrible thing to say   do you mind if we participate as well  sensei   of course  it was kushida who spoke up  most likely to support sakura    she asks for a place and horikita takes it  lunch in the classroom   thanks to kushida s persuasive tears  horikita joins the strategy meeting   can we really prove sudou s innocence tomorrow  mid argument she stops listening   kushida  seated beside me as the ike yamauchi spectacle unfolded  appeared deep in thought   perhaps    murmured  then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it   ah  nothing  it s nothing  there was just something on my mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch in the classroom; &quot;thanks to Kushida’s persuasive tears&quot; Horikita joins the strategy meeting. Mid-argument she stops listening: &quot;Kushida, seated beside me as the Ike/Yamauchi spectacle unfolded, appeared deep in thought.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Yes. Sakura-san saw everything from start to finish.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Sensei, Sakura-san is…&quot; — cut off: &quot;Chabashira-sensei cut Kushida off sharply.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Chabashira-sensei, that’s a horrible thing to say!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> &quot;Kushida called for Sakura, who stood quietly behind her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you mind if we participate as well, sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> &quot;Of course, it was Kushida who spoke up, most likely to support Sakura.&quot; — she asks for a place and Horikita takes it.<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Can we really prove Sudou’s innocence tomorrow?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Perhaps…&quot; — murmured, then she opens her phone and says nothing more about it.<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, nothing. It’s nothing. There was just something on my mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.168<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: she reads Horikita better than Horikita reads herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5 sec  5 2  she testifies in the faculty room  and the teacher tests her after homeroom  the faculty room  kushida brings her forward  ayanokoji waits at the back  out of consideration for sakura   yes  i saw it  she gives the account in full for the first time   none of us  not even the teacher  spoke a single word or even moved until the very end  asked why she is speaking now  she cannot answer cleanly   well  that s  i m just not good at talking with other people   umm  well  it s because our class is in trouble now  and i thought if if i testify  i can help  chabashira s interrogation reduces her physically   sakura hunched and shrank away  much like a frog cornered by a snake  the narrator s reading  kept as his   she should have realized that merely by speaking up  sakura had made great progress   yes    her answer to whether she mustered the courage  the page notes that  sakura  upon imagining this  turned pale and anguished   y yeah    answering kushida   sakura s reply lacked confidence  the deliberation itself is the threat  not the testimony   in addition to having to give her testimony in front of others  she was also going to have to sit alone with sudou   n no  it s fine  she agrees to an arrangement she does not want   she didn t seem to like this at all  but she also didn t have much choice right now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.163–166<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After homeroom, the faculty room. Kushida brings her forward; Ayanokōji waits at the back &quot;out of consideration for Sakura&quot;.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Yes. I saw it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Umm… Well, it’s because our…class is in trouble now, and…I thought if…if I testify, I can help…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Yes…&quot; — her answer to whether she mustered the courage; the page notes that &quot;Sakura, upon imagining this, turned pale and anguished.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She gives the account in full for the first time: &quot;None of us, not even the teacher, spoke a single word or even moved until the very end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.163<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Asked why she is speaking now, she cannot answer cleanly: &quot;Well… That’s… I’m just not good at talking with other people…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Chabashira&#x27;s interrogation reduces her physically: &quot;Sakura hunched and shrank away, much like a frog cornered by a snake.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator&#x27;s reading, kept as his: &quot;She should have realized that merely by speaking up, Sakura had made great progress.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.164<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Y-yeah…&quot; — answering Kushida; &quot;Sakura’s reply lacked confidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The deliberation itself is the threat, not the testimony: &quot;In addition to having to give her testimony in front of others, she was also going to have to sit alone with Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, it’s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She agrees to an arrangement she does not want: &quot;She didn’t seem to like this at all, but she also didn’t have much choice right now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p148-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.11: the call she cannot finish<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5 sec  5 2 5 3  she takes the seats and refuses the optimism  well  naturally that was the result  it s to be expected   now then  kushida san  it would be best for ayanokouji kun and me to sit in on the deliberation  i fully understand you supporting sakura san  however  if it comes to a debate  then that s a different story  she takes the two observer places kushida asked for  and sakura is left agreeing to it  at lunch she eats  her bread in silence  while the others argue   don t bring your dirty face so close to me   i can t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven  although you ve gained evidence that works in your favor  you re still in a very disadvantageous situation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.165–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At lunch she eats &quot;her bread in silence&quot; while the others argue.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Well, naturally that was the result. It’s to be expected.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Now then, Kushida-san. It would be best for Ayanokouji-kun and me to sit in on the deliberation. I fully understand you supporting Sakura-san. However, if it comes to a debate, then that’s a different story.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Don’t bring your dirty face so close to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She takes the two observer places Kushida asked for, and Sakura is left agreeing to it.<span class=\"pg\">p.166<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I can’t help but be mystified by your belief that your innocence can easily be proven. Although you’ve gained evidence that works in your favor, you’re still in a very disadvantageous situation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1: the face she does not intend to make<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p165-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 5 sec  5 2 5 3  told he will be there  and certain of the outcome he is not in the faculty room  chabashira says the school will inform him   we ll tell sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation  lunch strategy session  he and kushida both turn to horikita for a verdict   of course we will  it s obvious that i was set up  i m definitely innocent  right   hey  horikita  what do you think   but we have a witness who knows i m innocent  and the other guys were real jerks in the past  that should be enough  right  those guys are bad news   sudou  completely blind to his own shortcomings  arrogantly crossed his legs and nodded in agreement with himself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p165-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p165-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: told he will be there, and certain of the outcome<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.165–167<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Lunch strategy session; he and Kushida both turn to Horikita for a verdict.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Of course we will. It’s obvious that I was set up. I’m definitely innocent. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Hey, Horikita. What do you think?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;But we have a witness who knows I’m innocent, and the other guys were real jerks in the past. That should be enough, right? Those guys are bad news.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is not in the faculty room; Chabashira says the school will inform him: &quot;we’ll tell Sudou that he will be participating in the deliberation.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.165<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Sudou, completely blind to his own shortcomings, arrogantly crossed his legs and nodded in agreement with himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p146-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.10: the witness is secured for him, in a mall, without him<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the fighter who asks for honesty<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5 sec  5 3  the magazine fight  ike and yamauchi scrambled over a weekly manga magazine  during the lunch strategy meeting  the exchange that follows has one untagged line  and the second speaker is not assigned here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the magazine fight<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.167–168<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> &quot;Ike and Yamauchi scrambled over a weekly manga magazine&quot; during the lunch strategy meeting; the exchange that follows has one untagged line, and the second speaker is not assigned here.<span class=\"pg\">p.167<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p129-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.8, sec. 4.11: he is a category in someone else&#x27;s phone etiquette<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: he half-sees it first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5 sec  5 4  the night she asks him to come to her room evening  her dorm room 1106 on the eleventh floor    this was my first time setting foot there    reached by email rather than a call   if i was absent from school tomorrow  what do you think would happen   if it s okay with you  could we meet right now  i m in room 1106   if you could keep this a secret from everyone  that would really help me out   come on in     she greeted me wearing casual clothes   umm  ayanokouji kun  do you remember what you said before  you said i wasn t obligated to step forward  even though i was the witness  you also said it was meaningless to force me to testify   i just don t have any self confidence after all   i ve been terrible at it for so long  i m not good at speaking in front of others  if i m asked to testify in front of the teachers tomorrow  i don t think i ll have the confidence to answer properly  so   ahhhhh  jeez  why am i so completely useless  the outburst is new to him   it was the first time i d seen her like that  and  so she could be animated  i d had no idea  considering her usually depressed look   that s because i m not afraid of your eyes  ayanokouji kun   oh  no  i don t mean the eyes that you ve seen me with  i mean the pupils  way back in the eyes  if you look someone deep in their eyes  you ll understand  i m sorry  i can t really explain it well   well  it s just  when i see a man even if he seems kind i suddenly get afraid  a cause is guessed and not confirmed   i wondered if something had happened in sakura s past to cause her intense fear of men   i know it would be good to simply say what it is i saw  but no matter what i do  i can t seem to imagine it  how can i speak that assertively","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.169–175<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening, her dorm room 1106 on the eleventh floor — &quot;This was my first time setting foot there&quot; — reached by email rather than a call.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;If I was absent from school tomorrow, what do you think would happen?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;If it’s okay with you, could we meet right now? I’m in room 1106.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;If you could keep this a secret from everyone… That would really help me out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.169<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Come on in.&quot; — &quot;She greeted me wearing casual clothes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Umm… Ayanokouji-kun, do you remember what you said before? You said I wasn’t obligated to step forward, even though I was the witness. You also said it was meaningless to force me to testify.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I…just don’t have any self-confidence after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ve been terrible at it for so long… I’m not good at speaking in front of others. If I’m asked to testify in front of the teachers tomorrow, I don’t think I’ll have the confidence to answer properly. So…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ahhhhh. Jeez, why am I so completely useless?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The outburst is new to him: &quot;It was the first time I’d seen her like that.&quot; and &quot;So she could be animated. I’d had no idea, considering her usually depressed look.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171–172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s because I’m not afraid of your eyes, Ayanokouji-kun…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no. I don’t mean the eyes that you’ve seen me with. I mean the pupils, way back in the eyes… If you look someone deep in their eyes, you’ll understand. I’m sorry, I can’t really explain it well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, it’s just… When I see a man…even if he seems kind…I suddenly get afraid.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> A cause is guessed and not confirmed: &quot;I wondered if something had happened in Sakura’s past to cause her intense fear of men.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I know it would be good to simply say what it is I saw. But no matter what I do, I can’t seem to imagine it… How can I speak that assertively?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.172<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: she testifies in the faculty room, and the teacher tests her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 5 sec  5 4  the elevator  and a question she answers herself the elevator  she is inside with shopping bags  the thirteenth floor button lit  he presses eleven   what  you re not getting on   i was out shopping  did you not see   this isn t the tenth floor  is that okay   for someone who dislikes trouble  you ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case  or perhaps you have ulterior motives   you re going to meet with sakura san  aren t you   well  i suppose where you go is none of my business  she asks the question  then withdraws it  without waiting for the answer he does not give","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.170–171<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The elevator: she is inside with shopping bags, the thirteenth-floor button lit; he presses eleven.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What? You’re not getting on?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I was out shopping. Did you not see?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;This isn’t the tenth floor. Is that okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;For someone who dislikes trouble, you’ve been extremely proactive in involving yourself with this case. Or perhaps you have ulterior motives?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re going to meet with Sakura-san, aren’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.170<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well. I suppose where you go is none of my business.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.171<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She asks the question, then withdraws it, without waiting for the answer he does not give.<span class=\"pg\">p.170–171<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she takes the seats and refuses the optimism<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5 sec  5 5  the club building  and advice she did not ask for she takes him to the club activities building away from the school  the one  that hosted things like the archery club and the tea ceremony club  where arrows can be heard   i m not  but i ve wanted to come here at least once  i d stand out if i came by myself  so   why did you ask me to come out  anyway   horikita san  kushida san  ike kun  sudou kun  yamauchi kun   i don t know how to make friends at all  i m envious  you were the first person to call me a friend   yeah  i should apologize to kushida san sometime  she was the first one to call and invite me out  because i didn t have the courage  i actually wanted to hang out with her  i just couldn t answer her  no matter what i did  i m so pathetic   thank you  ayanokouji kun  whether the advice lands is left unresolved   hopefully  my words had found purchase somewhere in sakura s heart","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.176–178<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She takes him to the club-activities building away from the school, the one &quot;that hosted things like the archery club and the tea ceremony club&quot;, where arrows can be heard.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I’m not, but I’ve wanted to come here at least once. I’d stand out if I came by myself, so…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Why did you ask me to come out, anyway?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Horikita-san, Kushida-san, Ike-kun, Sudou-kun, Yamauchi-kun…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.176<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t know how to make friends at all. I’m envious. You were the first person to call me a friend.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. I should apologize to Kushida-san sometime. She was the first one to call and invite me out, because I didn’t have the courage… I actually wanted to hang out with her. I just couldn’t answer her, no matter what I did. I’m so pathetic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.177<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Whether the advice lands is left unresolved: &quot;Hopefully, my words had found purchase somewhere in Sakura’s heart.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.178<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p169-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the night she asks him to come to her room<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5 sec  5 6 5 7  proof  and what cannot be fixed by morning  no  kushida is definitely right  that s sakura  here   you can barely see it  but the door to her dorm room is in this picture   good job noticing this  kushida  the link he makes alone   i flashed on a memory of the man who worked at the campus electronic store   the clerk  on the other hand  had been in incredibly high spirits  after all  here was his chance to get his favorite idol s real name and phone number on the form she had to fill out   in the end  the only option was to wait on an sos from the girl in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–188<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;No, Kushida is definitely right. That’s Sakura. Here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;You can barely see it, but the door to her dorm room is in this picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Good job noticing this, Kushida.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The link he makes alone: &quot;I flashed on a memory of the man who worked at the campus electronic store.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The clerk, on the other hand, had been in incredibly high spirits. After all, here was his chance to get his favorite idol’s real name and phone number on the form she had to fill out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> &quot;In the end, the only option was to wait on an SOS from the girl in question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p159-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.1–5.5: the night visit, and a definition of friendship<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 5 sec  5 6  the idol  the persona theory  and the whisper at the door that night  under kushida s orders  everyone but sudo gathers in ayanokoji s room  she asks for his computer and opens a blog   there has been progress  yes  but i ve also noticed something incredible  ayanokouji kun  can i borrow your computer for a minute   okay  have a look at this  the reveal s opening exchange is untagged   wait  is that a picture of shizuku  then  shizuku  then  she s a gravure idol  she was just featured in a young men s magazine    only the next question   do you recognize her  carries her name   do you recognize her   look closely   no  not that  this is sakura san  isn t it   sakura san  from our class   when i saw ike kun reading that weekly magazine  i remembered something  i had the feeling i d seen sakura somewhere before   but just when shizuku started to become really popular  she suddenly disappeared   i was surprised when i found out that she was an idol  but i also kind of understood it  i wonder if that s her real personality  her theory of the double life   i think that most likely  sakura san would say that her idol self is actually her false face  then  i think that she s creating another personality with makeup   i ll tell you later  right now  our priority is to resolve this case  besides  it s a personal request   i m sorry  if i told you now  it d just be a bother   if you listen to my request  ayanokouji kun i ll give you my most precious possession    whispered at the door  on tiptoe  hand on his chest  by the time the door opens the change is gone   not even the faintest trace of that frightening kushida remained  she turns the request into a transaction before she has named it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–185<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">That night &quot;under Kushida’s orders&quot; everyone but Sudō gathers in Ayanokōji&#x27;s room; she asks for his computer and opens a blog.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;There has been progress, yes, but I’ve also noticed something incredible. Ayanokouji-kun, can I borrow your computer for a minute?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Okay. Have a look at this!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> &quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reveal&#x27;s opening exchange is untagged: &quot;Wait, is that a picture of Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;Shizuku?&quot; then &quot;She’s a gravure idol. She was just featured in a young men’s magazine.&quot; — only the next question, &quot;Do you recognize her?&quot;, carries her name.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Look closely.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, not that! This is Sakura-san, isn’t it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura-san, from our class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When I saw Ike-kun reading that weekly magazine, I remembered something. I had the feeling I’d seen Sakura somewhere before,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But just when Shizuku started to become really popular, she suddenly disappeared.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was surprised when I found out that she was an idol, but I also kind of understood it. I wonder if that’s her real personality?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her theory of the double life: &quot;I think that…most likely, Sakura-san would say that her idol self is actually her false face.&quot; then &quot;I think that she’s creating another personality with makeup.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.183<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll tell you later. Right now, our priority is to resolve this case. Besides, it’s a personal request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m sorry. If I told you now, it’d just be a bother.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you listen to my request, Ayanokouji-kun…I’ll give you my most precious possession.&quot; — whispered at the door, on tiptoe, hand on his chest.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> By the time the door opens the change is gone: &quot;Not even the faintest trace of that frightening Kushida remained.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.185<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She turns the request into a transaction before she has named it.<span class=\"pg\">p.184<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: she brings the witness, then loses the seat<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5 sec  5 6  the class finds out what she does with her face ayanokoji s room  that night  kushida has called everyone but sudo  she is not present when the class identifies her  the blog is found by kushida  under the name shizuku  the proof the narrator offers is a dormitory door visible in one photograph  and his line is   you can barely see it  but the door to her dorm room is in this picture  the double life  stated plainly   she lived a double life as an idol and a quiet  inconspicuous student at our school  why she made the second life is not answered   why had she wanted to create another life  it was like a coin with two very different sides  the lensless glasses she dropped the night before are the disguise the class is now discussing  though not in her own words","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–181<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Ayanokōji&#x27;s room, that night; Kushida has called everyone but Sudō.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is not present when the class identifies her; the blog is found by Kushida, under the name Shizuku.<span class=\"pg\">p.179<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The proof the narrator offers is a dormitory door visible in one photograph, and his line is: &quot;You can barely see it, but the door to her dorm room is in this picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The double life, stated plainly: &quot;She lived a double life as an idol and a quiet, inconspicuous student at our school.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Why she made the second life is not answered: &quot;Why had she wanted to create another life? It was like a coin with two very different sides.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.181<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The lensless glasses she dropped the night before are the disguise the class is now discussing, though not in her own words.<span class=\"pg\">p.180–181<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p176-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.5: the club building, and advice she did not ask for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\">→ After: Ch.5 sec. 5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 5 sec  5 6  he half sees it first the narration marks him as persuaded before ike   ike laughed  but yamauchi s expression stiffened   hey  ike  you know  when i actually get a good look at her  i think she probably does look a little like sakura   those are simplistic ways to identify somebody","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.6: he half-sees it first<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.179–180<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> &quot;Hey, Ike… You know, when I actually get a good look at her, I…think she probably does look a little like Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> &quot;Those are simplistic ways to identify somebody…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration marks him as persuaded before Ike: &quot;Ike laughed, but Yamauchi’s expression stiffened.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.180<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p167-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.3: the magazine fight<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the look he cannot stop<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 5 sec  5 7  the comments that explain her fear her blog ran about two years  starting when she began working as an idol  more than 5000 followers on twitter  she stopped replying after being accepted to the school  the record of one commenter escalates in public view   do you believe in fate  i do  i believe we will be together forever  then  look  god is real after all  the chapter s connection  kept as the narrator s inference  the electronics store clerk recognised her  and the repair form carried her real name and phone number  her fear at the repair counter is explained in hindsight by that inference  not by anything she says  nothing can be done before the hearing   in the end  the only option was to wait on an sos from the girl in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\">Ch.5 sec. 5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.186–188<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Her blog ran about two years, starting when she began working as an idol; more than 5000 followers on Twitter; she stopped replying after being accepted to the school.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The record of one commenter escalates in public view: &quot;Do you believe in fate? I do. I believe we will be together forever.&quot; then &quot;Look, God is real after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s connection, kept as the narrator&#x27;s inference: the electronics-store clerk recognised her, and the repair form carried her real name and phone number.<span class=\"pg\">p.187<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her fear at the repair counter is explained in hindsight by that inference, not by anything she says.<span class=\"pg\">p.187–188<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Nothing can be done before the hearing: &quot;In the end, the only option was to wait on an SOS from the girl in question.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.188<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the class finds out what she does with her face<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\">→ After: Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 open  the check he makes first the morning of the hearing  before anything else he confirms sakura came  and finds her in the usual corner   sakura sat quietly alone  so as not to get roped into other students  conversations   are you okay   don t forget what i said yesterday  testify for your own sake  more than anyone else s  the sentence is the volume s thesis carried forward from the club building  the testimony must belong to her  not to sudo or the class","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\">Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The morning of the hearing; before anything else he confirms Sakura came, and finds her in the usual corner: &quot;Sakura sat quietly alone, so as not to get roped into other students’ conversations.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Don’t forget what I said yesterday. Testify for your own sake, more than anyone else’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The sentence is the volume’s thesis carried forward from the club building: the testimony must belong to her, not to Sudō or the class.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.6–5.7: proof, and what cannot be fixed by morning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 open  the morning she comes anyway the day of the hearing  she is in the classroom early  sitting alone  so as not to get roped into other students  conversations  her expression  even gloomier than usual   ah  yeah  i m fine   i thought that things would be tough if i were absent today  so  her attendance is a decision  not a habit  she came because  the entire class would be upset if she were absent   yeah  i ll be okay  she can tell ike and yamauchi know about the idol work  and answers the room without being asked  she  quietly mouthed the words   it s all right  the narrator credits the double life with the sensitivity   maybe working as an idol had made her sensitive to subtle changes in a room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\">Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The day of the hearing; she is in the classroom early, sitting alone &quot;so as not to get roped into other students’ conversations,&quot; her expression &quot;even gloomier than usual.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Ah, yeah. I’m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I thought that things would be tough if I were absent today, so…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Yeah. I’ll be okay.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her attendance is a decision, not a habit: she came because &quot;the entire class would be upset if she were absent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She can tell Ike and Yamauchi know about the idol work, and answers the room without being asked: she &quot;quietly mouthed the words, &#x27;It’s all right.&#x27;&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator credits the double life with the sensitivity: &quot;Maybe working as an idol had made her sensitive to subtle changes in a room.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p186-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.7: the comments that explain her fear<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"yamauchi-haruki","q":"yamauchi haruki ch 6 open  the look he cannot stop he and ike watch sakura on the morning of the hearing because  they now knew of her idol identity  the narrator watches the watching  and notes that sakura guessed it  oh no  before anyone said anything  the chapter 5 doubt he voiced   that sakura looked a little like the idol   has been settled off the page  he gets no line here  only the glance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p190-1\">Ch.6 open: the look he cannot stop<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.190<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He and Ike watch Sakura on the morning of the hearing because &quot;they now knew of her idol identity&quot;; the narrator watches the watching, and notes that Sakura guessed it &quot;Oh no…&quot; before anyone said anything.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The Chapter 5 doubt he voiced — that Sakura looked a little like the idol — has been settled off the page; he gets no line here, only the glance.<span class=\"pg\">p.190<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: he half-sees it first<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the hearing he cannot fix class d s room before the 4 00 pm hearing  he watches sudo and horikita spar and reads sudo s cooperation as proof he does not hate her  his estimate of sakura is the chapter s first alarm   if she was in this psychological state before the meeting had even begun  she might not be able to speak satisfactorily  the student council room  three class c students  sakagami sensei  the president and secretary tachibana  horikita freezes at the word  student council  his read of the room before a word of evidence   considering they were brother and sister  the odds were not in our favor  he reads class c s testimony as invention   the veins on sudo s forehead make their account  rather obvious  as a lie   and horikita s silence as the real emergency   it was as if her mind was gone   get a grip on yourself  horikita  we re going to lose at this rate  you have to fight  he gets up  stands behind horikita  grips her sides  as hard as i could  and tickles her until she returns to herself  in front of the teachers and the student council  the provocation is deliberate and public  he accepts that he  might be killed later for doing this  but judged that no lesser stimulus would bring her back","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–200<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room before the 4:00 PM hearing; he watches Sudō and Horikita spar and reads Sudō’s cooperation as proof he does not hate her. The student council room: three Class C students, Sakagami-sensei, the president and Secretary Tachibana; Horikita freezes at the word &quot;student council.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Get a grip on yourself, Horikita. We’re going to lose at this rate. You have to fight!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His estimate of Sakura is the chapter’s first alarm: &quot;If she was in this psychological state before the meeting had even begun, she might not be able to speak satisfactorily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His read of the room before a word of evidence: &quot;Considering they were brother and sister, the odds were not in our favor.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He reads Class C’s testimony as invention — the veins on Sudō’s forehead make their account &quot;rather obvious&quot; as a lie — and Horikita’s silence as the real emergency: &quot;It was as if her mind was gone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He gets up, stands behind Horikita, grips her sides &quot;as hard as I could&quot; and tickles her until she returns to herself, in front of the teachers and the student council.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The provocation is deliberate and public: he accepts that he &quot;might be killed later for doing this&quot; but judged that no lesser stimulus would bring her back.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p190-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the check he makes first<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 open  the hearing she is not ready for class d s room  ten minutes before the hearing  sudo asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him   have you prepared for this  sudou kun   don t do anything selfish  actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do  yes  the narrator reads the exchange as habitual combat without hatred  sudo  would ve absolutely refused her help  if he truly resented her  kushida s send off    do your best  horikita san  sudou kun    is the only encouragement horikita receives before the hearing  and she does not answer it  outside the faculty room  chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in  horikita freezes at the words   i ll go  i m fine  the glance she gives the narrator is read as a request not to worry on her account","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–192<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room, ten minutes before the hearing; Sudō asks her to hear him out and she answers by refusing to reassure him. Outside the faculty room, Chabashira lets slip that the student council will sit in; Horikita freezes at the words.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Have you prepared for this, Sudou-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Don’t do anything selfish. Actually listening right now would be the clever thing to do, yes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’ll go. I’m fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator reads the exchange as habitual combat without hatred: Sudō &quot;would’ve absolutely refused her help&quot; if he truly resented her.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s send-off — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — is the only encouragement Horikita receives before the hearing, and she does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The glance she gives the narrator is read as a request not to worry on her account.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p170-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.4: the elevator, and a question she answers herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie","q":"hoshinomiya chie ch 6 open  the teacher at the door the faculty room minutes before the hearing  she greets the four class d students as they arrive   yahoo  hello  class d students   it seems like something rather incredible has happened  hmm  her interest is appetite  not concern   her eyes sparkled  as if she enjoyed sticking her nose into other people s business  the narrator adds  in parentheses   well  she did   oh no  i ve been found out already  huh   so i guess i can t join in  huh   aw  that s too bad  well  that s all right  the results should be out within the hour  i guess  she knows the hearing schedule before it starts and expects a result inside the hour  chabashira pushes her back into the faculty room before she can say more  her exclusion states the rule from the outside   outsiders cannot participate  in a disciplinary settlement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 open: the teacher at the door<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–192<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The faculty room minutes before the hearing; she greets the four Class D students as they arrive.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> &quot;Yahoo! Hello, Class D students!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> &quot;It seems like something rather incredible has happened, hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> &quot;Oh no. I’ve been found out already, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her interest is appetite, not concern: &quot;Her eyes sparkled, as if she enjoyed sticking her nose into other people’s business.&quot; The narrator adds, in parentheses, &quot;(Well, she did).&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So I guess I can’t join in, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Aw, that’s too bad. Well, that’s all right. The results should be out within the hour, I guess.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She knows the hearing schedule before it starts and expects a result inside the hour; Chabashira pushes her back into the faculty room before she can say more.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Her exclusion states the rule from the outside: &quot;outsiders cannot participate&quot; in a disciplinary settlement.<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6 open  the send off her only spoken line in the chapter is the room s send off to the two people going into the hearing    do your best  horikita san  sudou kun    and horikita does not answer it  she gives the encouragement to both of them together  including the girl who has spent the volume refusing her  and the page records no reply","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her only spoken line in the chapter is the room’s send-off to the two people going into the hearing — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — and Horikita does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She gives the encouragement to both of them together, including the girl who has spent the volume refusing her, and the page records no reply.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p179-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.6: the idol, the persona theory, and the whisper at the door<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 sec  6 1  the testimony that nearly does not start class d s classroom at 3 50 pm  ten minutes before the hearing  she is  still sitting down  her body rigid  and stands with her lips trembling   yeah  i m okay  thank you   sakura was far tenser than i d expected    enough that the narrator fears she  might not be able to speak satisfactorily  the student council room on the fourth floor  she enters only when called   looking worried and restless  and  down at her feet  as if scared of danger   y yes  okay  well  i  the silence is measured on the page   ten seconds  twenty seconds  she looks further down and her face goes pale  horikita s prompt does not reach her  chabashira orders her to leave  she  closed her eyes tightly  as if she couldn t bear it anymore  as if she regretted her own weakness   i definitely saw what happened  the narrator does not recognise the voice at first  and what identifies her is volume   what most struck me was the volume of her voice   the students in class c threw the first punch  there s no mistake about that  the delivery carries force beyond her manner   she spoke so desperately that you wanted to believe she was telling the truth","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191–200<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s classroom at 3:50 PM, ten minutes before the hearing; she is &quot;still sitting down, her body rigid&quot; and stands with her lips trembling. The student council room on the fourth floor; she enters only when called, &quot;looking worried and restless&quot; and &quot;down at her feet, as if scared of danger.&quot; Chabashira orders her to leave; she &quot;closed her eyes tightly, as if she couldn’t bear it anymore, as if she regretted her own weakness.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Yeah… I’m okay. Thank you…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Y-yes, okay… Well… I…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I definitely saw what happened!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Sakura was far tenser than I’d expected&quot; — enough that the narrator fears she &quot;might not be able to speak satisfactorily.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The silence is measured on the page: &quot;Ten seconds. Twenty seconds.&quot; She looks further down and her face goes pale; Horikita’s prompt does not reach her.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator does not recognise the voice at first, and what identifies her is volume: &quot;What most struck me was the volume of her voice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The students in Class C threw the first punch. There’s no mistake about that!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The delivery carries force beyond her manner: &quot;She spoke so desperately that you wanted to believe she was telling the truth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p190-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the morning she comes anyway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p191-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6 open  the fighter who asks for honesty class d s room before the hearing  he closes his eyes and folds his arms  as if mentally preparing himself  then opens them and asks horikita to say whatever she has to say now   yeah  i m good  i was born ready   you might call me a complete idiot and make fun of me  but i m me  if you have something you want to say  say it now   ugh  you always act so high and mighty  lady  the bickering is affection in his idiom  the narrator notes he would have refused horikita s help outright if he truly hated her  kushida s send off    do your best  horikita san  sudou kun    is answered by sudou pumping his fist to show resolve","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p191-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p191-1\">Ch.6 open: the fighter who asks for honesty<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.191<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D’s room before the hearing; he closes his eyes and folds his arms &quot;as if mentally preparing himself,&quot; then opens them and asks Horikita to say whatever she has to say now.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Yeah… I’m good. I was born ready.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;You might call me a complete idiot and make fun of me, but I’m me. If you have something you want to say, say it now.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Ugh, you always act so high and mighty, lady.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The bickering is affection in his idiom; the narrator notes he would have refused Horikita’s help outright if he truly hated her.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Kushida’s send-off — &quot;Do your best, Horikita-san. Sudou-kun.&quot; — is answered by Sudou pumping his fist to show resolve.<span class=\"pg\">p.191<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p165-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2–5.3: told he will be there, and certain of the outcome<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p194-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: his account, and the traps in it<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 open  the rules she releases one at a time the faculty room before the hearing  hoshinomiya tries to tag along and chabashira pushes her back inside   what are you doing this time   whenever you sneak out  that s around the time i start to feel suspicious   of course you can t  you know that outsiders cannot participate   well then  shall we be going   of course not  this school does have rather complicated rules  but in cases such as these a settlement is reached between the homeroom teacher of the class in question  the concerned parties  and the student council  the venue is disclosed last  after horikita has already agreed to attend  the narrator calls it her habit of revealing  an important detail right at the last minute   if you want to stop  now s the time  horikita  the fourth floor student council room  she enters first and sets the proceedings in motion   sorry we re late   have you already met   this is sakagami sensei  the homeroom teacher for class c  now then   this is the student council president   well then  i would now like to discuss the violent incident that occurred last tuesday with the members of the student council  the involved parties  and their homeroom teachers  you may begin the proceedings  student council secretary tachibana   so  this is all by chance  the question is aimed at the president s claim of attending by choice  he does not answer it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\">Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.192–193<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The faculty room before the hearing; Hoshinomiya tries to tag along and Chabashira pushes her back inside. The fourth-floor student council room; she enters first and sets the proceedings in motion.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;What are you doing this time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Whenever you sneak out, that’s around the time I start to feel suspicious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Of course you can’t. You know that outsiders cannot participate.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, shall we be going?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course not. This school does have rather complicated rules, but in cases such as these a settlement is reached between the homeroom teacher of the class in question, the concerned parties, and the student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The venue is disclosed last, after Horikita has already agreed to attend; the narrator calls it her habit of revealing &quot;an important detail right at the last minute.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you want to stop, now’s the time, Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.192<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry we’re late.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have you already met?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is Sakagami-sensei, the homeroom teacher for Class C. Now then.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the student council president.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, I would now like to discuss the violent incident that occurred last Tuesday with the members of the student council, the involved parties, and their homeroom teachers. You may begin the proceedings, student council secretary Tachibana.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So, this is all by chance?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question is aimed at the president’s claim of attending by choice; he does not answer it.<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p163-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.2: the teacher who will not take the witness on trust<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6 sec  6 1  the president at the head of the table the student council room on the fourth floor  he sits in the back and does not look at his sister as she enters   because i am quite busy  there are certain agenda topics upon which i will defer  as a general rule  though  i would prefer to attend to these issues  as i m entrusted to lead this student council  chabashira s probe about whether his presence is chance does not move him at all  the narrator notes his record   class a on entry  student council secretary  president by december of his first year on an overwhelming vote   it would seem there s no objection  given the arguments we ve heard thus far   regardless which party called the other over  the fact remains that it was a one sided fight between sudou and the other students  we can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained  we have no choice but to come up with a conclusion based on that  he decides the case on visible injuries and closes the evidentiary question before class d has finished speaking  the narrator describes his intervention as wanting  to draw a conclusion as soon as possible","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the president at the head of the table<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–196<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The student council room on the fourth floor; he sits in the back and does not look at his sister as she enters.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Because I am quite busy, there are certain agenda topics upon which I will defer. As a general rule, though, I would prefer to attend to these issues, as I’m entrusted to lead this student council.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;It would seem there’s no objection, given the arguments we’ve heard thus far.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Regardless which party called the other over, the fact remains that it was a one-sided fight between Sudou and the other students. We can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained. We have no choice but to come up with a…<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Chabashira’s probe about whether his presence is chance does not move him at all; the narrator notes his record — Class A on entry, student council secretary, president by December of his first year on an overwhelming vote.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Regardless which party called the other over, the fact remains that it was a one-sided fight between Sudou and the other students. We can clearly see that from the injuries they sustained. We have no choice but to come up with a conclusion based on that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He decides the case on visible injuries and closes the evidentiary question before Class D has finished speaking; the narrator describes his intervention as wanting &quot;to draw a conclusion as soon as possible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: witness and photograph<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 1  frozen  then roused  then cross examining her brother s presence undoes her before testimony begins   horikita  horikita the younger sister  i mean couldn t hide her trembling  and the narrator concludes their kinship makes the room  extremely disadvantageous   hyah   w wait  s stop  stop  she is physically roused by the narrator s tickling and returns to the room glaring  with startling intensity   tch   excuse me  may i ask a question   earlier  you said that sudou kun called you over to the special building  but who exactly did sudou call  and why   please answer   so then  why exactly were you in the special building  ishizaki kun  you re not on the basketball team  so you have no connection to this case  i d think your presence there would be rather odd   so in other words  you felt the situation might turn violent   i see  so you brought along ishizaki kun as your bodyguard  since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting  just in case there was an emergency   i do have some knowledge of martial arts  if only to a certain extent  i understand that when you re fighting against multiple enemies  victory becomes exponentially more difficult  so i don t understand how you were defeated so handily  how the fight could be so one sided  when you had a skilled fighter like ishizaki kun with you   the primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the  energy  between opponents  in the event that you don t have any intention of fighting  or that you re nonviolent  the probability that you ll be hurt should be very low  especially when there are three of you  her cross examination turns the witness list into a contradiction  if ishizaki came as a bodyguard because sudo was reputed violent  a rehearsed nonviolent group should not have been beaten so one sidedly  the narrator credits the method as  very objective  grounded in evidence  rules  and her own logic  and notes komiya answers it with his actual injuries rather than with argument   it s true that sudou injured the other students  however  class c started the fight  there is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–200<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Hyah?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;W-wait. S-stop, stop!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Tch…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>13 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her brother’s presence undoes her before testimony begins: &quot;Horikita —Horikita the younger sister, I mean—couldn’t hide her trembling,&quot; and the narrator concludes their kinship makes the room &quot;extremely disadvantageous.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193–194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She is physically roused by the narrator’s tickling and returns to the room glaring &quot;with startling intensity.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196–197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Excuse me. May I ask a question?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Earlier, you said that Sudou-kun called you over to the special building. But who exactly did Sudou call, and why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please answer.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So then, why exactly were you in the special building, Ishizaki-kun? You’re not on the basketball team, so you have no connection to this case. I’d think your presence there would be rather odd.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So in other words, you felt the situation might turn violent?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So you brought along Ishizaki-kun as your bodyguard, since he was reputed to be rather good at fighting. Just in case there was an emergency.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I do have some knowledge of martial arts, if only to a certain extent. I understand that when you’re fighting against multiple enemies, victory becomes exponentially more difficult. So I don’t understand how you were defeated so handily, how the fight could be so one-sided, when you had a skilled fighter like Ishizaki-kun with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The primary factor in triggering a fight is the collision of the ‘energy’ between opponents. In the event that you don’t have any intention of fighting, or that you’re nonviolent, the probability that you’ll be hurt should be very low. Especially when there are three of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Her cross-examination turns the witness list into a contradiction: if Ishizaki came as a bodyguard because Sudō was reputed violent, a rehearsed nonviolent group should not have been beaten so one-sidedly.<span class=\"pg\">p.197–199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator credits the method as &quot;very objective, grounded in evidence, rules, and her own logic,&quot; and notes Komiya answers it with his actual injuries rather than with argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.198<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s true that Sudou injured the other students. However, Class C started the fight. There is one student witness who saw the entire incident and can attest to this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the hearing she is not ready for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p193-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"tachibana-akane","q":"tachibana akane ch 6 sec  6 1  the secretary who runs the hearing the student council room on the fourth floor  she receives the parties and opens the proceedings  student council secretary  short haired  and by her own account handles the bulk of proceedings  as usual   of course  considering the magnitude of this dispute  there are times when the student council president will take over  there are several unusual things about this incident  other than that  the bulk of the proceedings will be handled solely by tachibana  as usual  her summary is the hearing s only neutral account  both sides  versions set out  in an easy to understand manner  with no need for further explanation   based on the aforementioned facts  we would like for you to identify which version of events is true   komiya kun and two other members of the basketball club went to the special building after sudou kun called them there  there  they claim to have been beaten up in a one sided brawl  is this true  the question is posed to class d as a whole  the page does not assign it to a named student   please calm down  sudou kun  right now  we re merely listening to what both parties have to say  komiya kun  we ask that you too please show some restraint  and not interrupt   both parties insist that the other called them over  so the accounts conflict  however  the stories share some commonality  there was a dispute between sudou kun  komiya kun  and kondou kun  correct   picking fights   both sides have given their grievances  but now we have to come to a judgment with the collected evidence  she keeps the hearing on evidence while the room escalates  and asks the question that turns komiya s grievance into a concession of shared history","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p193-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html#sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p193-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the secretary who runs the hearing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.193–195<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The student council room on the fourth floor; she receives the parties and opens the proceedings.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Of course, considering the magnitude of this dispute, there are times when the student council president will take over. There are several unusual things about this incident. Other than that, the bulk of the proceedings will be…<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Based on the aforementioned facts, we would like for you to identify which version of events is true.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Komiya-kun and two other members of the basketball club went to the special building after Sudou-kun called them there. There, they claim to have been beaten up in a one-sided brawl. Is this true?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Student council secretary; short-haired, and by her own account handles the bulk of proceedings &quot;as usual.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course, considering the magnitude of this dispute, there are times when the student council president will take over. There are several unusual things about this incident. Other than that, the bulk of the proceedings will be handled solely by Tachibana, as usual.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.193<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her summary is the hearing&#x27;s only neutral account: both sides&#x27; versions set out &quot;in an easy-to-understand manner,&quot; with no need for further explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question is posed to Class D as a whole; the page does not assign it to a named student.<span class=\"pg\">p.194–195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please calm down, Sudou-kun. Right now, we’re merely listening to what both parties have to say. Komiya-kun, we ask that you too please show some restraint, and not interrupt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Both parties insist that the other called them over, so the accounts conflict. However, the stories share some commonality. There was a dispute between Sudou-kun, Komiya-kun, and Kondou-kun, correct?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;&#x27;Picking fights&#x27;?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Both sides have given their grievances, but now we have to come to a judgment with the collected evidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She keeps the hearing on evidence while the room escalates, and asks the question that turns Komiya&#x27;s grievance into a concession of shared history.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p199-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the room&#x27;s procedure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p194-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6 sec  6 1  his account  and the traps in it  what those guys said was a lie  i was the one that got called over to the special building   that day  after practice  komiya and kondou asked me to go to the special building  honestly  i thought it was kind of annoying  but i also thought it might ve been because they were always hostile towards me  so  i went to meet them   don t screw with me  komiya  you were the one who called me  you jerk  irritated  he strikes the desk   immediate silence followed   not one bit of what komiya said was true  those guys are just jealous of my talent  when i practice  they constantly get in my way  that s the truth   that s a lie  they attacked first  it was self defense  his temper supplies the other side s best evidence  the veins on his forehead and the desk strike are read by the room as confirmation of violence   w wait  i can t accept that  it s just because those guys were a bunch of wimps   b but  hey  i was fighting against three people  three people  the wimps line hands sakagami the question that nearly ends the case   whether overwhelming force against weaker opponents can be self defence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p194-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p194-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: his account, and the traps in it<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.194–196<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;What those guys said was a lie. I was the one that got called over to the special building,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;That day, after practice, Komiya and Kondou asked me to go to the special building. Honestly, I thought it was kind of annoying, but I also thought it might’ve been because they were always hostile towards me. So, I went to meet…<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Don’t screw with me, Komiya! You were the one who called me, you jerk!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That day, after practice, Komiya and Kondou asked me to go to the special building. Honestly, I thought it was kind of annoying, but I also thought it might’ve been because they were always hostile towards me. So, I went to meet them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.194<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Irritated, he strikes the desk; &quot;Immediate silence followed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Not one bit of what Komiya said was true. Those guys are just jealous of my talent. When I practice, they constantly get in my way. That’s the truth.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s a lie. They attacked first. It was self-defense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> His temper supplies the other side’s best evidence: the veins on his forehead and the desk strike are read by the room as confirmation of violence.<span class=\"pg\">p.195<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;W-wait! I can’t accept that! It’s just because those guys were a bunch of wimps!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;B-but, hey. I was fighting against three people! Three people!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The wimps line hands Sakagami the question that nearly ends the case — whether overwhelming force against weaker opponents can be self-defence.<span class=\"pg\">p.196<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the fighter who asks for honesty<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise he refuses<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6 1  the witness she dismisses  why are you in such a hurry  sakagami sensei  when sakagami moves to strike the witness  she agrees with him instead of resisting   you d think that chabashira sensei would ally herself with class d  but that didn t seem to be the case   you re certainly right that this is a waste of time  so i suppose we have no choice  you can come down now  sakura  the order is what forces sakura s outburst  the chapter does not say whether chabashira expected it  and the narrator records only that she  ordered sakura to leave  almost as if she d lost interest","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–200<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Why are you in such a hurry, Sakagami-sensei?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;You’re certainly right that this is a waste of time, so I suppose we have no choice. You can come down now, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> When Sakagami moves to strike the witness, she agrees with him instead of resisting: &quot;You’d think that Chabashira-sensei would ally herself with Class D, but that didn’t seem to be the case.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199–200<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The order is what forces Sakura’s outburst; the chapter does not say whether Chabashira expected it, and the narrator records only that she &quot;ordered Sakura to leave, almost as if she’d lost interest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.200<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p192-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the rules she releases one at a time<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6 sec  6 1  witness and photograph  are you finished with your claims now  class d  the question lands after horikita s martial arts argument and is described as  few and icy  carrying the implication that class d should have said nothing   i ll allow it  however  please answer more quickly next time   i ll allow it   but sakagami sensei  don t you think this photo is different  he is the one who spots the decisive photograph among the set and slides it across to sakagami  converting sakura s self portraits into evidence of the fight   thank you  sakura san  the thanks is the only courtesy the hearing gives her before the cross examination resumes","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: witness and photograph<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–204<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Are you finished with your claims now, Class D?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;I’ll allow it. However, please answer more quickly next time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.197<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;I’ll allow it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The question lands after Horikita’s martial-arts argument and is described as &quot;few and icy,&quot; carrying the implication that Class D should have said nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But Sakagami-sensei, don’t you think this photo is different?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> He is the one who spots the decisive photograph among the set and slides it across to Sakagami, converting Sakura’s self-portraits into evidence of the fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Thank you, Sakura-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The thanks is the only courtesy the hearing gives her before the cross-examination resumes.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the president at the head of the table<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p199-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu tachibana-akane","q":"tachibana akane ch 6 sec  6 1  the room s procedure three lines in the witness sequence carry no speaker tag    1 d  sakura airi san   you may begin your testimony  if you wouldn t mind  sakura san  and  earlier   if class d has no further proof to offer  would you mind if we continued the proceedings  they sit where the secretary has been speaking  but the translation does not name her  so they are recorded as gaps  she walks to sakura  hesitates  then takes the photographs and hands them to the president   president   thank you very much  please take your seat now   will you take your seat now  the second request is made  as if she suspected that horikita couldn t hear her  and horikita still does not sit  after the hearing she locks the student council room door while the president speaks to ayanokoji  she defers the unusual case to him and runs everything else  and she is the one who closes the room behind him","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p199-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html#sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p199-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the room&#x27;s procedure<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.199–210<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;President.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Thank you very much. Please take your seat now,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Will you take your seat now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Three lines in the witness sequence carry no speaker tag — &quot;1-D, Sakura Airi-san.&quot;, &quot;You may begin your testimony, if you wouldn&#x27;t mind, Sakura-san.&quot; and, earlier, &quot;If Class D has no further proof to offer, would you mind if we continued the proceedings?&quot; They sit where the secretary has been speaking, but the translation does not name her, so they are recorded as gaps.<span class=\"pg\">p.199<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She walks to Sakura, hesitates, then takes the photographs and hands them to the president.<span class=\"pg\">p.203–204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The second request is made &quot;as if she suspected that Horikita couldn&#x27;t hear her,&quot; and Horikita still does not sit.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After the hearing she locks the student council room door while the president speaks to Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> She defers the unusual case to him and runs everything else, and she is the one who closes the room behind him.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the secretary who runs the hearing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p243-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5–7.6: running the room and the seat she does not expect to fill<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the performance of giving up his conclusion about sakagami before the photos   no matter what response we volleyed back  i was convinced that he d do anything to block us   horikita  are we really out of options   i m not very smart  so i can t really come up with a solution  i do  however  think that we probably should accept the compromise that you have offered us  sakagami sensei   we have no definitive proof of sudou s innocence  i suppose i should say such evidence just doesn t exist  if this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store  a greater number of students would have been around to see it  and there probably would have been sound evidence  there s no record of anyone watching this scene unfold  since this event took place in the special building  where there weren t any people around  there s nothing we can do   i understand why we re having this discussion  no matter how much we appeal to the contrary  class c won t admit that they lied  sudou won t admit that he lied  either  we really would just keep going back and forth  honestly  it s getting to the point where i would ve been happier never having had this discussion in the first place  don t you agree  the surrender speech is a performance aimed at horikita  not at sakagami   i spoke as if we were accepting defeat  he had decided to speak  perhaps out of respect for sakura s earlier courage  the move depends on sakagami taking it literally  which he does   in other words  as a declaration of defeat","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.202–206<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Horikita, are we really out of options?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I’m not very smart, so I can’t really come up with a solution. I do, however, think that we probably should accept the compromise that you have offered us, Sakagami-sensei,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;We have no definitive proof of Sudou’s innocence. I suppose I should say such evidence just doesn’t exist. If this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store, a greater number of students would have been around…<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His conclusion about Sakagami before the photos: &quot;no matter what response we volleyed back, I was convinced that he’d do anything to block us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We have no definitive proof of Sudou’s innocence. I suppose I should say such evidence just doesn’t exist. If this event had occurred in a classroom or the convenience store, a greater number of students would have been around to see it, and there probably would have been sound evidence. There’s no record of anyone watching this scene unfold. Since this event took place in the special building, where there weren’t any people around, there’s nothing we can do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand why we’re having this discussion. No matter how much we appeal to the contrary, Class C won’t admit that they lied. Sudou won’t admit that he lied, either. We really would just keep going back and forth. Honestly, it’s getting to the point where I would’ve been happier never having had this discussion in the first place. Don’t you agree?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The surrender speech is a performance aimed at Horikita, not at Sakagami: &quot;I spoke as if we were accepting defeat.&quot; He had decided to speak &quot;perhaps out of respect for Sakura’s earlier courage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The move depends on Sakagami taking it literally, which he does: &quot;In other words, as a declaration of defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the hearing he cannot fix<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 sec  6 1  the photographs  that s  well  that s  i didn t want to get involved   because i m not very good at talking with other people   that s  i m just telling the truth   n no  that s not it   if you want proof  i ll give it to you  she slams her hand on the desk and throws down what look like  a few small  rectangular pieces of paper    photographs  not paper   this is proof that i was in the special building that day   i m i was looking for places where no one was around so i could take pictures of myself  the pictures also show the date and time  which proves that i was there when i said   a digital camera  the photographs show her in the other life   this sakura wore a lovely expression that looked both similar and dissimilar to the sakura with us now  it was the idol  shizuku  the line presenting the decisive photo is untagged in the translation    i think that you ll believe i was there after seeing this    so it is recorded here without a speaker  the last photo shows the fight itself   the setting sun bathed the hallway in dusky light  and the image appears to be  what had happened immediately after sudou hit ishizaki","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.202–205<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;That’s… Well, that’s… I didn’t want to get involved…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Because I’m not very good at talking with other people…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;That’s… I’m just…telling the truth…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no, that’s not it…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.202<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you want proof… I’ll give it to you!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She slams her hand on the desk and throws down what look like &quot;a few small, rectangular pieces of paper&quot; — photographs, not paper.<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is proof that I was in the special building that day!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m…I was looking for places where no one was around so I could take pictures of myself. The pictures also show the date and time, which proves that I was there when I said.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A digital…camera.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The photographs show her in the other life: &quot;this Sakura wore a lovely expression that looked both similar and dissimilar to the Sakura with us now. It was the idol, Shizuku.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line presenting the decisive photo is untagged in the translation — &quot;I think that you’ll believe I was there after seeing…this.&quot; — so it is recorded here without a speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The last photo shows the fight itself: &quot;The setting sun bathed the hallway in dusky light,&quot; and the image appears to be &quot;what had happened immediately after Sudou hit Ishizaki.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.204<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the testimony that nearly does not start<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 1  the answer to the false witness charge  that is not the case  it is certainly true that sakura san is not good at speaking before others  however  it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today  otherwise  she most likely would not  even if we d asked her  don t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly  we would have found a replacement  sakagami answers it by claiming the choice of a poor speaker is itself the staging   it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.203<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not…<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That is not the case. It is certainly true that Sakura-san is not good at speaking before others. However, it is precisely because she witnessed the incident that she is standing here today. Otherwise, she most likely would not, even if we’d asked her. Don’t you think that if we needed someone who could speak boldly, we would have found a replacement?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Sakagami answers it by claiming the choice of a poor speaker is itself the staging: &quot;it would establish a sense of realism that you yourself could not.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.203<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p193-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: frozen, then roused, then cross-examining<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 6 sec  6 1  the compromise she will not refuse  compromise   we seem to have already reached a logical conclusion  there s no reason to refuse sakagami sensei s proposal  she treats the settlement as arithmetic rather than advocacy  the proposal is  certainly a reasonable compromise  and she says so in front of her own student   if this matter required some extra time before retrial  then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period  in other words  the amount of time granted should be enough for this case  extensions are only offered under special circumstances  the disciplinary settlement is heard by the two homeroom teachers  the concerned students and the student council  the retrial window is fixed by the council and cannot be extended on request  she warns horikita she can still withdraw  then closes the only procedural door horikita asks to reopen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.205–209<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Compromise?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;We seem to have already reached a logical conclusion. There’s no reason to refuse Sakagami-sensei’s proposal,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;If this matter required some extra time before retrial, then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period. In other words, the amount of time granted should be enough for this case. Extensions are…<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She treats the settlement as arithmetic rather than advocacy: the proposal is &quot;certainly a reasonable compromise,&quot; and she says so in front of her own student.<span class=\"pg\">p.206<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If this matter required some extra time before retrial, then the student council president would have offered a sufficient grace period. In other words, the amount of time granted should be enough for this case. Extensions are only offered under special circumstances,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The disciplinary settlement is heard by the two homeroom teachers, the concerned students and the student council; the retrial window is fixed by the council and cannot be extended on request.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She warns Horikita she can still withdraw, then closes the only procedural door Horikita asks to reopen.<span class=\"pg\">p.192, 209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the witness she dismisses<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p205-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6 sec  6 1  the compromise he refuses  you jerk  he stands ready to fly out of his chair  then grabs his own arms and pins himself down  the restraint is new and deliberate  the same anger that struck the desk at p 195 is now turned on himself   don t screw around  this isn t a joke   horikita   h hey  the bellow is his only answer to her closing statement  and he cannot tell that it is a performance  after she refuses to sit   sudou s clearly irritated bellow  fills the silence  he still does not understand the reversal until she states it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p205-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p205-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise he refuses<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.205–208<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;You jerk!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Don’t screw around! This isn’t a joke!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Horikita!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He stands ready to fly out of his chair, then grabs his own arms and pins himself down.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The restraint is new and deliberate: the same anger that struck the desk at p.195 is now turned on himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.205<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;H-hey!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bellow is his only answer to her closing statement, and he cannot tell that it is a performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> After she refuses to sit, &quot;Sudou’s clearly irritated bellow&quot; fills the silence; he still does not understand the reversal until she states it.<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p194-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: his account, and the traps in it<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 1  the false concession  then the refusal  i understand   i think that sudou  who caused the incident  has a problem  he doesn t ever stop to consider his actions  which inconveniences everyone around him  he has a history of getting in fights  he s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him  in the event of an uproar such as this  well  it should be obvious who caused it   you need to understand  sudou  your attitude caused all of this   this is why i wasn t motivated at all to help sudou kun in the beginning  i knew that even if i forced myself to lend a hand  he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again  the closing statement is a trap  she lets sakagami treat it as surrender  then refuses to sit  and the silence is what gives her the floor back   he should reflect on his actions  however  not in this particular case  when i say he should reflect  i mean that he should look back on his past actions  in regards to this particular incident  however  i don t think sudou kun did anything wrong  this was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance  i m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by class c  i have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat   if you did not understand  i will say it once again  we claim that sudou kun is completely innocent  therefore  we cannot accept his suspension from school  even for just one day   sudou kun is the victim  just as the witness testified  please do not make any errors in your judgment  the reversal is made for sakura s sake as much as sudo s  the narrator guesses she  had to be brave in front of sakura   would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene  the line answering the president s question to class d    i haven t lied  everything we ve said has been the truth    is untagged in the translation  it is recorded as class d s answer  not attributed to her by name on the page","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.207–209<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I understand…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and…<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You need to understand, Sudou. Your attitude caused all of this.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think that Sudou, who caused the incident, has a problem. He doesn’t ever stop to consider his actions, which inconveniences everyone around him. He has a history of getting in fights. He’s the type to raise his voice and fists right away whenever something displeases him. In the event of an uproar such as this, well, it should be obvious who caused it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is why I wasn’t motivated at all to help Sudou-kun in the beginning. I knew that even if I forced myself to lend a hand, he would just repeat the same mistakes again and again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.207<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The closing statement is a trap: she lets Sakagami treat it as surrender, then refuses to sit, and the silence is what gives her the floor back.<span class=\"pg\">p.207–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He should reflect on his actions. However, not in this particular case. When I say he should reflect, I mean that he should look back on his past actions. In regards to this particular incident, however, I don’t think Sudou-kun did anything wrong. This was not an unfortunate event that occurred merely by chance. I’m convinced that this was a deliberate move made by Class C. I have absolutely no intention of meekly accepting defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you did not understand, I will say it once again. We claim that Sudou-kun is completely innocent. Therefore, we cannot accept his suspension from school, even for just one day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sudou-kun is the victim, just as the witness testified. Please do not make any errors in your judgment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reversal is made for Sakura’s sake as much as Sudō’s: the narrator guesses she &quot;had to be brave in front of Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Would be possible to have a little more time before we reconvene?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line answering the president’s question to Class D — &quot;I haven’t lied. Everything we’ve said has been the truth.&quot; — is untagged in the translation; it is recorded as Class D’s answer, not attributed to her by name on the page.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p203-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the answer to the false-witness charge<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6 sec  6 1  the retrial and the expulsion warning  so then what do you mean  it is the first time he looks directly at his sister in the hearing   that s enough  continuing this discussion would just be a waste of time   what i ve learned today is that each side has an exact opposite claim  in that case  one side is propagating an extremely malicious falsehood   i ll ask you  class c  have you lied to us today   well  what about you  class d   then we will regroup here for a retrial tomorrow at 4 00 pm  if by then it hasn t been clearly established which party has lied  or in the event no one admits that they were at fault  we will pass judgment based on the evidence we ve collected thus far  of course  in that case we may have to consider the possibility of expulsion from this school  that is all  the retrial is set for 4 00 pm the next day  and if neither side is proven to have lied or admits fault  judgment falls back on the collected evidence with expulsion as a possible outcome  the escalation is deliberate  the charge shifts from a fight to which class lied to the school","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.208–209<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;So then…what do you mean?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;That’s enough. Continuing this discussion would just be a waste of time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;What I’ve learned today is that each side has an exact opposite claim. In that case, one side is propagating an extremely malicious falsehood.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> It is the first time he looks directly at his sister in the hearing.<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll ask you, Class C. Have you lied to us today?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, what about you, Class D?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then we will regroup here for a retrial tomorrow at 4:00 PM. If by then it hasn’t been clearly established which party has lied, or in the event no one admits that they were at fault, we will pass judgment based on the evidence we’ve collected thus far. Of course, in that case we may have to consider the possibility of expulsion from this school. That is all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The retrial is set for 4:00 PM the next day, and if neither side is proven to have lied or admits fault, judgment falls back on the collected evidence with expulsion as a possible outcome.<span class=\"pg\">p.208–209<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The escalation is deliberate: the charge shifts from a fight to which class lied to the school.<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: witness and photograph<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor conversation<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 sec  6 1  after the hearing  i tried my absolute hardest to speak up during the discussion  but do we even have a chance  horikita   you understand that we won t solve this problem just by being stubborn  won t that just hurt more people in the process   i m sorry  ayanokouji kun  if i d only stepped forward in the very beginning  everything would have been fine  but  everything turned out this way because i didn t have the courage   but   i i i just told the truth   but it s all my fault  hic   but  i   but  i  wasn t i completely useless  the narrator s read of the crying   sakura seemed to be the type who bottled up her feelings  and the hearing  might have been an important step forward for her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.209–212<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I tried my absolute hardest to speak up during the discussion, but do we even have a chance? Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.209<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;You understand that we won’t solve this problem just by being stubborn. Won’t that just hurt more people in the process?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I’m sorry, Ayanokouji-kun… If I’d only stepped forward in the very beginning, everything would have been fine, but… Everything turned out this way because I didn’t have the courage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I-I…I just…told the truth…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But…it’s all my fault… Hic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But… I…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But… I… Wasn’t I completely useless?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator’s read of the crying: &quot;Sakura seemed to be the type who bottled up her feelings,&quot; and the hearing &quot;might have been an important step forward for her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p202-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the photographs<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: walking out<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-manabu ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 1  the corridor  and what he will not concede  it would ve ended the same even if you had stepped forward at the beginning  they would ve fought to discredit your testimony simply because the witness came from class d  the result would be the same   i m not exactly zhuge liang or kuroda kanbei  i don t have any plans   hyperbole  you mean  i don t think so   i believe her  i believe sakura s testimony   i didn t say that i want to believe her  i said i believe her  those mean different things   that s not up to me  your sister will prove it  if sakura isn t lying  then she will find a way to convince everyone  the first long conversation between them without a crisis forcing it  the narrator finds him  easy to talk to now  and credits  a superior understanding of human nature  he separates belief from wish in one sentence  and refuses the president s framing that his support is merely class loyalty","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210–212<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It would’ve ended the same even if you had stepped forward at the beginning. They would’ve fought to discredit your testimony simply because the witness came from Class D. The result would be the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I’m not exactly Zhuge Liang or Kuroda Kanbei. I don’t have any plans.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Hyperbole, you mean? I don’t think so.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I believe her. I believe Sakura’s testimony,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I didn’t say that I want to believe her. I said I believe her. Those mean different things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not up to me. Your sister will prove it. If Sakura isn’t lying, then she will find a way to convince everyone.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> The first long conversation between them without a crisis forcing it; the narrator finds him &quot;easy to talk to now&quot; and credits &quot;a superior understanding of human nature.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210–212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He separates belief from wish in one sentence, and refuses the president’s framing that his support is merely class loyalty.<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p202-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the performance of giving up<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 6 sec  6 1  the corridor conversation  you re still here   what are you planning to do   i thought that when you came here with suzune  you d unveil some kind of master plan   so does that mean when suzune claimed sudou was completely innocent  she was merely getting carried away   i see   then there s what you said  sakura   eyewitness testimony and pictorial evidence certainly carry weight during deliberation  however  please keep in mind that how much we value the evidence is determined by how much we trust in its believability  no matter what you do  the evidence s legitimacy is reduced because you are a student from class d  no matter how detailed your account  we cannot accept it as one hundred percent true   if you can t prove it  then it s little more than nonsense   since she s a class d student  it s only natural that you would want to believe her   so can you prove it  can you prove she s not lying  the narrator s revised estimate  the first meeting left a bad impression  but  i found him easy to talk to now  and he credits  a superior understanding of human nature  he  chuckled softly  then smiled  at the claim that suzune will prove it   the chapter does not say whether the smile is disbelief or interest  he ignores her until she refuses to sit  then asks her meaning and listens  the hearing is the first time he treats her as an opponent rather than a disappointment  he thanks her for the photograph and then tells her the evidence cannot be accepted because of where she is enrolled  the corridor exchange is the longest conversation they have had  he tests whether the narrator has a plan and accepts the answer that suzune will supply it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor conversation<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210–212<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;You’re still here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;What are you planning to do?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;I thought that when you came here with Suzune, you’d unveil some kind of master plan.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So does that mean when Suzune claimed Sudou was completely innocent, she was merely getting carried away?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Then there’s what you said, Sakura.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Eyewitness testimony and pictorial evidence certainly carry weight during deliberation. However, please keep in mind that how much we value the evidence is determined by how much we trust in its believability. No matter what you do, the evidence’s legitimacy is reduced because you are a student from Class D. No matter how detailed your account, we cannot accept it as one hundred percent true.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you can’t prove it, then it’s little more than nonsense.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Since she’s a Class D student, it’s only natural that you would want to believe her.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So can you prove it? Can you prove she’s not lying?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The narrator’s revised estimate: the first meeting left a bad impression, but &quot;I found him easy to talk to now,&quot; and he credits &quot;a superior understanding of human nature.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He &quot;chuckled softly, then smiled&quot; at the claim that Suzune will prove it — the chapter does not say whether the smile is disbelief or interest.<span class=\"pg\">p.212<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He ignores her until she refuses to sit, then asks her meaning and listens; the hearing is the first time he treats her as an opponent rather than a disappointment.<span class=\"pg\">p.193–208<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He thanks her for the photograph and then tells her the evidence cannot be accepted because of where she is enrolled.<span class=\"pg\">p.204–211<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The corridor exchange is the longest conversation they have had; he tests whether the narrator has a plan and accepts the answer that Suzune will supply it.<span class=\"pg\">p.210–212<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p208-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the retrial and the expulsion warning<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 1  what she says to sakura on the way out  i won t give up  i will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end   i have no intention of losing  well then  i must excuse myself  she leaves immediately after the promise rather than staying to comfort sakura  and the chapter reads the haste as strategy  not coldness","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I won’t give up. I will keep fighting to support your testimony until the end,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I have no intention of losing. Well then, I must excuse myself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She leaves immediately after the promise rather than staying to comfort Sakura, and the chapter reads the haste as strategy, not coldness.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p207-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the false concession, then the refusal<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p210-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 6 sec  6 1  after the hearing he leaves the student council room behind horikita without a recorded line  the chapter gives him no scene with sakura after the testimony he did not defend","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p210-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p210-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.210<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He leaves the student council room behind Horikita without a recorded line; the chapter gives him no scene with Sakura after the testimony he did not defend.<span class=\"pg\">p.210<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise he refuses<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p242-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: waiting for the retrial to start<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2  leaving the hearing  and class b s offer the walk back after the hearing  sakura has stopped crying and the silence between them is comfortable   i m glad  when i was a kid  i used to cry in front of people all the time   yeah  i cried a lot  maybe 10 or 20 times in front of other people   it s not just me  horikita  kushida  and sudou do  too  all of our classmates believe you  the entranceway  ichinose and kanzaki are waiting  and sakura s unfinished sentence is lost   were you waiting for us   sorry  sakura  can we continue this later   no  it s fine   well  if sudou even got as little as one day s suspension  class c would win  his framing of the offer   the compromise had been a trap  a sweet trap set to lure us to our defeat   i see  i think so  too   our leader gave us her decision  we ll fight to the bitter end   you re still willing to help us  kanzaki argues for the compromise and then stays to search for evidence anyway  the narrator s verdict is  these were really good people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213–215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The walk back after the hearing; Sakura has stopped crying and the silence between them is comfortable. The entranceway; Ichinose and Kanzaki are waiting, and Sakura’s unfinished sentence is lost.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I’m glad. When I was a kid, I used to cry in front of people all the time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Yeah, I cried a lot. Maybe 10 or 20 times in front of other people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;It’s not just me. Horikita, Kushida, and Sudou do, too. All of our classmates believe you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Were you waiting for us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sorry, Sakura. Can we continue this later?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, it’s fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, if Sudou even got as little as one day’s suspension, Class C would win.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His framing of the offer: &quot;the compromise had been a trap. A sweet trap set to lure us to our defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. I think so, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Our leader gave us her decision. We’ll fight to the bitter end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re still willing to help us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Kanzaki argues for the compromise and then stays to search for evidence anyway; the narrator’s verdict is &quot;These were really good people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214–215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor, and what he will not concede<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 6 sec  6 2  named among the people who believe sakura ayanokoji tells sakura that the belief is not his alone    horikita  kushida  and sudou do  too  all of our classmates believe you  her part is reported by him  not shown in this chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Ayanokōji tells Sakura that the belief is not his alone — &quot;Horikita, Kushida, and Sudou do, too. All of our classmates believe you.&quot; Her part is reported by him, not shown in this chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p191-1\">← Before: Ch.6 open: the send-off<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 6 sec  6 2  walking out  i let you see something so embarrassing   it s been such a long time since i cried in front of someone  i feel a little relieved  actually   i had no idea that you were like that  ayanokouji kun  that s completely unlike the image i have of you   i was really happy when you said that you believed me   yeah  but you came out and told me directly  ayanokouji kun  you said it   you gave me courage  i was happy   u um  well  i don t think i should be saying this now  but   actually  i  right now   oh  no  it s nothing  i just wanted to say that i would try my best  i ll be brave  the sentence she begins at the entranceway is cut off by ichinose s arrival and never resumed  she opens her shoe locker  gives the smaller answer  and hurries out when the narrator calls after her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: walking out<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.213–214<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I let you see something so embarrassing…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;It’s been such a long time since I cried in front of someone. I feel a little relieved, actually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I had no idea that you were like that, Ayanokouji-kun. That’s completely unlike the image I have of you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was really happy…when you said that you believed me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah… But you came out and told me directly, Ayanokouji-kun. You said it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You gave me courage. I was happy,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;U-um, well… I don’t think I should be saying this now, but…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.213<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Actually… I… Right now…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, no, it’s nothing. I just…wanted to say that I would try my best. I’ll be brave.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The sentence she begins at the entranceway is cut off by Ichinose’s arrival and never resumed; she opens her shoe locker, gives the smaller answer, and hurries out when the narrator calls after her.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p209-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p214-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 6 sec  6 2  waiting at the entranceway the entranceway after the hearing  ichinose and kanzaki have been waiting   on tenterhooks about the trial s results   yahoo  you re really late  huh   we were wondering what happened   i m sorry  was this a bad time  the apology lands on the exact sentence sakura was about to finish  the narrator lets the moment go rather than reopen it   i see  so  you rejected the compromise  huh  class d is insisting on sudou s innocence until the very end   but like ayanokouji kun says  sudou s suspension would be a loss for class d  if sudou were suspended due to his bad behavior  then his chances of being a team regular would probably vanish  he d be back to square one   if you think so  shouldn t you have stopped it   if you re brought back into a retrial  you ll inevitably lose  just like kanzaki says  obtaining a not guilty verdict is virtually impossible   are you still going to fight  even without new evidence or testimony  she argues the case is unwinnable and then offers to work it anyway   the contradiction the chapter lets stand   hmm  well  i don t think we ll be able to obtain any more leads  but i ll go check what information i can gather from the internet  she laughs while offering help  though it wouldn t have been odd for her to wash her hands off us at this point","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p214-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p214-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: waiting at the entranceway<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.214–215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The entranceway after the hearing; Ichinose and Kanzaki have been waiting, &quot;on tenterhooks about the trial’s results.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Yahoo! You’re really late, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;We were wondering what happened.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I’m sorry. Was this a bad time?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The apology lands on the exact sentence Sakura was about to finish; the narrator lets the moment go rather than reopen it.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So, you rejected the compromise, huh? Class D is insisting on Sudou’s innocence until the very end?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But like Ayanokouji-kun says, Sudou’s suspension would be a loss for Class D. If Sudou were suspended due to his bad behavior, then his chances of being a team regular would probably vanish. He’d be back to square one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you think so, shouldn’t you have stopped it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you’re brought back into a retrial, you’ll inevitably lose. Just like Kanzaki says, obtaining a not-guilty verdict is virtually impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Are you still going to fight? Even without new evidence or testimony?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She argues the case is unwinnable and then offers to work it anyway — the contradiction the chapter lets stand.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm. Well, I don’t think we’ll be able to obtain any more leads, but I’ll go check what information I can gather from the Internet.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> She laughs while offering help &quot;though it wouldn’t have been odd for her to wash her hands off us at this point.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: a message board, a leaked past, and a screen<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request, and the price<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p214-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji ch 6 sec  6 2  the one who wanted the compromise the entranceway after the hearing  he has been waiting with ichinose for the result  he is present as ichinose s second rather than as a party to the case  the narrator records his position first through disagreement   kanzaki in particular insisted that we d made the wrong choice   the fact remains that he hit the other students  your opponents made a concession because of corroboration from the witness and her evidence  you should ve accepted the compromise   he might not just be sent back to square one  it might be worse  actually  if the school knew both sides shared the responsibility  they d take that into account when assigning punishments  however  if sudou s share of the blame increases tomorrow  it ll be bad news  his argument is institutional  not moral  a shared fault settlement caps the loss  while a retrial can increase sudou s share of blame   i ll do my absolute best to look for more evidence or another witness   we re in too deep now  besides  it s like we said before  we can t forgive liars  he loses the argument and then works the losing side anyway  the narrator s verdict is  these were really good people","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p214-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p214-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the one who wanted the compromise<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.214–215<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The entranceway after the hearing; he has been waiting with Ichinose for the result.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;The fact remains that he hit the other students. Your opponents made a concession because of corroboration from the witness and her evidence. You should’ve accepted the compromise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;He might not just be sent back to square one. It might be worse, actually. If the school knew both sides shared the responsibility, they’d take that into account when assigning punishments. However, if Sudou’s share of the blame…<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;I’ll do my absolute best to look for more evidence or another witness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is present as Ichinose&#x27;s second rather than as a party to the case.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narrator records his position first through disagreement: &quot;Kanzaki in particular insisted that we’d made the wrong choice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He might not just be sent back to square one. It might be worse, actually. If the school knew both sides shared the responsibility, they’d take that into account when assigning punishments. However, if Sudou’s share of the blame increases tomorrow, it’ll be bad news.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> His argument is institutional, not moral: a shared-fault settlement caps the loss, while a retrial can increase Sudou&#x27;s share of blame.<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’re in too deep now. Besides, it’s like we said before. We can’t forgive liars.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He loses the argument and then works the losing side anyway; the narrator&#x27;s verdict is &quot;These were really good people.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.215<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p216-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: what the request costs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 2  the request she makes of class b  i sincerely appreciate the offer  but it s not necessary   we cannot get sudou acquitted  even if a new witness were to come from class a or b  it would be impossible  however there is something i would like you to prepare for us  it is the only possible solution   i understand that i m in no position to ask this   the burden i d be placing upon you is exceptionally great  but   you re certainly right about that  well then  if i can convince you  will you cooperate with us   you should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy   just before the deliberation ended  only by chance  though   don t worry about that part  i ve confirmed it   if you ask the professor to assist us  it should be good  i ll talk to him   sure  i promise   well then  ayanokouji kun  there s something i d like you to help me with   helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time consuming  she has a plan before the hearing ends and has already verified that its material exists by the time she explains it in the entranceway  the plan requires a lie from a person who hates lying  horikita acknowledges the burden instead of softening it  and ichinose supplies the justification herself","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.216–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I sincerely appreciate the offer, but it’s not necessary.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;We cannot get Sudou acquitted. Even if a new witness were to come from Class A or B, it would be impossible. However…there is something I would like you to prepare for us. It is the only possible solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I understand that I’m in no position to ask this,&quot; &quot;The burden I’d be placing upon you is exceptionally great. But—&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re certainly right about that. Well then, if I can convince you, will you cooperate with us?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You should understand the risks as well as the usefulness of this strategy,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Just before the deliberation ended. Only by chance, though.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t worry about that part. I’ve confirmed it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you ask the Professor to assist us, it should be good. I’ll talk to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sure. I promise.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well then, Ayanokouji-kun. There’s something I’d like you to help me with.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Helping others is fundamentally bothersome and time-consuming.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> She has a plan before the hearing ends and has already verified that its material exists by the time she explains it in the entranceway.<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> The plan requires a lie from a person who hates lying; Horikita acknowledges the burden instead of softening it, and Ichinose supplies the justification herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: what she says to Sakura on the way out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">→ After: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p216-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 6 sec  6 2  the request  and the price  not necessary  what do you mean  horikita san   preparing something   oh  that s going to be a really hard request   ah  no  well  this should be within the range of what we can do  i think  that s because i plan to figure out what s happening to class d  i ve got tons and tons of things i want to know  but  well  maybe it would be better for you not to tell us why   when did you come up with this   that an incredible move  i went to the scene of the crime and even i didn t think of that  or  i guess i should say  i was completely in the dark about it  it wasn t even close to what i could imagine   an unusual idea  you can probably anticipate the results  too  but does such a thing even exist   ha ha  yeah  you might be right  it s a change for me  but it s certainly one way of doing things   well  since a lie started all this trouble  maybe it ll take another lie to close the books on this incident  that s what i think  anyway  the reply that follows    mmmhmm  i see  an eye for an eye  a lie for a lie  yeah  but is that even possible  i wonder  i can t imagine such a thing would be easy to obtain    is untagged  it is not assigned to her here   hey  kanzaki kun  did you help us so that we would outpace class c   but i was just thinking  perhaps what we re doing right now might end up coming back to bite you in the ass later   man  i completely neglected to calculate the fact that class d has a girl like you  she takes out her phone and hands it over   i ll lend this to you  please return it later  her cooperation is explicitly costly to her principles  the plan depends on a lie  and  for someone like ichinose  who hated lying  it was a harsh request  the compliment is professional and ungrudging   she names horikita as a factor class d has that she failed to price in  kanzaki warns her the favor may be turned against class b later  and she accepts that risk without extracting a condition","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p216-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request, and the price<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.216–218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Not necessary? What do you mean, Horikita-san?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Preparing something?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Oh… That’s going to be a really hard request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, no. Well, this should be within the range of what we can do, I think. That’s because I plan to figure out what’s happening to Class D. I’ve got tons and tons of things I want to know, but… Well, maybe it would be better for you not to tell us why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When did you come up with this?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That…an incredible move. I went to the scene of the crime and even I didn’t think of that. Or, I guess I should say, I was completely in the dark about it. It wasn’t even close to what I could imagine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;An unusual idea. You can probably anticipate the results, too. But does such a thing even exist?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha, yeah. You might be right. It’s a change for me. But…it’s certainly one way of doing things.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, since a lie started all this trouble, maybe it’ll take another lie to close the books on this incident. That’s what I think, anyway.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply that follows — &quot;Mmmhmm, I see. An eye for an eye, a lie for a lie, yeah? But is that even possible, I wonder? I can’t imagine such a thing would be easy to obtain.&quot; — is untagged; it is not assigned to her here.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, Kanzaki-kun. Did you help us so that we would outpace Class C?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;But I was just thinking, perhaps what we’re doing right now might end up coming back to bite you in the ass later?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Man. I completely neglected to calculate the fact that Class D has a girl like you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She takes out her phone and hands it over.<span class=\"pg\">p.217–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll lend this to you. Please return it later.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her cooperation is explicitly costly to her principles: the plan depends on a lie, and &quot;For someone like Ichinose, who hated lying, it was a harsh request.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> The compliment is professional and ungrudging — she names Horikita as a factor Class D has that she failed to price in.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Kanzaki warns her the favor may be turned against Class B later, and she accepts that risk without extracting a condition.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p214-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: waiting at the entranceway<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p226-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: she steps into the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p216-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami horikita-suzune kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji ch 6 sec  6 2  what the request costs horikita s request leaves him silent   kanzaki fell silent and appeared deep in thought   it might be contrary to your ethics and morals  ichinose   yeah  that s what i thought as well  it s something that never should have been done  he names the plan s cost before agreeing to it  and his objection is to the method rather than to helping class d   yeah  that s right  the answer confirms ichinose s guess that class b helped so class d could outpace class c   that could happen  he accepts  without defensiveness  that the favor may later be used against class b  they work as a pair  he takes the hard institutional line and she supplies the accommodation  and neither undercuts the other  he treats her plan as a serious strategy  not a favor  and answers her risk disclosure with agreement rather than reassurance  his earlier part in the case   the bounty flyer on the bulletin board   is not mentioned in this chapter  the page introduces him here only as the friend who disagreed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p216-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p216-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: what the request costs<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.216–217<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;It might be contrary to your ethics and morals, Ichinose.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;Yeah. That’s what I thought as well. It’s something that never should have been done.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> &quot;Yeah. That’s right.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita&#x27;s request leaves him silent: &quot;Kanzaki fell silent and appeared deep in thought.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.216<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He names the plan&#x27;s cost before agreeing to it, and his objection is to the method rather than to helping Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer confirms Ichinose&#x27;s guess that Class B helped so Class D could outpace Class C.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That could happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He accepts, without defensiveness, that the favor may later be used against Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> They work as a pair; he takes the hard institutional line and she supplies the accommodation, and neither undercuts the other.<span class=\"pg\">p.214–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He treats her plan as a serious strategy, not a favor, and answers her risk disclosure with agreement rather than reassurance.<span class=\"pg\">p.216–217<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> His earlier part in the case — the bounty flyer on the bulletin board — is not mentioned in this chapter; the page introduces him here only as the friend who disagreed.<span class=\"pg\">p.214<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p214-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the one who wanted the compromise<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p234-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.3: he installs the fake cameras<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 6 sec  6 2  the price of touching horikita  if it s not something really bothersome  sure  i ll help   wha  ah  ah  horikita answers the tickling in the hearing with a blow to his side that drops him into the corner  and warns him   i ll forgive you for touching me this time  however  next time i ll pay you back double  his private arithmetic after the blow  if  double  meant twice the force   that was unimaginable","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If it’s not something really bothersome, sure. I’ll help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Wha— Ah, ah!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita answers the tickling in the hearing with a blow to his side that drops him into the corner, and warns him: &quot;I’ll forgive you for touching me this time. However, next time I’ll pay you back double.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His private arithmetic after the blow: if &quot;double&quot; meant twice the force, &quot;That was unimaginable!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: leaving the hearing, and Class B’s offer<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 6 sec  6 2  the debt she collects she answers the hearing s tickling with a blow to the narrator s side that drops him into the corner   i ll forgive you for touching me this time  however  next time i ll pay you back double  the chapter runs her from paralysis to leadership and closes the account with the blow  she accepts his intervention in the hearing and prices it immediately","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the debt she collects<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.218<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’ll forgive you for touching me this time. However, next time I’ll pay you back double.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She answers the hearing’s tickling with a blow to the narrator’s side that drops him into the corner.<span class=\"pg\">p.218<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter runs her from paralysis to leadership and closes the account with the blow: she accepts his intervention in the hearing and prices it immediately.<span class=\"pg\">p.196–218<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request she makes of Class B<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 0  the morning walk to the retrial summer morning on the tree lined path to school  horikita waits against the handrail specifically for him  and the case is decided the same day   were you waiting for someone  horikita   i guess if you wanted to confess your feelings  it d be best just to get the words out   everything will be decided today  two lines in this exchange carry no speaker tag   would you be happy if we d compromised  and  after horikita takes the responsibility onto herself   so you do worry about things like this  huh  the page says only  i didn t want to think about it  but horikita continued  so neither line is assigned   we have the strategy you proposed yesterday  ichinose will be there  too  we ll manage  he pats her shoulder lightly and walks on  he thinks about capturing the idyllic scene in a photograph but lacks the nerve   however  i didn t have the guts to take her picture   hmm  horikita begins  nothing  after we settle this case  and shuts her mouth  the sentence is never finished","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.220–221<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summer morning on the tree-lined path to school; Horikita waits against the handrail specifically for him, and the case is decided the same day.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Were you waiting for someone, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I guess if you wanted to confess your feelings, it’d be best just to get the words out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Everything will be decided today,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Two lines in this exchange carry no speaker tag: &quot;Would you be happy if we’d compromised?&quot; and, after Horikita takes the responsibility onto herself, &quot;So you do worry about things like this, huh?&quot; The page says only &quot;I didn’t want to think about it, but Horikita continued&quot;, so neither line is assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We have the strategy you proposed yesterday. Ichinose will be there, too. We’ll manage.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He pats her shoulder lightly and walks on.<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He thinks about capturing the idyllic scene in a photograph but lacks the nerve: &quot;However, I didn’t have the guts to take her picture.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita begins &quot;Nothing. After we settle this case,&quot; and shuts her mouth; the sentence is never finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the price of touching Horikita<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 0 7 1  waiting on the path  judging the change  good morning  ayanokouji kun   yes  i was waiting for you   are you an idiot   i was thinking maybe i made a mistake  the wrong choice   if sudou kun is penalized for this  it ll be my responsibility   the truth is that we re gambling  i m a little anxious of the outcome  are you okay   nothing  after we settle this case   what s with her   people don t change so easily  trying to change yourself is virtually impossible  the page calls it a  brief but realistic statement  that shattered the image ayanokoji had built   as long as she doesn t overdo it  i think it ll be fine   if she tries to do what isn t possible for someone like her yet  she ll just set herself up to fail  the warning lands with  a mysterious yet convincing power  almost as if she were speaking from experience   do you want to die for good","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.220–223<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Yes. I was waiting for you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Are you an idiot?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I was thinking…maybe I made a mistake. The wrong choice…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Sudou-kun is penalized for this, it’ll be my responsibility.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The truth is that we’re gambling. I’m a little anxious of the outcome. Are you okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.220<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nothing. After we settle this case,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.221<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s with her?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;People don’t change so easily. Trying to change yourself is virtually impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The page calls it a &quot;brief but realistic statement&quot; that shattered the image Ayanokōji had built.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;As long as she doesn’t overdo it, I think it’ll be fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If she tries to do what isn’t possible for someone like her yet, she’ll just set herself up to fail.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The warning lands with &quot;a mysterious yet convincing power,&quot; almost as if she were speaking from experience.<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you want to die for good?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p218-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the debt she collects<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 1 7 2  sakura s first greeting in the classroom sakura is already at her desk  sitting up straight  as if ready for something  and gives her first morning greeting to both of them  the reply to horikita s  what s with her     maybe because of what happened yesterday  she took a step forward on the path to adulthood    carries no speaker tag  the page only says her next remark  shattered the lovely image i d created  so the line is not assigned  he judges the change smaller than it looks   there was no truly major difference between the today s sakura and yesterday s   well  as a loner who loves her solitude  you re very persuasive on this topic   perhaps she didn t come from solitude  but rather from hell  on not pushing sakura past what she can carry   we should take care with how we executed our strategy   sakura  are you heading back now   i m not participating   what s wrong   sakura  you don t really need to testify today  there s no need for you to be so worked up  right   what are you thinking about   hey  sakura  do you have any time later  i wanted to talk to you about something  the invitation feels  like they were being squeezed out of me  she answers that she has plans today  and he lets her go","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.222–225<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">In the classroom Sakura is already at her desk, sitting up straight &quot;as if ready for something,&quot; and gives her first morning greeting to both of them.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Well, as a loner who loves her solitude, you’re very persuasive on this topic.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Sakura. Are you heading back now?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I’m not participating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The reply to Horikita’s &quot;What’s with her?&quot; — &quot;Maybe because of what happened yesterday, she took a step forward on the path to adulthood?&quot; — carries no speaker tag; the page only says her next remark &quot;shattered the lovely image I’d created&quot;, so the line is not assigned.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He judges the change smaller than it looks: &quot;There was no truly major difference between the today’s Sakura and yesterday’s.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Perhaps she didn’t come from solitude, but rather from hell…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On not pushing Sakura past what she can carry: &quot;We should take care with how we executed our strategy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.223<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What’s wrong?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura, you don’t really need to testify today. There’s no need for you to be so worked up, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What are you thinking about?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Hey, Sakura. Do you have any time later? I wanted to talk to you about something.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The invitation feels &quot;like they were being squeezed out of me&quot;; she answers that she has plans today, and he lets her go.<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p220-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.0: the morning walk to the retrial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7 sec  7 1 7 2  the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial she is already at her desk when ayanokoji arrives   earlier than usual   sitting up straight   as if ready for something   um  good morning  ayanokouji kun  horikita san  the answer she gets back   g good morning  is printed with no speaker  the narrator only records that his own response stuck in his throat   ayanokouji kun  we re having the trial today   i see   it s because everyone s doing their best  i thought i d do my best  too  the page reads the line  felt like that she was saying that to herself  rather than to me   well  if there s something i need to move forward  i ll do it  her farewell smile and words  seemed so unlike her  and leave him with an unpleasant feeling   see you later  ayanokouji kun   i have plans today  maybe tomorrow","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.222–225<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She is already at her desk when Ayanokōji arrives — earlier than usual — sitting up straight, &quot;as if ready for something.&quot;<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Um… Good morning, Ayanokouji-kun. Horikita-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun… We’re having the trial today.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I see…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The answer she gets back, &quot;G-good morning…&quot;, is printed with no speaker; the narrator only records that his own response stuck in his throat.<span class=\"pg\">p.222<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s because everyone’s doing their best. I thought I’d do my best, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page reads the line &quot;felt like that she was saying that to herself, rather than to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, if there’s something I need to move forward… I’ll do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her farewell smile and words &quot;seemed so unlike her&quot; and leave him with an unpleasant feeling.<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;See you later, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.224<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have plans today. Maybe tomorrow?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: walking out<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 2  the special building rendezvous and the camera trap after 3 40  in the special building  the three class c students arrive expecting a date or a confession from kushida   kushida won t be here  i asked her to send an email to compel you all to come   if i hadn t used an underhanded method  you would ve just ignored me  right  i wanted to talk to you   i have no intension of arguing  that would be a waste of time  i fully understand that neither class c nor class d will retract what they claimed yesterday   the school s waiting  right  go ahead and tell us the truth  after giving you a grace period  the student council president himself asked if you had lied  if you think back  don t you realize that the student council saw through everything  the bluff s second half is his  and he knows it is a bluff   of course  the student council had not seen through their lies  he nods along with ichinose s ultimatum   confirm the footage now and the three will be expelled  on the escort to the student council room   horikita had put everything together really well  he supplies the trap and the pressure   the luring email  the student council gambit  the nod to the ultimatum   and hands the open argument to her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.225–233<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">After 3:40, in the special building: the three Class C students arrive expecting a date or a confession from Kushida.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Kushida won’t be here. I asked her to send an email to compel you all to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;If I hadn’t used an underhanded method, you would’ve just ignored me, right? I wanted to talk to you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I have no intension of arguing. That would be a waste of time. I fully understand that neither Class C nor Class D will retract what they claimed yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The school’s waiting, right? Go ahead and tell us the truth. After giving you a grace period, the student council president himself asked if you had lied. If you think back, don’t you realize that the student council saw through everything?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The bluff’s second half is his, and he knows it is a bluff: &quot;Of course, the student council had not seen through their lies.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He nods along with Ichinose’s ultimatum — confirm the footage now and the three will be expelled.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the escort to the student council room: &quot;Horikita had put everything together really well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> He supplies the trap and the pressure — the luring email, the student-council gambit, the nod to the ultimatum — and hands the open argument to her.<span class=\"pg\">p.225–232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: Sakura’s first greeting<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"kushida-kikyou","q":"kushida kikyo ch 7  her email  and the reward still to come ayanokoji states that he asked her to send the email that lured the three class c students to the special building   i asked her to send an email to compel you all to come  horikita lists her hearing actions among those that  would be rewarded as well","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p225-1\">Ch.7: her email, and the reward still to come<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.225–246<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji states that he asked her to send the email that lured the three Class C students to the special building: &quot;I asked her to send an email to compel you all to come.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.225<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Horikita lists her hearing actions among those that &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v2-p213-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: named among the people who believe Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p226-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 7 sec  7 2  she steps into the corridor as the three turn to leave  one other person stands in their way   the page introduces her as  who d been waiting for all of the players in this drama to appear    and she puts herself between class c and the exit   i think you guys might want to consider that idea  actually   what do you mean  what if i said that i m here because i m involved in this case   ha ha  well  i guess i m well known among the members of class c   you re certainly right that class b has nothing to do with this  but how do you feel about involving so many people in your lies   so evildoers remain obstinate until the very end  it s about time for you to pay the piper   you lied  we can all see through you  you got violent in the end  if you don t want that fact to become public knowledge  withdraw your claim right away  she  grinned and talked with greater animation  as if relishing this  walking toward them like a detective revealing the culprit   didn t you think that the school s response to this incident was rather strange   when you raised the issue with the school  why wasn t sudou punished immediately  why give an opportunity to escape by granting a grace period of several days  what do you think was the reason   is that really okay  though  if you leave this place  you might regret it for the rest of your life   don t you understand  the school knows that you re lying  class c  they ve known from the beginning   ha ha ha ha  you guys are so funny   you ve been dancing to my tune all this time   i have actual evidence","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p226-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p226-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: she steps into the corridor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.226–228<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">As the three turn to leave, one other person stands in their way — the page introduces her as &quot;who’d been waiting for all of the players in this drama to appear&quot; — and she puts herself between Class C and the exit.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;I think you guys might want to consider that idea, actually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;What do you mean? What if I said that I’m here because I’m involved in this case?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Ha ha. Well, I guess I’m well known among the members of Class C.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.226<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re certainly right that Class B has nothing to do with this. But how do you feel about involving so many people in your lies?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So evildoers remain obstinate until the very end. It’s about time for you to pay the piper!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You lied. We can all see through you. You got violent in the end. If you don’t want that fact to become public knowledge, withdraw your claim right away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She &quot;grinned and talked with greater animation, as if relishing this,&quot; walking toward them like a detective revealing the culprit.<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Didn’t you think that the school’s response to this incident was rather strange?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When you raised the issue with the school, why wasn’t Sudou punished immediately? Why give an opportunity to escape by granting a grace period of several days? What do you think was the reason?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.227<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that really okay, though? If you leave this place, you might regret it for the rest of your life.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Don’t you understand? The school knows that you’re lying, Class C. They’ve known from the beginning.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha ha ha. You guys are so funny.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’ve been dancing to my tune all this time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I have actual evidence,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: the request, and the price<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p228-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the security-camera argument<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p228-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 7 sec  7 2  the security camera argument  did you know that there are security cameras installed everywhere around the school  it s a measure they ve taken in order to monitor what we do every day   that s too bad  isn t it  if you want to set a trap for someone  you d need to do it in a place without any cameras   you re right that  by and large  cameras aren t installed in most of this building s hallways  however  there are exceptions  and several places in which security cameras have been installed  like in front of the faculty room and the science lab  obviously  there are many valuables stored in the faculty room  you know  additionally  the science lab has many chemical products  since the science lab is on this level  it s only natural that a camera would be installed here   have you looked back there  behind you  there s one there too  right   so if we d installed a camera  like you said  would we have prepared one on that side  too  besides  how exactly would we have prepared surveillance cameras when we can t even leave campus in the first place   this is the third floor  but did you really check  maybe you only looked at the second or the fourth  perhaps the cameras were truly set up here as a trap   also  you realize that you just destroyed yourselves  right  normal people wouldn t think to check whether there were security cameras  right  that s basically admitting your guilt   the security cameras couldn t record the sounds of your voices  but they definitely captured the decisive moment you threw the first punch  she passes the baton to ayanokoji for the student council half of the bluff   innocence  that depends on what you re innocent of  we know that both parties took damage during the incident  no matter the circumstances  sudou hit the three of you  that s undeniable  of course  if the security footage can prove that sudou wasn t the one who called you three over here  he d probably receive the lightest possible punishment  however  his position as a regular would still be threatened  he might not be allowed to participate in tournaments   if someone checked the security camera footage  it would expose your lies  if that were to happen  chances are good you d be expelled  anyone could see that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p228-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p228-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the security-camera argument<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.228–231<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Did you know that there are security cameras installed everywhere around the school? It’s a measure they’ve taken in order to monitor what we do every day.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.228–229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;That’s too bad, isn’t it? If you want to set a trap for someone, you’d need to do it in a place without any cameras.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;You’re right that, by and large, cameras aren’t installed in most of this building’s hallways. However, there are exceptions, and several places in which security cameras have been installed, like in front of the faculty room…<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re right that, by and large, cameras aren’t installed in most of this building’s hallways. However, there are exceptions, and several places in which security cameras have been installed, like in front of the faculty room and the science lab. Obviously, there are many valuables stored in the faculty room, you know? Additionally, the science lab has many chemical products. Since the science lab is on this level, it’s only natural that a camera would be installed here.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.229<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Have you looked back there, behind you? There’s one there too, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So if we’d installed a camera, like you said, would we have prepared one on that side, too? Besides, how exactly would we have prepared surveillance cameras when we can’t even leave campus in the first place?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;This is the third floor, but did you really check? Maybe you only looked at the second or the fourth? Perhaps the cameras were truly set up here as a trap?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Also, you realize that you just destroyed yourselves, right? Normal people wouldn’t think to check whether there were security cameras, right? That’s basically admitting your guilt.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The security cameras couldn’t record the sounds of your voices, but they definitely captured the decisive moment you threw the first punch.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She passes the baton to Ayanokōji for the student-council half of the bluff.<span class=\"pg\">p.230<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Innocence? That depends on what you’re innocent of. We know that both parties took damage during the incident. No matter the circumstances, Sudou hit the three of you. That’s undeniable. Of course, if the security footage can prove that Sudou wasn’t the one who called you three over here, he’d probably receive the lightest possible punishment. However, his position as a regular would still be threatened. He might not be allowed to participate in tournaments.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If someone checked the security camera footage, it would expose your lies. If that were to happen, chances are good you’d be expelled. Anyone could see that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.231<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p226-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: she steps into the corridor<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p232-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.2–7.3: the only way out, and the cameras that were never the school’s<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p232-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 7 sec  7 2 7 3  the only way out  and the cameras that were never the school s  it s rather early to draw a conclusion  we ll give you one last chance  there s only one way to save both class c and class d   there s only one way to resolve this issue  tell the school that you wish to withdraw your complaint  if you do that  the school will not bring forward the security camera footage  if there s no complaint  no one can be punished  additionally  if the security footage is never brought up  class d benefits  too  as we already know  if the security footage were brought produced  sudou would still face some degree of punishment  in other words  class c and class d can come to a compromise together  the school can t investigate if they can t watch the video and see that you lied  right  she refuses to let ishizaki call anyone and gives him no time to think   well  you re not being very cooperative  therefore  we have no choice but to prepare  we ll have the school confirm the security footage right away  and you ll be expelled  she walks the three class c students to the student council room  sandwiched between her and ayanokoji   whew  i feel so much better  thanks so much  thanks for giving me such a huge role  i was so happy   ha ha ha  yeah  i guess so  but the case is closed  eh  she and kanzaki bought the cameras  and with the professor installed them during the lunch break   when the day comes  you guys will probably become formidable rivals for class c  ayanokouji kun   if horikita san were in class b  we might have gotten to class a right away   i ll definitely return the points i borrowed  just tell me when you want them   huh  w wait a minute   oh  yeah  that reminds me  there was one thing i wanted to tell you  ayanokouji kun  what she wanted to tell him is cut off by his sprint  it comes out later as the warning about ryuuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p232-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p232-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.2–7.3: the only way out, and the cameras that were never the school’s<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.232–235<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;It’s rather early to draw a conclusion. We’ll give you one last chance. There’s only one way to save both Class C and Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;There’s only one way to resolve this issue. Tell the school that you wish to withdraw your complaint. If you do that, the school will not bring forward the security camera footage. If there’s no complaint, no one can be…<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Well, you’re not being very cooperative. Therefore, we have no choice but to prepare. We’ll have the school confirm the security footage right away, and you’ll be expelled.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s only one way to resolve this issue. Tell the school that you wish to withdraw your complaint. If you do that, the school will not bring forward the security camera footage. If there’s no complaint, no one can be punished. Additionally, if the security footage is never brought up, Class D benefits, too. As we already know, if the security footage were brought produced, Sudou would still face some degree of punishment. In other words, Class C and Class D can come to a compromise together. The school can’t investigate if they can’t watch the video and see that you lied, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She refuses to let Ishizaki call anyone and gives him no time to think.<span class=\"pg\">p.232<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She walks the three Class C students to the student council room, sandwiched between her and Ayanokōji.<span class=\"pg\">p.233<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Whew! I feel so much better! Thanks so much! Thanks for giving me such a huge role! I was so happy!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ha ha ha, yeah. I guess so. But the case is closed, eh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She and Kanzaki bought the cameras, and with the Professor installed them during the lunch break.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;When the day comes, you guys will probably become formidable rivals for Class C, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If Horikita-san were in Class B, we might have gotten to Class A right away.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’ll definitely return the points I borrowed. Just tell me when you want them.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh?! W-wait a minute!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, yeah, that reminds me. There was one thing I wanted to tell you, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> What she wanted to tell him is cut off by his sprint; it comes out later as the warning about Ryuuen.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p228-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the security-camera argument<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p236-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the act at the shutter, and the warning about Ryuuen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 3 7 4  the fake cameras and the shuttered door  i was wondering what you were up to when you asked me to lend you some points yesterday   as long as you pay me back by graduation  it s fine  so what are you going to do now  wait in front of the student council room  sakura s  plans today  keep bothering him  he runs off before ichinose can say what she wanted to tell him  and she follows  tracking sakura s phone to the electronics store entrance  he signals ichinose to be quiet as a precaution   ah  looks like we caught them  that old guy s doing something naughty   me and my girlfriend saw everything  so we took pictures  if you show your face to that girl again  or send her any more disgusting letters  we ll expose you  got it   you don t know what i m talking about  you re not weaseling out of this  old man  if you so much as raise a hand at or even just ogle this idol  that ll be the end for you  i ll beat the shit out of you  got it  after the clerk loses his fight  he deliberately gives him time to run  then catches sakura before she can fall   you did really well   i m really glad that i exchanged contact information with you   that s not true  it was really cool when you threw those letters to the ground  ichinose asks who the  mystery person  is and his  that s  stops there  the page records that he did not want to hide anything from her but hesitated to speak without sakura s permission   sakura over here was an idol when she was in junior high  her name was shizuku  he tells ichinose the idol name only after sakura meets his eyes and gives him a slight nod   a little while ago  sorry  several other people in class realized  too   i think there s a possibility that people at school might panic when they notice but i think it ll be fine  the impulse to help unsettles him   was this the real me   it s nothing you have to apologize for  we don t have to talk about it  however  i think that now we have the type of relationship where we can talk about things  if you re suffering or if you feel lost  you can talk to me  you should consult horikita and kushida  too  on ichinose s warning about ryuuen   i didn t know who this ryuuen was  but he was undoubtedly a very dangerous opponent   yeah  i ll keep that in mind","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.234–241<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;I was wondering what you were up to when you asked me to lend you some points yesterday.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;As long as you pay me back by graduation, it’s fine. So what are you going to do now? Wait in front of the student council room?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Ah, looks like we caught them! That old guy’s doing something naughty!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Sakura’s &quot;plans today&quot; keep bothering him; he runs off before Ichinose can say what she wanted to tell him, and she follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tracking Sakura’s phone to the electronics-store entrance, he signals Ichinose to be quiet as a precaution.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Me and my girlfriend saw everything. So we took pictures. If you show your face to that girl again, or send her any more disgusting letters, we’ll expose you. Got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You don’t know what I’m talking about? You’re not weaseling out of this, old man. If you so much as raise a hand at or even just ogle this idol, that’ll be the end for you. I’ll beat the shit out of you. Got it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After the clerk loses his fight, he deliberately gives him time to run, then catches Sakura before she can fall.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You did really well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m really glad that I exchanged contact information with you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not true. It was really cool when you threw those letters to the ground.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Ichinose asks who the &quot;mystery person&quot; is and his &quot;That’s…&quot; stops there: the page records that he did not want to hide anything from her but hesitated to speak without Sakura’s permission.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Sakura over here was an idol when she was in junior high. Her name was Shizuku.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He tells Ichinose the idol name only after Sakura meets his eyes and gives him a slight nod.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;A little while ago. Sorry. Several other people in class realized, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I think there’s a possibility that people at school might panic when they notice…but I think it’ll be fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The impulse to help unsettles him: &quot;Was this the real me?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;It’s nothing you have to apologize for. We don’t have to talk about it. However, I think that now we have the type of relationship where we can talk about things. If you’re suffering or if you feel lost, you can talk to me. You should consult Horikita and Kushida, too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Ichinose’s warning about Ryuuen: &quot;I didn’t know who this Ryuuen was, but he was undoubtedly a very dangerous opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yeah. I’ll keep that in mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p225-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2: the special-building rendezvous and the camera trap<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the corridor after the withdrawal<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p234-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"kanzaki ryuji ch 7 sec  7 3  he installs the fake cameras he and ichinose bought the cameras  and with the professor installed them during the lunch break  the class b operation is theirs together  she applies the pressure in the corridor  he handles the hardware","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p234-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.3: he installs the fake cameras<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.234<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">He and Ichinose bought the cameras, and with the Professor installed them during the lunch break.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The Class B operation is theirs together: she applies the pressure in the corridor, he handles the hardware.<span class=\"pg\">p.234<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v2-p216-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.2: what the request costs<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-private-points-y1v2-p234-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"","q":"private points ch 7  loans  fees  and the cost of a withdrawn case closing a withdrawn case still costs   we will require a certain payment of points in order to cover of miscellaneous expenses incurred over the course of deliberations    announced in the hearing with no speaker attached  and the first time any student has heard of it  ayanokoji lends ichinose the points for the camera purchase  she will return them   i ll definitely return the points i borrowed  just tell me when you want them    he sets the deadline at graduation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p234-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html#sc-private-points-y1v2-p234-1\">Ch.7: loans, fees, and the cost of a withdrawn case<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.234–245<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../school/system/private-points.html\">Private Points<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Closing a withdrawn case still costs: &quot;we will require a certain payment of points in order to cover of miscellaneous expenses incurred over the course of deliberations&quot; — announced in the hearing with no speaker attached, and the first time any student has heard of it.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji lends Ichinose the points for the camera purchase; she will return them: &quot;I’ll definitely return the points I borrowed. Just tell me when you want them.&quot; — he sets the deadline at graduation.<span class=\"pg\">p.234–235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-private-points-y1v2-p152-1\">← Before: Ch.5 sec. 5.0: paying informants, and paying them anonymously<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p236-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 7 sec  7 4  the act at the shutter  and the warning about ryuuen she sticks close when ayanokoji runs to the electronics store and goes quiet on his signal  matching the delinquent act   her tone was cruel  she pinches the letters up by their corners with finger and thumb   huh  idol  that s amazing  she s an entertainer  ooh  shake my hand  shake my hand   even so  that s so amazing  i ve never thought about becoming an idol or anything   whoa  you re so amazingly cute  you make a completely different impression without your glasses    after looking shizuku up on her phone  ah  i ll help out too   i m ichinose  from class b  it s nice to meet you  sakura san   i probably shouldn t be saying this right now  but there was someone pulling the strings behind this whole sudou incident   to tell the truth  there was a dispute between class b and class c students before  that time  though  the school didn t get involved  someone named ryuuen kun masterminded that one   ichinose  who always looked so bright  now appeared somber and grim   that s because he hasn t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet  there s no reason that you d know him   i m the most vigilant of all the first years here  i think he set up sudou kun to look like a liar  and instigated the dispute with class b  this was all his handiwork  he doesn t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests  he s a formidable opponent   somehow  yeah  however  if you looked at it like a game  i can t say whether i won or lost  anyway  i think because what he devised was easier to see through this time  i ve started to understand how this school is structured  you should be careful   so if anything ever happens  you can come to me for help  talk to me whenever you need it  she names the road not taken  if horikita had been in class b  class b might already have reached class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p236-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the act at the shutter, and the warning about Ryuuen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.236–241<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Huh?! Idol?! That’s amazing! She’s an entertainer! Ooh, shake my hand, shake my hand!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Even so, that’s so amazing! I’ve never thought about becoming an idol or anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> &quot;Whoa… You’re so amazingly cute! You make a completely different impression without your glasses!&quot; — after looking Shizuku up on her phone<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She sticks close when Ayanokōji runs to the electronics store and goes quiet on his signal.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Matching the delinquent act, &quot;her tone was cruel&quot;; she pinches the letters up by their corners with finger and thumb.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ah, I’ll help out too.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m Ichinose, from Class B. It’s nice to meet you, Sakura-san.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I probably shouldn’t be saying this right now, but…there was someone pulling the strings behind this whole Sudou incident.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;To tell the truth, there was a dispute between Class B and Class C students before. That time, though, the school didn’t get involved. Someone named Ryuuen-kun masterminded that one.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;Ichinose, who always looked so bright, now appeared somber and grim.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s because he hasn’t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet. There’s no reason that you’d know him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m the most vigilant of all the first-years here. I think he set up Sudou-kun to look like a liar, and instigated the dispute with Class B. This was all his handiwork. He doesn’t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests. He’s a formidable opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Somehow, yeah. However, if you looked at it like a game, I can’t say whether I won or lost… Anyway, I think because what he devised was easier to see through this time, I’ve started to understand how this school is structured. You should be careful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;So if anything ever happens, you can come to me for help. Talk to me whenever you need it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She names the road not taken: if Horikita had been in Class B, Class B might already have reached Class A.<span class=\"pg\">p.235<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v2-p232-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.2–7.3: the only way out, and the cameras that were never the school’s<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7 sec  7 4  the shuttered door at the electronics store entrance her fan   the store clerk who has been sending hundreds of letters to her room   catches her alone   please don t contact me anymore   stop  please  stop it   how do you know my room number  why do you keep sending these   please stop it  it s bothering me  she throws the bundle of letters to the floor  rejecting him   d don t come any closer  he latches onto her arm and shoves her against the store s shuttered door   no  let me go  she is  completely dumbfounded  by the delinquent tone ayanokoji puts on for the act  when the clerk runs she is exhausted enough to topple  and ayanokoji catches her arms and holds her up   ayanokouji  kun  why are you here   i guess i m no good after all  i couldn t do anything by myself in the end","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the shuttered door<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.236–238<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the electronics-store entrance her fan — the store clerk who has been sending hundreds of letters to her room — catches her alone.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Please don’t contact me anymore!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;Stop… Please, stop it!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;How do you know my room number? Why do you keep sending these?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Please stop it. It’s bothering me!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She throws the bundle of letters to the floor, rejecting him.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;D-don’t come any closer!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He latches onto her arm and shoves her against the store’s shuttered door.<span class=\"pg\">p.236<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, let me go!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She is &quot;completely dumbfounded&quot; by the delinquent tone Ayanokōji puts on for the act.<span class=\"pg\">p.237<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the clerk runs she is exhausted enough to topple, and Ayanokōji catches her arms and holds her up.<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji… kun. Why are you here?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I guess I’m no good after all… I couldn’t do anything by myself in the end.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.238<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p222-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.1–7.2: the morning greeting and the last talk before the trial<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: permission, and a footing with Class B<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi","q":"sakura airi ch 7 sec  7 4  permission  and a footing with class b she meets ayanokoji s eyes and gives him a slight nod   permission to tell ichinose the idol name   when did you realize  ayanokouji kun   but i never appeared on tv or anything   i think i m actually glad about this  though  it s been hard to lie   she laughed while seemingly on the verge of tears   ayanokouji kun  don t look at me with such strange eyes   never mind  it s nothing   do you think everyone would notice if i came to class without my glasses  and changed my hairstyle   okay  i understand  a little hesitant  she shakes ichinose s outstretched hand  the new footing is stated to her  if she suffers or feels lost she can talk to ayanokoji  and she should consult horikita and kushida too","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p239-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.4: permission, and a footing with Class B<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.239–240<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;When did you realize, Ayanokouji-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;But I never appeared on TV or anything…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> &quot;I think I’m actually glad about this, though… It’s been hard to lie.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She meets Ayanokōji’s eyes and gives him a slight nod — permission to tell Ichinose the idol name.<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> &quot;She laughed while seemingly on the verge of tears.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun… Don’t look at me with such strange eyes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Never mind, it’s nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you think everyone would notice if I came to class without my glasses, and changed my hairstyle?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.239<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Okay. I understand,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> A little hesitant, she shakes Ichinose’s outstretched hand.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The new footing is stated to her: if she suffers or feels lost she can talk to Ayanokōji, and she should consult Horikita and Kushida too.<span class=\"pg\">p.240<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v2-p236-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7 sec  7 4  named before he is seen the volume names him for the first time in ichinose s warning   someone named ryuuen kun masterminded that one    the earlier class b class c dispute  and the sudou setup behind this case  as ichinose describes him   he doesn t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests  he s a formidable opponent  she adds that he  hasn t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet  which is why ayanokoji does not know the name","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.4: named before he is seen<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.241<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The volume names him for the first time in Ichinose’s warning: &quot;Someone named Ryuuen-kun masterminded that one.&quot; — the earlier Class B–Class C dispute, and the Sudou setup behind this case.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> As Ichinose describes him: &quot;He doesn’t hesitate to hurt other people for the sake of his own interests. He’s a formidable opponent.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> She adds that he &quot;hasn’t seen any reason to reveal himself just yet,&quot; which is why Ayanokōji does not know the name.<span class=\"pg\">p.241<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 5  the retrial  from her side she and sudo arrive ten minutes before deliberation  tachibana is already in the room  and neither her brother nor class c has come in yet  the chapter turns to her first person here   i feel the same as ever  the line she has committed to   i d declared that sudou was completely innocent  after all  if my strategy failed  it would be for nothing   reconciliation was another name for defeat  on a failed strategy   it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other  when the doors open for her brother she turns her eyes away from him and faces the opponents who matter today   even though i should have understood it  i felt attacked   i was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling  nervousness  and dizziness  but i couldn t repeat yesterday s mistakes   he s not participating   well  even if he s not here  the results will be the same  her read on chabashira s puzzlement   i had the gut feeling that what chabashira sensei was seeing was the evidence of ayanokouji kun s involvement   this was a battle between truth and lies  we could bandy about ideas  but there could only be one solution","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.242–243<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Sudō arrive ten minutes before deliberation; Tachibana is already in the room, and neither her brother nor Class C has come in yet. The chapter turns to her first person here.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I feel the same as ever.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;He’s not participating.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Well, even if he’s not here, the results will be the same.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The line she has committed to: &quot;I’d declared that Sudou was completely innocent, after all. If my strategy failed, it would be for nothing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Reconciliation was another name for defeat.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On a failed strategy: &quot;it would likely devolve into a verbal battle where we hurled abuse at each other.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> When the doors open for her brother she turns her eyes away from him and faces the opponents who matter today.<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Even though I should have understood it, I felt attacked.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I was wracked with various symptoms such as trembling, nervousness, and dizziness. But I couldn’t repeat yesterday’s mistakes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Her read on Chabashira’s puzzlement: &quot;I had the gut feeling that what Chabashira-sensei was seeing was the evidence of Ayanokouji-kun’s involvement.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;This was a battle between truth and lies. We could bandy about ideas, but there could only be one solution.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p220-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.0–7.1: waiting on the path, judging the change<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p242-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 7 sec  7 5  waiting for the retrial to start he arrives ten minutes before deliberation with horikita  nervous about the verdict they walked into   oh jeez  i m so nervous  how about you  horikita   huh  don t screw around  i didn t do anything   wait  i don t get it  why are you guys just withdrawing your complaint like that   horikita  horikita pulls him down into his seat mid question and shuts him up","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p242-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p242-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: waiting for the retrial to start<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.242–245<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He arrives ten minutes before deliberation with Horikita, nervous about the verdict they walked into.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Oh jeez, I’m so nervous. How about you, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.242<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Huh? Don’t screw around. I didn’t do anything,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Wait. I don’t get it. Why are you guys just withdrawing your complaint like that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Horikita pulls him down into his seat mid-question and shuts him up.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: after the hearing<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5–7.6: the lecture, the apology, the party<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  the empty seat and the unexpected ending she arrives with sakagami for the retrial and finds ayanokoji s seat empty   what happened to ayanokouji  horikita   not participating  she stares at the vacant seat  as if the proceedings would be meaningless without him   you re withdrawing your complaint  she chuckles with  a thin smile  as if she found something amusing   oh  excuse me  i was just surprised because i hadn t foreseen this  i figured we would argue all day until one side collapsed  or until we could propose an acceptable compromise  however  unbelievably  they ve said that they want to withdraw the complaint  she confirms the practical result to both sides  no suspension for sudo  no punishment for class c  with this incident as the example to remember next time   of course  the same goes for the students in class c  naturally  youthful zeal is a good quality  however  the next time you think about causing problems  you should remember this incident as an example  do not forget  okay","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.243–246<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She arrives with Sakagami for the retrial and finds Ayanokōji’s seat empty.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;What happened to Ayanokouji, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Not participating?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;You’re withdrawing your complaint?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She stares at the vacant seat &quot;as if the proceedings would be meaningless without him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She chuckles with &quot;a thin smile, as if she found something amusing.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh, excuse me. I was just surprised because I hadn’t foreseen this. I figured we would argue all day until one side collapsed, or until we could propose an acceptable compromise. However, unbelievably, they’ve said that they want to withdraw the complaint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> She confirms the practical result to both sides: no suspension for Sudō, no punishment for Class C, with this incident as the example to remember next time.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Of course. The same goes for the students in Class C, naturally. Youthful zeal is a good quality. However, the next time you think about causing problems, you should remember this incident as an example. Do not forget. Okay?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p205-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the compromise she will not refuse<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p243-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu tachibana-akane","q":"tachibana akane ch 7 sec  7 5 7 6  running the room and the seat she does not expect to fill she urges the standing class c students to sit down  they do not move   can you please sit down   the unflappable secretary tachibana clapped her hands   yes  a first year class a student applied the other day  but was rejected after the first interview   s student council president  do you really mean that   n no  if you say so  i have no objections  but   huh  are you refusing an invitation from the student council president   y yes  the secretary seat is confirmed open   one first year class a applicant  rejected after the first interview   and ayanokoji s refusal leaves it open  she answers the seat question for him and is more shocked than ayanokoji by both the offer and the refusal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p243-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html#sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p243-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5–7.6: running the room and the seat she does not expect to fill<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.243–253<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/tachibana-akane.html\">Tachibana Akane<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Can you please sit down?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;Yes. A first-year Class A student applied the other day, but was rejected after the first interview.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Tachibana Akane<\/b> &quot;S-student council president… Do you really mean that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She urges the standing Class C students to sit down; they do not move.<span class=\"pg\">p.243<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> &quot;The unflappable Secretary Tachibana clapped her hands.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;N-no. If you say so, I have no objections. But…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Huh? Are you refusing an invitation from the student council president?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Y-yes.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The secretary seat is confirmed open — one first-year Class A applicant, rejected after the first interview — and Ayanokōji’s refusal leaves it open.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> She answers the seat question for him and is more shocked than Ayanokōji by both the offer and the refusal.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-tachibana-akane-y1v2-p199-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the room&#x27;s procedure<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7 sec  7 5  the withdrawal ruling  did you want to come to an agreement  or did you already do something to the effect  he gazes sharply at the class c students while they signal that they do not want to compromise   if you wish to withdraw your complaint  we have no intention of fighting it  we accept  the regulations line that demands a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached   very well  the proceedings have come to an end  we will now call this discussion closed","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.244–246<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Did you want to come to an agreement? Or did you already do something to the effect?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;If you wish to withdraw your complaint, we have no intention of fighting it. We accept.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Very well, the proceedings have come to an end. We will now call this discussion closed.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He gazes sharply at the Class C students while they signal that they do not want to compromise.<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The regulations line that demands a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p210-1\">← Before: Ch.6 sec. 6.1: the corridor conversation<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the thanks, and the secretary seat<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 5  the withdrawal she did not have to ask for  it wasn t just me  everyone else noticed that this situation was strange   it seemed that ayanokouji kun and ichinose san had handled things quite well  i tried to act calm and collected  without letting my relief show  she grabs sudo s arm to stop his question and pulls him down into his seat   shut up   if the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers  this was what we d been working toward  the regulations line that announces a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.244–245<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It wasn’t just me. Everyone else noticed that this situation was strange.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;It seemed that Ayanokouji-kun and Ichinose-san had handled things quite well. I tried to act calm and collected, without letting my relief show.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.244<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Shut up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> She grabs Sudō’s arm to stop his question and pulls him down into his seat.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;If the complaint was withdrawn there would be no winners or losers. This was what we’d been working toward.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The regulations line that announces a point payment for the deliberation expenses is printed with no speaker attached.<span class=\"pg\">p.245<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p242-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the retrial, from her side<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  what she says to sudo  i m glad  sudou   personally  i think you should have been punished   the reason this incident occurred at all is because of your behavior  who told the truth and who lied is trivial  it s important that you don t let this kind of thing happen again  you do understand that  yes   however  admitting your own faults isn t  cool  so even if you acknowledge that your personality was partly to blame  you act tough  you get stronger  that s fine  however  if you act like that  you won t be able to make real friends  eventually  horikita will abandon you  she ll leave   there s strength in admitting your mistakes  sudou  the page records it as the first time she has tried to reach out to one of her students as a homeroom teacher   you shouldn t make promises so casually  you ll cause trouble soon again   what do you think  horikita  do you think that sudou will become a model student","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–247<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;I’m glad, Sudou,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Personally, I think you should have been punished,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;The reason this incident occurred at all is because of your behavior. Who told the truth and who lied is trivial. It’s important that you don’t let this kind of thing happen again. You do understand that, yes?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;However, admitting your own faults isn’t ‘cool.’ So even if you acknowledge that your personality was partly to blame, you act tough. You get stronger. That’s fine. However, if you act like that, you won’t be able to make real friends. Eventually, Horikita will abandon you. She’ll leave.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246–247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There’s strength in admitting your mistakes, Sudou.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The page records it as the first time she has tried to reach out to one of her students as a homeroom teacher.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You shouldn’t make promises so casually. You’ll cause trouble soon again.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What do you think, Horikita? Do you think that Sudou will become a model student?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p243-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the empty seat and the unexpected ending<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"","w":"hirata-yousuke","q":"hirata yosuke ch 7  a passing mention in the verdict he is named once  in horikita s summary of pending rewards for the hearing   kushida s and his actions  would be rewarded as well    and appears nowhere else in the chapter","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p246-1\">Ch.7: a passing mention in the verdict<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He is named once, in Horikita’s summary of pending rewards for the hearing — Kushida’s and his actions &quot;would be rewarded as well&quot; — and appears nowhere else in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v2-p120-1\">← Before: Ch.4 sec. 4.7, sec. 4.11: he is the name people reach for when a conversation is going badly<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 5  the verdict  and chabashira s lecture to sudo  you will no longer face suspension  the school will not consider you a problem child  you will be able to participate in club activities from today onward  right  she notes that kushida san and hirata kun s actions in the hearing  would be rewarded as well   no  i don t    asked whether sudo will become a model student  however sudou kun certainly made some progress today  he admitted he was at fault  so i m sure that he ll grow more tomorrow   no  i ve already abandoned him  i just won t allow him to run loose anymore  on his exit for club practice   he was not remorseful  he was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon  he was a nuisance  she stays behind at chabashira s request once her brother and tachibana are sent out","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–248<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You will no longer face suspension. The school will not consider you a problem child. You will be able to participate in club activities from today onward. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;No, I don’t.&quot; — asked whether Sudō will become a model student<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;However…Sudou-kun certainly made some progress today. He admitted he was at fault. So I’m sure that he’ll grow more tomorrow.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She notes that Kushida-san and Hirata-kun’s actions in the hearing &quot;would be rewarded as well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No, I’ve already abandoned him. I just won’t allow him to run loose anymore.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On his exit for club practice: &quot;He was not remorseful. He was definitely going to cause trouble for us again soon. He was a nuisance.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> She stays behind at Chabashira’s request once her brother and Tachibana are sent out.<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p244-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal she did not have to ask for<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p246-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sudou-ken","q":"sudo ken ch 7 sec  7 5 7 6  the lecture  the apology  the party dissatisfied but nodding  the suspension is gone and his club activities restart that day   he he  well  of course    to  i m glad  sudou   yeah    after chabashira tells him the incident happened because of his behavior  that s    on being told horikita will eventually leave him  i understand  if i hadn t acted that way in the first place  then i wouldn t have hit those guys  it wouldn t have been such a big deal  i knew that  somewhere   i always fought all i wanted for my own satisfaction  but it s not like that anymore  i m a class d student  and my personal actions affect the entire class  now i ve experienced that firsthand   i won t cause problems again  sensei  horikita   tch    when chabashira rejects the promise as too casual  y yeah    on hearing that horikita has not abandoned him  wh what does that mean   well  i m gonna get going  i have club activities  see you later  horikita  he leaves smiling  as if he just shaken off something heavy   man  i don t understand what happened  but horikita did something for me  right   well  i gotta head to my club  we should have a party tonight  the page marks the apology as his first penitent words  while insisting he is still himself  a person can t change in one day","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p246-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p246-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5–7.6: the lecture, the apology, the party<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.246–252<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;He he. Well, of course!&quot; — to &quot;I’m glad, Sudou&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;Yeah…&quot; — after Chabashira tells him the incident happened because of his behavior<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> &quot;That’s…&quot; — on being told Horikita will eventually leave him<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Dissatisfied but nodding: the suspension is gone and his club activities restart that day.<span class=\"pg\">p.246<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I understand… If I hadn’t acted that way in the first place, then I wouldn’t have hit those guys. It wouldn’t have been such a big deal. I knew that, somewhere.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I always fought all I wanted for my own satisfaction. But it’s not like that anymore… I’m a Class D student, and my personal actions affect the entire class. Now I’ve experienced that firsthand…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I won’t cause problems again, sensei. Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Tch!&quot; — when Chabashira rejects the promise as too casual<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Y-yeah…&quot; — on hearing that Horikita has not abandoned him<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wh-what does that mean?!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’m gonna get going. I have club activities. See you later, Horikita.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> He leaves smiling &quot;as if he just shaken off something heavy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Man, I don’t understand what happened, but Horikita did something for me. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I gotta head to my club. We should have a party tonight.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> The page marks the apology as his first penitent words, while insisting he is still himself: a person can’t change in one day.<span class=\"pg\">p.247<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v2-p242-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: waiting for the retrial to start<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"chabashira sae ch 7 sec  7 5  the private lesson about ayanokoji  so  what methods did you use  horikita   don t try to dodge the question  they wouldn t withdraw their complaint without a reason  would they   so it s a secret  hmm  well  allow me to change the question  who came up with the strategy that defeated class c   ayanokouji isn t here  so i m a little curious   i see  so you recognize that  hmm   his potential  hmm   there are various things to consider  but if you want to reach class a  i ll give you one bit of advice   the students in class d all have some kind of defect  more or less  to borrow an expression used by others in this school  class d is an assemblage of people that could be called  defective products  you already understand this quite well though  don t you   well  what do you think is ayanokouji s defect   oh  and what is it   he dislikes trouble  hmm  is that what you perceive when you look at ayanokouji   well  horikita  let s try to learn as much as we possibly can about the boy called ayanokouji  without delay  shall we  otherwise  it ll be too late  you already seem to have fallen into ayanokouji s trap   why do you think ayanokouji purposefully got scores of 50 points across on the board on his entrance examination  why do you think ayanokouji is helping you  why do you think that ayanokouji doesn t put himself forward as a superior student  despite having superior ability  is ayanokouji kiyotaka really someone who  dislikes trouble   in my personal opinion  ayanokouji is the most defective student in class d   higher functioning products are more difficult to handle  if you misunderstand how to handle him  the class might be completely destroyed in short order   get to know the person called ayanokouji  what is he thinking  what focal point does he base his actions around  what is his fatal flaw  there s definitely an answer there  she says nothing more  and the page gives no reason for the warning beyond horikita s own unanswered question  her usual manner is  unaware of and unconcerned with her class  which is why the session itself is the surprise","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p248-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.248–251<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;So. What methods did you use, Horikita?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Don’t try to dodge the question. They wouldn’t withdraw their complaint without a reason, would they?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;So it’s a secret, hmm? Well, allow me to change the question. Who came up with the strategy that defeated Class C?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji isn’t here, so I’m a little curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I see. So you recognize that, hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;His potential, hmm?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;There are various things to consider. But if you want to reach Class A, I’ll give you one bit of advice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;The students in Class D all have some kind of defect, more or less. To borrow an expression used by others in this school, Class D is an assemblage of people that could be called ‘defective products.’ You already understand this quite well though, don’t you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, what do you think is Ayanokouji’s defect?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Oh? And what is it?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He dislikes trouble, hmm? Is that what you perceive when you look at Ayanokouji?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249–250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, Horikita. Let’s try to learn as much as we possibly can about the boy called Ayanokouji, without delay, shall we? Otherwise, it’ll be too late. You already seem to have fallen into Ayanokouji’s trap.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Why do you think Ayanokouji purposefully got scores of 50 points across on the board on his entrance examination? Why do you think Ayanokouji is helping you? Why do you think that Ayanokouji doesn’t put himself forward as a superior student, despite having superior ability? Is Ayanokouji Kiyotaka really someone who ‘dislikes trouble’?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;In my personal opinion, Ayanokouji is the most defective student in Class D.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Higher functioning products are more difficult to handle. If you misunderstand how to handle him, the class might be completely destroyed in short order.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Get to know the person called Ayanokouji. What is he thinking? What focal point does he base his actions around? What is his fatal flaw? There’s definitely an answer there.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> She says nothing more, and the page gives no reason for the warning beyond Horikita’s own unanswered question.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Her usual manner is &quot;unaware of and unconcerned with her class,&quot; which is why the session itself is the surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v2-p246-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: what she says to Sudō<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"chabashira-sae horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 5  the private lesson about ayanokoji  what do you mean   why do you care about that   i ll leave that to your imagination   we d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner   i don t want to admit this  but ayanokouji kun might have something exceptional to him   is that surprising  you were the one who first put me together with ayanokouji kun  chabashira sensei  you did it because you couldn t overlook ayanokouji kun s potential  right   though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot  for some mysterious reason   yes  he was truly incomprehensible  i could not find meaning in such behavior   i don t intend to admit that i have a defect  but i do understand   we ve already established it  he already knows what his own defect is   he  dislikes trouble  answering with confidence  she still feels  a strange sense of discomfort that i couldn t explain   no  it s because he said it himself   had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well   that unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort   chabashira sensei  do you really understand what about him can be considered defective   why was chabashira sensei telling me such things  the session ends with chabashira saying nothing more and horikita carrying the questions out of the room","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.248–251<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;What do you mean?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Why do you care about that?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;I’ll leave that to your imagination.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;We’d fabricated a lie because we were backed into a corner.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.248<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t want to admit this, but Ayanokouji-kun…might have something exceptional to him.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Is that surprising? You were the one who first put me together with Ayanokouji-kun, Chabashira-sensei. You did it because you couldn’t overlook Ayanokouji-kun’s potential, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Though he does try to hide his ability by pretending to be an idiot, for some mysterious reason.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Yes, he was truly incomprehensible. I could not find meaning in such behavior.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I don’t intend to admit that I have a defect. But I do understand.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;We’ve already established it. He already knows what his own defect is.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;He ‘dislikes trouble,’&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Answering with confidence, she still feels &quot;a strange sense of discomfort that I couldn’t explain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.249<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;No… It’s because he said it himself.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Had he deliberately poked his nose into this incident as well?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;That unconscious realization must have been the cause of my earlier discomfort.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Chabashira-sensei, do you really understand what about him can be considered defective?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.250<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;Why was Chabashira-sensei telling me such things?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.251<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The session ends with Chabashira saying nothing more and Horikita carrying the questions out of the room.<span class=\"pg\">p.248–251<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p246-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the verdict, and Chabashira’s lecture to Sudō<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\">→ After: Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the puppet question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"inner spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 7 sec  7 6  the corridor after the withdrawal he waits outside the student council room  sudo leaves cheerful  then the president and secretary tachibana come out   looks like it went well   yeah    to sudo s proposal of a party that night  is that so   well  i guess miracles do happen   your little sister handled things well  i didn t do anything  the president holds still and looks him in the eyes  the page withholds what he makes of the answer   nah  i hate troublesome stuff  besides  being in the student council is no joke  i want to lead an ordinary student life at this school   well  i d just never do anything that i m not interested in   yo    greeted by the hardest glare he has seen from horikita  which she covers at once  what were the results   i m glad to hear that  looks like your strategy worked well   my puppet  what are you talking about   you re overthinking it  it s just coincidence   what do you mean  who am i  i m just a guy who dislikes trouble  right   well  i ll be heading back now    he turns on the feeling that it would be better not to be seen together with her he admits the involvement went too far and needs to be dialed back   i had to dial it back a little  i just wanted my life here to be peaceful  the black haired boy who stops in front of them has  black hair  styled so it was worn long  is about his height  and never fully turns to face them  the page does not name him here   i m done talking   you sort of forced me to  you helped sudou in this case  too  right   i m thinking  this is annoying  and  i don t have any motivation to do this  stuff like that  that s what i m thinking  even if you took back what you said just now  horikita  i do intend to live my life quietly  whether we aim for class a or whatever  that s it   i thought that i should help the first friends i ve ever made  probably  he suspects chabashira is behind horikita s new questions   i wouldn t be surprised if she knew about my past  his conclusion  walked to in the corridor   we d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as ryuuen  on the road ahead   in other words  it was fair to say that trying to reach class a in three years was hopeless  he turns the analysis on himself   i knew more about me than anyone else  i knew just how defective  just how foolish i was  i was a horrible human being","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p252-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the corridor after the withdrawal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.252–256<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He waits outside the student council room; Sudō leaves cheerful, then the president and Secretary Tachibana come out.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Looks like it went well&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Yeah.&quot; — to Sudō’s proposal of a party that night<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> &quot;Is that so?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I guess miracles do happen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Your little sister handled things well. I didn’t do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The president holds still and looks him in the eyes; the page withholds what he makes of the answer.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Nah, I hate troublesome stuff. Besides, being in the student council is no joke. I want to lead an ordinary student life at this school,&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well, I’d just never do anything that I’m not interested in…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Yo.&quot; — greeted by the hardest glare he has seen from Horikita, which she covers at once<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What were the results?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m glad to hear that. Looks like your strategy worked well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;My puppet? What are you talking about?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You’re overthinking it. It’s just coincidence.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;What do you mean, who am I? I’m just a guy who dislikes trouble, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Well. I’ll be heading back now.&quot; — he turns on the feeling that it would be better not to be seen together with her<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He admits the involvement went too far and needs to be dialed back: &quot;I had to dial it back a little. I just wanted my life here to be peaceful.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The black-haired boy who stops in front of them has &quot;black hair, styled so it was worn long,&quot; is about his height, and never fully turns to face them; the page does not name him here.<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m done talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You sort of forced me to. You helped Sudou in this case, too. Right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I’m thinking ‘This is annoying,’ and ‘I don’t have any motivation to do this.’ Stuff like that. That’s what I’m thinking. Even if you took back what you said just now, Horikita, I do intend to live my life quietly. Whether we aim for Class A or whatever, that’s it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;I thought that I should help the first friends I’ve ever made. Probably.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He suspects Chabashira is behind Horikita’s new questions: &quot;I wouldn’t be surprised if she knew about my past.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His conclusion, walked to in the corridor: &quot;We’d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On the road ahead: &quot;In other words, it was fair to say that trying to reach Class A in three years was hopeless.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> He turns the analysis on himself: &quot;I knew more about me than anyone else. I knew just how defective, just how foolish I was. I was a horrible human being.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.256<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v2-p234-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.3–7.4: the fake cameras and the shuttered door<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-manabu","q":"horikita manabu ch 7 sec  7 6  the thanks  and the secretary seat  excellent work   i have approved class c s request to withdraw their complaint   so this was all to prove that sakura wasn t a liar  as you said  i suppose if class c withdrew their complaint  then talk would spread quite naturally  if sudou or sakura weren t the liars  then class c was  he stops in his tracks to address ayanokoji instead of exchanging a light greeting  and stays still while he is looked at   tachibana  do you still have one seat open for secretary   ayanokouji  if you wanted it  i would appoint you to the position   do you disapprove  he spells out the result as the proof of her credibility  with the withdrawal  class c becomes the liar  he offers him the secretary position on the spot  the offer is refused without discussion","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html#sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p252-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the thanks, and the secretary seat<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.252–253<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-manabu.html\">Horikita Manabu<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;Excellent work.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;I have approved Class C’s request to withdraw their complaint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Manabu<\/b> &quot;So this was all to prove that Sakura wasn’t a liar, as you said? I suppose if Class C withdrew their complaint, then talk would spread quite naturally. If Sudou or Sakura weren’t the liars, then Class C was.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He stops in his tracks to address Ayanokōji instead of exchanging a light greeting, and stays still while he is looked at.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Tachibana. Do you still have one seat open for secretary?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji. If you wanted it, I would appoint you to the position.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Do you disapprove?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> He spells out the result as the proof of her credibility: with the withdrawal, Class C becomes the liar.<span class=\"pg\">p.252<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> He offers him the secretary position on the spot; the offer is refused without discussion.<span class=\"pg\">p.252–253<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-manabu-y1v2-p244-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the withdrawal ruling<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"horikita suzune ch 7 sec  7 6  the puppet question  you d already know  right   hey  ayanokouji kun  am i just your puppet   ayanokouji kun  you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms  next  you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras  then  you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence  so that we could parse the truth from lies  when i look back on it now  that s all i can think of   who are you    thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case  just coincidence   and you are    to the black haired boy who stops in front of them  wait  we re not done talking  ayanokouji kun   you promised  right  you promised you d help me reach class a   that s not what i meant  i want to know what you re thinking   if you really hated drawing attention  you wouldn t make all this effort to get involved  you say you re someone who  dislikes trouble  after all  yet you act all evasive and non committal even while you help me  why  the chapter ends with her accusation of being steered and his evasion  unanswered","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p253-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the puppet question<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.253–255<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;You’d already know, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Hey, Ayanokouji-kun. Am I just your puppet?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false…<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Ayanokouji-kun, you brought up the idea of surveillance cameras in the classrooms. Next, you took me to the special building and made me realize that there were no cameras. Then, you guided me to the idea of inventing false evidence, so that we could parse the truth from lies… When I look back on it now, that’s all I can think of.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.253–254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Who are you?&quot; — thrown back at him after he calls her account of the case &quot;just coincidence&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;And you are?&quot; — to the black-haired boy who stops in front of them<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;Wait. We’re not done talking, Ayanokouji-kun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;You promised, right? You promised you’d help me reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;That’s not what I meant. I want to know what you’re thinking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> &quot;If you really hated drawing attention, you wouldn’t make all this effort to get involved. You say you’re someone who ‘dislikes trouble,’ after all. Yet you act all evasive and non-committal even while you help me. Why?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter ends with her accusation of being steered and his evasion, unanswered.<span class=\"pg\">p.253–255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v2-p248-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.5: the private lesson about Ayanokōji<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1","v":"y1v2","y":1,"o":2,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ryuen kakeru ch 7 sec  7 6  the boy in the corridor he stops in front of ayanokoji and horikita in the corridor   black hair worn long  about ayanokoji s height  a wide grin the page calls ominous  never fully turning to face them  the scene does not name him   setting up a camera  you really did something funny  huh   next time  i ll be your opponent  i look forward to it  he walks on without answering horikita s  and you are  ayanokoji s closing inventory names the encounter   we d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as ryuuen","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p254-1\">Ch.7 sec. 7.6: the boy in the corridor<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V2 · p.254–255<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">He stops in front of Ayanokōji and Horikita in the corridor — black hair worn long, about Ayanokōji’s height, a wide grin the page calls ominous, never fully turning to face them. The scene does not name him.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Setting up a camera? You really did something funny, huh?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> &quot;Next time, I’ll be your opponent. I look forward to it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> He walks on without answering Horikita’s &quot;And you are?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.254<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Ayanokōji’s closing inventory names the encounter: &quot;We’d received a declaration of war from some guy apparently known as Ryuuen.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.255<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v2-p241-1\">← Before: Ch.7 sec. 7.4: named before he is seen<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
